a:5006:{i:0;a:37:{s:4:"Name";s:28:"Lansweeper-Network-Discovery";s:10:"Repository";s:58:"ghcr.io/007darkmatter5/lansweeper-network-discovery:latest";s:8:"Registry";s:106:"https://github.com/007darkmatter5/lansweeper-network-discovery/pkgs/container/lansweeper-network-discovery";s:7:"Network";s:4:"host";s:5:"Shell";s:4:"bash";s:10:"Privileged";s:5:"false";s:7:"Support";s:69:"https://github.com/007darkmatter5/lansweeper-network-discovery/issues";s:7:"Project";s:62:"https://github.com/007darkmatter5/lansweeper-network-discovery";s:6:"ReadMe";s:69:"https://github.com/007darkmatter5/lansweeper-network-discovery#readme";s:11:"TemplateURL";s:113:"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/007darkmatter5/unraid-templates/main/templates/lansweeper-network-discovery.xml";s:4:"Icon";s:96:"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/007darkmatter5/lansweeper-network-discovery/main/docs/icon.png";s:5:"WebUI";s:26:"https://[IP]:[PORT:59525]/";s:8:"Overview";s:1097:"Unofficial container for Lansweeper Network Discovery. It runs the Hub and the IT Sensor
    together: the sensor scans your network, and the Hub sends what it finds to your
    Lansweeper Site. Not affiliated with or supported by Lansweeper.

    The image installs the official Linux packages from Lansweeper's apt repository when it
    is built, and is rebuilt when Lansweeper releases a new version.

    To link it to your Site, paste the linking code from your Site (Discovery > Discovery
    systems > Link discovery system) into Linking Code, or link it from the web UI after
    the first start. The web UI uses a self-signed certificate.

    First start: open https://your-server:59526/ (the Setup Port) and set the admin
    password. The Hub only allows this from the server itself, so the container relays that
    port locally until the password is set, then closes it. After that, use the WebUI link.

    Host networking is required for discovery to see your LAN. Keep appdata on cache or an
