";s:4:"Mask";s:5:"false";}s:5:"value";s:0:"";}i:9;a:2:{s:11:"@attributes";a:9:{s:4:"Name";s:9:"Log Level";s:6:"Target";s:17:"SUBLARR_LOG_LEVEL";s:7:"Default";s:4:"INFO";s:4:"Mode";s:0:"";s:11:"Description";s:58:"Advanced: log verbosity — DEBUG, INFO, WARNING or ERROR.";s:4:"Type";s:8:"Variable";s:7:"Display";s:8:"advanced";s:8:"Required";s:5:"false";s:4:"Mask";s:5:"false";}s:5:"value";s:4:"INFO";}}s:12:"TemplatePath";s:34:"/tmp/GitHub/AppFeed/my-sublarr.xml";s:4:"Repo";s:22:"Abrechen2's Repository";s:12:"CategoryList";a:3:{i:0;s:14:"MediaApp-Video";i:1;s:11:"Downloaders";i:2;s:15:"Tools-Utilities";}s:9:"downloads";i:5944;s:9:"FirstSeen";i:1781352286;s:10:"LastUpdate";i:1790493493;s:14:"LastUpdateScan";i:1791850487;s:8:"Category";s:43:"MediaApp:Video Downloaders: Tools:Utilities";s:2:"ID";i:121;s:11:"Displayable";b:1;s:6:"Author";s:9:"abrechen2";s:13:"DockerHubName";s:7:"sublarr";s:8:"RepoName";s:22:"Abrechen2's Repository";s:10:"SortAuthor";s:9:"abrechen2";s:8:"SortName";s:7:"Sublarr";s:6:"random";i:1270193304;s:9:"Blacklist";b:0;s:6:"MinVer";s:3:"6.0";s:4:"Path";s:112:"/tmp/community.applications/tempFiles/templates-community-apps/Abrechen2sRepository/abrechen2-Sublarr-latest.xml";s:4:"Date";N;s:11:"BrandNewApp";b:1;s:10:"Deprecated";b:0;s:10:"DonateText";s:29:"Support TravStats development";s:10:"DonateLink";s:60:"https://www.paypal.com/donate?hosted_button_id=HW9MPYVURCT42";s:10:"Compatible";b:1;s:16:"ModeratorComment";N;}i:122;a:50:{s:4:"Name";s:12:"travstats-db";s:10:"Repository";s:22:"postgis/postgis:15-3.4";s:8:"Registry";s:40:"https://hub.docker.com/r/postgis/postgis";s:7:"Network";s:6:"bridge";s:5:"Shell";s:2:"sh";s:10:"Privileged";s:5:"false";s:7:"Support";s:84:"https://forums.unraid.net/topic/198320-support-travstats-self-hosted-flight-tracker/";s:7:"Project";s:41:"https://github.com/postgis/docker-postgis";s:8:"Overview";s:2377:"PostgreSQL 15 with the PostGIS 3.4 spatial extension — the database TravStats expects.

This template is pre-filled with the container name `travstats-db` and the database/user pair `flights/flights` so the default `DATABASE_URL` in the TravStats template matches without further editing. **Change the password to a strong value** (e.g. `openssl rand -base64 32`) and reuse it in TravStats.

**Install order:** this container **first**, then the TravStats template. The database is published on the Unraid host at port 5432 (adjustable below) so TravStats can reach it via `host.docker.internal:5432` without needing a shared Docker network. Keep the port free of conflicts with other PostgreSQL containers you may already run.

**Storage:** the default Application Data path (`/mnt/user/appdata/travstats-db`) maps to PostgreSQL's data directory. The actual cluster lives in a `pgdata/` subdirectory (see the `PGDATA` variable below) — this is the officially recommended layout from the `postgres` Docker image and avoids a well-known Unraid permission issue where `chown` from inside the container can't reach the FUSE-backed share root.

The initial cluster is created on first start and then kept in place on updates; deleting the `pgdata/` subdirectory wipes the database, so point your backup tool at this folder.

**Why PostGIS, not plain Postgres?** TravStats uses PostGIS for airport and route geometry. Plain `postgres:15` fails the first TravStats migration.

---

**Troubleshooting — "FATAL: could not open file global/pg_filenode.map: Permission denied"**

If you see this error in the container log and TravStats shows "Error querying the database" on its setup page, your `pgdata/` directory was created under the wrong UID by a previous (broken) install. Fix:

1. Stop both containers (`TravStats`, `travstats-db`).
2. On the Unraid console: `rm -rf /mnt/user/appdata/travstats-db/pgdata` *(or whichever Application Data path you chose)*.
3. Start `travstats-db` — it now re-runs `initdb` with the correct UID (999, the Postgres user inside the image).
4. Start `TravStats` — setup page should load without errors.

If the fresh start still fails on `/mnt/user/...`, switch the Application Data path to `/mnt/cache/appdata/travstats-db` (direct cache-pool mount, bypasses Unraid's FUSE layer) and repeat step 3. Requires a cache pool to be configured.";s:11:"TemplateURL";s:85:"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/Abrechen2/docker-templates/main/my-travstats-db.xml";s:4:"Icon";s:87:"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/Abrechen2/docker-templates/main/icon-travstats-db.png";s:11:"ExtraParams";s:24:"--restart=unless-stopped";s:8:"Requires";s:57:"Used together with the TravStats Community Apps template.";s:6:"Config";a:7:{i:0;a:2:{s:11:"@attributes";a:9:{s:4:"Name";s:16:"Application Data";s:6:"Target";s:24:"/var/lib/postgresql/data";s:7:"Default";s:30:"/mnt/user/appdata/travstats-db";s:4:"Mode";s:2:"rw";s:11:"Description";s:217:"Parent directory for the PostgreSQL data. The actual cluster is created as a `pgdata/` subfolder here (see PGDATA). One persistent mount, survives container updates. Back this path up with your regular appdata backup.";s:4:"Type";s:4:"Path";s:7:"Display";s:6:"always";s:8:"Required";s:4:"true";s:4:"Mask";s:5:"false";}s:5:"value";s:30:"/mnt/user/appdata/travstats-db";}i:1;a:2:{s:11:"@attributes";a:9:{s:4:"Name";s:6:"PGDATA";s:6:"Target";s:6:"PGDATA";s:7:"Default";s:31:"/var/lib/postgresql/data/pgdata";s:4:"Mode";s:0:"";s:11:"Description";s:266:"Actual PostgreSQL data subdirectory inside the Application Data mount. Using a subfolder (instead of the bind-mount root) is the official postgres-image recommendation and avoids a common Unraid FUSE permission issue. Do not change unless you know what you're doing.";s:4:"Type";s:8:"Variable";s:7:"Display";s:8:"advanced";s:8:"Required";s:4:"true";s:4:"Mask";s:5:"false";}s:5:"value";s:31:"/var/lib/postgresql/data/pgdata";}i:2;a:2:{s:11:"@attributes";a:9:{s:4:"Name";s:11:"POSTGRES_DB";s:6:"Target";s:11:"POSTGRES_DB";s:7:"Default";s:7:"flights";s:4:"Mode";s:0:"";s:11:"Description";s:51:"Database name. TravStats default expects 'fli