GitHub/AppFeed/mkv-language-remover/mkv-language-remover.xml";s:4:"Repo";s:20:"BBergle's Repository";s:12:"CategoryList";a:1:{i:0;s:15:"Tools-Utilities";}s:4:"Beta";s:4:"true";s:9:"downloads";i:1756;s:9:"FirstSeen";i:1699716989;s:10:"LastUpdate";i:1707086154;s:14:"LastUpdateScan";i:1791198847;s:8:"Category";s:15:"Tools:Utilities";s:2:"ID";i:162;s:11:"Displayable";b:1;s:6:"Author";s:7:"bbergle";s:13:"DockerHubName";s:28:"bbergle-mkv-language-remover";s:8:"RepoName";s:20:"BBergle's Repository";s:10:"SortAuthor";s:7:"bbergle";s:8:"SortName";s:28:"bbergle mkv language remover";s:6:"random";i:944591251;s:9:"Blacklist";b:0;s:6:"MinVer";s:3:"6.0";s:4:"Path";s:126:"/tmp/community.applications/tempFiles/templates-community-apps/BBerglesRepository/bbergle-bberglemkvlanguageremover-latest.xml";s:4:"Date";N;s:11:"BrandNewApp";b:1;s:10:"Deprecated";b:0;s:10:"Compatible";b:1;s:16:"ModeratorComment";N;}i:163;a:34:{s:4:"Name";s:11:"plezy-relay";s:10:"Repository";s:34:"ghcr.io/bbergle/plezy-relay:latest";s:8:"Registry";s:65:"https://github.com/BBergle/plezy-relay/pkgs/container/plezy-relay";s:7:"Network";s:6:"bridge";s:10:"Privileged";s:5:"false";s:7:"Support";s:39:"https://github.com/edde746/plezy/issues";s:7:"Project";s:32:"https://github.com/edde746/plezy";s:8:"Overview";s:1117:"Self-hosted relay server for Plezy's "Watch Together" feature.

Plezy is a cross-platform Plex & Jellyfin client. Watch Together syncs playback between viewers through a small relay server, and this container runs your own instead of using the public one.

This container has NO web interface. After starting it, open Plezy on each device and set Settings - Watch Together Relay to:
    http://YOUR-Unraid-IP:9977

The URL must be http:// or https://. To watch together, everyone must be using the same relay.

To reach the relay from outside your LAN, put a reverse proxy with TLS in front of it (it has no TLS of its own), give clients the proxy's https:// address, and set TRUSTED_PROXY_CIDRS so rate limiting sees real client IPs.

