c latest tag was verified as v30.1.5.1 on September 13, 2026; provenance and immutable tags are recorded in the template repository. Browser GUI is unauthenticated: use only a trusted private LAN or an authenticated VPN/proxy, never direct Internet exposure. Preserve wallet backups, UID/GID 1000 access and the existing appdata mapping; never share one data directory between running clients. Allow 150 seconds for shutdown. Staking and claim mining are disabled at startup; no wallet is created or unlocked automatically. Publishing an image does not update existing containers. See https://projectblackcoin.org/upgrade and the repository publishing guide before upgrading.";s:5:"WebUI";s:32:"http://[IP]:[PORT:8080]/vnc.html";s:11:"TemplateURL";s:83:"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/Blackcoin-Dev/unraid-templates/main/blackcoin.xml";s:4:"Icon";s:37:"https://blackcoin.org/images/logo.png";s:11:"ExtraParams";s:43:"--restart unless-stopped --stop-timeout 150";s:6:"Config";a:3:{i:0;a:2:{s:11:"@attributes";a:9:{s:4:"Name";s:10:"WebUI Port";s:6:"Target";s:4:"8080";s:7:"Default";s:4:"9595";s:4:"Mode";s:3:"tcp";s:11:"Description";s:55:"The port to access the visual Wallet UI in your browser";s:4:"Type";s:4:"Port";s:7:"Display";s:6:"always";s:8:"Required";s:4:"true";s:4:"Mask";s:5:"false";}s:5:"value";s:4:"9595";}i:1;a:2:{s:11:"@attributes";a:9:{s:4:"Name";s:8:"P2P Port";s:6:"Target";s:5:"15714";s:7:"Default";s:5:"15714";s:4:"Mode";s:3:"tcp";s:11:"Description";s:50:"The P2P network port for connecting to other nodes";s:4:"Type";s:4:"Port";s:7:"Display";s:6:"always";s:8:"Required";s:4:"true";s:4:"Mask";s:5:"false";}s:5:"value";s:5:"15714";}i:2;a:2:{s:11:"@attributes";a:9:{s:4:"Name";s:17:"Appdata Directory";s:6:"Target";s:26:"/home/blackcoin/.blackcoin";s:7:"Default";s:27:"/mnt/user/appdata/blackcoin";s:4:"Mode";s:2:"rw";s:11:"Description";s:69:"Location to safely store the blockchain data and your wallet.dat file";s:4:"Type";s:4:"Path";s:7:"Display";s:6:"always";s:8:"Required";s:4:"true";s:4:"Mask";s:5:"false";}s:5:"value";s:27:"/mnt/user/appdata/blackcoin";}}s:12:"TemplatePath";s:33:"/tmp/GitHub/AppFeed/blackcoin.xml";s:4:"Repo";s:24:"QQBlackcoin's Repository";s:12:"CategoryList";a:3:{i:0;s:7:"Network";i:1;s:10:"WebServers";i:2;s:12:"Productivity";}s:9:"downloads";i:19472;s:9:"FirstSeen";i:1783382637;s:10:"LastUpdate";i:1790508656;s:14:"LastUpdateScan";i:1791198847;s:8:"Category";s:34:"Network: WebServers: Productivity:";s:2:"ID";i:196;s:11:"Displayable";b:1;s:6:"Author";s:11:"qqblackcoin";s:13:"DockerHubName";s:24:"blackcoin-quantum-quasar";s:8:"RepoName";s:24:"QQBlackcoin's Repository";s:10:"SortAuthor";s:11:"qqblackcoin";s:8:"SortName";s:24:"Blackcoin Quantum Quasar";s:6:"random";i:986248734;s:9:"Blacklist";b:0;s:6:"MinVer";s:3:"6.0";s:4:"Path";s:131:"/tmp/community.applications/tempFiles/templates-community-apps/QQBlackcoinsRepository/qqblackcoin-BlackcoinQuantumQuasar-latest.xml";s:4:"Date";N;s:11:"BrandNewApp";b:1;s:10:"Deprecated";b:0;s:10:"Compatible";b:1;s:16:"ModeratorComment";N;}i:197;a:41:{s:4:"Name";s:6:"ROMarr";s:10:"Repository";s:33:"ghcr.io/blizzhacker/romarr:latest";s:8:"Registry";s:59:"https://github.com/BlizzHacker/romarr/pkgs/container/romarr";s:7:"Network";s:6:"bridge";s:10:"Privileged";s:5:"false";s:5:"Shell";s:2:"sh";s:7:"Support";s:44:"https://github.com/BlizzHacker/romarr/issues";s:7:"Project";s:37:"https://github.com/BlizzHacker/romarr";s:6:"ReadMe";s:67:"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/BlizzHacker/romarr/main/README.md";s:4:"Icon";s:83:"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/BlizzHacker/cartridge-unraid/main/icon/romarr.png";s:11:"TemplateURL";s:88:"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/BlizzHacker/cartridge-unraid/main/templates/romarr.xml";s:5:"WebUI";s:23:"http://[IP]:[PORT:6868]";s:16:"ExtraSearchTerms";s:85:"romarr rom roms retro emulation arr romm gaseous retrom prowlarr game games cartridge";s:7:"License";s:3:"MIT";s:6:"MinVer";s:3:"6.9";s:8:"Overview";s:1732:"The *arr for games. Request a title, ROMarr searches your indexers through Prowlarr, hands the winner to your download client, and files the ROM into your game library where it can actually be played. If you run Radarr for films and Sonarr for TV, this is the missing one.

ROMarr is not tied to one library: RomM, Gaseous and Retrom are all supported and chosen with a single setting. There is also a "folder" mode that writes a plain directory tree laid out by platform, which is what Batocera, RetroPie, EmulationStation, ES-DE, EmuDeck, Pegasus, Lakka, muOS and LaunchBox all read.

READ THIS BEFORE YOU HIT APPLY. ROMarr reads these variables ONCE, on first start, and copies them into its own settings. After that the saved settings win and editing the variables here does nothing at all. That is deliberate -- it is what lets you change things on the Settings page without the template overriding you every restart -- but it is the opposite of how most Unraid containers behave, so get the values right the first time. To change something later, use ROMarr's own Settings page, not this template.

One more thing worth getting right up front:

The "Completed downloads" path must match what your download client REPORTS, character for character. ROMarr asks the client where a finished download is and then opens that path itself, so if qBittorrent says /data/completed then ROMarr needs to see /data/completed too. Check qBittorrent's Options - Downloads "Save path", or SABnzbd's Config - Folders "Completed Download Folder", and set the container path to match. If the two genuinely cannot agree, leave it and add a remap under Settings - Media Management instead.

Unofficial. Not affiliated with RomM, Gaseous or Retrom.";s:8:"Requires";s:341:"<br>A running Prowlarr, at least one download client (qBittorrent, SABnzbd or NZBGet), and somewhere to put the ROMs -- either RomM, Gaseous or Retrom, or a plain folder.<br><br>At least one download client is genuinely required, not merely recommended: a release found with no client that speaks its protocol is ranked and then refused.<br>";s:10:"Screenshot";a:5:{i:0;s:77:"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/BlizzHacker/romarr/main/docs/img/status.png";i:1;s:89:"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/BlizzHacker/romarr/main/docs/img/interactive-search.png";i:2;s:78:"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/BlizzHacker/romarr/main/docs/img/library.png";i:3;s:80:"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/BlizzHacker/romarr/main/docs/img/libraries.png";i:4;s:82:"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/BlizzHacker/romarr/main/docs/img/hub-plugins.png";}s:6:"Config";a:24:{i:0;a:2:{s:11:"@attributes";a:9:{s:4:"Name";s:5:"WebUI";s:6:"Target";s:4:"6868";s:7:"Default";s:4:"6868";s:4:"Mode";s:3:"tcp";s:11:"Description";s:32:"Port for ROMarr's web interface.";s:4:"Type";s:4:"Port";s:7:"Display";s:6:"always";s:8:"Required";s:4:"true";s:4:"Mask";s:5:"false";}s:5:"value";s:4:"6868";}i:1;a:2:{s:11:"@attributes";a:9:{s:4:"Name";s:7:"Appdata";s:6:"Target";s:7:"/config";s:7:"Default";s:24:"/mnt/user/appdata/romarr";s:4:"Mode";s:2:"rw";s:11:"Description";s:64:"ROMarr's settings, history and indexer configuration. Keep this.";s:4:"Type";s:4:"Path";s:7:"Display";s:6:"always";s:8:"Required";s:4:"true";s:4:"Mask";s:5:"false";}s:5:"value";s:24:"/mnt/user/appdata/romarr";}i:2;a:2:{s:11:"@attributes";a:9:{s:4:"Name";s:11:"ROM library";s:6:"Target";s:5:"/roms";s:7:"Default";s:14:"/mnt/user/roms";s:4:"Mode";s:2:"rw";s:11:"Description";s:161:"Where finished ROMs are filed. Point the left-hand side at the same share your library app reads. The right-hand side must match the Library path variable below.";s:4:"Type";s:4:"Path";s:7:"Display";s:6:"