Most likely: appdata/beoradioscrobbler";s:4:"Type";s:4:"Path";s:7:"Display";s:6:"always";s:8:"Required";s:4:"true";s:4:"Mask";s:5:"false";}s:5:"value";s:35:"/mnt/user/appdata/beoradioscrobbler";}i:8;a:2:{s:11:"@attributes";a:9:{s:4:"Name";s:8:"LOGLEVEL";s:6:"Target";s:8:"LOGLEVEL";s:7:"Default";s:0:"";s:4:"Mode";s:0:"";s:11:"Description";s:61:"Log level in general log file. INFO, DEBUG. Defaults to INFO.";s:4:"Type";s:8:"Variable";s:7:"Display";s:6:"always";s:8:"Required";s:5:"false";s:4:"Mask";s:5:"false";}s:5:"value";s:4:"INFO";}}s:17:"TailscaleStateDir";s:0:"";s:12:"TemplatePath";s:63:"/tmp/GitHub/AppFeed/beo_radio_scrobbler/beo_radio_scrobbler.xml";s:4:"Repo";s:26:"CaptainPimpJr's Repository";s:12:"CategoryList";a:1:{i:0;s:14:"MediaApp-Music";}s:9:"downloads";i:1516;s:9:"FirstSeen";i:1768847777;s:10:"LastUpdate";i:1774011705;s:14:"LastUpdateScan";i:1790525754;s:8:"Category";s:14:"MediaApp:Music";s:2:"ID";i:222;s:11:"Displayable";b:1;s:6:"Author";s:8:"cptpijun";s:13:"DockerHubName";s:17:"beoradioscrobbler";s:8:"RepoName";s:26:"CaptainPimpJr's Repository";s:10:"SortAuthor";s:8:"cptpijun";s:8:"SortName";s:17:"BeoRadioScrobbler";s:6:"random";i:1807295095;s:9:"Blacklist";b:0;s:6:"MinVer";s:3:"6.0";s:4:"Path";s:125:"/tmp/community.applications/tempFiles/templates-community-apps/CaptainPimpJrsRepository/cptpijun-BeoRadioScrobbler-latest.xml";s:4:"Date";N;s:11:"BrandNewApp";b:1;s:10:"Deprecated";b:0;s:10:"Compatible";b:1;s:16:"ModeratorComment";N;}i:223;a:40:{s:4:"Name";s:12:"Beltr-NVIDIA";s:10:"Repository";s:36:"ghcr.io/casavargas/beltr:latest-cuda";s:8:"Registry";s:67:"https://github.com/orgs/CasaVargas/packages/container/package/beltr";s:7:"Network";s:6:"bridge";s:5:"Shell";s:4:"bash";s:10:"Privileged";s:5:"false";s:7:"Support";s:51:"https://github.com/CasaVargas/beltr-releases/issues";s:7:"Project";s:17:"https://beltr.app";s:8:"Overview";s:3171:"Karaoke night from the music already on your server. Beltr strips the vocals with local AI, puts word-synced lyrics on the TV, and makes every phone a remote, no app needed. NVIDIA build: separates a song in well under a minute. No NVIDIA card? Pick Beltr.

Beltr turns any song in your music library into a karaoke track. It separates the vocals out with a local AI model, finds synced lyrics online (or drafts them locally when no provider has the song), force-aligns them to the vocal word by word, and displays them on a TV while everyone's phone acts as a remote — scan the QR code on screen, no app to install.

Everything runs on your server. Nothing about your library is uploaded.

THIS IS THE NVIDIA GPU BUILD. It needs the Unraid "Nvidia-Driver" plugin installed and your GPU passed through. Two settings below do that: NVIDIA_VISIBLE_DEVICES must hold your card's UUID (the Nvidia-Driver plugin page in Settings shows it, like GPU-1a2b3c4d-...), and "Extra Parameters" must contain --runtime=nvidia, which this template already sets.

If you do not have an NVIDIA GPU, install plain "Beltr" instead. This image is several GB larger and gains you nothing without a card. It will still run — it falls back to the CPU — so a broken passthrough shows up as "slow", not "broken". Check the GPU panel in Settings after install to confirm the card was actually found.

FIRST RUN: Beltr downloads about 2 GB of model weights into /cache the first time it needs them. That happens once and survives container updates as long as /cache stays mapped. Watch the container log if a first song seems to sit still — the download is what it's doing.

SPEED: with a working GPU, separating a 3-4 minute song takes well under a minute. Most songs then get their lyrics instantly from an online lyrics database; the ones no provider knows fall back to local transcription, which the GPU also accelerates.

LICENSE: Beltr is a one-time purchase (no subscription). Run it free for five songs, then enter your key from beltr.app in the License key field below — or drop it in a file at /config/license.key. It activates once and then works offline. Container updates and restarts do not re-activate, as long as you keep the Config path mapped; a key covers two installs.

AFTER INSTALL: open the WebUI, go to Settings, and add /media as a music folder. Then open http://your-server:8477/tv on whatever screen you're singing at, and scan the QR with a phone.

MICROPHONES NEED HTTPS: browsers only allow microphone access on a secure page. Beltr serves one itself on port 8478 with a self-signed certificate: open https://your-server:8478/tv on the laptop or phone that has the microphone and accept the browser's warning once. Everything else — queueing, playback, lyrics, stem mixing, the QR the TV shows — works over plain http on 8477. A reverse proxy with a real certificate is only needed if you want no warning at all.

NOTE: Beltr assumes everyone who can reach it is trusted. Set AUTH_PASSWORD to put a password on the TV and dashboard screens, but do not expose this container to the internet without a reverse proxy doing real authentication in front of it.";s:5:"WebUI";s:33:"http://[IP]:[PORT:8477]/dashboard";s:11:"TemplateURL";s:87:"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/CasaVargas/beltr-unraid/main/templates/beltr-cuda.xml";s:4:"Icon";s:78:"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/CasaVargas/beltr-unraid/main/icon-nvidia.png";s:6:"ReadMe";s:72:"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/CasaVargas/beltr-unraid/main/README.md";s:16:"ExtraSearchTerms";s:115:"karaoke sing singalong lyrics vocals stems vocal-remover mdx-net party microphone cdg mp3g midi kar nvidia gpu cuda";s:7:"License";s:55:"Proprietary — one-time purchase, five-song free trial";s:10:"Screenshot";a:3:{i:0;s:89:"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/CasaVargas/beltr-unraid/main/screenshots/tv-lyrics.webp";i:1;s:88:"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/CasaVargas/beltr-unraid/main/screenshots/dashboard.png";i:2;s:92:"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/CasaVargas/beltr-unraid/main/screenshots/phone-remote.webp";}s:4:"Date";s:10:"2026-09-01";s:11:"ExtraParams";s:16:"--runtime=nvidia";s:8:"Requires";s:215:"Unraid Nvidia-Driver plugin, and an NVIDIA GPU with driver 525 or newer (the image ships a CUDA 12.8 build of ONNX Runtime). Internet access on first start to activate a license key, or to begin the five-song trial.";s:6:"Config";a:16:{i:0;a:2:{s:11:"@attributes";a:9:{s:4:"Name";s:10:"WebUI Port";s:6:"Target";s:4:"8477";s:7:"Default";s:4:"8477";s:4:"Mode";s:3:"tcp";s:11:"Description";s:116:"Port for the web interface, the TV screen and the phone remotes. Change the host side only if 8477 is already taken.";s:4:"Type";s:4:"Port";s:7:"Display";s:6:"always";s:8:"Required";s:4:"true";s:4:"Mask";s:5:"false";}s:5:"value";s:4:"8477";}i:1;a:2:{s:11:"@attributes";a:9:{s:4:"Name";s:10:"HTTPS Port";s:6:"Target";s:4:"8478";s:7:"Default";s:4:"8478";s:4:"Mode";s:3:"tcp";s:11:"Description";s:259:"Self-signed HTTPS for microphones (browsers only allow the mic on a secure page). Open https://your-server:8478/tv on the device with the mic and accept the warning once. Keep host and container sides equal: Beltr builds the address it shows from this number.";s:4:"Type";s:4:"Port";s:7:"Display";s:6:"always";s:8:"Required";s:5:"false";s:4:"Mask";s:5:"false";}s:5:"value";s:4:"8478";}i:2;a:2:{s:11:"@attributes";a:9:{s:4:"Name";s:5:"HTTPS";s:6:"Target";s:9:"BELTR_TLS";s:7:"Default";s:2:"on";s:4:"Mode";s:0:"";s:11:"Description";s:194:"on = also serve https on the HTTPS Port with a self-signed certificate Beltr generates and keeps in /config/tls. off = plain http only (microphones then need a reverse proxy with a certificate).";s:4:"Type";s:8:"Variable";s:7:"Display";s:8:"advanced";s:8:"Required";s:5:"false";s:4:"Mask";s:5:"false";}s:5:"value";s:2:"on";}i:3;a:2:{s:11:"@attributes";a:9:{s:4:"Name";s:6:"Config";s:6:"Target";s:7:"/config";s:7:"Default";s:23:"/mnt/user/appdata/beltr";s:4:"Mode";s:2:"rw";s:11:"Description";s:109:"App state: database, settings, logs, lyrics. Small and written often — keep it on appdata (SSD/cache pool).";s:4:"Type";s:4:"Path";s:7:"Display";s:6:"always";s:8:"Required";s:4:"true";s:4:"Mask";s:5:"false";}s:5:"value";s:23:"/mnt/user/appdata/beltr";}i:4;a:2:{s:11:"@attributes";a:9:{s:4:"Name";s:7:"Library";s:6:"Target";s:8:"/library";s:7:"Default";s:15:"/mnt/user/beltr";s:4:"Mode";s:2:"rw";s:11:"Description";s:134:"Processed karaoke library: separated stems and imported audio. Roughly 60-120 MB per song, so point this at the array, NOT at appdata.";s:4:"Type";s:4:"Path";s:7:"Display";s:6:"always";s:8:"Required";s:4:"true";s:4:"Mask";s:5:"false";}s:5:"value";s:15:"/mnt/user/beltr";}i:5;a:2:{s:11:"@attributes";a:9:{s:4:"Name";s:17:"Music (read-only)";s:6:"Target";s:6:"/media";s:7:"Default";s:15:"/mnt/user/Music";s:4:"Mode";s:2:"ro";s:11:"Description";s:154:"Your existing music. Mounted read-only — Beltr copies what it imports and never writes here. Add it as a music folder in Settings after the first start.";s:4:"Type";s:4:"Path";s:7:"Display";s:6:"always";s:8:"Required";s:4:"true";s:4:"Mask";s:5:"false";}s:5:"value";s:15:"/mnt/user/Music";}i:6;a:2:{s:11:"@attributes";a:9:{s:4:"Name";s:11:"Model cache";s:6:"Target";s:6:"/cache";s:7:"Default";s:29:"/mnt/user/appdata/beltr-cache";s:4:"Mode";s:2:"rw";s:11:"Description";s:146:"Downloaded AI model weights, about 2 GB. Keep this mapped or every container update re-downloads them. Faster storage makes model loading quicker.";s:4:"Type";s:4:"Path";s:7:"Display";s:6:"always";s:8:"Required";s:4:"true";s:4:"Mask";s:5:"false";}s:5:"value";s:29:"/mnt/user/appdata/beltr-cache";}i:7;a:2:{s:11:"@attributes";a:9:{s:4:"Name";s:22:"NVIDIA_VISIBLE_DEVICES";s:6:"Target";s:22:"NVIDIA_VISIBLE_DEVICES";s:7:"Default";s:3:"all";s:4:"Mode";s:0:"";s:11:"Description";s:228:"Which GPU to use. Paste the UUID shown on the Nvidia-Driver plugin page in Settings (it looks like GPU-1a2b3c4d-...). 'all' works on a single-GPU server. Getting this wrong is not an error — Beltr just quietly runs on the CPU.";s:4:"Type";s:8:"Variable";s:7:"Display";s:6:"always";s:8:"Required";s:4:"true";s:4:"Mask";s:5:"false";}s:5:"value";s:3:"all";}i:8;a:2:{s:11:"@attributes";a:9:{s:4:"Name";s:26:"NVIDIA_DRIVER_CAPABILITIES";s:6:"Target";s:26:"NVIDIA_DRIVER_CAPABILITIES";s:7:"Default";s:15:"compute,utility";s:4:"Mode";s:0:"";s:11:"Description";s:170:"Driver features exposed to the container. Beltr needs compute (CUDA) and utility (nvidia-smi). It does not need video or graphics — this is not a transcoding container.";s:4:"Type";s:8:"Variable";s:7:"Display";s:8:"advanced";s:8:"Required";s:4:"true";s:4:"Mask";s:5:"false";}s:5:"value";s:15:"compute,utility";}i:9;a:2:{s:11:"@attributes";a:9:{s:4:"Name";s:4:"PUID";s:6:"Target";s:4:"PUID";s:7:"Default";s:2:"99";s:4:"Mode";s:0:"";s:11:"Description";s:76:"User ID that owns the files Beltr writes. 99 (nobody) is the Unraid default.";s:4:"Type";s:8:"Variable";s:7:"Display";s:8:"advanced";s:8:"Required";s:4:"true";s:4:"Mask";s:5:"false";}s:5:"value";s:2:"99";}i:10;a:2:{s:11:"@attributes";a:9:{s:4:"Name";s:4:"PGID";s:6:"Target";s:4:"PGID";s:7:"Default";s:3:"100";s:4:"Mode";s:0:"";s:11:"Description";s:77:"Group ID that owns the files Beltr writes. 100 (users) is the Unraid default.";s:4:"Type";s:8:"Variable";s:7:"Display";s:8:"advanced";s:8:"Required";s:4:"true";s:4:"Mask";s:5:"false";}s:5:"value";s:3:"100";}i:11;a:2:{s:11:"@attributes";a:9:{s:4:"Name";s:2:"TZ";s:6:"Target";s:2:"TZ";s:7:"Default";s:7:"Etc/UTC";s:4:"Mode";s:0:"";s:11:"Description";s:56:"Timezone, e.g. America/New_York. Affects log timestamps.";s:4:"Type";s:8:"Variable";s:7:"Display";s:6:"always";s:8:"Required";s:5:"false";s:4:"Mask";s:5:"false";}s:5:"value";s:7:"Etc/UTC";}i:12;a:2:{s:11:"@attributes";a:9:{s:4:"Name";s:11:"License key";s:6:"Target";s:17:"BELTR_LICENSE_KEY";s:7:"Default";s:0:"";s:4:"Mode";s:0:"";s:11:"Description";s:318:"Your key from beltr.app. Activates once against this install and then works offline — updating or recreating the container does not re-activate, as long as you keep the Config path. Leave blank to try Beltr free: five songs, then it asks you to buy. You can also put the key in a file at /config/license.key instead.";s:4:"Type";s:8:"Variable";s:7:"Display";s:6:"always";s:8:"Required";s:5:"false";s:4:"Mask";s:4:"true";}s:5:"value";s:0:"";}i:13;a:2:{s:11:"@attributes";a:9:{s:4:"Name";s:8:"Host PIN";s:6:"Target";s:16:"KARAOKE_HOST_PIN";s:7:"Default";s:0:"";s:4:"Mode";s:0:"";s:11:"Description";s:180:"Six digits that unlock host controls on a phone (skip, reorder, delete). Leave blank and Beltr picks a random one on every start, which changes if the container restarts mid-party.";s:4:"Type";s:8:"Variable";s:7:"Display";s:6:"always";s:8:"Required";s:5:"false";s:4:"Mask";s:4:"true";}s:5:"value";s:0:"";}i:14;a:2:{s:11:"@attributes";a:9:{s:4:"Name";s:13:"Host password";s:6:"Target";s:13:"AUTH_PASSWORD";s:7:"Default";s:0:"";s:4:"Mode";s:0:"";s:11:"Description";s:205:"Optional password on the TV and dashboard screens and the settings endpoints. Phones joining a room are NOT affected. This keeps the household out of your settings; it is not internet-grade authentication.";s:4:"Type";s:8:"Variable";s:7:"Display";s:6:"always";s:8:"Required";s:5:"false";s:4:"Mask";s:4:"true";}s:5:"value";s:0:"";}i:15;a:2:{s:11:"@attributes";a:9:{s:4:"Name";s:15:"Fix permissions";s:6:"Target";s:15:"BELTR_FIX_PERMS";s:7:"Default";s:9:"first-run";s:4:"Mode";s:0:"";s:11:"Description";s:156:"first-run: fix ownership once, then only the top-level folders. always: fix everything on every start (slow on a big library). never: leave ownership alone.";s:4:"Type";s:8:"Variable";s:7:"Display";s:8:"advanced";s:8:"Required";s:5:"false";s:4:"Mask";s:5:"false";}s:5:"value";s:9:"first-run";}}s:12:"TemplatePath";s:44:"/tmp/GitHub/AppFeed/templates/beltr-cuda.xml";s:4:"Repo";s:18:"Beltr's Repository";s:12:"CategoryList";a:2:{i:0;s:14:"MediaApp-Music";i:1;s:17:"MediaServer-Music";}s:16:"ChangeLogPresent";s:1:"1";s:9:"FirstSeen";i:1786834286;s:8:"Category";s:32:"MediaApp:Music MediaServer:Music";s:2:"ID";i:223;s:11:"Displayable";b:1;s:6:"Author";s:10:"casavargas";s:13:"DockerHubName";s:12:"beltr-nvidia";s:8:"RepoName";s:18:"Beltr's Repository";s:10:"SortAuthor";s:10:"casavargas";s:8:"SortName";s:12:"Beltr NVIDIA";s:6:"random";i:688167716;s:9:"Blacklist";b:0;s:6:"MinVer";s:3:"6.0";s:4:"Path";s:118:"/tmp/community.applications/tempFiles/templates-community-apps/BeltrsRepository/casavargas-BeltrNVIDIA-latest-cuda.xml";s:10:"Deprecated";b:0;s:10:"Compatible";b:1;s:16:"ModeratorComment";N;}i:224;a:40:{s:4:"Name";s:11:"Beltr-Intel";s:10:"Repository";s:40:"ghcr.io/casavargas/beltr:latest-openvino";s:8:"Registry";s:67:"https://github.com/orgs/CasaVargas/packages/container/package/beltr";s:7:"Network";s:6:"bridge";s:5:"Shell";s:4:"bash";s:10:"Privileged";s:5:"false";s:7:"Support";s:51:"https://github.com/CasaVargas/beltr-releases/issues";s:7:"Project";s:17:"https://beltr.app";s:8:"Overview";s:3501:"Karaoke night from the music already on your server. Beltr strips the vocals with local AI, puts word-synced lyrics on the TV, and makes every phone a remote, no app needed. Intel build: 6th-gen Core graphics onward (N100 too) or Arc. No Intel GPU? Pick Beltr.

Beltr turns any song in your music library into a karaoke track. It separates the vocals out with a local AI model, finds synced lyrics online (or drafts them locally when no provider has the song), force-aligns them to the vocal word by word, and displays them on a TV while everyone's phone acts as a remote — scan the QR code on screen, no app to install.

Everything runs on your server. Nothing about your library is uploaded.

THIS IS THE INTEL GPU BUILD. It runs the vocal separation on an Intel integrated GPU (the one inside most Intel desktop and NAS processors from 6th gen Core onward, including the N100 family) or an Intel Arc A-series card. It needs the Unraid "Intel GPU TOP" plugin installed, which loads the graphics driver, and the GPU passed through: "Extra Parameters" must contain --device=/dev/dri, which this template already sets. Nothing else to install — the Intel compute runtime ships inside the image.

If you have an NVIDIA card, install "Beltr-NVIDIA" instead; with no GPU at all, plain "Beltr". This image will still run without a usable GPU — it falls back to the CPU — so a broken passthrough shows up as "slow", not "broken". Check the GPU panel in Settings after install to confirm the GPU was actually found. Intel Arc B-series and Panther Lake are newer than the driver this image carries and are not supported yet.

FIRST RUN: Beltr downloads about 2 GB of model weights into /cache the first time it needs them. That happens once and survives container updates as long as /cache stays mapped. Watch the container log if a first song seems to sit still — the download is what it's doing.

SPEED: depends heavily on the GPU. An Iris Xe or Arc-class GPU separates a 3-4 minute song in about a minute; an older UHD 630-class iGPU is not much faster than a modern CPU. Most songs then get their lyrics instantly from an online lyrics database; the ones no provider knows fall back to local transcription, which runs on the CPU.

LICENSE: Beltr is a one-time purchase (no subscription). Run it free for five songs, then enter your key from beltr.app in the License key field below — or drop it in a file at /config/license.key. It activates once and then works offline. Container updates and restarts do not re-activate, as long as you keep the Config path mapped; a key covers two installs.

AFTER INSTALL: open the WebUI, go to Settings, and add /media as a music folder. Then open http://your-server:8477/tv on whatever screen you're singing at, and scan the QR with a phone.

MICROPHONES NEED HTTPS: browsers only allow microphone access on a secure page. Beltr serves one itself on port 8478 with a self-signed certificate: open https://your-server:8478/tv on the laptop or phone that has the microphone and accept the browser's warning once. Everything else — queueing, playback, lyrics, stem mixing, the QR the TV shows — works over plain http on 8477. A reverse proxy with a real certificate is only needed if you want no warning at all.

NOTE: Beltr assumes everyone who can reach it is trusted. Set AUTH_PASSWORD to put a password on the TV and dashboard screens, but do not expose this container to the internet without a reverse proxy doing real authentication in front of it.";s:5:"WebUI";s:33:"http://[IP]:[PORT:8477]/dashboard";s:11:"TemplateURL";s:91:"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/CasaVargas/beltr-unraid/main/templates/beltr-openvino.xml";s:4:"Icon";s:77:"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/CasaVargas/beltr-unraid/main/icon-intel.png";s:6:"ReadMe";s:72:"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/CasaVargas/beltr-unraid/main/README.md";s:16:"ExtraSearchTerms";s:137:"karaoke sing singalong lyrics vocals stems vocal-remover mdx-net party microphone cdg mp3g midi kar intel igpu arc openvino quicksync gpu";s:7:"License";s:55:"Proprietary — one-time purchase, five-song free trial";s:10:"Screenshot";a:3:{i:0;s:89:"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/CasaVargas/beltr-unraid/main/screenshots/tv-lyrics.webp";i:1;s:88:"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/CasaVargas/beltr-unraid/main/screenshots/dashboard.png";i:2;s:92:"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/CasaVargas/beltr-unraid/main/screenshots/phone-remote.webp";}s:4:"Date";s:10:"2026-09-01";s:11:"ExtraParams";s:17:"--device=/dev/dri";s:8:"Requires";s:222:"Unraid Intel GPU TOP plugin, and an Intel GPU from 6th gen Core (Skylake) through Arrow Lake / Lunar Lake, or an Arc A-series card. Internet access on first start to activate a license key, or to begin the five-song trial.";s:6:"Config";a:18:{i:0;a:2:{s:11:"@attributes";a:9:{s:4:"Name";s:10:"WebUI Port";s:6:"Target";s:4:"8477";s:7:"Default";s:4:"8477";s:4:"Mode";s:3:"tcp";s:11:"Description";s:116:"Port for the web interface, the TV screen and the phone remotes. Change the host side only if 8477 is already taken.";s:4:"Type";s:4:"Port";s:7:"Display";s:6:"always";s:8:"Required";s:4:"true";s:4:"Mask";s:5:"false";}s:5:"value";s:4:"8477";}i:1;a:2:{s:11:"@attributes";a:9:{s:4:"Name";s:10:"HTTPS Port";s:6:"Target";s:4:"8478";