ounted read-only — Beltr copies what it imports and never writes here. Add it as a music folder in Settings after the first start.";s:4:"Type";s:4:"Path";s:7:"Display";s:6:"always";s:8:"Required";s:4:"true";s:4:"Mask";s:5:"false";}s:5:"value";s:15:"/mnt/user/Music";}i:6;a:2:{s:11:"@attributes";a:9:{s:4:"Name";s:11:"Model cache";s:6:"Target";s:6:"/cache";s:7:"Default";s:29:"/mnt/user/appdata/beltr-cache";s:4:"Mode";s:2:"rw";s:11:"Description";s:146:"Downloaded AI model weights, about 2 GB. Keep this mapped or every container update re-downloads them. Faster storage makes model loading quicker.";s:4:"Type";s:4:"Path";s:7:"Display";s:6:"always";s:8:"Required";s:4:"true";s:4:"Mask";s:5:"false";}s:5:"value";s:29:"/mnt/user/appdata/beltr-cache";}i:7;a:2:{s:11:"@attributes";a:9:{s:4:"Name";s:10:"GPU device";s:6:"Target";s:25:"BELTR_MDX_OPENVINO_DEVICE";s:7:"Default";s:3:"GPU";s:4:"Mode";s:0:"";s:11:"Description";s:266:"Which OpenVINO device runs the separation. GPU is the first Intel GPU found and is right for nearly everyone. GPU.1 picks a second Intel GPU (say, an Arc card in a box that also has an iGPU). Getting this wrong is not an error — Beltr just quietly runs on the CPU.";s:4:"Type";s:8:"Variable";s:7:"Display";s:8:"advanced";s:8:"Required";s:5:"false";s:4:"Mask";s:5:"false";}s:5:"value";s:3:"GPU";}i:8;a:2:{s:11:"@attributes";a:9:{s:4:"Name";s:13:"GPU precision";s:6:"Target";s:28:"BELTR_MDX_OPENVINO_PRECISION";s:7:"Default";s:4:"FP32";s:4:"Mode";s:0:"";s:11:"Description";s:234:"FP32 is the default and matches the CPU output. FP16 is usually faster on Intel GPUs but its separation quality has not been measured here; try it if separation feels slow and listen to the result. FP16 also halves what the GPU holds.";s:4:"Type";s:8:"Variable";s:7:"Display";s:8:"advanced";s:8:"Required";s:5:"false";s:4:"Mask";s:5:"false";}s:5:"value";s:4:"FP32";}i:9;a:2:{s:11:"@attributes";a:9:{s:4:"Name";s:38:"Hold the model between songs (seconds)";s:6:"Target";s:28:"BELTR_WARM_SEPARATION_IDLE_S";s:7:"Default";s:0:"";s:4:"Mode";s:0:"";s:11:"Description";s:278:"How long the separation worker keeps its model loaded after finishing a song. Leave blank for Beltr's default (10 seconds in a container, so the memory is released between songs during a big import). Raise it to trade memory for a little speed; lower it if memory is very tight.";s:4:"Type";s:8:"Variable";s:7:"Display";s:8:"advanced";s:8:"Required";s:5:"false";s:4:"Mask";s:5:"false";}s:5:"value";s:0:"";}i:10;a:2:{s:11:"@attributes";a:9:{s:4:"Name";s:27:"OpenVINO runtime properties";s:6:"Target";s:30:"BELTR_MDX_OPENVINO_LOAD_CONFIG";s:7:"Default";s:0:"";s:4:"Mode";s:0:"";s:11:"Description";s:338:"Advanced. Raw OpenVINO properties as JSON, keyed by device — for example {&quot;GPU&quot;: {&quot;PERFORMANCE_HINT&quot;: &quot;LATENCY&quot;, &quot;NUM_STREAMS&quot;: &quot;1&quot;}}, which is what Beltr sends by default. Set to off to send none. Only worth touching if you have read OpenVINO's property list and measured your own box.";s:4:"Type";s:8:"Variable";s:7:"Display";s:8:"advanced";s:8:"Required";s:5:"false";s:4:"Mask";s:5:"false";}s:5:"value";s:0:"";}i:11;a:2:{s:11:"@attributes";a:9:{s:4:"Name";s:4:"PUID";s:6:"Target";s:4:"PUID";s:7:"Default";s:2:"99";s:4:"Mode";s:0:"";s:11:"Description";s:76:"User ID that owns the files Beltr writes. 99 (nobody) is the Unraid default.";s:4:"Type";s:8:"Variable";s:7:"Display";s:8:"advanced";s:8:"Required";s:4:"true";s:4:"Mask";s:5:"false";}s:5:"value";s:2:"99";}i:12;a:2:{s:11:"@attributes";a:9:{s:4:"Name";s:4:"PGID";s:6:"Target";s:4:"PGID";s:7:"Default";s:3:"100";s:4:"Mode";s:0:"";s:11:"Description";s:77:"Group ID that owns the files Beltr writes. 100 (users) is the Unraid default.";s:4:"Type";s:8:"Variable";s:7:"Display";s:8:"advanced";s:8:"Required";s:4:"true";s:4:"Mask";s:5:"false";}s:5:"value";s:3:"100";}i:13;a:2:{s:11:"@attributes";a:9:{s:4:"Name";s:2:"TZ";s:6:"Target";s:2:"TZ";s:7:"Default";s:7:"Etc/UTC";s:4:"Mode";s:0:"";s:11:"Description";s:56:"Timezone