 fix everything on every start (slow on a big library). never: leave ownership alone.";s:4:"Type";s:8:"Variable";s:7:"Display";s:8:"advanced";s:8:"Required";s:5:"false";s:4:"Mask";s:5:"false";}s:5:"value";s:9:"first-run";}}s:12:"TemplatePath";s:48:"/tmp/GitHub/AppFeed/templates/beltr-openvino.xml";s:4:"Repo";s:18:"Beltr's Repository";s:12:"CategoryList";a:2:{i:0;s:14:"MediaApp-Music";i:1;s:17:"MediaServer-Music";}s:16:"ChangeLogPresent";s:1:"1";s:9:"FirstSeen";i:1786834286;s:8:"Category";s:32:"MediaApp:Music MediaServer:Music";s:2:"ID";i:224;s:11:"Displayable";b:1;s:6:"Author";s:10:"casavargas";s:13:"DockerHubName";s:11:"beltr-intel";s:8:"RepoName";s:18:"Beltr's Repository";s:10:"SortAuthor";s:10:"casavargas";s:8:"SortName";s:11:"Beltr Intel";s:6:"random";i:1812392551;s:9:"Blacklist";b:0;s:6:"MinVer";s:3:"6.0";s:4:"Path";s:121:"/tmp/community.applications/tempFiles/templates-community-apps/BeltrsRepository/casavargas-BeltrIntel-latest-openvino.xml";s:10:"Deprecated";b:0;s:10:"Compatible";b:1;s:16:"ModeratorComment";N;}i:225;a:39:{s:4:"Name";s:5:"Beltr";s:10:"Repository";s:31:"ghcr.io/casavargas/beltr:latest";s:8:"Registry";s:67:"https://github.com/orgs/CasaVargas/packages/container/package/beltr";s:7:"Network";s:6:"bridge";s:5:"Shell";s:4:"bash";s:10:"Privileged";s:5:"false";s:7:"Support";s:51:"https://github.com/CasaVargas/beltr-releases/issues";s:7:"Project";s:17:"https://beltr.app";s:8:"Overview";s:2802:"Karaoke night from the music already on your server. Beltr strips the vocals with local AI, puts word-synced lyrics on the TV, and makes every phone a remote, no app needed. CPU build: runs on any server. Got a GPU? Pick Beltr-NVIDIA or Beltr-Intel.

Beltr turns any song in your music library into a karaoke track. It separates the vocals out with a local AI model, finds synced lyrics online (or drafts them locally when no provider has the song), force-aligns them to the vocal word by word, and displays them on a TV while everyone's phone acts as a remote — scan the QR code on screen, no app to install.

Everything runs on your server. Nothing about your library is uploaded.

FIRST RUN: Beltr downloads about 2 GB of model weights into /cache the first time it needs them. That happens once and survives container updates as long as /cache stays mapped. Watch the container log if a first song seems to sit still — the download is what it's doing.

SPEED: this is the CPU image. On a modern multi-core server, separating a 3-4 minute song takes a few minutes; most songs then get their lyrics instantly from an online lyrics database. The slow case is a song no lyrics provider knows, which falls back to local transcription and can take a couple of minutes. If your server has an NVIDIA GPU, install "Beltr-NVIDIA" instead; it is dramatically faster. An Intel processor with integrated graphics (6th gen Core onward, N100 included) or an Arc A-series card can use "Beltr-Intel". AMD GPUs are not supported in the container.

LICENSE: Beltr is a one-time purchase (no subscription). Run it free for five songs, then enter your key from beltr.app in the License key field below — or drop it in a file at /config/license.key. It activates once and then works offline. Container updates and restarts do not re-activate, as long as you keep the Config path mapped; a key covers two installs.

AFTER INSTALL: open the WebUI, go to Settings, and add /media as a music folder. Then open http://your-server:8477/tv on whatever screen you're singing at, and scan the QR with a phone.

MICROPHONES NEED HTTPS: browsers only allow microphone access on a secure page. Beltr serves one itself on port 8478 with a self-signed certificate: open https://your-server:8478/tv on the laptop or phone that has the microphone and accept the browser's warning once. Everything else — queueing, playback, lyrics, stem mixing, the QR the TV shows — works over plain http on 8477. A reverse proxy with a real certificate is only needed if you want no warning at all.

NOTE: Beltr assumes everyone who can reach it is trusted. Set AUTH_PASSWORD to put a password on the TV and dashboard screens, but do not expose this container to the internet without a reverse proxy doing real authentication in front of it.";s:5:"WebUI";s:33:"http://[IP]:[PORT:8477]/dashboard";s:11:"TemplateURL";s:82:"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/CasaVargas/beltr-unraid/main/templates/beltr.xml";s:4:"Icon";s:71:"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/CasaVargas/beltr-unraid/main/icon.png";s:6:"ReadMe";s:72:"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/CasaVargas/beltr-unraid/main/README.md";s:16:"ExtraSearchTerms";s:99:"karaoke sing singalong lyrics vocals stems vocal-remover mdx-net party microphone cdg mp3g midi kar";s:7:"License";s:55:"Proprietary — one-time purchase, five-song free trial";s:10:"Screenshot";a:3:{i:0;s:89:"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/CasaVargas/beltr-unraid/main/screenshots/tv-lyrics.webp";i:1;s:88:"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/CasaVargas/beltr-unraid/main/screenshots/dashboard.png";i:2;s:92:"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/CasaVargas/beltr-unraid/main/screenshots/phone-remote.webp";}s:4:"Date";s:10:"2026-09-01";s:8:"Requires";s:131:"Internet access on first start to activate a license key (or to begin the five-song trial). After that Beltr keeps working offline.";s:6:"Config";a:14:{i:0;a:2:{s:11:"@attributes";a:9:{s:4:"Name";s:10:"WebUI Port";s:6:"Target";s:4:"8477";s:7:"Default";s:4:"8477";s:4:"Mode";s:3:"tcp";s:11:"Description";s:116:"Port for the web interface, the TV screen and the phone remotes. Change the host side only if 8477 is already taken.";s:4:"Type";s:4:"Port";s:7:"Display";s:6:"always";s:8:"Required";s:4:"true";s:4:"Mask";s:5:"false";}s:5:"value";s:4:"8477";}i:1;a:2:{s:11:"@attributes";a:9:{s:4:"Name";s:10:"HTTPS Port";s:6:"Target";s:4:"8478";s:7:"Default";s:4:"8478";s:4:"Mode";s:3:"tcp";s:11:"Description";s:259:"Self-signed HTTPS for microphones (browsers only allow the mic on a secure page). Open https://your-server:8478/tv on