eratorComment";N;}i:241;a:34:{s:4:"Name";s:9:"LAN-Games";s:10:"Repository";s:35:"ghcr.io/codyburker/lan-games:latest";s:8:"Registry";s:36:"https://ghcr.io/codyburker/lan-games";s:7:"Network";s:6:"bridge";s:5:"Shell";s:2:"sh";s:10:"Privileged";s:5:"false";s:7:"Support";s:50:"https://github.com/CodyBurker/unraid-rumpus/issues";s:7:"Project";s:41:"https://github.com/kbennett2000/lan-games";s:8:"Overview";s:741:"Self-hosted LAN board game platform: eight turn-based classics — Monopoly, Risk, Battleship, Yahtzee, Life, Checkers, Connect Four, and Tic-Tac-Toe — playable in any browser on your network. Real-time multiplayer via Socket.IO, with lobbies, hidden-information support (Battleship/Risk), and spectator mode.

Unlike most party game servers it has real user accounts: JWT-based auth with bcrypt-hashed passwords, and game state persists in a SQLite database (mount the data path so it survives updates). Designed for trusted local networks — don't expose it to the internet.

