Built for long serialized fiction: no subscription wall, no account required, runs on your own machine. Bring your own TTS key (Azure, OpenAI-compatible, MiniMax) or point it at a local engine such as Kokoro and it costs nothing per word. Open source (MIT).

• EPUB, pasted story links, and Archive of Our Own (with optional login cookie)
• Per-chapter audio you can replay, plus continuous "whole book" mode
• Local filesystem storage by default; SQLite metadata by default, MySQL/MariaDB optional
• Character-capacity accounting hooks for hosted use; self-host is free

