ot;. Leave empty if you use a password file or store the password in the configuration instead.";s:4:"Type";s:8:"Variable";s:7:"Display";s:6:"always";s:8:"Required";s:5:"false";s:4:"Mask";s:4:"true";}s:5:"value";s:0:"";}i:9;a:2:{s:11:"@attributes";a:8:{s:4:"Name";s:9:"Time zone";s:6:"Target";s:2:"TZ";s:7:"Default";s:3:"UTC";s:11:"Description";s:145:"Time zone used for schedules, next-run times and log timestamps, e.g. Europe/Berlin. Set this - it decides what '02:00' means for your schedules.";s:4:"Type";s:8:"Variable";s:7:"Display";s:6:"always";s:8:"Required";s:4:"true";s:4:"Mask";s:5:"false";}s:5:"value";s:0:"";}i:10;a:2:{s:11:"@attributes";a:8:{s:4:"Name";s:4:"Mode";s:6:"Target";s:7:"DK_MODE";s:7:"Default";s:3:"gui";s:11:"Description";s:104:"gui = web UI plus scheduler (recommended). cli = headless scheduler, no web UI and no persisted history.";s:4:"Type";s:8:"Variable";s:7:"Display";s:8:"advanced";s:8:"Required";s:5:"false";s:4:"Mask";s:5:"false";}s:5:"value";s:0:"";}i:11;a:2:{s:11:"@attributes";a:8:{s:4:"Name";s:35:"Restic password (second repository)";s:6:"Target";s:28:"DK_RESTIC_PASSWORD_SECONDARY";s:7:"Default";s:0:"";s:11:"Description";s:224:"Password for a second repository, for example an off-site copy. Reference it from config.toml as password_env = &quot;DK_RESTIC_PASSWORD_SECONDARY&quot;. The variable name is only a convention - any name you reference works.";s:4:"Type";s:8:"Variable";s:7:"Display";s:8:"advanced";s:8:"Required";s:5:"false";s:4:"Mask";s:4:"true";}s:5:"value";s:0:"";}i:12;a:2:{s:11:"@attributes";a:8:{s:4:"Name";s:9:"SMTP user";s:6:"Target";s:9:"SMTP_USER";s:7:"Default";s:0:"";s:11:"Description";s:226:"User name for mail notifications. Reference it from the [global.notifications.mail] section as username_env = &quot;SMTP_USER&quot;. Leave empty if your mail server needs no authentication or you do not use mail notifications.";s:4:"Type";s:8:"Variable";s:7:"Display";s:8:"advanced";s:8:"Required";s:5:"false";s:4:"Mask";s:5:"false";}s:5:"va