he host - leave empty unless you need it.";s:4:"Type";s:4:"Path";s:7:"Display";s:8:"advanced";s:8:"Required";s:5:"false";s:4:"Mask";s:5:"false";}s:5:"value";s:0:"";}i:18;a:2:{s:11:"@attributes";a:8:{s:4:"Name";s:18:"Allow inline hooks";s:6:"Target";s:21:"DK_ALLOW_INLINE_HOOKS";s:7:"Default";s:5:"false";s:11:"Description";s:81:"Set to true to allow inline shell commands as hooks instead of script files only.";s:4:"Type";s:8:"Variable";s:7:"Display";s:8:"advanced";s:8:"Required";s:5:"false";s:4:"Mask";s:5:"false";}s:5:"value";s:0:"";}i:19;a:2:{s:11:"@attributes";a:8:{s:4:"Name";s:25:"App data retention (days)";s:6:"Target";s:25:"DK_APPDATA_RETENTION_DAYS";s:7:"Default";s:0:"";s:11:"Description";s:153:"Maximum age of persisted run history records. Empty means unlimited - the database grows for as long as the installation runs. 360 is a reasonable value.";s:4:"Type";s:8:"Variable";s:7:"Display";s:8:"advanced";s:8:"Required";s:5:"false";s:4:"Mask";s:5:"false";}s:5:"value";s:0:"";}i:20;a:2:{s:11:"@attributes";a:8:{s:4:"Name";s:26:"App data retention (count)";s:6:"Target";s:26:"DK_APPDATA_RETENTION_COUNT";s:7:"Default";s:0:"";s:11:"Description";s:97:"Maximum number of persisted records per group. Empty means unlimited. 1000 is a reasonable value.";s:4:"Type";s:8:"Variable";s:7:"Display";s:8:"advanced";s:8:"Required";s:5:"false";s:4:"Mask";s:5:"false";}s:5:"value";s:0:"";}i:21;a:2:{s:11:"@attributes";a:8:{s:4:"Name";s:4:"PUID";s:6:"Target";s:4:"PUID";s:7:"Default";s:0:"";s:11:"Description";s:257:"Optional non-root operation. Set PUID and PGID together or not at all - the container refuses to start with only one of them. Dockkeep does NOT recursively chown mounted directories; grant this user access on the host first. Leave both empty to run as root.";s:4:"Type";s:8:"Variable";s:7:"Display";s:8:"advanced";s:8:"Required";s:5:"false";s:4:"Mask";s:5:"false";}s:5:"value";s:0:"";}i:22;a:2:{s:11:"@attributes";a:8:{s:4:"Name";s:4:"PGID";s:6:"Target";s:4:"PGID";s:7:"Default";s:0:"";