l Workbench listen port. Normally keep this at 8787.";s:4:"Type";s:8:"Variable";s:7:"Display";s:8:"advanced";s:8:"Required";s:4:"true";s:4:"Mask";s:5:"false";}s:5:"value";s:4:"8787";}i:4;a:2:{s:11:"@attributes";a:8:{s:4:"Name";s:22:"Disable Workbench Auth";s:6:"Target";s:15:"FEYNMAN_NO_AUTH";s:7:"Default";s:4:"true";s:11:"Description";s:136:"true = convenient trusted-LAN access. false = Feynman generates a token URL on each container start; retrieve it from the container log.";s:4:"Type";s:8:"Variable";s:7:"Display";s:6:"always";s:8:"Required";s:4:"true";s:4:"Mask";s:5:"false";}s:5:"value";s:4:"true";}i:5;a:2:{s:11:"@attributes";a:8:{s:4:"Name";s:8:"Timezone";s:6:"Target";s:2:"TZ";s:7:"Default";s:7:"Etc/UTC";s:11:"Description";s:49:"Container timezone, for example Europe/Ljubljana.";s:4:"Type";s:8:"Variable";s:7:"Display";s:8:"advanced";s:8:"Required";s:5:"false";s:4:"Mask";s:5:"false";}s:5:"value";s:7:"Etc/UTC";}}s:12:"TemplatePath";s:41:"/tmp/GitHub/AppFeed/templates/feynman.xml";s:4:"Repo";s:20:"Grmi508's Repository";s:12:"CategoryList";a:1:{i:0;s:15:"Tools-Utilities";}s:16:"ChangeLogPresent";s:1:"1";s:9:"FirstSeen";i:1789615119;s:8:"Category";s:15:"Tools:Utilities";s:2:"ID";i:339;s:11:"Displayable";b:1;s:6:"Author";s:9:"denisb508";s:13:"DockerHubName";s:7:"feynman";s:8:"RepoName";s:20:"Grmi508's Repository";s:10:"SortAuthor";s:9:"denisb508";s:8:"SortName";s:7:"Feynman";s:6:"random";i:132209869;s:9:"Blacklist";b:0;s:4:"Path";s:110:"/tmp/community.applications/tempFiles/templates-community-apps/Grmi508sRepository/denisb508-Feynman-latest.xml";s:10:"Deprecated";b:0;s:10:"Compatible";b:1;s:16:"ModeratorComment";N;}i:340;a:39:{s:4:"Name";s:7:"nexbeat";s:10:"Repository";s:25:"ghcr.io/derkezorm/nexbeat";s:8:"Registry";s:59:"https://github.com/DerKezorm/nexbeat/pkgs/container/nexbeat";s:7:"Network";s:6:"bridge";s:5:"Shell";s:2:"sh";s:10:"Privileged";s:5:"false";s:7:"Support";s:43:"https://github.com/DerKezorm/nexbeat/issues";s:6:"GitHub";s:36:"https://github.com/DerKezorm/nexbeat";s:6:"ReadMe";s:43:"https://github.com/DerKezorm/nexbeat#readme";s:7:"Project";s:36:"https://github.com/DerKezorm/nexbeat";s:8:"Overview";s:687:"nexbeat finds music and requests it from Lidarr. A discover page recommends artists from what your library and each user already have, twenty main genres can be browsed, and every artist page shows the discography, the most played albums, similar artists and thirty second previews.A request adds the album to Lidarr and monitors just that one; a whole artist adds the studio albums and future releases. Everyone gets an account with a quota counted per request, optional approval, and invitations by email or as a link to pass on. The interface is available in English and German.nexbeat downloads nothing itself and never changes Lidarr settings. It needs a Lidarr you already run.";s:5:"WebUI";s:24:"http://[IP]:[PORT:8000]/";s:11:"TemplateURL";s:87:"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/DerKezorm/unraid-templates/main/templates/nexbeat.xml";s:4:"Icon";s:83:"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/DerKezorm/unraid-templates/main/icons/nexbeat.png";s:4:"Date";s:10:"2026-09-20";s:10:"Networking";a:1:{s:4:"Mode";s:6:"bridge";}s:6:"Config";a:9:{i:0;a:2:{s:11:"@attributes";a:9:{s:4:"Name";s:10:"WebUI Port";s:6:"Target";s:4:"8000";s:7:"Default";s:4:"8030";s:4:"Mode";s:3:"tcp";s:11:"Description";s:47:"Port you reach nexbeat at. Container port: 8000";s:4:"Type";s:4:"Port";s:7:"Display";s:6:"always";s:8:"Required";s:4:"true";s:4:"Mask";s:5:"false";}s:5:"value";s:4:"8030";}i:1;a:2:{s:11:"@attributes";a:9:{s:4:"Name";s:28:"Data (Container Path: /data)";s:6:"Target";s:5:"/data";s:7:"Default";s:25:"/mnt/user/appdata/nexbeat";s:4:"Mode";s:2:"rw";s:11:"Description";s:145:"Holds the SQLite database with accounts, requests and settings, and the key that signs sessions. Keep it on a local disk, not on a network share.";s:4:"Type";s:4:"Path";s:7:"Display";s:6:"always";s:8:"Required";s:4:"true";s:4:"Mask";s:5:"false";}s:5:"value";s:25:"/mnt/user/appdata/nexbeat";}i:2;a:2:{s:11:"@attributes";a:9:{s:4:"Name";s:4:"PUID";s:6:"Target";s:4:"PUID";s:7:"Default";s:2:"99";s:4:"Mode";s:0:"";s:11:"Description";s:69:"User id that should own the files in /data. 99 is the Unraid default.";s:4:"Type";s:8:"Variable";s:7:"Display";s:6:"always";s:8:"Required";s:4:"true";s:4:"Mask";s:5:"false";}s:5:"value";s:2:"99";}i:3;a:2:{s:11:"@attributes";a:9:{s:4:"Name";s:4:"PGID";s:6:"Target";s:4:"PGID";s:7:"Default";s:3:"100";s:4:"Mode";s:0:"";s:11:"Description";s:71:"Group id that should own the files in /data. 100 is the Unraid default.";s:4:"Type";s:8:"Variable";s:7:"Display";s:6:"always";s:8:"Required";s:4:"true";s:4:"Mask";s:5:"false";}s:5:"value";s:3:"100";}i:4;a:2:{s:11:"@attributes";a:9:{s:4:"Name";s:9:"Time Zone";s:6:"Target";s:2:"TZ";s:7:"Default";s:0:"";s:4:"Mode";s:0:"";s:11:"Description";s:144:"The zone the container runs in, for example Europe/Berlin. Quotas count in calendar days, weeks and months of this zone. Leave blank to use UTC.";s:4:"Type";s:8:"Variable";s:7:"Display";s:6:"always";s:8:"Required";s:5:"false";s:4:"Mask";s:5:"false";}s:5:"value";s:0:"";}i:5;a:2:{s:11:"@attributes";a:9:{s:4:"Name";s:37:"Container Port (host networking only)";s:6:"Target";s:12:"NEXBEAT_PORT";s:7:"Default";s:0:"";s:4:"Mode";s:0:"";s:11:"Description";s:339:"Leave this empty unless you switched Network Type to Host. In bridge mode the WebUI Port above already does the job and setting this will break it, because the mapping still points at 8000. On host networking the port inside the container is the port on your server, so use this to move nexbeat off 8000 if something else is already there.";s:4:"Type";s:8:"Variable";s:7:"Display";s:8:"advanced";s:8:"Required";s:5:"false";s:4:"Mask";s:5:"false";}s:5:"value";s:0:"";}i:6;a:2:{s:11:"@attributes";a:9:{s:4:"Name";s:10:"Secret Key";s:6:"Target";s:18:"NEXBEAT_SECRET_KEY";s:7:"Default";s:0:"";s:4:"Mode";s:0:"";s:11:"Description";s:242:"Signs sessions and encrypts the stored credentials, such as the Lidarr API key and the password of the mail server. Leave blank: nexbeat creates one on first start and keeps it in /data/secret.key. Back it up together with the data directory.";s:4:"Type";s:8:"Variable";s:7:"Display";s:8:"advanced";s:8:"Required";s:5:"false";s:4:"Mask";s:4:"true";}s:5:"value";s:0:"";}i:7;a:2:{s:11:"@attributes";a:9:{s:4:"Name";s:13:"Secure Cookie";s:6:"Target";s:21:"NEXBEAT_COOKIE_SECURE";s:7:"Default";s:4:"auto";s:4:"Mode";s:0:"";s:11:"Description";s:240:"auto marks the session cookie Secure when the request arrived over https. Use on only if a proxy terminates TLS and forwards plain http, and never if nexbeat should also be reachable over http, or nobody stays signed in. off never marks it.";s:4:"Type";s:8:"Variable";s:7:"Display";s:8:"advanced";s:8:"Required";s:5:"false";s:4:"Mask";s:5:"false";}s:5:"value";s:4:"auto";}i:8;a:2:{s:11:"@attributes";a:9:{s:4:"Name";s:15:"Trusted Proxies";s:6:"Target";s:19:"FORWARDED_ALLOW_IPS";s:7:"Default";s:0:"";s:4:"Mode";s:0:"";s:11:"Description";s:309:"Addresses or networks of your reverse proxies, comma separated, for example 172.16.0.0/12. Only their X-Forwarded-For and X-Forwarded-Proto (the rightmost value) are believed, so only they can tell nexbeat that a request came in over https. Leave blank when nexbeat is not behind a proxy; blank trusts nobody.";s:4:"Type";s:8:"Variable";s:7:"Display";s:8:"advanced";s:8:"Required";s:5:"false";s:4:"Mask";s:5:"false";}s:5:"value";s:0:"";}}s:12:"TemplatePath";s:41:"/tmp/GitHub/AppFeed/templates/nexbeat.xml";s:4:"Repo";s:22:"DerKezorm's Repository";s:12:"CategoryList";a:2:{i:0;s:14:"MediaApp-Music";i:1;s:15:"Tools-Utilities";}s:9:"downloads";i:110;s:9:"FirstSeen";i:1790002781;s:10:"LastUpdate";i:1791886369;s:14:"LastUpdateScan";i:1791953108;s:8:"Category";s:30:"MediaApp:Music Tools:Utilities";s:2:"ID";i:340;s:11:"Displayable";b:1;s:6:"Author";s:9:"derkezorm";s:13:"DockerHubName";s:7:"nexbeat";s:8:"RepoName";s:22:"DerKezorm's Repository";s:10:"SortAuthor";s:9:"derkezorm";s:8:"SortName";s:7:"nexbeat";s:6:"random";i:1530045141;s:9:"Blacklist";b:0;s:6:"MinVer";s:3:"6.0";s:4:"Path";s:112:"/tmp/community.applications/tempFiles/templates-community-apps/DerKezormsRepository/derkezorm-nexbeat-latest.xml";s:10:"Deprecated";b:0;s:10:"Compatible";b:1;s:16:"ModeratorComment";N;}i:341;a:39:{s:4:"Name";s:8:"nexbrand";s:10:"Repository";s:26:"ghcr.io/derkezorm/nexbrand";s:8:"Registry";s:61:"https://github.com/DerKezorm/nexbrand/pkgs/container/nexbrand";s:7:"Network";s:6:"bridge";s:5:"Shell";s:2:"sh";s:10:"Privileged";s:5:"false";s:7:"Support";s:44:"https://github.com/DerKezorm/nexbrand/issues";s:6:"GitHub";s:37:"https://github.com/DerKezorm/nexbrand";s:6:"ReadMe";s:44:"https://github.com/DerKezorm/nexbrand#readme";s:7:"Project";s:37:"https://github.com/DerKezorm/nexbrand";s:8:"Overview";s:980:"nexbrand keeps the corporate design of your clients in one place, on your own server: colours with their print values, fonts with their licence, logos with the ground they belong on, a type scale, rules and example files, per client and per project, with every version kept on a time line.Checks are computed from the set: contrast of every pair by WCAG 2.2, logos at 3:1, colour vision deficiencies, nearly identical colours, fonts that must not leave the house. A workbench builds a new CI from a few words, a picture or one colour, clients review the directions through a link without an account, and the choice becomes version 1.0. Every version comes as CSS variables, a Tailwind 4 theme, SCSS or design tokens, over an API and over MCP for an AI in your editor. Access per client for people and teams, accounts by invitation or OpenID Connect (one-button setup for authentik), an optional second factor, public pages, backups and a log. English and German, light and dark.";s:5:"WebUI";s:24:"http://[IP]:[PORT:8000]/";s:11:"TemplateURL";s:88:"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/DerKezorm/unraid-templates/main/templates/nexbrand.xml";s:4:"Icon";s:84:"https://ra