-matic";s:8:"Overview";s:533:"Disc-o-Matic: a disc-ripping appliance with a web UI. Insert a disc and it is read and recognised: Blu-ray, UHD, DVD and HD DVD are backed up whole or ripped to MKV with MakeMKV (movies, TV season discs, concerts; Plex/Jellyfin naming); audio CDs are read with cdparanoia, checked against AccurateRip and CTDB, tagged from MusicBrainz and saved as FLAC, MP3 or Opus with cover art; data discs are copied as ISO images. Optional automatic jobs with a countdown, live progress, history with logs. Nothing is overwritten without asking.";s:5:"WebUI";s:24:"http://[IP]:[PORT:8088]/";s:11:"TemplateURL";s:81:"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/Disc-o-Matic/disc-o-matic/main/disc-o-matic.xml";s:4:"Icon";s:73:"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/Disc-o-Matic/disc-o-matic/main/logo.png";s:7:"License";s:117:"Free to use; source not published. The templates and docs in its repository: MIT. Bundles MakeMKV under its own EULA.";s:10:"Screenshot";a:4:{i:0;s:88:"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/Disc-o-Matic/disc-o-matic/main/screenshots/console.png";i:1;s:91:"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/Disc-o-Matic/disc-o-matic/main/screenshots/cd-ripping.png";i:2;s:88:"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/Disc-o-Matic/disc-o-matic/main/screenshots/history.png";i:3;s:89:"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/Disc-o-Matic/disc-o-matic/main/screenshots/settings.png";}s:11:"ExtraParams";s:11:"--memory=4g";s:8:"Requires";s:322:"An optical drive passed through as two devices: /dev/sr0 and its SCSI generic device /dev/sgN. To find N, run on the server: ls /sys/block/sr0/device/scsi_generic (it prints sgN, the one of that very drive; for a second drive, sr1). UHD discs need a drive MakeMKV can use in LibreDrive mode. Bundles MakeMKV: see its EULA.";s:6:"Config";a:8:{i:0;a:2:{s:11:"@attributes";a:9:{s:4:"Name";s:11:"Web UI port";s:6:"Target";s:4:"8088";s:7:"Default";s:4:"8099";s:4:"Mode";s:3:"tcp";s:11:"Description";s:105:"Web UI, REST API and live updates: the port on the server (the app listens on 8088 inside the container).";s:4:"Type";s:4:"Port";s:7:"Display";s:6:"always";s:8:"Required";s:4:"true";s:4:"Mask";s:5:"false";}s:5:"value";s:4:"8099";}i:1;a:2:{s:11:"@attributes";a:9:{s:4:"Name";s:6:"Config";s:6:"Target";s:7:"/config";s:7:"Default";s:30:"/mnt/user/appdata/disc-o-matic";s:4:"Mode";s:2:"rw";s:11:"Description";s:98:"Database (dom.db), job logs, MakeMKV settings and downloaded data. Optional dom.yaml for settings.";s:4:"Type";s:4:"Path";s:7:"Display";s:6:"always";s:8:"Required";s:4:"true";s:4:"Mask";s:5:"false";}s:5:"value";s:30:"/mnt/user/appdata/disc-o-matic";}i:2;a:2:{s:11:"@attributes";a:9:{s:4:"Name";s:7:"Backups";s:6:"Target";s:8:"/backups";s:7:"Default";s:23:"/mnt/user/media/Backups";s:4:"Mode";s:2:"rw";s:11:"Description";s:348:"Default home of all output: Bluray/ and DVD/ (full backups), MKV/, TV/, Concerts/, Music/ (CDs), CD Images/, ISO/ (data discs). Each can be moved elsewhere in Settings → Storage (map that folder here first, e.g. /mnt/user/Music → /music). Use a /mnt/user/... path: the mover leaves it alone (a /mnt/cache/... folder is moved away by the mover).";s:4:"Type";s:4:"Path";s:7:"Display";s:6:"always";s:8:"Required";s:4:"true";s:4:"Mask";s:5:"false";}s:5:"value";s:23:"/mnt/user/media/Backups";}i:3;a:2:{s:11:"@attributes";a:9:{s:4:"Name";s:13:"Optical drive";s:6:"Target";s:0:"";s:7:"Default";s:8:"/dev/sr0";s:4:"Mode";s:0:"";s:11:"Description";s:34:"Block device of the optical drive.";s:4:"Type";s:6:"Device";s:7:"Display";s:6:"always";s:8:"Required";s:4:"true";s:4:"Mask";s:5:"false";}s:5:"value";s:8:"/dev/sr0";}i:4;a:2:{s:11:"@attributes";a:9:{s:4:"Name";s:28:"Optical drive (SCSI generic)";s:6:"Target";s:0:"";s:7:"Default";s:0:"";s:4:"Mode";s:0:"";s:11:"Description";s:155:"SCSI generic device of the same drive (MakeMKV talks to the drive through it). The number can change when disks are added; see Requires for how to find it.";s:4:"Type";s:6:"Device";s:7:"Display";s:6:"always";s:8:"Required";s:4:"true";s:4:"Mask";s:5:"false";}s:5:"value";s:0:"";}i:5;a:2:{s:11:"@attributes";a:9:{s:4:"Name";s:4:"PUID";s:6:"Target";s:4:"PUID";s:7:"Default";s:2:"99";s:4:"Mode";s:0:"";s:11:"Description";s:35:"User the app runs as (99 = nobody).";s:4:"Type";s:8:"Variable";s:7:"Display";s:8:"advanced";s:8:"Required";s:4:"true";s:4:"Mask";s:5:"false";}s:5:"value";s:2:"99";}i:6;a:2:{s:11:"@attributes";a:9:{s:4:"Name";s:4:"PGID";s:6:"Target";s:4:"PGID";s:7:"Default";s:3:"100";s:4:"Mode";s:0:"";s:11:"Description";s:84:"Group the app runs as (100 = users). The drive's own groups are added automatically.";s:4:"Type";s:8:"Variable";s:7:"Display";s:8:"advanced";s:8:"Required";s:4:"true";s:4:"Mask";s:5:"false";}s:5:"value";s:3:"100";}i:7;a:2:{s:11:"@attributes";a:9:{s:4:"Name";s:5:"UMASK";s:6:"Target";s:5:"UMASK";s:7:"Default";s:3:"000";s:4:"Mode";s:0:"";s:11:"Description";s:185:"Permissions of new backups and rips: 000 (rw for everyone, Unraid's own convention) lets SMB users rename and delete them; 002 keeps them from others; 022 read-only for all but the app.";s:4:"Type";s:8:"Variable";s:7:"Display";s:8:"advanced";s:8:"Required";s:5:"false";s:4:"Mask";s:5:"false";}s:5:"value";s:3:"000";}}s:12:"TemplatePath";s:36:"/tmp/GitHub/AppFeed/disc-o-matic.xml";s:4:"Repo";s:25:"Disc-o-Matic's Repository";s:12:"CategoryList";a:3:{i:0;s:14:"MediaApp-Video";i:1;s:14:"MediaApp-Music";i:2;s:15:"Tools-Utilities";}s:9:"downloads";i:142;s:9:"FirstSeen";i:1791058168;s:10:"LastUpdate";i:1791053809;s:14:"LastUpdateScan";i:1791058168;s:8:"Category";s:45:"MediaApp:Video MediaApp:Music Tools:Utilities";s:2:"ID";i:371;s:11:"Displayable";b:1;s:6:"Author";s:10:"simplic17y";s:13:"DockerHubName";s:12:"disc-o-matic";s:8:"RepoName";s:25:"Disc-o-Matic's Repository";s:10:"SortAuthor";s:10:"simplic17y";s:8:"SortName";s:12:"Disc o Matic";s:6:"random";i:2078236917;s:9:"Blacklist";b:0;s:6:"MinVer";s:3:"6.0";s:4:"Path";s:117:"/tmp/community.applications/tempFiles/templates-community-apps/DiscoMaticsRepository/simplic17y-DiscoMatic-latest.xml";s: