"bridge";s:5:"Shell";s:2:"sh";s:10:"Privileged";s:5:"false";s:7:"Support";s:51:"https://github.com/EzekielTheMad/healthtrack/issues";s:7:"Project";s:44:"https://github.com/EzekielTheMad/healthtrack";s:8:"Overview";s:763:"Self-hosted personal health tracker. Track medications, conditions, allergies, labs, vitals, procedures, vaccines, appointments and notes for yourself and your dependents — all data stays in a single SQLite database and uploads folder under /data on your server. No cloud services required. The first registered user becomes the instance admin; after that, registration is invite-only by default (create single-use invite links under Settings, or set SIGNUPS_ENABLED to true to open registration). Optional integrations (each enabled only when its keys are set): Anthropic API key for AI health summaries, natural-language queries and lab/vaccine PDF parsing; Google OAuth for "Sign in with Google"; Oura for ring data sync. Back up /data to back up everything.";s:5:"WebUI";s:23:"http://[IP]:[PORT:3000]";s:11:"TemplateURL";s:87:"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/EzekielTheMad/healthtrack/main/unraid/healthtrack.xml";s:4:"Icon";s:80:"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/EzekielTheMad/healthtrack/main/public/icon.png";s:10:"Screenshot";a:3:{i:0;s:96:"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/EzekielTheMad/healthtrack/main/docs/screenshots/dashboard.webp";i:1;s:100:"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/EzekielTheMad/healthtrack/main/docs/screenshots/vitals-trends.webp";i:2;s:100:"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/EzekielTheMad/healthtrack/main/docs/screenshots/import-review.webp";}s:6:"Config";a:16:{i:0;a:2:{s:11:"@attributes";a:9:{s:4:"Name";s:10:"WebUI Port";s:6:"Target";s:4:"3000";s:7:"Default";s:4:"3000";s:4:"Mode";s:3:"tcp";s:11:"Description";s:216:"Host port for the HealthTrack web interface. If another container already uses 3000 (Mealie, Grafana, etc.), change this to a free port and update APP_URL to match — the container always listens on 3000 internally.";s:4:"Type";s:4:"Port";s:7:"Display";s:6:"always";s:8:"Required";s:4:"true";s:4:"Mask";s:5:"false";}s:5:"value";s:4:"3000";}i:1;a:2:{s:11:"@attributes";a:9:{s:4:"Name";s:4:"Data";s:6:"Target";s:5:"/data";s:7:"Default";s:29:"/mnt/user/appdata/healthtrack";s:4:"Mode";s:2:"rw";s:11:"Description";s:164:"All application state: SQLite database (healthtrack.db), uploaded lab PDFs (uploads/) and auto-generated secrets (keys/). Back up this folder to back up everything.";s:4:"Type";s:4:"Path";s:7:"Display";s:6:"always";s:8:"Required";s:4:"true";s:4:"Mask";s:5:"false";}s:5:"value";s:29:"/mnt/user/appdata/healthtrack";}i:2;a:2:{s:11:"@attributes";a:8:{s:4:"Name";s:7:"APP_URL";s:6:"Target";s:7:"APP_URL";s:7:"Default";s:0:"";s:11:"Description";s:199:"The URL users browse to — required for login/auth callbacks to work. Use your server's address and the mapped port, e.g. http://YOUR_SERVER_IP:3000 (or your reverse-proxy HTTPS URL if you use one).";s:4:"Type";s:8:"Variable";s:7:"Display";s:6:"always";s:8:"Required";s:4:"true";s:4:"Mask";s:5:"false";}s:5:"value";s:0:"";}i:3;a:2:{s:11:"@attributes";a:8:{s:4:"Name";s:15:"SIGNUPS_ENABLED";s:6:"Target";s:15:"SIGNUPS_ENABLED";s:7:"Default";s:0:"";s:11:"Description";s:254:"Registration policy. Leave EMPTY (recommended): the first account registers freely and becomes admin, then new accounts require a single-use invite link (Settings &gt; Invites). Set to true to open registration to anyone, or false to close it completely.";s:4:"Type";s:8:"Variable";s:7:"Display";s:6:"always";s:8:"Required";s:5:"false";s:4:"Mask";s:5:"false";}s:5:"value";s:0:"";}i:4;a:2:{s:11:"@attributes";a:8:{s:4:"Name";s:17:"ANTHROPIC_API_KEY";s:6:"Target";s:17:"ANTHROPIC_API_KEY";s:7:"Default";s:0:"";s:11:"Description";s:197:"Optional. Anthropic API key — enables AI features: health summaries, natural-language health queries, medication interaction checks and lab/vaccine PDF parsing. AI features are hidden when unset.";s:4:"Type";s:8:"Variable";s:7:"Display";s:6:"always";s:8:"Required";s:5:"false";s:4:"Mask";s:4:"true";}s:5:"value";s:0:"";}i:5;a:2:{s:11:"@attributes";a:8:{s:4:"Name";s:16:"GOOGLE_CLIENT_ID";s:6:"Target";s:16:"GOOGLE_CLIENT_ID";s:7:"Default";s:0:"";s:11:"Description";s:400:"Optional. Google OAuth client ID — enables the 'Sign in with Google' button. REQUIRES serving over HTTPS on a real hostname (reverse proxy or tunnel): Google rejects http:// and LAN-IP redirect URIs, so this will NOT work on a bare 192.168.x.x address. In the Google Cloud Console, add this authorized redirect URI: APP_URL/api/auth/callback/google (email/password login works without any of this).";s:4:"Type";s:8:"Variable";s:7:"Display";s:6:"always";s:8:"Required";s:5:"false";s:4:"Mask";s:5:"false";}s:5:"value";s:0:"";}i:6;a:2:{s:11:"@attributes";a:8:{s:4:"Name";s:20:"GOOGLE_CLIENT_SECRET";s:6:"Target";s:20:"GOOGLE_CLIENT_SECRET";s:7:"Default";s:0:"";s:11:"Description";s:67:"Optional. Google OAuth client secret (pairs with GOOGLE_CLIENT_ID).";s:4:"Type";s:8:"Variable";s:7:"Display";s:6:"always";s:8:"Required";s:5:"false";s:4:"Mask";s:4:"true";}s:5:"value";s:0:"";}i:7;a:2:{s:11:"@attributes";a:8:{s:4:"Name";s:14:"OURA_CLIENT_ID";s:6:"Target";s:14:"OURA_CLIENT_ID";s:7:"Default";s:0:"";s:11:"Description";s:169:"Optional. Oura OAuth client ID — enables Oura Ring sync (sleep, heart rate, activity). In the Oura developer portal, set the redirect URI to: APP_URL/api/oura/callback";s:4:"Type";s:8:"Variable";s:7:"Display";s:6:"always";s:8:"Required";s:5:"false";s:4:"Mask";s:4:"true";}s:5:"value";s:0:"";}i:8;a:2:{s:11:"@attributes";a:8:{s:4:"Name";s:18:"OURA_CLIENT_SECRET";s:6:"Target";s:18:"OURA_CLIENT_SECRET";s:7:"Default";s:0:"";s:11:"Description";s:63:"Optional. Oura OAuth client secret (pairs with OURA_CLIENT_ID).";s:4:"Type";s:8:"Variable";s:7:"Display";s:6:"always";s:8:"Required";s:5:"false";s:4:"Mask";s:4:"true";}s:5:"value";s:0:"";}i:9;a:2:{s:11:"@attributes";a:8:{s:4:"Name";s:17:"OURA_SYNC_ENABLED";s:6:"Target";s:17:"OURA_SYNC_ENABLED";s:7:"Default";s:4:"