_SECURE_COOKIES";s:7:"Default";s:5:"false";s:11:"Description";s:64:"Set true only when Hermitage is accessed exclusively over HTTPS.";s:4:"Type";s:8:"Variable";s:7:"Display";s:8:"advanced";s:8:"Required";s:4:"true";s:4:"Mask";s:5:"false";}s:5:"value";s:0:"";}i:6;a:2:{s:11:"@attributes";a:8:{s:4:"Name";s:23:"Session Lifetime (days)";s:6:"Target";s:26:"HERMITAGE_SESSION_TTL_DAYS";s:7:"Default";s:2:"30";s:11:"Description";s:31:"Sliding login lifetime in days.";s:4:"Type";s:8:"Variable";s:7:"Display";s:8:"advanced";s:8:"Required";s:4:"true";s:4:"Mask";s:5:"false";}s:5:"value";s:0:"";}i:7;a:2:{s:11:"@attributes";a:8:{s:4:"Name";s:19:"Artwork Cache Items";s:6:"Target";s:27:"HERMITAGE_COVER_CACHE_ITEMS";s:7:"Default";s:3:"160";s:11:"Description";s:41:"Maximum in-process artwork cache entries.";s:4:"Type";s:8:"Variable";s:7:"Display";s:8:"advanced";s:8:"Required";s:4:"true";s:4:"Mask";s:5:"false";}s:5:"value";s:0:"";}i:8;a:2:{s:11:"@attributes";a:8:{s:4:"Name";s:30:"Persistent Artwork Cache Items";s:6:"Target";s:32:"HERMITAGE_COVER_DISK_CACHE_ITEMS";s:7:"Default";s:4:"1200";s:11:"Description";s:71:"Maximum persistent artwork renditions retained under /data/cover-cache.";s:4:"Type";s:8:"Variable";s:7:"Display";s:8:"advanced";s:8:"Required";s:4:"true";s:4:"Mask";s:5:"false";}s:5:"value";s:0:"";}i:9;a:2:{s:11:"@attributes";a:8:{s:4:"Name";s:16:"Login Rate Limit";s:6:"Target";s:26:"HERMITAGE_LOGIN_RATE_LIMIT";s:7:"Default";s:2:"10";s:11:"Description";s:60:"Failed login attempts allowed per client IP in five minutes.";s:4:"Type";s:8:"Variable";s:7:"Display";s:8:"advanced";s:8:"Required";s:4:"true";s:4:"Mask";s:5:"false";}s:5:"value";s:0:"";}i:10;a:2:{s:11:"@attributes";a:8:{s:4:"Name";s:11:"Trust Proxy";s:6:"Target";s:21:"HERMITAGE_TRUST_PROXY";s:7:"Default";s:5:"false";s:11:"Description";s:91:"Express trust-proxy value. 1 is suitable when one reverse proxy sits in front of Hermitage.";s:4:"Type";s:8:"Variable";s:7:"Display";s:8:"advanced";s:8:"Required";s:5:"false";s:4:"Mask";s:5:"false";}s:5:"value";s:0:"";}}s:12:"TemplatePath";s:43:"/tmp/GitHub/AppFeed/templates/hermitage.xml";s:4:"Repo";s:18:"Fenris' Repository";s:12:"CategoryList";a:1:{i:0;s:14:"MediaApp-Music";}s:16:"ChangeLogPresent";s:1:"1";s:9:"FirstSeen";i:1787702772;s:8:"Category";s:14:"MediaApp:Music";s:2:"ID";i:424;s:11:"Displayable";b:1;s:6:"Author";s:11:"fenrisskoll";s:13:"DockerHubName";s:9:"hermitage";s:8:"RepoName";s:18:"Fenris' Repository";s:10:"SortAuthor";s:11:"fenrisskoll";s:8:"SortName";s:9:"Hermitage";s:6:"random";i:1786820769;s:9:"Blacklist";b:0;s:6:"MinVer";s:3:"6.0";s:4:"Path";s:112:"/tmp/community.applications/tempFiles/templates-community-apps/FenrisRepository/fenrisskoll-Hermitage-latest.xml";s:10:"Deprecated";b:0;s:10:"Compatible";b:1;s:16:"ModeratorComment";N;}i:425;a:38:{s:4:"Name";s:4:"Sylo";s:10:"Repository";s:29:"docker.io/iwgamin/sylo:latest";s:8:"Registry";s:37:"https://hub.docker.com/r/iwgamin/sylo";s:7:"Network";s:6:"bridge";s:5:"Shell";s:2:"sh";s:10:"Privileged";s:5:"false";s:7:"Support";s:42:"https://github.com/Ferdinand99/Sylo/issues";s:7:"Project";s:35:"https://github.com/Ferdinand99/Sylo";s:8:"Overview";s:4853:"Sylo is a multi-function bot for Discord and Fluxer with a web dashboard. It runs on Discord, on Fluxer, or on both from one container (Fluxer support is experimental). It has a per-guild module system (35 modules) - moderation with warning thresholds and a numbered case log (/history, /case), server logging, tickets/modmail answered from the dashboard, reaction roles & autoroles, verification (Verify button or Cloudflare Turnstile captcha), welcome/leave messages, a Welcome Channel builder, birthday announcements, sticky messages, auto-moderation (invite/link/flood/mention/caps/word filters, optionally pushed to Discord's native AutoMod), a counting mini-game, action-based custom slash commands, an autoresponder, reminders (one-off or recurring channel posts), leveling (text + optional voice XP, per-role/channel multipliers, all-time/weekly/monthly public leaderboard), AFK, server statistics (live-count voice channels), server insights (activity charts - messages, joins/leaves and voice-channel usage over time), a free games notifier (Epic Games Store, plus more stores with an IsThereAnyDeal key), ban appeals (banned members get a DM'd link to an appeal form; staff accept/deny from the dashboard), MEE6-style temporary voice channels ("join to create" hubs plus /voice-* control commands), a starboard (re-posts messages that get enough of a reaction into a highlights channel), an invite tracker (credits who invited each member and ranks inviters), reaction polls (/poll with a timer or vote cap), prize giveaways (Enter button, auto-drawn winners), optional Battlefield-series and RuneScape (OSRS/RS3) player stats (/stats, gated by the Game stats module), Twitch / YouTube / Kick go-live & new-video alerts (with an optional "delete the message when the stream ends" mode), RSS/Atom feed alerts (plus Reddit / Mastodon / Bluesky handles), scheduled channel cleanup (auto-delete messages older than a threshold from a channel, on a weekly schedule you pick), and a message/embed creator - plus per-server command management, a Prometheus /metrics endpoint (a ready-made Grafana dashboard ships in the repo), and an editable Discord presence/activity. State is stored in a single SQLite file under /app/data and survives updates (Postgres is optional, see DATABASE_URL). The database is snapshotted automatically (before every schema migration and on a schedule) into /app/data/backups - optionally shipped off-site as well (WebDAV and/or a Discord webhook, optionally encrypted; see BACKUP_WEBDAV_URL / BACKUP_WEBHOOK_URL / BACKUP_ENCRYPTION_KEY); from the dashboard's Health page you can also create, download, import and restore a snapshot (restore swaps the file and lets the container restart on the restored data).

Setup (Discord): create a Discord application at https://discord.com/developers/applications, then set DISCORD_TOKEN (Bot tab) and DISCORD_CLIENT_ID (General Information). Invite the bot with the scopes "bot" and "applications.commands".

Setup (Fluxer): create an application on your Fluxer instance and set FLUXER_TOKEN (bot token) and FLUXER_CLIENT_ID. For a self-hosted Fluxer instance also set FLUXER_WEB_URL. Fluxer has no slash commands yet, so commands run from chat with a prefix (!ping, set with COMMAND_PREFIX) and buttons are shown as reactions. Set only the platform(s) you use; at least one is required. See https://github.com/Ferdinand99/Sylo/blob/main/docs/fluxer.md

Intents (Discord only; Fluxer has none): the member/message-driven modules (logging, welcome, reaction roles, verification, leveling, server statistics, invite tracker, auto-moderation, counting, autoresponder, starboard) need the "Server Members" and/or "Message Content" intents enabled on the Developer Portal Bot page. Leave INTENT_GUILD_MEMBERS / INTENT_MESSAGE_CONTENT at their defaults, or set one to false to boot without that intent (its modules stay unavailable).

Dashboard: runs open by default (use only on a trusted LAN). To require a login for server admins, set DISCORD_CLIENT_SECRET ("Log in with Discord") and/or FLUXER_CLIENT_SECRET ("Log in with Fluxer") and add http://[Unraid-IP]:[HOST-PORT]/auth/discord/callback and/or http://[Unraid-IP]:[HOST-PORT]/auth/fluxer/callback to the app's OAuth redirect URLs. One dashboard account can hold both logins. Put your own ids in OWNER_IDS (Discord) and FLUXER_OWNER_IDS (Fluxer), or nobody can open the Health page once login is on.

Sylo app (iOS): the native app signs in to your instance with the same Discord/Fluxer login (needs DISCORD_CLIENT_SECRET or FLUXER_CLIENT_SECRET and DASHBOARD_URL). Ticket notifications reach the phone through the hosted relay (PUSH_RELAY_URL); operators also get the Health page and dev-log notifications. See https://github.com/Ferdinand99/Sylo/blob/main/docs/mobile-app.md

