;s:4:"5514";}}s:12:"TemplatePath";s:31:"/tmp/GitHub/AppFeed/netlens.xml";s:4:"Repo";s:20:"GeorgeK's Repository";s:12:"CategoryList";a:2:{i:0;s:18:"Network-Management";i:1;s:15:"Tools-Utilities";}s:9:"downloads";i:285;s:9:"FirstSeen";i:1791745164;s:10:"LastUpdate";i:1791514920;s:14:"LastUpdateScan";i:1791745164;s:8:"Category";s:34:"Network:Management Tools:Utilities";s:2:"ID";i:499;s:11:"Displayable";b:1;s:6:"Author";s:7:"gjergjk";s:13:"DockerHubName";s:7:"netlens";s:8:"RepoName";s:20:"GeorgeK's Repository";s:10:"SortAuthor";s:7:"gjergjk";s:8:"SortName";s:7:"netlens";s:6:"random";i:848056067;s:9:"Blacklist";b:0;s:6:"MinVer";s:3:"6.0";s:4:"Path";s:108:"/tmp/community.applications/tempFiles/templates-community-apps/GeorgeKsRepository/gjergjk-netlens-latest.xml";s:4:"Date";N;s:11:"BrandNewApp";b:1;s:10:"Deprecated";b:0;s:10:"Compatible";b:1;s:16:"ModeratorComment";N;}i:500;a:39:{s:4:"Name";s:15:"pia-qbittorrent";s:10:"Repository";s:23:"gjergjk/pia-qbittorrent";s:8:"Registry";s:48:"https://hub.docker.com/r/gjergjk/pia-qbittorrent";s:5:"Shell";s:2:"sh";s:10:"Privileged";s:5:"false";s:7:"Network";s:6:"bridge";s:7:"Support";s:59:"https://github.com/GeorgeAL78/pia-qbittorrent-docker/issues";s:7:"Project";s:52:"https://github.com/GeorgeAL78/pia-qbittorrent-docker";s:8:"Overview";s:2042:"qBittorrent 5.2.4 combined with Private Internet Access (PIA) VPN, built on Alpine Linux for a minimal footprint.

Features:
• Your real IP stays hidden - if the VPN drops, the container loses its internet
• It fixes itself - spots a VPN that has stopped working, even if it still looks connected
• A dead PIA server is not your problem - it moves to another one nearby, and your forwarded port moves with it
• Keeps up with PIA - the server list refreshes on every container start, so it still works when PIA moves a region
• Faster seeding - PIA port forwarding is set up for you, where your region supports it
• Port forwarding keeps trying - if PIA cannot give you a port at startup, it retries in the background and switches qBittorrent over once it works, with no restart
• Downloads survive updates - progress is saved on shutdown, so nothing re-checks
• Files land with the right owner, so they are readable on Unraid without fixing permissions
• Your PIA login can stay in a protected file instead of the container settings
• Runs on amd64 and arm64

Components:
• qBittorrent 5.2.4 with libtorrent 2.0.15
• Alpine Linux 3.24, Boost 1.92.0
• OpenVPN 2.7.7, WireGuard 1.0.20260223, iptables 1.8.13

Full feature and configuration details: https://github.com/GeorgeAL78/pia-qbittorrent-docker

Custom bridge networks work fine (the VPN tunnel runs inside the container either way). Avoid Host networking: the container would then share the Unraid server's own network stack, so the kill switch's firewall rules, routes and IPv6 settings would be applied to the server — including flushing the iptables rules Docker itself relies on, which breaks networking for other containers.

Extra Parameters must keep --cap-add=NET_ADMIN (the VPN and kill switch need it) and --restart unless-stopped (lets the container restart itself to recover).

Pair with the Windows 11 desktop app: https://github.com/GeorgeAL78/qbittorrent-desktop

