er directory used for persistent dashboard data. Normally this should remain /data.";s:4:"Type";s:8:"Variable";s:7:"Display";s:8:"advanced";s:8:"Required";s:4:"true";s:4:"Mask";s:5:"false";}s:5:"value";s:0:"";}}s:12:"TemplatePath";s:54:"/tmp/GitHub/AppFeed/templates/x-onu-sfpp-dashboard.xml";s:4:"Repo";s:23:"JPetovello's Repository";s:12:"CategoryList";a:1:{i:0;s:12:"Tools-System";}s:16:"ChangeLogPresent";s:1:"1";s:9:"FirstSeen";i:1788624404;s:8:"Category";s:12:"Tools:System";s:2:"ID";i:643;s:11:"Displayable";b:1;s:6:"Author";s:10:"jpetovello";s:13:"DockerHubName";s:20:"x-onu-sfpp-dashboard";s:8:"RepoName";s:23:"JPetovello's Repository";s:10:"SortAuthor";s:10:"jpetovello";s:8:"SortName";s:20:"X ONU SFPP Dashboard";s:6:"random";i:745069735;s:9:"Blacklist";b:0;s:6:"MinVer";s:3:"6.0";s:4:"Path";s:124:"/tmp/community.applications/tempFiles/templates-community-apps/JPetovellosRepository/jpetovello-XONUSFPPDashboard-latest.xml";s:10:"Deprecated";b:0;s:10:"Compatible";b:1;s:16:"ModeratorComment";N;}i:644;a:45:{s:4:"Name";s:8:"dify-aio";s:10:"Repository";s:25:"jsonbored/dify-aio:latest";s:8:"Registry";s:43:"https://hub.docker.com/r/jsonbored/dify-aio";s:7:"Network";s:6:"bridge";s:5:"Shell";s:2:"sh";s:10:"Privileged";s:5:"false";s:7:"Support";s:44:"https://github.com/JSONbored/dify-aio/issues";s:7:"Project";s:37:"https://github.com/JSONbored/dify-aio";s:8:"Overview";s:2572:"Dify is a self-hosted AI application platform for agentic workflows, RAG pipelines, tools, model-provider integrations, and observability.

[b]All-In-One Unraid Edition[/b]
`dify-aio` packages the Dify API, workers, web UI, plugin daemon, code sandbox, SSRF proxy, Nginx, PostgreSQL with pgvector, and Redis into one practical Unraid-first container.

[b]Quick Install (Beginners)[/b]
1. Install this template and leave [code]Web UI Port[/code] and [code]AppData[/code] at their defaults unless you already have a port conflict.
2. Start the container and give first boot a few minutes. The wrapper initializes bundled PostgreSQL, pgvector, Redis, generated secrets, local storage, the sandbox, plugin daemon, and the Dify services.
3. Open the Web UI and create the first admin account. You can optionally set [code]Initial Admin Password[/code] before first boot, but it is not required.
4. Add model-provider credentials inside Dify first. For a reverse proxy or published apps, set [code]Public URL[/code] to your external HTTPS URL and restart.
5. Keep Advanced View defaults for the easiest install. The bundled database, cache, vector store, local file storage, sandbox, and SSRF proxy are already wired together.

[b]Power Users (Advanced View)[/b]
- Advanced View exposes external PostgreSQL-compatible databases, Redis, object storage, vector databases, SMTP/mail, plugin storage, observability, CORS/CSP, sandbox, proxy, token expiry, indexing, cleanup, and broader upstream Dify environment controls.
- If you switch a backend selector such as [code]VECTOR_STORE[/code], [code]STORAGE_TYPE[/code], [code]DB_TYPE[/code], or internal service toggles, configure the matching companion fields for that backend.
- Blank secret fields generate and persist values in [code]/appdata/config/generated.env[/code]. Explicit Unraid template values override generated secrets, and [code]/appdata/config/extra.env[/code] remains the final advanced override escape hatch.
- [code]CHECK_UPDATE_URL[/code] is blank by default to avoid outbound update checks unless you intentionally opt in.

[b]Important Notes[/b]
- Dify is a heavier multi-service stack. Plan for at least 2 CPU cores and 4 GiB RAM, with more memory for real indexing, workflow, or model-heavy workloads.
- Public exposure should sit behind a trusted reverse proxy with TLS. Review sandbox/network settings before allowing untrusted users to run code or tools.
- External vector stores, object storage, SMTP, and model providers are optional but real production deployments may need them.";s:5:"WebUI";s:23:"http://[IP]:[PORT:8080]";s:11:"TemplateURL";s:76:"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/JSONbored/awesome-unraid/main/dify-aio.xml";s:6:"ReadMe";s:44:"https://github.com/JSONbored/dify-aio#readme";s:4:"Icon";s:78:"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/JSONbored/awesome-unraid/main/icons/dify.png";s:16:"ExtraSearchTerms";s:88:"ai agent workflow llm rag chatbot mcp openai anthropic ollama app builder knowledge base";s:8:"Requires";s:327:"Dify is a heavier multi-service application. Plan for at least 2 CPU cores and 4 GiB RAM, with more memory for real workloads. Public exposure should be placed behind a trusted reverse proxy with TLS. Model-provider API keys, SMTP, object storage, and external vector stores are optional but may be required for production use.";s:10:"Screenshot";a:3:{i:0;s:97:"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/JSONbored/awesome-unraid/main/screenshots/dify-aio/01-login.png";i:1;s:101:"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/JSONbored/awesome-unraid/main/screenshots/dify-aio/02-workspace.png";i:2;s:98:"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/JSONbored/awesome-unraid/main/screenshots/dify-aio/03-studio.png";}s:10:"Networking";a:1:{s:4:"Mode";s:6:"bridge";}s:6:"Config";a:565:{i:0;a:2:{s:11:"@attributes";a:9:{s:4:"Name";s:11:"Web UI Port";s:6:"Target";s:4:"8080";s:7:"Default";s:4:"8080";s:4:"Mode";s:3:"tcp";s:11:"Description";s:33:"Dify Web UI and API gateway port.";s:4:"Type";s:4:"Port";s:7:"Display";s:6:"always";s:8:"Required";s:4:"true";s:4:"Mask";s:5:"false";}s:5:"value";s:4:"8080";}i:1;a:2:{s:11:"@attributes";a:9:{s:4:"Name";s:7:"AppData";s:6:"Target";s:8:"/appdata";s:7:"Default";s:26:"/mnt/user/appdata/dify-aio";s:4:"Mode";s:2:"rw";s:11:"Description";s:121:"Persistent Dify data, generated secrets, PostgreSQL data, Redis data, uploads, plugin storage, and sandbox configuration.";s:4:"Type";s:4:"Path";s:7:"Display";s:6:"always"