y.applications/tempFiles/templates-community-apps/JSONboredsRepository/jsonbored-nanoclawaio-latest.xml";s:4:"Date";N;s:11:"BrandNewApp";b:1;s:10:"Deprecated";b:0;s:10:"DonateText";s:165:"If these AIO templates save you time, please consider supporting ongoing maintenance via Ko-fi (ko-fi.com/jsonbored) or Buy Me a Coffee (buymeacoffee.com/jsonbored).";s:10:"DonateLink";s:27:"https://ko-fi.com/jsonbored";s:10:"Compatible";b:1;s:16:"ModeratorComment";N;}i:649;a:45:{s:4:"Name";s:10:"penpot-aio";s:10:"Repository";s:27:"jsonbored/penpot-aio:latest";s:8:"Registry";s:45:"https://hub.docker.com/r/jsonbored/penpot-aio";s:7:"Network";s:6:"bridge";s:5:"Shell";s:2:"sh";s:10:"Privileged";s:5:"false";s:7:"Support";s:46:"https://github.com/JSONbored/penpot-aio/issues";s:7:"Project";s:39:"https://github.com/JSONbored/penpot-aio";s:8:"Overview";s:2336:"Penpot is an open-source design and prototyping platform for product teams, designers, and developers.

[b]All-In-One Unraid Edition[/b]
`penpot-aio` packages Penpot frontend, backend, exporter, MCP server, PostgreSQL, Redis-compatible cache, Nginx, and Mailpit into one practical Unraid-first container.

[b]Quick Install (Beginners)[/b]
1. Install this template and leave [code]Web UI Port[/code] and [code]AppData[/code] at their defaults unless you have a port or path conflict.
2. Set [code]Public URL[/code] to the URL users will actually visit, such as [code]http://tower.local:9001[/code] or your reverse-proxy HTTPS URL.
3. Start the container and give first boot a few minutes. The wrapper initializes bundled PostgreSQL, Redis-compatible cache, filesystem assets, Mailpit, MCP, and generated secrets.
4. Open the Web UI and create your first account. The default lab path disables email verification and uses local Mailpit; change the flags and SMTP settings before public production use.

[b]Power Users (Advanced View)[/b]
- Advanced View exposes upstream Penpot configuration, Penpot flags, external PostgreSQL, external Redis/Valkey, SMTP, S3-compatible object storage, OAuth/OIDC/LDAP, telemetry, MCP, SSRF controls, rate/limit/performance tuning, and AIO runtime controls.
- Leave database, cache, SMTP, and storage fields blank/defaulted for the bundled one-container path. Set the matching external fields only when intentionally moving that service out of the AIO container.
- Blank secret fields generate and persist values in [code]/appdata/config/generated.env[/code]. Explicit template values override generated values.
- [code]/appdata/config/extra.env[/code] is loaded as a final sanitized key/value escape hatch, not a substitute for the exposed template options. Only [code]PENPOT_[/code], [code]AWS_[/code], and core runtime keys are accepted; shell syntax is not executed.

[b]Important Notes[/b]
- Penpot is a real multi-service stack. Plan for at least 2 CPU cores and 4 GiB RAM, with more for active teams or large files.
- Public exposure should sit behind a trusted HTTPS reverse proxy. Remove [code]disable-secure-session-cookies[/code] and [code]disable-email-verification[/code] for production.
- The bundled Mailpit inbox is for local/lab capture, not real mail deliverability.";s:5:"WebUI";s:23:"http://[IP]:[PORT:8080]";s:11:"TemplateURL";s:78:"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/JSONbored/awesome-unraid/main/penpot-aio.xml";s:6:"ReadMe";s:46:"https://github.com/JSONbored/penpot-aio#readme";s:4:"Icon";s:80:"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/JSONbored/awesome-unraid/main/icons/penpot.png";s:16:"ExtraSearchTerms";s:82:"design prototype figma alternative whiteboard mcp ux ui product design self-hosted";s:8:"Requires";s:156:"Penpot is a heavier multi-service application. Plan for at least 2 CPU cores and 4 GiB RAM. Use HTTPS and production-safe flags before exposing it publicly.";s:10:"Screenshot";a:3:{i:0;s:99:"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/JSONbored/awesome-unraid/main/screenshots/penpot-aio/01-login.png";i:1;s:102:"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/JSONbored/awesome-unraid/main/screenshots/penpot-aio/02-projects.png";i:2;s:100:"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/JSONbored/awesome-unraid/main/screenshots/penpot-aio/03-editor.png";}s:10:"Networking";a:1:{s:4:"Mode";s:6:"bridge";}s:6:"Config";a:253:{i:0;a:2:{s:11:"@attributes";a:9:{s:4:"Name";s:11:"Web UI Port";s:6:"Target";s:4:"8080";s:7:"Default";s:4:"9001";s:4:"Mode";s:3:"tcp";s:11:"Description";s:61:"Penpot frontend, API gateway, exporter routes, and MCP proxy.";s:4:"Type";s:4:"Port";s:7:"Display";s:6:"always";s:8:"Required";s:4:"true";s:4:"Mask";s:5:"false";}s:5:"value";s:4:"9001";}i:1;a:2:{s:11:"@attributes";a:9:{s:4:"Name";s:15:"Mailpit UI Port";s:6:"Target";s:4:"8025";s:7:"Default";s:4:"8026";s:4:"Mode";s:3:"tcp";s:11:"Description";s:114:"Bundled Mailpit inbox UI for local/lab mail capture. Advanced because normal Penpot use starts through the Web UI.";s:4:"Type";s:4:"Port";s:7:"Display";s:8:"advanced";s:8:"Required";s:5:"false";s:4:"Mask";s:5:"false";}s:5:"value";s:4:"8026";}i:2;a:2:{s:11:"@attributes";a:9:{s:4:"Name";s:13:"MCP HTTP Port";s:6:"Target";s:4:"4401";s:7:"Default";s:0:"";s:4:"Mode";s:3:"t