lished through Pangolin. Runs fully in user space: no network interface is created and the system resolver is left untouched. Optionally exposes the Docker socket read only, so the Pangolin dashboard can list your containers when picking targets. Installed alongside the Pangolin CLI plugin, both share a single Settings entry with a tab each. This is not the Pangolin CLI!";s:10:"Repository";s:72:"https://github.com/Joly0/unraid-pangolin_newt/raw/main/pangolin_newt.plg";s:12:"CategoryList";a:3:{i:0;s:12:"Tools-System";i:1;s:18:"Network-Management";i:2;s:7:"Plugins";}s:13:"pluginVersion";s:10:"2026.10.03";s:6:"Author";s:5:"Joly0";s:16:"ChangeLogPresent";s:1:"1";s:9:"downloads";i:120;s:9:"FirstSeen";i:1786637093;s:14:"LastUpdateScan";i:1792383193;s:11:"pluginStats";a:13:{i:10;i:16;i:11;i:0;i:12;i:0;s:2:"01";i:0;s:2:"02";i:0;s:2:"03";i:0;s:2:"04";i:0;s:2:"05";i:0;s:2:"06";i:0;s:2:"07";i:0;s:2:"08";i:64;s:2:"09";i:40;s:1:"T";i:120;}s:8:"Category";s:40:"Tools:System Network:Management Plugins:";s:2:"ID";i:734;s:11:"Displayable";b:1;s:13:"DockerHubName";s:13:"pangolin newt";s:8:"RepoName";s:18:"joly0's Repository";s:10:"SortAuthor";s:5:"Joly0";s:8:"SortName";s:13:"Pangolin Newt";s:6:"random";i:1130428892;s:9:"Blacklist";b:0;s:4:"Path";s:169:"/tmp/community.applications/tempFiles/templates-community-apps/joly0sRepository/Joly0-PangolinNewt-//github.com/Joly0/unraid-pangolin_newt/raw/main/pangolin_newt.plg.xml";s:4:"Date";N;s:11:"BrandNewApp";b:1;s:10:"Deprecated";b:0;s:10:"DonateLink";s:33:"https://github.com/sponsors/Joly0";s:10:"Compatible";b:1;s:16:"ModeratorComment";N;}i:735;a:40:{s:4:"Name";s:16:"FTB-Skies-2-Aero";s:10:"Repository";s:31:"jonaxio/ftb-skies-2-aero:latest";s:8:"Registry";s:49:"https://hub.docker.com/r/jonaxio/ftb-skies-2-aero";s:7:"Network";s:6:"bridge";s:5:"Shell";s:4:"bash";s:10:"Privileged";s:5:"false";s:7:"Support";s:61:"https://github.com/JonaxScript/ftb-skies-2-aero-docker/issues";s:7:"Project";s:54:"https://github.com/JonaxScript/ftb-skies-2-aero-docker";s:6:"ReadMe";s:84:"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/JonaxScript/ftb-skies-2-aero-docker/main/README.md";s:8:"Overview";s:557:"Dedicated server for the FTB Skies 2: Aero modpack (Minecraft 1.21.1, NeoForge, Java 21), a skyblock pack built around airships. On the first start the container installs the modpack into the appdata folder with the official FTB server installer (about 1.3 GB, takes a few minutes); after that the server starts right away. Set EULA to true to accept the Minecraft EULA. Ops, MOTD, world name and Java memory are set through the variables. The newest modpack version is installed on the first start; to update later, enter the new version in FTB_VERSION_ID.";s:11:"TemplateURL";s:105:"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/JonaxScript/ftb-skies-2-aero-docker/main/templates/ftb-skies-2-aero.xml";s:4:"Icon";s:102:"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/JonaxScript/ftb-skies-2-aero-docker/main/images/ftb-skies-2-aero.png";s:11:"ExtraParams";s:18:"--stop-timeout=120";s:8:"Requires";s:125:"About 8 GB of free RAM for the server (JVM_OPTS default -Xms6G -Xmx8G). Players need the same modpack version in the FTB App.";s:16:"ExtraSearchTerms";s:85:"minecraft modpack ftb feed-the-beast skyblock neoforge airship aeronautics skies aero";s:6:"Config";a:10:{i:0;a:2:{s:11:"@attributes";a:9:{s:4:"Name";s:4:"EULA";s:6:"Target";s:4:"EULA";s:7:"Default";s:5:"false";s:4:"Mode";s:0:"";s:11:"Description";s:163:"Do you agree to the Mojang EULA available at https://account.mojang.com/documents/minecraft_eula? Server will not start without accepting. Set to 'true' to accept.";s:4:"Type";s:8:"Variable";s:7:"Display";s:6:"always";s:8:"Required";s:4:"true";s:4:"Mask";s:5:"false";}s:5:"value";s:5:"false";}i:1;a:2:{s:11:"@attributes";a:9:{s:4:"Name";s:8:"JVM_OPTS";s:6:"Target";s:8:"JVM_OPTS";s:7:"Default";s:13:"-Xms6G -Xmx8G";s:4:"Mode";s:0:"";s:11:"Description";s:12:"Java Options";s:4:"Type";s:8:"Variable";s:7:"Display";s:6:"always";s:8:"Required";s:5:"false";s:4:"Mask";s:5:"false"