Nothing is ever deleted automatically. The dashboard can only ask: each request is shown on the device itself, with every path, to approve or deny. Servers without a screen send their requests to an approver phone, which can only be chosen on the server (freesize approver set), never from the dashboard.

Sign-in is OpenID Connect against Authentik: make an OAuth2/OpenID provider and application there, with the redirect URI [Hub address]/auth/callback, and fill in the fields below.";s:7:"License";s:16:"GPL-3.0-or-later";s:5:"WebUI";s:24:"http://[IP]:[PORT:9090]/";s:11:"TemplateURL";s:88:"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/McGeaverBeaver/FreeSize/master/unraid/freesize-hub.xml";s:4:"Icon";s:86:"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/McGeaverBeaver/FreeSize/HEAD/unraid/freesize-hub.png";s:8:"Requires";s:63:"An Authentik (or other OpenID Connect) provider for signing in.";s:6:"Config";a:17:{i:0;a:2:{s:11:"@attributes";a:9:{s:4:"Name";s:8:"Web port";s:6:"Target";s:4:"9090";s:7:"Default";s:4:"9090";s:4:"Mode";s:3:"tcp";s:11:"Description";s:178:"Port of the dashboard and of the address devices report to, over HTTPS with the Hub's own certificate. To keep the Hub off the internet, reach it over your LAN or WireGuard only.";s:4:"Type";s:4:"Port";s:7:"Display";s:6:"always";s:8:"Required";s:4:"true";s:4:"Mask";s:5:"false";}s:5:"value";s:4:"9090";}i:1;a:2:{s:11:"@attributes";a:9:{s:4:"Name";s:7:"Appdata";s:6:"Target";s:5:"/data";s:7:"Default";s:30:"/mnt/user/appdata/freesize-hub";s:4:"Mode";s:2:"rw";s:11:"Description";s:123:"The database and the Hub's key. Back this folder up: devices trust the key, and a new one means pairing every device again.";s:4:"Type";s:4:"Path";s:7:"Display";s:6:"always";s:8:"Required";s:4:"true";s:4:"Mask";s:5:"false";}s:5:"value";s:30:"/mnt/user/appdata/freesize-hub";}i:2;a:2:{s:11:"@attributes";a:9:{s:4:"Name";s:11:"Hub address";s:6:"Target";s:16:"FREESIZE_HUB_URL";s:7:"Default";s:0:"";s:4:"Mode";s:0:"";s:11:"Description";s:255:"The address people and devices use to reach the Hub, e.g. https://freesize.home.lan or https://192.168.10.200:9090. The Hub makes its certificate for this host. It goes into pairing codes, and [address]/auth/callback is the redirect URI to give Authentik.";s:4:"Type";s:8:"Variable";s:7:"Display";s:6:"always";s:8:"Required";s:4:"true";s:4:"Mask";s:5:"false";}s:5:"value";s:0:"";}i:3;a:2:{s:11:"@attributes";a:9:{s:4:"Name";s:8:"Hub name";s:6:"Target";s:17:"FREESIZE_HUB_NAME";s:7:"Default";s:12:"FreeSize Hub";s:4:"Mode";s:0:"";s:11:"Description";s:53:"Shown in the dashboard and on devices when they pair.";s:4:"Type";s:8:"Variable";s:7:"Display";s:6:"always";s:8:"Required";s:5:"false";s:4:"Mask";s:5:"false";}s:5:"value";s:12:"FreeSize Hub";}i:4;a:2:{s:11:"@attributes";a:9:{s:4:"Name";s:20:"Authentik issuer URL";s:6:"Target";s:20:"FREESIZE_OIDC_ISSUER";s:7:"Default";s:0:"";s:4:"Mode";s:0:"";s:11:"Description";s:109:"The OpenID Configuration Issuer of the Authentik provider, e.g. https://auth.home.lan/application/o/freesize/";s:4:"Type";s:8:"Variable";s:7:"Display";s:6:"always";s:8:"Required";s:4:"true";s:4:"Mask";s:5:"false";}s:5:"value";s:0:"";}i:5;a:2:{s:11:"@attributes";a:9:{s:4:"Name";s:9:"Client ID";s:6:"Target";s:23:"FREESIZE_OIDC_CLIENT_ID";s:7:"Default";s:0:"";s:4:"Mode";s:0:"";s:11:"Description";s:25:"The provider's Client ID.";s:4:"Type";s:8:"Variable";s:7:"Display";s:6:"always";s:8:"Required";s:4:"true";s:4:"Mask";s:5:"false";}s:5:"value";s:0:"";}i:6;a:2:{s:11:"@attributes";a:9:{s:4:"Name";s:13:"Client secret";s:6:"Target";s:27:"FREESIZE_OIDC_CLIENT_SECRET";s:7:"Default";s:0:"";s:4:"Mode";s:0:"";s:11:"Description";s:53:"The provider's Client Secret (a confidential client).";s:4:"Type";s:8:"Variable";s:7:"Display";s:6:"always";s:8:"Required";s:4:"true";s:4:"Mask";s:4:"true";}s:5:"value";s:0:"";}i:7;a:2:{s:11:"@attributes";a:9:{s:4:"Name";s:11:"Admin group";s:6:"Target";s:20:"FREESIZE_ADMIN_GROUP";s:7:"Default";s:15:"freesize-admins";s:4:"Mode";s:0:"";s:11:"Description";s:138:"Authentik group whose members can pair devices, send requests and change settings. Authentik sends a user's groups with the profile scope.";s:4:"Type";s:8:"Variable";s:7:"Display";s:6:"always";s:8:"Required";s:4:"true";s:4:"Mask";s:5:"false";}s:5:"value";s:15:"freesize-admins";}i:8;a:2:{s:11:"@attributes";a:9:{s:4:"N