ity-apps/LindwormsRepository/joinc-CamofoxBrowser-latest.xml";s:4:"Date";N;s:11:"BrandNewApp";b:1;s:10:"Deprecated";b:0;s:10:"Compatible";b:1;s:16:"ModeratorComment";N;}i:889;a:36:{s:4:"Name";s:13:"Gods-Eye-View";s:10:"Repository";s:39:"ghcr.io/mircoblitz/gods-eye-view:latest";s:8:"Registry";s:72:"https://github.com/MircoBlitz/gods-eye-view/pkgs/container/gods-eye-view";s:7:"Network";s:6:"bridge";s:5:"Shell";s:2:"sh";s:10:"Privileged";s:5:"false";s:7:"Support";s:50:"https://github.com/MircoBlitz/gods-eye-view/issues";s:7:"Project";s:45:"https://github.com/bilawalsidhu/gods-eye-view";s:8:"Overview";s:425:"God's Eye View is a browser-based 3D globe for exploring public aircraft, ship, satellite, earthquake, traffic, camera, radio, fire, and other geospatial data. This image packages the upstream v0.2.1 application and its required Vite proxy server. It starts without API keys. Optional provider credentials unlock additional data and voice features. Intended for a trusted home LAN; the application has no user authentication.";s:5:"WebUI";s:24:"http://[IP]:[PORT:4173]/";s:11:"TemplateURL";s:99:"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/MircoBlitz/unraid-community-apps/main/templates/gods-eye-view.xml";s:4:"Icon";s:88:"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/MircoBlitz/gods-eye-view/main/assets/gods-eye-view.png";s:11:"ExtraParams";s:24:"--init --stop-timeout=15";s:8:"Requires";s:493:"WebGL-capable browser. Keep this container on a trusted LAN or behind a separately reviewed authenticated reverse proxy. Anyone who can reach the web interface can use configured provider-backed endpoints and consume their quotas. Provider Settings inside the app is intentionally unavailable for a network-shared container; configure optional keys in this template. Restrict client-visible Google Maps and Cesium credentials at their providers and set provider-side quotas or spending limits.";s:6:"Config";a:15:{i:0;a:2:{s:11:"@attributes";a:9:{s:4:"Name";s:11:"Web UI Port";s:6:"Target";s:4:"4173";s:7:"Defau