Setup: install the "mcsm" template first (it explains the shared "infrarust" network). Copy config.toml from https://github.com/Niki2k1/mcsm/tree/main/Unraid/infrarust into the config folder mapped below before starting. Point a DNS wildcard such as *.mc.example.com at your Unraid IP and forward port 25565.

Turn on Autostart for this container in the Docker tab. Unraid stops containers with docker stop, so the restart policy alone does not bring it back after a reboot or Docker restart.";s:11:"TemplateURL";s:72:"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/Niki2k1/mcsm/main/unraid/infrarust.xml";s:4:"Icon";s:72:"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/Niki2k1/mcsm/main/unraid/infrarust.png";s:11:"ExtraParams";s:33:"--restart unless-stopped --user 0";s:8:"PostArgs";s:66:"--config /app/config/config.toml --plugins-dir /app/config/plugins";s:8:"Requires";s:175:"The &quot;mcsm&quot; template, the user-defined Docker network &quot;infrarust&quot;, and a config.toml in the config folder (sample in the MCSM repo under unraid/infrarust/).";s:6:"Config";a:4:{i:0;a:2:{s:11:"@attributes";a:9:{s:4:"Name";s:14:"Minecraft port";s:6:"Target";s:5:"25565";s:7:"Default";s:5:"25565";s:4:"Mode";s:3:"tcp";s:11:"Description";s:51:"Port players connect to. Forward it on your router.";s:4:"Type";s:4:"Port";s:7:"Display";s:6:"always";s:8:"Required";s:4:"true";s:4:"Mask";s:5:"false";}s:5:"value";s:5:"25565";}i:1;a:2:{s:11:"@attributes";a:9:{s:4:"Name";s:13:"Config folder";s:6:"Target";s:11:"/app/config";s:7:"Default";s:27:"/mnt/user/appdata/infrarust";s:4:"Mode";s:2:"rw";s:11:"Description";s:123:"Must contain config.toml (see the MCSM repo, unraid/infrarust/config.toml). Infrarust creates plugins/ here on first start.";s:4:"Type";s:4:"Path";s:7:"Display";s:6:"always";s:8:"Required";s:4:"true";s:4:"Mask";s:5:"false";}s:5:"value";s:27:"/mnt/user/appdata/infrarust";}i:2;a:2:{s:11:"@attributes";a:9:{s:4:"Name";s:14:"Servers folder";s:6:"Target";s:19:"/app/config/servers";s:7:"Default";s:35:"/mnt/user/appdata/infrarust/servers";s:4:"Mode";s:2:"rw";s:11:"Description";s:166:"Infrarust refuses to start without this folder, even though MCSM servers are discovered through Docker labels. Mapping it makes Unraid create it. Usually stays empty.";s:4:"Type";s:4:"Path";s:7:"Display";s:8:"advanced";s:8:"Required";s:4:"true";s:4:"Mask";s:5:"false";}s:5:"value";s:35:"/mnt/user/appdata/infrarust/servers";}i:3;a:2:{s:11:"@attributes";a:9:{s:4:"Name";s:13:"Docker socket";s:6:"Target";s:20:"/var/run/docker.sock";s:7:"Default";s:20:"/var/run/docker.sock";s:4:"Mode";s:2:"ro";s:11:"Description";s:125:"Infrarust watches container events to discover MCSM servers. Mounting it read-only does not limit what the Docker API allows.";s:4:"Type";s:4:"Path";s:7:"Display";s:8:"advanced";s:8:"Required";s:4:"true";s:4:"Mask";s:5:"false";}s:5:"value";s:20:"/var/run/docker.sock";}}s:12:"TemplatePath";s:40:"/tmp/GitHub/AppFeed/unraid/infrarust.xml";s:4:"Repo";s:20:"Niki2k1's Repository";s:12:"CategoryList";a:2:{i:0;s:11:"GameServers";i:1;s:13:"Network-Proxy";}s:9:"CAComment";s:124:"This template is set up to use a custom network. You may have to adjust the network or IP address etc to match your system  ";s:9:"downloads";i:9788;s:9:"FirstSeen";i:1790813612;s:10:"LastUpdate";i:1772898243;s:14:"LastUpdateScan";i:1790813612;s:8:"Category";s:26:"GameServers: Network:Proxy";s:2:"ID";i:946;s:11:"Displayable";b:1;s:6:"Author";s:9:"shadowner";s:13:"DockerHubName";s:9:"infrarust";s:8:"RepoName";s:20:"Niki2k1's Repository";s:10:"SortAuthor";s:9:"shadowner";s:8:"SortName";s:9:"infrarust";s:6:"random";i:574756638;s:9:"Blacklist";b:0;s:6:"MinVer";s:3:"6.0";s:4:"Path";s:112:"/tmp/community.applications/tempFiles/templates-community-apps/Niki2k1sRepository/shadowner-infrarust-latest.xml";s:4:"Date";N;s:11:"BrandNewApp";b:1;s:10:"Deprecated";b:0;s:10:"Compatible";b:1;s:16:"ModeratorComment";N;}i:947;a:37:{s:4:"Name";s:4:"mcsm";s:10:"Repository";s:27:"ghcr.io/niki2k1/mcsm:latest";s:8:"Registry";s:51:"https://github.com/Niki2k1/mcsm/pkgs/container/mcsm";s:7:"Network";s:9:"infrarust";s:5:"Shell";s:2:"sh";s:10:"Privileged";s:5:"false";s:7:"Support";s:38:"https://github.com/Niki2k1/mcsm/issues";s:7:"Project";s:31:"https://github.com/Niki2k1/mcsm";s:8:"Overview";s:1125:"Minecraft Server Manager: a web dashboard that provisions and manages Minecraft servers (Vanilla, Paper, Fabric, Forge, FTB and CurseForge modpacks) as Docker containers on your Unraid box. Guided create wizard, live console, player management, mod/plugin browser with Modrinth updates, backups, world pre-generation, BlueMap and per-server analytics.

Before installing: create the shared network once with `docker network create infrarust` and enable "Preserve user defined networks" under Settings > Docker, otherwise Unraid removes it on the next Docker restart. Then set NUXT_SESSION_PASSWORD (any string of 32+ characters) and check the server data root (worlds and backups are stored there, not in the Docker vDisk), open the WebUI and run the first-launch wizard. Install the companion "infrarust" template to route several servers by domain on port 25565; without it, publish a host port per server in the create wizard.

Turn on Autostart for mcsm (and infrarust) in the Docker tab. Unraid stops containers with docker stop, so the restart policy alone does not bring them back after a reboot or Docker restart.";s:5:"WebUI";s:23:"http://[IP]:[PORT:3000]";s:11:"TemplateURL";s:67:"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/Niki2k1/mcsm/main/unraid/mcsm.xml";s:4:"Icon";s:70:"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/Niki2k1/mcsm/main/public/favicon.png";s:11:"ExtraParams";s:24:"--restart unless-stopped";s:8:"Requires";s:92:"A user-defined Docker network named &quot;infrarust&quot; (docker network create infrarust).";s:6:"Config";a:15:{i:0;a:2:{s:11:"@attributes";a:9:{s:4:"Name";s:10:"WebUI port";s:6:"Target";s:4:"3000";s:7:"Default";s:4:"3000";s:4:"Mode";s:3:"tcp";s:11:"Description";s:23:"Dashboard and API port.";s:4:"Type";s:4:"Port";s:7:"Display";s:6:"always";s:8:"Required";s:4:"true";s:4:"Mask";s:5:"false";}s:5:"value";s:4:"3000";}i:1;a:2:{s:11:"@attributes";a:9:{s:4:"Name";s:8:"App data";s:6:"Target";s:10:"/app/.data";s:7:"Default";s:22:"/mnt/user/appdata/mcsm";s:4:"Mode";s:2:"rw";s:11:"Description";s:45:"SQLite database, uploaded icons and settings.";s:4:"Type";s:4:"Path";s:7:"Display";s:6:"always";s:8:"Required";s:4:"true";s:4:"Mask";s:5:"false";}s:5:"value";s:22:"/mnt/user/appdata/mcsm";}i:2;a:2:{s:11:"@attributes";a:9:{s:4:"Name";s:16:"Server data root";s:6:"Target";s:21:"NUXT_DOCKER_DATA_ROOT";s:7:"Default";s:27:"/mnt/user/appdata/mcsm-data";s:4:"Mode";s:0:"";s:11:"Description";s:287:"Host folder where worlds (servers/NAME) and backups (backups/) are stored. Keeps them out of the Docker vDisk, which worlds would quickly fill, and makes them visible to appdata backups. Leave empty to use Docker named volumes. Changing it later does not move existing worlds or backups.";s:4:"Type";s:8:"Variable";s:7:"Display";s:6:"always";s:8:"Required";s:5:"false";s:4:"Mask";s:5:"false";}s:5:"value";s:27:"/mnt/user/appdata/mcsm-data";}i:3;a:2:{s:11:"@attributes";a:9:{s:4:"Name";s:13:"Docker socket";s:6:"Target";s: