rk-autofix/issues";s:7:"Project";s:56:"https://github.com/prophetse7en/containernetwork-autofix";s:8:"Overview";s:1168:"ContainerNetwork AutoFix (CNAF) - Automatically recreates Docker containers that depend on a master container's network when the master container restarts. Perfect for containers routing through VPN containers like GluetunVPN.

This is the ProphetSe7en fork of buxxdev/containernetwork-autofix with the Unraid template parser rewritten using xmlstarlet. The rewrite fixes three bugs in the upstream sed-based parser:
- Healthchecks broken after rebuild (XML entities not decoded)
- WebUI right-click broken in Unraid GUI (missing net.Unraid.docker.* labels)
- Hardware passthrough lost on rebuild (no Device case in parser)

The fork is a drop-in replacement: same env vars, same mounts, same behavior - only the Repository line needs to change.

When a master container (e.g., VPN) restarts and gets a new container ID, dependent containers using --net=container: lose network connectivity. CNAF automatically detects and recreates those dependent containers.

Features:
- Auto-detects dependent containers
- Preserves container states (running/stopped)
- Smart waiting for VPN establishment
- Automatic log rotation
- Zero manual configuration needed";s:4:"Date";s:10:"2026-06-06";s:11:"TemplateURL";s:97:"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/ProphetSe7en/unraid-templates/main/containernetwork-autofix.xml";s:4:"Icon";s:85:"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/prophetse7en/containernetwork-autofix/main/icon.png";s:11:"ExtraParams";s:132:"--restart=unless-stopped -v /var/run/docker.sock:/var/run/docker.sock -v /boot/config/plugins/dockerMan/templates-user:/templates:ro";s:6:"Config";a:7:{i:0;a:2:{s:11:"@attributes";a:9:{s:4:"Name";s:7:"AppData";s:6:"Target";s:8:"/var/log";s:7:"Default";s:42:"/mnt/user/appdata/containernetwork-autofix";s:4:"Mode";s:2:"rw";s:11:"Description";s:37:"Optional: Persistent storage for logs";s:4:"Type";s:4:"Path";s:7:"Display";s:6:"always";s:8:"Required";s:5:"false";s:4:"Mask";s:5:"false";}s:5:"value";s:42:"/mnt/user/appdata/containernetwork-autofix";}i:1;a:2:{s:11:"@attributes";a:9:{s:4:"Name";s:21:"Master Container Name";s:6:"Target";s:16:"MASTER_CONTAINER";s:7:"Default";s:94:"vpn-gateway|GluetunVPN|OpenVPN-Client|WireGuard|NordVPN|binhex-delugevpn|binhex-qbittorrentvpn";s:4:"Mode";s:0:"";s:11:"Description";s:129:"Select your VPN/master container from the dropdown. For custom container names, click EDIT and enter the name in the Value field.";s:4:"Type";s:8:"Variable";s:7:"Display";s:6:"always";s:8:"Required";s:4:"true";s:4:"Mask";s:5:"false";}s:5:"value";s:11:"vpn-gateway";}i:2;a:2:{s:11:"@attributes";a:9:{s:4:"Name";s:17:"Restart Wait Time";s:6:"Target";s:17:"RESTART_WAIT_TIME";s:7:"Default";s:2:"15";s:4:"Mode";s:0:"";s:11:"Description";s:102:"Seconds to wait after master container restarts before recreating dependents (allows VPN to establish)";s:4:"Type";s:8:"Variable";s:7:"Display";s:6:"always";s:8:"Required";s:5:"false";s:4:"Mask";s:5:"false";}s:5:"value";s:2:"15";}i:3;a:2:{s:11:"@attributes";a:9:{s:4:"Name";s:13:"Max Log Lines";s:6:"Target";s:13:"MAX_LOG_LINES";s:7:"Default";s:4:"1000";s:4:"Mode";s:0:"";s:11:"Description";s:56:"Maximum number of log lin