 your phone with any CalDAV client. It does what you want — and just that.";s:5:"WebUI";s:22:"http://[IP]:[PORT:80]/";s:11:"TemplateURL";s:98:"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/Richy1989/unraid-templates/main/calendarit/calendarit.unraid.xml";s:4:"Icon";s:86:"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/Richy1989/calendarIT/refs/heads/main/public/logo.png";s:10:"Screenshot";a:3:{i:0;s:102:"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/Richy1989/calendarIT/refs/heads/main/docs/ScreenShot_List_Search.png";i:1;s:96:"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/Richy1989/calendarIT/refs/heads/main/docs/ScreenShot_Month.png";i:2;s:95:"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/Richy1989/calendarIT/refs/heads/main/docs/ScreenShot_Week.png";}s:10:"Networking";a:1:{s:4:"Mode";s:6:"bridge";}s:6:"Config";a:14:{i:0;a:2:{s:11:"@attributes";a:9:{s:4:"Name";s:10:"WebUI Port";s:6:"Target";s:2:"80";s:7:"Default";s:4:"8080";s:4:"Mode";s:3:"tcp";s:11:"Description";s:78:"Host port for the CalendarIT web UI. Browse to http://[Unraid-IP]:[this port].";s:4:"Type";s:4:"Port";s:7:"Display";s:6:"always";s:8:"Required";s:4:"true";s:4:"Mask";s:5:"false";}s:5:"value";s:4:"8080";}i:1;a:2:{s:11:"@attributes";a:9:{s:4:"Name";s:8:"App Data";s:6:"Target";s:5:"/data";s:7:"Default";s:28:"/mnt/user/appdata/calendarit";s:4:"Mode";s:2:"rw";s:11:"Description";s:179:"Host folder where CalendarIT stores its SQLite database, uploaded avatars, and the auto-generated JWT signing key. Point this at your appdata share to persist data across updates.";s:4:"Type";s:4:"Path";s:7:"Display";s:6:"always";s:8:"Required";s:4:"true";s:4:"Mask";s:5:"false";}s:5:"value";s:28:"/mnt/user/appdata/calendarit";}i:2;a:2:{s:11:"@attributes";a:8:{s:4:"Name";s:15:"JWT Signing Key";s:6:"Target";s:15:"JWT_SIGNING_KEY";s:7:"Default";s:0:"";s:11:"Description";s:250:"Optional. Secret (at least 32 characters) used to sign login tokens. LEAVE EMPTY to auto-generate one and persist it under /data (recommended). Set your own only if you need a fixed key across multiple instances; changing it later signs everyone out.";s:4:"Type";s:8:"Variable";s:7:"Display";s:8:"advanced";s:8:"Required";s:5:"false";s:4:"Mask";s:4:"true";}s:5:"value";s:0:"";}i:3;a:2:{s:11:"@attributes";a:8:{s:4:"Name";s:11:"Environment";s:6:"Target";s:22:"ASPNETCORE_ENVIRONMENT";s:7:"Default";s:10:"Production";s:11:"Description";s:113:"Optional. Production (default) or Development. Development also exposes the OpenAPI document at /openapi/v1.json.";s:4:"Type";s:8:"Variable";s:7:"Display";s:8:"advanced";s:8:"Required";s:5:"false";s:4:"Mask";s:5:"false";}s:5:"value";s:10:"Production";}i:4;a:2:{s:11:"@attributes";a:8:{s:4:"Name";s:17:"Database Provider";s:6:"Target";s:17:"DATABASE_PROVIDER";s:7:"Default";s:6:"Sqlite";s:11:"Description";s:152:"Optional. Sqlite (built-in, default — recommended for most self-hosters) or Postgres. If set to Postgres, also fill in the Postgres Connection string.";s:4:"Type";s:8:"Variable";s:7:"Display";s:8:"advanced";s:8:"Required";s:5:"false";s:4:"Mask";s:5:"false";}s:5:"value";s:6:"Sqlite";}i:5;a:2:{s:11:"@attributes";a:8:{s:4:"Name";s:19:"Postgres Connection";s:6:"Target";s:19:"POSTGRES_CONNECTION";s:7:"Default";s:0:"";s:11:"Description";s:227:"Optional. Full Npgsql connection string, required only when Database Provider is Postgres. Example: Host=192.168.1.10;Port=5432;Database=calendarit;Username=calendarit;Password=secret. Ignored while Database Provider is Sqlite.";s:4:"Type";s:8:"Variable";s:7:"Display";s:8:"advanced";s:8:"Required";s:5:"false";s:4:"Mask";s:4:"true";}s:5:"value";s:0:"";}i:6;a:2:{s:11:"@attributes";a:8:{s:4:"Name";s:20:"Disable Registration";s:6:"Target";s:20:"DISABLE_REGISTRATION";s:7:"Default";s:5:"false";s:11:"Description";s:320:"Optional. Set to true once everyone who needs an account has one. Your server is reachable by anyone who knows its address — that is what makes phone sync work — so leaving sign-up open means strangers can create accounts on it. Existing accounts keep working and the Register tab disappears from the sign-in screen.";s:4:"Type";s:8:"Variable";s:7:"Display";s:6:"always";s:8:"Required";s:5:"false";s:4:"Mask";s:5:"false";}s:5:"value";s:5:"false";}i:7;a:2:{s:11:"@attributes";a:8:{s:4:"Name";s:15:"Public Base URL";s:6:"Target";s:15:"PUBLIC_BASE_URL";s:7:"Default";s:0:"";s:11:"Description";s:430:"Optional — required only for self-service password reset: the address users actually type, e.g. https://calendar.example.com. Reset links are built from this and never from the request, because the address in a request is a header anyone can set — otherwise a stranger could have a working reset link mailed to a site of their choosing. Leave empty and reset emails are simply not sent; sign-in and everything else still work.";s:4:"Type";s:8:"Variable";s:7:"Display";s:6:"always";s:8:"Required";s:5:"false";s:4:"Mask";s:5:"false";}s:5:"value";s:0:"";}i:8;a:2:{s:11:"@attributes";a:8:{s:4:"Name";s:18:"Trusted Proxy Hops";s:6:"Target";s:20:"FORWARDED_PROXY_HOPS";s:7:"Default";s:1:"1";s:11:"Description";s:373:"Optional. How many proxies sit in front of the app, used to work out each visitor's real IP address (which the login rate limit and the logs rely on). Leave at 1 when you browse straight to this container's port. Set it to 2 if you put your own reverse proxy in front of it — counting too few makes every visitor look like one address, too many lets visitors fake theirs.";s:4:"Type";s:8:"Variable";s:7:"Display";s:8:"advanced";s:8:"Required";s:5:"false";s:4:"Mask";s:5:"false";}s:5:"value";s:1:"1";}i:9;a:2:{s:11:"@attributes";a:8:{s:4:"Name";s:15:"Auth Rate Limit";s:6:"Target";s:26:"AUTH_RATE_LIMIT_PER_MINUTE";s:7:"Default";s:2:"20";s:11:"Description";s:231:"Optional. How many sign-in, registration, and token-refresh requests one IP address may make per minute before being turned away. The default suits a household; raise it only if legitimate users share one address and hit the limit.";s:4:"Type";s:8:"Variable";s:7:"Display";s:8:"advanced";s:8:"Required";s:5:"false";s:4:"Mask";s:5:"false";}s:5:"value";s:2:"20";}i:10;a:2:{s:11:"@attributes";a:8:{s:4:"Name";s:9:"Log Level";s:6:"Target";s:30:"Serilog__MinimumLevel__Default";s:7:"Default";s:11:"Information";s:11:"Description";s:122:"Optional. Minimum log level written to the container log: Verbose, Debug, Information (default), Warning, Error, or Fatal.";s:4:"Type";s:8:"Variable";s:7:"Display";s:8:"advanced";s:8:"Required";s:5:"false";s:4:"Mask";s:5:"false";}s:5:"value";s:11:"Information";}i:11;a:2:{s:11:"@attributes";a:8:{s:4:"Name";s:16:"VAPID Public Key";s:6:"Target";s:16:"VAPID_PUBLIC_KEY";s:7:"Default";s:0:"";s:11:"Description";s:329:"Optional. Public half of the VAPID key pair that signs browser (Web Push) reminder notifications. LEAVE EMPTY to auto-generate a pair on first run and persist it under /data (recommended) — browser notifications then work with no setup. Set your own (both keys) only to keep the same keys across multiple instances or rebuilds.";s:4:"Type";s:8:"Variable";s:7:"Display";s:8:"advanced";s:8:"Required";s:5:"false";s:4:"Mask";s:5:"false";}s:5:"value";s:0:"";}i:12;a:2:{s:11:"@attributes";a:8:{s:4:"Name";s:17:"VAPID Private Key";s:6:"Target";s:17:"VAPID_PRIVATE_KEY";s:7:"Default";s:0:"";s:11:"Description";s:169:"Optional. Private half of the VAPID key pair (keep secret). Leave empty to auto-generate it alongside the public key. Only set this if you also set the VAPID Public Key.";s:4:"Type";s:8:"Variable";s:7:"Display";s:8:"advanced";s:8:"Required";s:5:"false";s:4:"Mask";s:4:"true";}s:5:"value";s:0:"";}i:13;a:2:{s:11:"@attributes";a:8:{s:4:"Name";s:13:"VAPID Subject";s:6:"Target";s:13:"VAPID_SUBJECT";s:7:"Default";s:0:"";s:11:"Description";s:190:"Optional. Contact URI sent to push services with each notification, e.g. mailto:admin@example.com. Leave empty to use the built-in default. Only relevant when browser notifications are used.";s:4:"Type";s:8:"Variable";s:7:"Display";s:8:"advanced";s:8:"Required";s:5:"false";s:4:"Mask";s:5:"false";}s:5:"value";s:0:"";}}s:12:"TemplatePath";s:52:"/tmp/GitHub/AppFeed/calendarit/calendarit.unraid.xml";s:4:"Repo";s:22:"Richy1989's Repository";s:12:"CategoryList";a:1:{i:0;s:12:"Productivity";}s:9:"downloads";i:2748;s:9:"FirstSeen";i:1785743710;s:10:"LastUpdate";i:1785875989;s:14:"LastUpdateScan";i:1790969388;s:8:"Category";s:13:"Productivity:";s:2:"ID";i:1110;s:11:"Displayable";b:1;s:6:"Author";s:9:"richy1989";s:13:"DockerHubName";s:10:"calendarit";s:8:"RepoName";s:22:"Richy1989's Repository";s:10:"SortAuthor";s:9:"richy1989";s:8:"SortName";s:10:"CalendarIT";s:6:"random";i:644907527;s:9:"Blacklist";b:0;s:6:"MinVer";s:3:"6.0";s:4:"Path";s:115:"/tmp/community.applications/tempFiles/templates-community-apps/Richy1989sRepository/richy1989-CalendarIT-latest.xml";s:4:"Date";N;s:11:"BrandNewApp";b:1;s:10:"Deprecated";b:0;s:10:"Compatible";b:1;s:16:"ModeratorComment";N;}i:1111;a:39:{s:4:"Name";s:6:"keepIT";s:10:"Repository";s:23:"richy1989/keepit:latest";s:8:"Registry";s:41:"https://hub.docker.com/r/richy1989/keepit";s:7:"Network";s:6:"bridge";s:5:"Shell";s:4:"bash";s:10:"Privileged";s:5:"false";s:7:"Support";s:42:"https://github.com/Richy1989/keepIT/issues";s:7:"Project";s:35:"https://github.com/Richy1989/keepIT";s:8:"Overview";s:163:"A self-hosted notes app with sharing between users, real-time sync, search, and reminders - plus a native Android app with offline support and a home-screen widget";s:5:"WebUI";s:22:"http://[IP]:[PORT:80]/";s:11:"TemplateURL";s:92:"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/Richy1989/unraid-templates/main/keepit/keepit-template.xml";s:4:"Icon";s:69:"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/richy1989/keepIT/main/docs/logo.png";s:10:"Screenshot";a:2:{i:0;s:90:"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/Richy1989/keepIT/refs/heads/main/images/screenshot_1.png";i:1;s:94:"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/Richy1989/keepIT/refs/heads/main/images/screenshot_phone.png";}s:10:"Networking";a:1:{s:4:"Mode";s:6:"bridge";}s:6:"Config";a:19:{i:0;a:2:{s:11:"@attributes";a:9:{s:4:"Name";s:10:"WebUI Port";s:6:"Target";s:2:"80";s:7:"Default";s:4:"8080";s:4:"Mode";s:3:"tcp";s:11:"Description";s:74:"Host port for the keepIT web UI. Browse to http://[Unraid-IP]:[this port].";s:4:"Type";s:4:"Port";s:7:"Display";s:6:"always";s:8:"Required";s:4:"true";s:4:"Mask";s:5:"false";}s:5:"value";s:4:"8080";}i:1;a:2:{s:11:"@attributes";a:9:{s:4:"Name";s:8:"App Data";s:6:"Target";s:5:"/data";s:7:"Default";s:24:"/mnt/user/appdata/keepit";s:4:"Mode";s:2:"rw";s:11:"Description";s:154:"Host folder where keepIT stores its SQLite database, encryption keys and uploaded images. Point this at your appdata share to persist data across updates.";s:4:"Type";s:4:"Path";s:7:"Display";s:6:"always";s:8:"Required";s:4:"true";s:4:"Mask";s:5:"false";}s:5:"value";s:24:"/mnt/user/appdata/keepit";}i:2;a:2:{s:11:"@attributes";a:8:{s:4:"Name";s:7:"JWT Key";s:6:"Target";s:8:"Jwt__Key";s:7:"Default";s:0:"";s:11:"Description";s:146:"REQUIRED. A random secret of at least 32 characters used to sign login tokens. Change this before first use; changing it later signs everyone out.";s:4:"Type";s:8:"Variable";s:7:"Display";s:6:"always";s:8:"Required";s:4:"true";s:4:"Mask";s:4:"true";}s:5:"value";s:54:"change-me-to-a-random-secret-of-at-least-32-characters";}i:3;a:2:{s:11:"@attributes";a:8:{s:4:"Name";s:11:"Environment";s:6:"Target";s:22:"ASPNETCORE_ENVIRONMENT";s:7:"Default";s:10:"Production";s:11:"Description";s:100:"Production (default) or Development. Development also enables the Scalar API explorer at /scalar/v1.";s:4:"Type";s:8:"Variable";s:7:"Display";s:8:"advanced";s:8:"Required";s:5:"false";s:4:"Mask";s:5:"false";}s:5:"value";s:10:"Production";}i:4;a:2:{s:11:"@attributes";a:8:{s:4:"Name";s:21:"Refresh Cookie Secure";s:6:"Target";s:27:"Auth__RefreshCookie__Secure";s:7:"Default";s:5:"false";s:11:"Description";s:129:"Keep false when accessing over plain http. Set true only when keepIT is served over https (e.g. behind a reverse proxy with TLS).";s:4:"Type";s:8:"Variable";s:7:"Display";s:8:"advanced";s:8:"Required";s:5:"false";s:4:"Mask";s:5:"false";}s:5:"value";s:5:"false";}i:5;a:2:{s:11:"@attributes";a:8:{s:4:"Name";s:10:"Proxy Hops";s:6:"Target";s:23:"App__ForwardedProxyHops";s:7:"Default";s:1:"1";s:11:"Description";s:350:"Number of reverse-proxy hops in front of the API. This image already contains one nginx hop, so: 1 = you reach keepIT directly (browser → this container); 2 = another reverse proxy such as Traefik sits in front (Traefik → nginx → api). Must be exact: too low and all clients share one rate-limit bucket; too high and clients can spoof their IP.";s:4:"Type";s:8:"Variable";s:7:"Display";s:8:"advanced";s:8:"Required";s:5:"false";s:4:"Mask";s:5:"false";}s:5:"value";s:1:"1";}i:6;a:2:{s:11:"@attributes";a:8:{s:4:"Name";s:18:"Allow Registration";s:6:"Target";s:22:"App__AllowRegistration";s:7:"Default";s:4:"true";s:11:"Description";s:196:"Whether new accounts may be created. If keepIT is reachable from the internet, register your own accounts first and then set this to false so strangers cannot sign up. Existing users keep working.";s:4:"Type";s:8:"Variable";s:7:"Display";s:8:"advanced";s:8:"Required";s:5:"false";s:4:"Mask";s:5:"false";}s:5:"value";s:4:"true";}i:7;a:2:{s:11:"@attributes";a:8:{s:4:"Name";s:15:"Public Base URL";s:6:"Target";s:18:"App__PublicBaseUrl";s:7:"Default";s:0:"";s:11:"Description";s:213:"Optional. Public address of your instance (e.g. https://notes.example.com), used to build password-reset links in emails. Usually auto-detected from the request; set it only if reset links point to the wrong host.";s:4:"Type";s:8:"Variable";s:7:"Display";s:8:"advanced";s:8:"Required";s:5:"false";s:4:"Mask";s:5:"false";}s:5:"value";s:0:"";}i:8;a:2:{s:11:"@attributes";a:8:{s:4:"Name";s:9:"SMTP Host";s:6:"Target";s:15:"Email__SmtpHost";s:7:"Default";s:0:"";s:11:"Description";s:230:"Optional. SMTP server for outgoing email (password-reset links). LEAVE EMPTY to run without email — reset links then land in the container log instead. Setting this is the switch that enables email delivery (then also set From).";s:4:"Type";s:8:"Variable";s:7:"Display";s:8:"advanced";s:8:"Required";s:5:"false";s:4:"Mask";s:5:"false";}s:5:"value";s:0:"";}i:9;a:2:{s:11:"@attributes";a:8:{s:4:"Name";s:9:"SMTP From";s:6:"Target";s:11:"Email__From";s:7:"Default";s:0:"";s:11:"Description";s:132:"From address for outgoing email, e.g. keepIT no-reply@example.com. Required once SMTP Host is set; ignored while SMTP Host is empty.";s:4:"Type";s:8:"Variable";s:7:"Display";s:8:"advanced";s:8:"Required";s:5:"false";s:4:"Mask";s:5:"false";}s:5:"value";s:0:"";}i:10;a:2:{s:11:"@attributes";a:8:{s:4:"Name";s:13:"SMTP Username";s:6:"Target";s:19:"Email__SmtpUsername";s:7:"Default";s:0:"";s:11:"Description";s:126:"Optional SMTP login username. Leave empty (with SMTP Password) for an unauthenticated relay. Ignored while SMTP Host is empty.";s:4:"Type";s:8:"Variable";s:7:"Display";s:8:"advanced";s:8:"Required";s:5:"false";s:4:"Mask";s:5:"false";}s:5:"value";s:0:"";}i:11;a:2:{s:11:"@attributes";a:8:{s:4:"Name";s:13:"SMTP Password";s:6:"Target";s:19:"Email__SmtpPassword";s:7:"Default";s:0:"";s:11:"Description";s:90:"Optional SMTP login password, paired with SMTP Username. Ignored while SMTP Host is empty.";s:4:"Type";s:8:"Variable";s:7:"Display";s:8:"advanced";s:8:"Required";s:5:"false";s:4:"Mask";s:4:"true";}s:5:"value";s:0:"";}i:12;a:2:{s:11:"@attributes";a:8:{s:4:"Name";s:9:"SMTP Port";s:6:"Target";s:15:"Email__SmtpPort";s:7:"Default";s:3:"587";s:11:"Description";s:140:"SMTP port — 587 for STARTTLS submission (default), 465 for implicit TLS (set Use STARTTLS to false too). Ignored while SMTP Host is empty.";s:4:"Type";s:8:"Variable";s:7:"Display";s:8:"advanced";s:8:"Required";s:5:"false";s:4:"Mask";s:5:"false";}s:5:"value";s:3:"587";}i:13;a:2:{s:11:"@attributes";a:8:{s:4:"Name";s:12:"Use STARTTLS";s:6:"Target";s:18:"Email__UseStartTls";s:7:"Default";s:4:"true";s:11:"Description";s:106:"true = STARTTLS on port 587 (default); false = implicit TLS on port 465. Ignored while