 up to date. With Live TV on, it does the same for the shows and movies in the Plex or Jellyfin guide.[br][br]It starts with Dry Run on: images go to the previews folder in Data and the server is not touched. Set Dry Run to false when you like them.[br][br]For new titles right away, add the webhook http://Unraid-IP:8098/webhook/YOUR-WEBHOOK-SECRET in Plex under Settings, Webhooks. For Jellyfin and Emby, see the README. Without it, new titles get posters within 15 minutes.";s:8:"Requires";s:56:"A free TMDB API key and a Plex, Jellyfin or Emby server.";s:11:"TemplateURL";s:87:"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/SandObserver/Posteryard/main/templates/posteryard.xml";s:4:"Icon";s:87:"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/SandObserver/Posteryard/main/site/public/icon-512.png";s:10:"Screenshot";s:84:"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/SandObserver/Posteryard/main/docs/before-after.jpg";s:16:"ExtraSearchTerms";s:55:"plex jellyfin emby posters artwork tmdb kometa textless";s:6:"Config";a:35:{i:0;a:2:{s:11:"@attributes";a:9:{s:4:"Name";s:12:"Webhook Port";s:6:"Target";s:4:"8000";s:7:"Default";s:4:"8098";s:4:"Mode";s:3:"tcp";s:11:"Description";s:67:"Port for the Plex, Jellyfin or Emby webhook and the /healthz check.";s:4:"Type";s:4:"Port";s:7:"Display";s:6:"always";s:8:"Required";s:4:"true";s:4:"Mask";s:5:"false";}s:5:"value";s:4:"8098";}i:1;a:2:{s:11:"@attributes";a:9:{s:4:"Name";s:4:"Data";s:6:"Target";s:5:"/data";s:7:"Default";s:28:"/mnt/user/appdata/posteryard";s:4:"Mode";s:2:"rw";s:11:"Description";s:92:"Database, previews and custom art. Keep this, or every image is rendered and uploaded again.";s:4:"Type";s:4:"Path";s:7:"Display";s:6:"always";s:8:"Required";s:4:"true";s:4:"Mask";s:5:"false";}s:5:"value";s:28:"/mnt/user/appdata/posteryard";}i:2;a:2:{s:11:"@attributes";a:9:{s:4:"Name";s:12:"TMDB API Key";s:6:"Target";s:12:"TMDB_API_KEY";s:7:"Default";s:0:"";s:4:"Mode";s:0:"";s:11:"Description";s:79:"A free key from TMDB, under Settings, API. The API Read Access Token works too.";s:4:"Type";s:8:"Variable";s:7:"Display";s:6:"always";s:8:"Required";s:4:"true";s:4:"Mask";s:4:"true";}s:5:"value";s:0:"";}i:3;a:2:{s:11:"@attributes";a:9:{s:4:"Name";s:8:"Plex URL";s:6:"Target";s:8:"PLEX_URL";s:7:"Default";s:0:"";s:4:"Mode";s:0:"";s:11:"Description";s:129:"Your Plex server's address on the network, such as http://192.168.1.10:32400. Not localhost. Leave it empty for Jellyfin or Emby.";s:4:"Type";s:8:"Variable";s:7:"Display";s:6:"always";s:8:"Required";s:5:"false";s:4:"Mask";s:5:"false";}s:5:"value";s:0:"";}i:4;a:2:{s:11:"@attributes";a:9:{s:4:"Name";s:10:"Plex Token";s:6:"Target";s:10:"PLEX_TOKEN";s:7:"Default";s:0:"";s:4:"Mode";s:0:"";s:11:"Description";s:53:"Your Plex token. Leave it empty for Jellyfin or Emby.";s:4:"Type";s:8:"Variable";s:7:"Display";s:6:"always";s:8:"Required";s:5:"false";s:4:"Mask";s:4:"true";}s:5:"value";s:0:"";}i:5;a:2:{s:11:"@attributes";a:9:{s:4:"Name";s:14:"Webhook Secret";s:6:"Target";s:14:"WEBHOOK_SECRET";s:7:"Default";s:0:"";s:4:"Mode";s:0:"";s:11:"Description";s:100:"Any long random text, such as the output of openssl rand -hex 16. It is part of the webhook address.";s:4:"Type";s:8:"Variable";s:7:"Display";s:6:"always";s:8:"Required";s:4:"true";s:4:"Mask";s:4:"true";}s:5:"value";s:0:"";}i:6;a:2:{s:11:"@attributes";a:9:{s:4:"Name";s:7:"Dry Run";s:6:"Target";s:7:"DRY_RUN";s:7:"Default";s:4:"true";s:4:"Mode";s:0:"";s:11:"Description";s:96:"true saves previews and changes nothing on your server. false uploads the images and locks them.";s:4:"Type";s:8:"Variable";s:7:"Display";s:6:"always";s:8:"Required";s:4:"true";s:4:"Mask";s:5:"false";}s:5:"value";s:4:"true";}i:7;a:2:{s:11:"@attributes";a:9:{s:4:"Name";s:9:"Libraries";s:6:"Target";s:9:"LIBRARIES";s:7:"Default";s:15:"Movies,TV Shows";s:4:"Mode";s:0:"";s:11:"Description";s:129:"Libraries to manage, separated by commas, named as your server shows them. Movie and TV libraries only. PLEX_LIBRARIES works too.";s:4:"Type";s:8:"Variable";s:7:"Display";s:6:"always";s:8:"Requir