"Date";N;s:11:"BrandNewApp";b:1;s:10:"Deprecated";b:0;s:10:"Compatible";b:1;s:16:"ModeratorComment";N;}i:1138;a:42:{s:4:"Name";s:10:"blockparty";s:10:"Repository";s:39:"ghcr.io/scottschneck/block-party:latest";s:8:"Registry";s:70:"https://github.com/ScottSchneck/block-party/pkgs/container/block-party";s:7:"Network";s:3:"br0";s:5:"Shell";s:4:"bash";s:10:"Privileged";s:5:"false";s:7:"Support";s:114:"https://forums.unraid.net/topic/200896-support-block-party-minecraft-bedrock-java-hytale-and-console-server-panel/";s:7:"Project";s:43:"https://github.com/ScottSchneck/block-party";s:6:"ReadMe";s:50:"https://github.com/ScottSchneck/block-party#readme";s:8:"Overview";s:1226:"Block Party runs your family's game servers at home: Minecraft Bedrock, Minecraft Java (Paper) and Hytale, from one web panel that works on a desktop or a phone.

Xbox, PlayStation and Switch players can join without any extra apps: the panel has its own console server list and a small DNS server, so consoles see your servers in a menu.

- Add, start, stop, update and restart servers, with a live console
- Players page: who's online, the allowlist, operators, and an Allow button for anyone who tried to join
- Settings as plain labelled controls, worlds and add-ons, Java plugins
- Scheduled backups with one-click restore, without kicking anyone off
- Accounts for the kids, with what each one can do on each server
- Friends outside the house, overnight updates, notifications to your phone, Discord or email
- Two-factor sign-in, and import from Crafty Controller

IMPORTANT: give the container its own IP on your home network (Network Type br0, with a Fixed IP address). Consoles look for DNS on port 53 and the server list on port 19132, and every game server needs its own ports, so it can't share Unraid's IP.

