:"Compatible";b:1;s:16:"ModeratorComment";N;}i:1311;a:41:{s:4:"Name";s:9:"NoteTrace";s:10:"Repository";s:34:"ghcr.io/traceapps/notetrace:latest";s:8:"Registry";s:70:"https://github.com/orgs/TraceApps/packages/container/package/notetrace";s:7:"Network";s:6:"bridge";s:5:"Shell";s:2:"sh";s:10:"Privileged";s:5:"false";s:7:"Support";s:50:"https://github.com/TraceApps/notetrace/discussions";s:7:"Project";s:38:"https://github.com/TraceApps/notetrace";s:8:"Overview";s:1054:"NoteTrace is a self-hosted notes app: quick to capture, easy to find, and it works offline. Notes, checklists and reminders sit in a card grid with labels and colors, with a Markdown editor, [[note links]], voice notes, drawings, file attachments, full-text search, version history and sharing with other accounts on your server. Import from Google Keep (Takeout, images included), Evernote (.enex), Memos, Blinko and Markdown exports such as Obsidian or Joplin, and export everything as Markdown at any time. The installed web app and the native Android app keep working with no connection. Multi-user with OIDC single sign-on and scheduled backups. No telemetry and no accounts on external services; your data stays in your appdata folder.

