ompatible";b:1;s:16:"ModeratorComment";N;}i:1312;a:41:{s:4:"Name";s:10:"NutriTrace";s:10:"Repository";s:35:"ghcr.io/traceapps/nutritrace:latest";s:8:"Registry";s:71:"https://github.com/orgs/TraceApps/packages/container/package/nutritrace";s:7:"Network";s:6:"bridge";s:5:"Shell";s:2:"sh";s:10:"Privileged";s:5:"false";s:7:"Support";s:51:"https://github.com/TraceApps/nutritrace/discussions";s:7:"Project";s:39:"https://github.com/TraceApps/nutritrace";s:8:"Overview";s:1018:"NutriTrace is a self-hosted personal nutrition tracker. Log what you eat in a daily diary with your own meal slots, keep a personal database of foods, meals and recipes, look up products by barcode or name from Open Food Facts and USDA, and set calorie and macro goals with fixed, dynamic or adaptive TDEE modes. It also tracks activity and intermittent fasting, connects to Fitbit (through Google Health), Withings, Garmin and Health Connect, and imports from MyFitnessPal, Lose It, Cronometer and Waistline. Multi-user with OIDC single sign-on, a browser app that keeps working offline, and a native Android app. No telemetry and no accounts on external services; your data stays in your appdata folder.

