583;s:9:"Blacklist";b:0;s:6:"MinVer";s:3:"6.0";s:4:"Path";s:103:"/tmp/community.applications/tempFiles/templates-community-apps/am385sRepository/am385-Lineup-latest.xml";s:10:"Deprecated";b:0;s:10:"Compatible";b:1;s:16:"ModeratorComment";N;}i:1448;a:39:{s:4:"Name";s:13:"Crowbarr-CUDA";s:10:"Repository";s:39:"ghcr.io/amanofvaly/crowbarr:latest-cuda";s:8:"Registry";s:62:"https://github.com/amanofvaly/crowbarr/pkgs/container/crowbarr";s:7:"Network";s:6:"bridge";s:5:"Shell";s:4:"bash";s:10:"Privileged";s:5:"false";s:7:"Support";s:45:"https://github.com/amanofvaly/crowbarr/issues";s:7:"Project";s:38:"https://github.com/amanofvaly/crowbarr";s:6:"ReadMe";s:63:"https://github.com/amanofvaly/crowbarr/blob/main/docs/unraid.md";s:8:"Overview";s:991:"Audio-grounded subtitle synchronization and transcription for Sonarr, Radarr and Bazarr.

Crowbarr watches your Sonarr and Radarr libraries and keeps subtitles in sync with the dialogue. It waits for Bazarr to find a subtitle, checks its timing against the audio with Whisper, and corrects it only when the audio says it is wrong. When no subtitle turns up, it transcribes one. Results are written as a new .crowbarr.en.srt file next to the video. Existing media and subtitles are never modified.

This template uses an NVIDIA GPU for speech recognition. Install the Nvidia Driver plugin first, then select CUDA under Settings after the first start. Without a GPU, install Crowbarr instead.

