HOW IT WORKS: Health Auto Export (or any client) POSTs JSON to the ingest endpoint (POST /api/ingest) on port 8000, authenticated with the INGEST_SECRET you set (sent as the X-Ingest-Token header). Samples are deduplicated and stored idempotently in a TimescaleDB/PostgreSQL database. A nightly job (ANALYSIS_CRON, default 03:30) runs the statistical pipeline with FDR-controlled correlations, GPS route/geo analysis and workout dashboards; results and optional LLM-generated narration reports are written under /config. Check the service with GET /api/health.

DATABASE (required): HealthLog needs a TimescaleDB/PostgreSQL 16 database (recommended image timescale/timescaledb:2.17.2-pg16). Run it as a companion container named healthlog-db on the same Docker network, then set DATABASE_URL to the psycopg v3 connection string, e.g. postgresql+psycopg://healthlog:PASSWORD@healthlog-db:5432/healthlog.

STORAGE: Map /config to persist the optional config.yaml, the import/ backfill directory, narration/ reports and logs. Set PUID=99 / PGID=100 so the files are owned by nobody:users on Unraid.

OPTIONAL CONFIG FILE: Drop a config.yaml into /config to tune the analysis pipeline, your personal profile (birth year, sex, HR zones), workout load metrics, Ollama narration and push notifications. Changes are picked up automatically without a restart. A Grafana dashboard is included in the project.

