oopback ranges, the usual container-behind-a-proxy-on-a-private-network setup.";s:4:"Type";s:8:"Variable";s:7:"Display";s:8:"advanced";s:8:"Required";s:5:"false";s:4:"Mask";s:5:"false";}s:5:"value";s:0:"";}i:8;a:2:{s:11:"@attributes";a:9:{s:4:"Name";s:13:"ANALYSIS_CRON";s:6:"Target";s:13:"ANALYSIS_CRON";s:7:"Default";s:10:"30 3 * * *";s:4:"Mode";s:0:"";s:11:"Description";s:92:"When the nightly analysis runs (5-field cron expression, evaluated in TZ). Default is 03:30.";s:4:"Type";s:8:"Variable";s:7:"Display";s:8:"advanced";s:8:"Required";s:5:"false";s:4:"Mask";s:5:"false";}s:5:"value";s:10:"30 3 * * *";}i:9;a:2:{s:11:"@attributes";a:9:{s:4:"Name";s:9:"LOG_LEVEL";s:6:"Target";s:9:"LOG_LEVEL";s:7:"Default";s:4:"INFO";s:4:"Mode";s:0:"";s:11:"Description";s:45:"Log verbosity: DEBUG, INFO, WARNING or ERROR.";s:4:"Type";s:8:"Variable";s:7:"Display";s:8:"advanced";s:8:"Required";s:5:"false";s:4:"Mask";s:5:"false";}s:5:"value";s:4:"INFO";}i:10;a:2:{s:11:"@attributes";a:9:{s:4:"Name";s:10:"LOG_FORMAT";s:6:"Target";s:10:"LOG_FORMAT";s:7:"Default";s:4:"text";s:4:"Mode";s:0:"";s:11:"Description";s:32:"Log output format: text or json.";s:4:"Type";s:8:"Variable";s:7:"Display";s:8:"advanced";s:8:"Required";s:5:"false";s:4:"Mask";s:5:"false";}s:5:"value";s:4:"text";}i:11;a:2:{s:11:"@attributes";a:9:{s:4:"Name";s:11:"CONFIG_FILE";s:6:"Target";s:11:"CONFIG_FILE";s:7:"Default";s:19:"/config/config.yaml";s:4:"Mode";s:0:"";s:11:"Description";s:72:"Path to the optional structured configuration file inside the container.";s:4:"Type";s:8:"Variable";s:7:"Display";s:8:"advanced";s:8:"Required";s:5:"false";s:4:"Mask";s:5:"false";}s:5:"value";s:19:"/config/config.yaml";}}s:17:"TailscaleStateDir";s:0:"";s:12:"TemplatePath";s:41:"/tmp/GitHub/AppFeed/anym001/healthlog.xml";s:4:"Repo";s:20:"Anym001's Repository";s:9:"downloads";i:2298;s:9:"FirstSeen";i:1783152268;s:10:"LastUpdate";i:1788970548;s:14:"LastUpdateScan";i:1790969388;s:12:"CategoryList";a:0:{}s:8:"Category";s:6:"Other:";s:2:"ID";i:1499;s:11:"Displayable";b:1;s:6:"Author";s:7:"anym001";s:13:"DockerHubName";s:9:"healthlog";s:8:"RepoName";s:20:"Anym001's Repository";s:10:"SortAuthor";s:7:"anym001";s:8:"SortName";s:9:"healthlog";s:6:"random";i:248472093;s:9:"Blacklist";b:0;s:6:"MinVer";s:3:"6.0";s:4:"Path";s:110:"/tmp/community.applications/tempFiles/templates-community-apps/Anym001sRepository/anym001-healthlog-latest.xml";s:4:"Date";N;s:11:"BrandNewApp";b:1;s:10:"Deprecated";b:0;s:10:"Compatible";b:1;s:16:"ModeratorComment";N;}i:1500;a:38:{s:4:"Name";s:18:"pocketlog-importer";s:10:"Repository";s:41:"ghcr.io/anym001/pocketlog-importer:latest";s:8:"Registry";s:42:"https://ghcr.io/anym001/pocketlog-importer";s:7:"Network";s:6:"bridge";s:5:"Shell";s:2:"sh";s:10:"Privileged";s:5:"false";s:7:"Support";s:75:"https://forums.unraid.net/topic/195410-support-anym001-application-dockers/";s:7:"Project";s:45:"https://github.com/anym001/pocketlog-importer";s:8:"Overview";s:1871:"PocketLog Importer is a companion container for PocketLog (https://github.com/anym001/pocketlog) that turns bank CSV exports into PocketLog transactions automatically. It has no web interface - it runs as a background service.

HOW IT WORKS: Drop a bank CSV into /data/input. An internal scheduler (cron, default hourly) auto-detects the bank format (easybank, dadat), parses and normalises each booking, then matches it against a regex rules whitelist (config/rules.yaml). A booking that matches a rule is enriched (description, category, tags) and imported into PocketLog via its CSV import API. A booking that matches no rule is dropped and written to a *.unmatched.csv for review - only curated bookings reach PocketLog. PocketLog deduplicates server-side, so re-runs are safe.

Processed originals move to /data/processed; files that fail to parse or import move to /data/failed. You can also trigger a run on demand with the User Scripts plugin: docker exec pocketlog-importer pocketlog-import --once (add --dry-run to write output CSVs without importing).

SETUP: In PocketLog create an API key with the "import" scope and provide it via POCKETLOG_API_KEY. On first start the container seeds config/config.yaml and config/rules.yaml from bundled examples (it logs a WARNING) - then edit config/config.yaml to set pocketlog.base_url (or use POCKETLOG_BASE_URL), edit config/rules.yaml to match your bookings, and restart.

STORAGE: Map /config (config.yaml, rules.yaml, optional logs) and /data (input, output, processed, failed). Set PUID=99 / PGID=100 so the files are owned by nobody:users on Unraid.

NOTIFICATIONS (optional): Run-outcome push notifications to any Gotify-compatible endpoint (PushBits, Gotify). Set notify.url in config.yaml and provide the application token via NOTIFY_TOKEN.

