(through OAuth apps you create) and Yahoo, AOL, iCloud or any IMAP mailbox (app
password). Ghost-Hub reads message headers only, never bodies, to find the
services you have signed up for, scores each one for risk using Have I Been
Pwned's public breach list, shows how to delete the accounts you do not need,
helps you unsubscribe from newsletters after you review exactly what will be
sent, and finds public profiles under your own usernames. Nothing happens
without your approval, and your data stays on your server.

Requires a PostgreSQL container (set its address in Database URL). Every mail
provider is optional: Gmail and Outlook need an OAuth app you create once (see
the project docs), Yahoo and IMAP need only an app password. Google and
Microsoft only allow sign-in over HTTPS (or localhost), so put Ghost-Hub behind
a reverse proxy and set App URL to its https address. Full guide: docs/Unraid.md.

