content.com/aon082910/AoN-Unraid-Apps/main/Model-Hub/model-hub.xml";s:6:"ReadMe";s:70:"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/aon082910/model-hub/master/README.md";s:4:"Icon";s:83:"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/aon082910/AoN-Unraid-Apps/main/Model-Hub/icon.png";s:5:"WebUI";s:24:"http://[IP]:[PORT:8420]/";s:8:"Overview";s:1363:"Self-hosted, open 3D print file library manager: STL/3MF/OBJ/STEP/FBX
organization, thumbnails, duplicate detection, tagging, semantic search, smart
collections, filament inventory and a print queue. AI tagging/search can run
against a local Ollama instance (nothing leaves your network) or an external
OpenRouter/OpenAI-compatible API using your own key -- switch anytime from
the in-app Settings tab. Point "Library Path" at the share where your STL/3MF
files already live; nothing is modified on disk, files are only read and hashed.

On first open you'll be asked to create an admin login (or set Admin
Username/Password below to skip that screen). Also includes print time/filament
weight estimates, projects that track the electronics/parts/supplies each
build needs (with an exportable shopping list and a Supplies page for what you
already own) and subtract the filament used when a project is marked printed,
matching of your models (one by one or your whole library) to their Printables/MakerWorld
listings (pictures, designer, license, tags, parts lists), a Search page across sites with a wishlist, a print log, duplicate cleanup, backup and restore, several logins, printer status and G-code upload, a page for every model and project with
PDF export, a browser extension for one-click import, and optional webhook notifications (ntfy/Discord/Slack).";s:16:"ExtraSearchTerms";s:211:"3d printing stl 3mf obj step fbx model library slicer filament print queue project parts bom shopping list supplies inventory makerworld printables sketchfab thingiverse myminifactory cults3d pdf search download";s:8:"Requires";s:161:"Optional: an Ollama container (install the official &quot;ollama&quot; template from<br>Community Applications first) if you want local AI instead of an API key.";s:4:"Date";s:10:"2026-10-12";s:7:"License";s:3:"MIT";s:6:"MinVer";s:3:"6.9";s:6:"Config";a:13:{i:0;a:2:{s:11:"@attributes";a:9:{s:4:"Name";s:10:"WebUI Port";s:6:"Target";s:4:"8420";s:7:"Default";s:4:"8420";s:4:"Mode";s:3:"tcp";s:11:"Description";s:37:"Port for the Model Hub web interface.";s:4:"Type";s:4:"Port";s:7:"Display";s:6:"always";s:8:"Required";s:4:"true";s:4:"Mask";s:5:"false";}s:5:"value";s:4:"8420";}i:1;a:2:{s:11:"@attributes";a:9:{s:4:"Name";s:12:"Library Path";s:6:"Target";s:5:"/data";s:7:"Default";s:34:"/mnt/user/models/model-hub-library";s:4:"Mode";s:2:"rw";s:11:"Description";s:117:"Folder containing your STL/3MF/OBJ/STEP/FBX files. Read-only usage: files are hashed and thumbnailed, never modified.";s:4:"Type";s:4:"Path";s:7:"Display";s:6:"always";s:8:"Required";s:4:"true";s:4:"Mask";s:5:"false";}s:5:"value";s:34:"/mnt/user/models/model-hub-library";}i:2;a:2:{s:11:"@attributes";a:9:{s:4:"Name";s:13:"App Config/DB";s:6:"Target";s:7:"/config";s:7:"Default";s:27:"/mnt/user/appdata/model-hub";s:4:"Mode";s:2:"rw";s:11:"Description";s:63:"Where the SQLite database, thumbnails, and settings are stored.";s:4:"Type";s:4:"Path";s:7:"Display";s:6:"always";s:8:"Required";s:4:"true";s:4:"Mask";s:5:"false";}s:5:"value";s:27:"/mnt/user/appdata/model-hub";}i:3;a:2:{s:11:"@attributes";a:9:{s:4:"Name";s:4:"PUID";s:6:"Target";s:4:"PUID";s:7:"Default";s:2:"99";s:4:"Mode";s:0:"";s:11:"Description";s:60:"Unraid's nobody user -- keeps /config 