lications/tempFiles/templates-community-apps/allornothingsRepository/allornothing-repairhub-latest.xml";s:10:"Deprecated";b:0;s:10:"Compatible";b:1;s:16:"ModeratorComment";N;}i:1512;a:41:{s:4:"Name";s:7:"sop-hub";s:10:"Repository";s:27:"allornothing/sop-hub:latest";s:8:"Registry";s:45:"https://hub.docker.com/r/allornothing/sop-hub";s:7:"Network";s:6:"bridge";s:5:"Shell";s:2:"sh";s:10:"Privileged";s:5:"false";s:7:"Support";s:43:"https://github.com/aon082910/sop-hub/issues";s:7:"Project";s:36:"https://github.com/aon082910/sop-hub";s:11:"TemplateURL";s:84:"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/aon082910/AoN-Unraid-Apps/main/SOP-Hub/sop-hub.xml";s:6:"ReadMe";s:66:"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/aon082910/sop-hub/main/README.md";s:4:"Icon";s:81:"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/aon082910/AoN-Unraid-Apps/main/SOP-Hub/icon.png";s:5:"WebUI";s:24:"http://[IP]:[PORT:8080]/";s:7:"License";s:3:"MIT";s:8:"Overview";s:1431:"Self-hosted step-by-step visual guide builder, with AI help from either a
local model or a cloud provider.

Capture a process two ways -- upload screenshots manually in the editor, or
install the included Chrome extension and just click through the workflow;
it auto-captures a screenshot and click position for every click and uploads
the whole walkthrough as a new guide in one step. From there, AI can describe
each screenshot, write the guide's title and summary, rewrite step text for
clarity, and answer questions about a guide in a chat panel -- all routed
through one provider abstraction so local (Ollama) and cloud (Anthropic
Claude, OpenAI, or any OpenAI-compatible endpoint) are interchangeable per
request. Finished guides publish to a public read-only share link, or export
straight to PDF, HTML, or Markdown with embedded step images.

Everything -- Postgres, the API, and the built frontend -- runs in this one
container. SET JWT_SECRET before starting (any long random string). AI is
optional and defaults to a local Ollama instance you point it at (does not
run inside this container); set the Anthropic/OpenAI/custom variables
instead if you'd rather use a cloud provider, or skip AI entirely and use
SOP-Hub as a plain guide editor.

Everything lives under the single /config mount: the embedded Postgres
database and all uploaded step screenshots. Back that one directory up and
you've backed up the whole app.";s:16:"ExtraSearchTerms";s:110:"documentation how-to guide sop standard operating procedure process screenshot tutorial knowledge base wiki ai";s:8:"Requires";s:176:"Internet access is optional -- only needed if you point it at a cloud AI provider. Everything else, including local AI via your own Ollama instance, works fully offline/on-LAN.";s:4:"Date";s:10:"2026-09-03";s:6:"MinVer";s:3:"6.1";s:6:"Config";a:19:{i:0;a:2:{s:11:"@attributes";a:9:{s:4:"Name";s:10:"WebUI Port";s:6:"Target";s:4:"8080";s:7:"Default";s:4:"8080";s:4:"Mode";s:3:"tcp";s:11:"Description";s:17:"Web UI / API port";s:4:"Type";s:4:"Port";s:7:"Display";s:6:"always";s:8:"Required";s:4:"true";s:4:"Mask";s:5:"false";}s:5:"value";s:4:"8080";}i:1;a:2:{s:11:"@attributes";a:9:{s:4:"Name";s:7:"Appdata";s:6:"Target";s:7:"/config";s:7:"Default";s:25:"/mnt/user/appdata/sop-hub";s:4:"Mode";s:2:"rw";s:11:"Description";s:99:"Embedded Postgres database and all uploaded step screenshots -- the only folder you need to back up";s:4:"Type";s:4:"Path";s:7:"Display";s:6:"always";s:8:"Required";s:4:"true";s:4:"Mask";s:5:"false";}s:5:"value";s:25:"/mnt/user/appdata/sop-hub";}i:2;a:2:{s:11:"@attributes";a:9:{s:4:"Name";s:4:"PUID";s:6:"Target";s:4:"PUID";s:7:"Default";s:2:"99";s:4:"Mode";s:0:"";s:11:"Description";s:60:"Unraid's nobody user -- keeps appdata editable from the host";s:4:"Type";s:8:"Variable";s:7:"Display";s:6:"always";s:8:"Required";s:4:"true";s:4:"Mask";s:5:"false";}s:5:"value";s:2:"99";}i:3;a:2:{s:11:"@attributes";a:9:{s:4:"Name";s:4:"PGID";s:6:"Target";s:4:"PGID";s:7:"Default";s:3:"100";s:4:"Mode";s:0:"";s:11:"Description";s:20:"Unraid's users group";s:4:"Type";s:8:"Variable";s:7:"Display";s:6:"always";s:8:"Required";s:4:"true";s:4:"Mask";s:5:"false";}s:5:"value";s:3:"100";}i:4;a:2:{s:11:"@attributes";a:9:{s:4:"Name";s:2:"TZ";s:6:"Target";s:2:"TZ";s:7:"Default";s:7:"Etc/UTC";s:4:"Mode";s:0:"";s:11:"Description";s:35:"Timezone for dates shown in the app";s:4:"Type";s:8:"Variab