nections through them, if for some reason SSH doesn't cut it for you. It's very lightweight, and very light on resources too: for every client, a thread with a stack size of 8KB is spawned. the main process basically doesn't consume any resources at all. The only limits are the amount of file descriptors and the RAM. This Docker includes OpenVPN and WireGuard to ensure a secure and private connection to the Internet, including use of iptables to prevent IP leakage when the tunnel is down.";s:5:"WebUI";s:26:"http://config.privoxy.org/";s:11:"TemplateURL";s:94:"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/binhex/templates/main/unraid/binhex/templates/privoxyvpn.xml";s:4:"Icon";s:93:"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/binhex/templates/main/unraid/binhex/images/privoxy-icon.png";s:4:"Date";s:10:"1970-01-01";s:6:"Config";a:30:{i:0;a:2:{s:11:"@attributes";a:9:{s:4:"Name";s:13:"Port: Privoxy";s:6:"Target";s:4:"8118";s:7:"Default";s:4:"8118";s:4:"Mode";s:3:"tcp";s:11:"Description";s:62:"This is the port for Privoxy application - HTTPS proxy server.";s:4:"Type";s:4:"Port";s:7:"Display";s:6:"always";s:8:"Required";s:5:"false";s:4:"Mask";s:5:"false";}s:5:"value";s:0:"";}i:1;a:2:{s:11:"@attributes";a:9:{s:4:"Name";s:16:"Port: microsocks";s:6:"Target";s:4:"9118";s:7:"Default";s:4:"9118";s:4:"Mode";s:3:"tcp";s:11:"Description";s:66:"This is the port for microsocks application - Socks5 proxy server.";s:4:"Type";s:4:"Port";s:7:"Display";s:6:"always";s:8:"Required";s:5:"false";s:4:"Mask";s:5:"false";}s:5:"value";s:0:"";}i:2;a:2:{s:11:"@attributes";a:9:{s:4:"Name";s:23:"Port: Incoming port TCP";s:6:"Target";s:5:"58946";s:7:"Default";s:5:"58946";s:4:"Mode";s:3:"tcp";s:11:"Description";s:62:"This is the TCP incoming port when VPN_ENABLED is set to 'no'.";s:4:"Type";s:4:"Port";s:7:"Display";s:8:"advanced";s:8:"Required";s:5:"false";s:4:"Mask";s:5:"false";}s:5:"value";s:0:"";}i:3;a:2:{s:11:"@attributes";a:9:{s:4:"Name";s:23:"Port: Incoming port UDP";s:6:"Target";s:5:"58946";s:7:"Default";s:5:"58946"