;s:38:"https://github.com/binhex/arch-trimarr";s:8:"Overview";s:319:"Removes (trims) unwanted audio and subtitles from matroska container format video files using mkvmerge. Features recursive scanning, smart skip via SQLite tracking, commentary track safety, multi-language support, auto-managed mkvmerge binary, and space savings reporting. Supports one-shot or cron-scheduled operation.";s:8:"Requires";s:682:"**Media directory**<br>You must map at least one media directory (/media or custom path) containing your .mkv files.<br><br>**Language configuration**<br>The TRIMARR_LANGUAGE variable must be set to one or more ISO 639-2 language codes (comma-separated), e.g. 'eng' for English only or 'eng,fre' for English and French.<br><br>**First run**<br>On first run, trimarr downloads the mkvmerge binary automatically. Subsequent runs check for updates unless TRIMARR_NO_UPDATE_CHECK is set to 'yes'.<br><br>**Schedule (optional)**<br>Set TRIMARR_SCHEDULE to a cron expression to run repeatedly (e.g. '0 2 * * *' for daily at 2am). Omit for one-shot mode (container exits after processing).";s:11:"TemplateURL";s:91:"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/binhex/templates/main/unraid/binhex/templates/trimarr.xml";s:4:"Icon";s:93:"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/binhex/templates/main/unraid/binhex/images/trimarr-icon.png";s:4:"Date";s:10:"2026-05-20";s:6:"Config";a:36:{i:0;a:2:{s:11:"@attributes";a:9:{s:4:"Name";s:13:"Path: /config";s:6:"Target";s:7:"/config";s:7:"Default";s:25:"/mnt/user/appdata/trimarr";s:4:"Mode";s:2:"rw";s:11:"Description";s:72:"Container path for configuration files, database (trimarr.db), and logs.";s:4:"Type";s:4:"Path";s:7:"Display";s:6:"always";s:8:"Required";s:4:"true";s:4:"Mask";s:5:"false";}s:5:"value";s:0:"";}i:1;a:2:{s:11:"@attributes";a:9:{s:4:"Name";s:12:"Path: /media";s:6:"Target";s:6:"/media";s:7:"Default";s:9:"/mnt/user";s:4:"Mode";s:2:"rw";s:11:"Description";s:93:"Container path to your media files (e.g. movies, tv). Matches the default TRIMARR_MEDIA_PATH.";s:4:"Type";s:4:"Path";s:7:"Display";s:6:"always";s:8:"Required";s:4:"true";s:4:"Mask";s:5:"false";}s:5:"value";s:0:"";}i:2;a:2:{s:11:"@attributes";a:8:{s:4:"Name";s:26:"Variable: TRIMARR_LANGUAGE";s:6:"Target";s:16:"TRIMARR_LANGUAGE";s:7:"Default";s:0:"";s:11:"Description";s:171:"(Required) ISO 639-2 language code(s) for tracks to keep. Comma-separate multiple codes, e.g. 'eng' or 'eng,fre'. See https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/List_of_ISO_639-2_codes";s:4:"Type";s:8:"Variable";s:7:"Display";s:6:"always";s:8:"Required";s:4:"true";s:4:"Mask";s:5:"false";}s:5:"value";s:0:"";}i:3;a:2:{s:11:"@attributes";a:8:{s:4:"Name";s:28:"Variable: TRIMARR_MEDIA_PATH";s:6:"Target";s:18:"TRIMARR_MEDIA_PATH";s:7:"Default";s:6:"/media";s:11:"Description";s:121:"Directories containing media files to process. Use pipe (|) as separator for multiple paths, e.g. /media/Movies|/media/TV";s:4:"Type";s:8:"Variable";s:7:"Display";s:6:"always";s:8:"Required";s:4:"true";s:4:"Mask";s:5:"false";}s:5:"value";s:0:"";}i:4;a:2:{s:11:"@attributes";a:8:{s:4:"Name";s:26:"Variable: TRIMARR_SCHEDULE";s:6:"Target";s:16:"TRIMARR_SCHEDULE";s:7:"Default";s:0:"";s:11:"Description";s:150:"Cron schedule for repeated runs, e.g. '0 2 * * *' (daily at 2am), '@daily', '*/30 * * * *'. Omit for one-shot mode (container exits after processing).";s:4:"Type";s:8:"Variable";s:7:"Display";s:6:"always";s:8:"Required";s:5:"false";s:4:"Mask";s:5:"false";}s:5:"value";s:0:"";}i:5;a:2:{s:11:"@attributes";a:8:{s:4:"Name";s:37:"Variable: TRIMARR_EDIT_METADATA_TITLE";s:6:"Target";s:27:"TRIMARR_EDIT_METADATA_TITLE";s:7:"Default";s:6:"no|yes";s:11:"Description";s:77:"If set to 'yes', each file's title metadata is updated to match its filename.";s:4:"Type";s:8:"Variable";s:7:"Display";s:6:"always";s:8:"Required";s:5:"false";s:4:"Mask";s:5:"false";}s:5:"value";s:0:"";}i:6;a:2:{s:11:"@attributes";a:8:{s:4:"Name";s:39:"Variable: TRIMARR_DELETE_METADATA_TITLE";s:6:"Target";s:29:"TRIMARR_DELETE_METADATA_TITLE";s:7:"Default";s:6:"no|yes";s:11:"Description";s:107:"If set to 'yes', title metadata is deleted from files. Mutually exclusive with TRIMARR_EDIT_METADATA_TITLE.";s:4:"Type";s:8:"Variable";s:7:"Display";s:6:"always";s:8:"Required";s:5:"false";s:4:"Mask";s:5:"false";}s:5:"value";s:0:"";}i:7;a:2:{s:11:"@attributes";a:8:{s:4:"Name";s:32:"Variable: TRIMARR_KEEP_SUBTITLES";s:6:"Target";s:22:"TRIMARR_KEEP_SUBTITLES";s:7:"Default";s:6:"no|yes";s:11:"Description";s:69:"If set to 'yes', all subtitle tracks are kept regardless of language.";s:4:"Type";s:8:"Variable";s:7:"Display";s:6:"always";s:8:"Required";s:5:"false";s:4:"Mask";s:5:"false";}s:5:"value";s:0:"";}i:8;a:2:{s:11:"@attributes";a:8:{s:4:"Name";s:28:"Variable: TRIMARR_KEEP_AUDIO";s:6:"Target";s:18:"TRIMARR_KEEP_AUDIO";s:7:"Default";s:6:"no|yes";s:11:"Description";s:66:"If set to 'yes', all audio tracks are kept regardless of language.";s:4:"Type";s:8:"Variable";s:7:"Display";s:6:"always";s:8:"Required";s:5:"false";s:4:"Mask";s:5:"false";}s:5:"value";s:0:"";}i:9;a:2:{s:11:"@attributes";a:8:{s:4:"Name";s:35:"Variable: TRIMARR_KEEP_NATIVE_AUDIO";s:6:"Target";s:25:"TRIMARR_KEEP_NATIVE_AUDIO";s:7:"Default";s:6:"no|yes";s:11:"Description";s:169:"If set to 'yes', audio tracks matching the film's original language (detected via IMDb/TMDb) are kept even if they don't match TRIMARR_LANGUAGE. Useful for dubbed films.";s:4:"Type";s:8:"Variable";s:7:"Display";s:6:"always";s:8:"Required";s:5:"false";s:4:"Mask";s:5:"false";}s:5:"value";s:0:"";}i:10;a:2:{s:11:"@attributes";a:8:{s:4:"Name";s:27:"Variable: TRIMARR_NO_BACKUP";s:6:"Target";s:17:"TRIMARR_NO_BACKUP";s:7:"Default";s:6:"no|yes";s:11:"Description";s:99:"If set to 'yes', original files are deleted instead of renamed to .bak after successful processing.";s:4:"Type";s:8:"Variable";s:7:"Display";s:6:"always";s:8:"Required";s:5:"false";s:4:"Mask";s:5:"false";}s:5:"value";s:0:"";}i:11;a:2:{s:11:"@attributes";a:8:{s:4:"Name";s:25:"Variable: TRIMARR_DRY_RUN";s:6:"Target";s:15:"TRIMARR_DRY_RUN";s:7:"Default";s:6:"yes|no";s:11:"Description";s:137:"If set to 'yes', performs a dry run without modifying any files. Defaults to 'yes' for safety — set to 'no' to allow actual processing.";s:4:"Type";s:8:"Variable";s:7:"Display";s:6:"always";s:8:"Required";s:5:"false";s:4:"Mask";s:5:"false";}s:5:"value";s:0:"";}i:12;a:2:{s:11:"@attributes";a:8:{s:4:"Name";s:38:"Variable: TRIMARR_STRIP_LOWER_CHANNELS";s:6:"Target";s:28:"TRIMARR_STRIP_LOWER_CHANNELS";s:7:"Default";s:6:"no|yes";s:11:"Description";s:126:"If set to 'yes', audio tracks with channel count below the maximum surviving track are removed (e.g. drops 2ch if 8ch exists).";s:4:"Type";s:8:"Variable";s:7:"Display";s:6:"always";s:8:"Required";s:5:"false";s:4:"Mask";s:5:"false";}s:5:"value";s:0:"";}i:13;a:2:{s:11:"@attributes";a:8:{s:4:"Name";s:34:"Variable: TRIMARR_STRIP_COMMENTARY";s:6:"Target";s:24:"TRIMARR_STRIP_COMMENTARY";s:7:"Default";s:6:"no|yes";s:11:"Description";s:107:"If set to 'yes', audio and subtitle tracks whose name contains 'commentary' (case-insensitive) are removed.";s:4:"Type";s:8:"Variable";s:7:"Display";s:6:"always";s:8:"Required";s:5:"false";s:4:"Mask";s:5:"false";}s:5:"value";s:0:"";}i:14;a:2:{s:11:"@attributes";a:8:{s:4:"Name";s:38:"Variable: TRIMARR_STRIP_SUBTITLE_REGEX";s:6:"Target";s:28:"TRIMARR_STRIP_SUBTITLE_REGEX";s:7:"Default";s:0:"";s:11:"Description";s:171:"Python regex pattern. Any subtitle track whose name matches is removed after language filtering, regardless of language. Uses Python re syntax. Example: '(?i)songs.*signs'";s:4:"Type";s:8:"Variable";s:7:"Display";s:6:"always";s:8:"Required";s:5:"false";s:4:"Mask";s:5:"false";}s:5:"value";s:0:"";}i:15;a:2:{s:11:"@attributes";a:8:{s:4:"Name";s:30:"Variable: TRIMARR_RUN_ON_START";s:6:"Target";s:20:"TRIMARR_RUN_ON_START";s:7:"Default";s:6:"no|yes";s:11:"Description";s:128:"If set to 'yes', fires one run immediately on startup before the first scheduled cron fire. Requires TRIMARR_SCHEDULE to be set.";s:4:"Type";s:8:"Variable";s:7:"Display";s: