[p]It uses [code]inotify[/code] to monitor the input directory efficiently, and is fairly configurable.[/p]
[h4]Configuration Details[/h4]
[p]See the descriptions of the Unraid volumes and environment variables for highlights of the configurability of [code]ocrmypdf-auto[/code], but for details including how to specify custom commandline parameters to [code]ocrmydf[/code] itself, or custom [code]tesseract[/code] configuration files, see the full README at [a href='https://github.com/cmccambridge/ocrmypdf-auto/blob/master/README.md']https://github.com/cmccambridge/ocrmypdf-auto/blob/master/README.md[/a][/p]";s:11:"TemplateURL";s:101:"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/cmccambridge/unraid-templates/master/cmccambridge/ocrmypdf-auto.xml";s:4:"Icon";s:82:"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/cmccambridge/ocrmypdf-auto/master/media/logo.png";s:10:"Networking";a:1:{s:4:"Mode";s:6:"bridge";}s:6:"Config";a:11:{i:0;a:2:{s:11:"@attributes";a:9:{s:4:"Name";s:15:"Input Directory";s:6:"Target";s:6:"/input";s:7:"Default";s:0:"";s:4:"Mode";s:2:"rw";s:11:"Description";s:89:"Input directory from which to process files for OCR. emContainer path: code/input/code/em";s:4:"Type";s:4:"Path";s:7:"Display";s:6:"always";s:8:"Required";s:4:"true";s:4:"Mask";s:5:"false";}s:5:"value";s:0:"";}i:1;a:2:{s:11:"@attributes";a:9:{s:4:"Name";s:16:"Output Directory";s:6:"Target";s:7:"/output";s:7:"Default";s:0:"";s:4:"Mode";s:2:"rw";s:11:"Description";s:95:"Output directory to which post-OCR files will be written. emContainer path: code/output/code/em";s:4:"Type";s:4:"Path";s:7:"Display";s:6:"always";s:8:"Required";s:4:"true";s:4:"Mask";s:5:"false";}s:5:"value";s:0:"";}i:2;a:2:{s:11:"@attributes";a:9:{s:4:"Name";s:16:"Config Directory";s:6:"Target";s:7:"/config";s:7:"Default";s:31:"/mnt/user/appdata/ocrmypdf-auto";s:4:"Mode";s:2:"rw";s:11:"Description";s:63:"Config/appdata directory. emContainer path: code/config/code/em";s:4:"Type";s:4:"Path";s:7:"Display";s:6:"always";s:8:"Required";s:4:"true";s:4:"Mask";s:5:"false";}s:5:"value";s:31:"/mnt/user/appdata/ocrmypdf-auto";}i:3;a:2:{s:11:"@attributes";a:9:{s:4:"Name";s:11:"Output Mode";s:6:"Target";s:15:"OCR_OUTPUT_MODE";s:7:"Default";s:11:"MIRROR_TREE";s:4:"Mode";s:0:"";s:11:"Description";s:412:"Controls the output directory layout: br / codeMIRROR_TREE/code - (Default) Mirror the directory structure of the input directory, i.e. for an input file code/input/foo/bar.pdf/code create an output file code/output/foo/bar.pdf/code. br / codeSINGLE_FOLDER/code - Collect all output files in a single flat folder, i.e. for an input file code/input/foo/bar.pdf/code create an output file code/output/bar.pdf/code.";s:4:"Type";s:8:"Variable";s:7:"Display";s:6:"always";s:8:"Required";s:4:"true";s:4:"Mask";s:5:"false";}s:5:"value";s:11:"MIRROR_TREE";}i:4;a:2:{s:11:"@attributes";a:9:{s:4:"Name";s:17:"Action On Success";s:6:"Target";s:21:"OCR_ACTION_ON_SUCCESS";s:7:"Default";s:7:"NOTHING";s:4:"Mode";s:0:"";s:11:"Description";s:406:"Controls the action (if any) to perform after successful OCR processing: br / codeNOTHING/code - (Default) Do nothing. Input files remain in place where they were found. br / codeARCHIVE_INPUT_FILES/code - Archive input files by strongmoving/strong them em(overwriting existing files!)/em to the code/archive/code Volume br / codeDELETE_INPUT_FILES/code - Delete the input file after successful processing.";s:4:"Type";s:8:"Variable";s:7:"Display";s:6:"always";s:8:"Required";s:4:"true";s:4:"Mask";s:5:"false";}s:5:"value";s:7:"NOTHING";}i:5;a:2:{s:11:"@attributes";a:9:{s:4:"Name";s:20:"Additional Languages";s:6:"Target";s:13:"OCR_LANGUAGES";s:7:"Default";s:0:"";s:4:"Mode";s:0:"";s:11:"Description";s:353:"Additional languages (besides English) to install, given as a space-separated list of language abbreviations. All available languages can be found on the a href=https://packages.ubuntu.com/search?keywords=tesseract-ocr-&searchon=names&suite=bionic&section=allUbuntu site/a. Example for German, Chinese - Simplified, and Italian: codedeu chi-sim ita/code";s:4:"Type";s:8:"Variable";s:7:"Display";s:6:"always";s:8:"Required";s:5:"false";s:4:"Mask";s:5:"false";}s:5:"value";s:0:"";}i:6;a:2:{s:11:"@attributes";a:9:{s:4:"Name";s:10:"Notify URL";s:6:"Target";s:14:"OCR_NOTIFY_URL";s:7:"Default";s:0:"";s:4:"Mode";s:0:"";s:11:"Description";s:370:"On a successful completion, a POST will be made to the given URL, with a JSON payload of code{'pdf': '/output/doc.pdf', 'txt': '/output/doc.pdf.txt'} /code. The txt property will only be present if you add the code--sidecar /code option to the codeocr.config/code file. This could be used to kick off additional processing, like indexing of the content or notifications.";s:4:"Type";s:8:"Variable";s:7:"Display";s:6:"always";s:8:"Required";s:5:"false";s:4:"Mask";s:5:"false";}s:5:"value";s:0:"";}i:7;a:2:{s:11:"@attributes";a:9:{s:4:"Name";s:27:"Process Existing on Startup";s:6:"Target";s:29:"OCR_PROCESS_EXISTING_ON_START";s:7:"Default";s:1:"0";s:4:"Mode";s:0:"";s:11:"Description";s:197:"Set to code1/code to enable processing of any files in the input directory when the container is launched. br/ Set to code0/code (Default) or unset to ignore existing files until they are modified.";s:4:"Type";s:8:"Variable";s:7:"Display";s:6:"always";s:8:"Required";s:5:"false";s:4:"Mask";s:5:"false";}s:5:"value";s:1:"0";}i:8;a:2:{s:11:"@attributes";a:9:{s:4:"Name";s:9:"Verbosity";s:6:"Target";s:13:"OCR_VERBOSITY";s:7:"Default";s:0:"";s:4:"Mode";s:0:"";s:11:"Description";s:145:"Control the verbosity of debug logging. Accepts python codelogging/code levels, e.g. codewarn/code (Default), codeinfo/code, codedebug/code, etc.";s:4:"Type";s:8:"Variable";s:7:"Display";s:8:"advanced";s:8:"Required";s:5:"false";s:4:"Mask";s:5:"false";}s:5:"value";s:0:"";}i:9;a:2:{s:11:"@attributes";a:9:{s:4:"Name";s:12:"UID Override";s:6:"Target";s:11:"USERMAP_UID";s:7:"Default";s:2:"99";s:4:"Mode";s:0:"";s:11:"Description";s:66:"Set the UID that the OCR tools will run as. unRAID standard is 99.";s:4:"Type";s:8:"Variable";s:7:"Display";s:8:"advanced";s:8:"Required";s:5:"false";s:4:"Mask";s:5:"false";}s:5:"value";s:2:"99";}i:10;a:2: