/templates-community-apps/cookiesncachesRepository/cookiesncache-openclaw-latest.xml";s:4:"Date";N;s:11:"BrandNewApp";b:1;s:10:"Deprecated";b:0;s:10:"Compatible";b:1;s:16:"ModeratorComment";N;}i:1780;a:47:{s:4:"Name";s:5:"Xeoma";s:10:"Repository";s:12:"coppit/xeoma";s:8:"Registry";s:38:"https://hub.docker.com/r/coppit/xeoma/";s:7:"Network";s:6:"bridge";s:5:"Shell";s:4:"bash";s:10:"Privileged";s:5:"false";s:11:"ExtraParams";s:19:"--cap-add=NET_ADMIN";s:7:"Project";s:29:"https://felenasoft.com/xeoma/";s:7:"Support";s:66:"https://forums.unraid.net/topic/56659-xeoma-surveillance-software/";s:11:"TemplateURL";s:81:"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/coppit/docker-templates/master/coppit/xeoma.xml";s:6:"ReadMe";s:70:"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/coppit/docker-xeoma/master/README.md";s:8:"Overview";s:2433:"Xeoma is video surveillance software for connecting security cameras and recording detected movement.
    Connect with the Xeoma desktop client on port 8090. The optional Xeoma web interface uses port 10090.

    On first start without a password, the container creates xeoma.conf and an empty xeoma_password in the config
    directory, then exits. Put only your password in xeoma_password, without quotes or escaping, then restart.
    Trailing newlines are ignored. Startup is prevented if no password is supplied.

    Alternatively, select an existing host file under Password File to mount it read-only at /config/xeoma_password.
    Create that file before installing the container; leave the field blank to use the file in the config directory.
    A valid password file overrides legacy PASSWORD settings. The legacy password environment variable remains
    supported but logs a warning; add a Variable named PASSWORD if needed. A password file is recommended because
    its contents are not stored in the template. Environment variables override matching config-file settings.

    On bridged networking, the container saves its detected MAC in xeoma.conf when MAC_ADDRESS is empty and uses it for
    later starts. Extra Parameters includes --cap-add=NET_ADMIN by default to allow the MAC to be set.  This helps
    preserve Xeoma's licensing identity across container recreation, but does not guarantee license stability. When
    migrating a licensed installation, set MAC_ADDRESS to the old container's MAC before starting.

    Alternatively, set the saved MAC using Unraid's MAC address field, then remove --cap-add=NET_ADMIN from
    Extra Parameters in Advanced View. Keep MAC_ADDRESS in xeoma.conf for comparison: matching addresses require
    no capability. If the address changes and cannot be restored, startup continues with a licensing warning.
    Only veth interfaces (Docker bridge networking) are changed automatically. For host networking, remove
    --cap-add=NET_ADMIN and clear MAC_ADDRESS; for other network types, manage the MAC through Docker/Unraid.

    PUID and PGID default to Unraid's nobody/users IDs (99/100). On migration from the older image, storage ownership
    is updated once; this can take time for large archives. Choose IDs before starting and preserve existing storage
