mpFiles/templates-community-apps/corgansRepository/stefanknaak-Prometheusphoenixstats-latest.xml";s:4:"Date";N;s:11:"BrandNewApp";b:1;s:10:"Deprecated";b:0;s:10:"trendDelta";d:0.33;s:12:"trendAverage";d:0.6899;s:10:"DonateText";s:45:"If you like my work please consider Donating.";s:10:"DonateLink";s:29:"https://paypal.me/StefanKnaak";s:10:"Compatible";b:1;s:16:"ModeratorComment";N;}i:1790;a:43:{s:4:"Name";s:17:"fclones-scheduler";s:10:"Repository";s:40:"cplieger/docker-fclones-scheduler:latest";s:8:"Registry";s:59:"https://hub.docker.com/r/cplieger/docker-fclones-scheduler/";s:7:"Network";s:6:"bridge";s:10:"Privileged";s:5:"false";s:7:"Support";s:59:"https://github.com/cplieger/docker-fclones-scheduler/issues";s:7:"Project";s:52:"https://github.com/cplieger/docker-fclones-scheduler";s:6:"ReadMe";s:82:"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/cplieger/docker-fclones-scheduler/main/README.md";s:8:"Overview";s:479:"Runs the fclones duplicate finder on a schedule and gets back the disk space that duplicate files take.

Scans your share every 3 hours by default, or when your own scheduler asks. Replaces each extra copy with a hardlink or a copy-on-write clone, deletes it, or only reports it, and logs each duplicate it found and the space it freed. The default action only reports, so switch to link, remove or dedupe once a report has shown you what it would touch. No web UI, no open port.";s:4:"Icon";s:92:"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/cplieger/unraid-templates/main/icons/fclones-scheduler.png";s:11:"TemplateURL";s:96:"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/cplieger/unraid-templates/main/templates/fclones-scheduler.xml";s:7:"License";s:10:"Apache-2.0";s:16:"ExtraSearchTerms";s:64:"fclones duplicate files dedupe dedup hardlink reflink disk space";s:8:"Requires";s:499:"Start with the default action, group, which only reports. link, remove and dedupe modify the files under the scan path, and remove deletes them.<br>Hardlinks cannot span disks. For the link action, scan a single disk path such as /mnt/disk1/Media rather than /mnt/user/Media, or duplicates that live on two disks fail the run.<br>The container reports unhealthy until its first scan completes, and on a large share that can take hours. Later scans reuse the hash cache in /cache and are much faster.";s:11:"ExtraParams";s:38:"--user 99:100 --health-start-period=6h";s:6:"Config";a:10:{i:0;a:2:{s:11:"@attributes";a:9:{s:4:"Name";s:9:"Scan path";s:6:"Target";s:8:"/scandir";s:7:"Default";s:0:"";s:4:"Mode";s:2:"rw";s:11:"Description";s:115:"The share or folder to scan for duplicates, for example /mnt/user/Media. link, remove and dedupe need it read-write";s:4:"Type";s:4:"Path";s:7:"Display";s:6:"always";s:8:"Required";s:4:"true";s:4:"Mask";s:5:"false";}s:5:"value";s:0:"";}i:1;a:2:{s:11:"@attributes";a:9:{s:4:"Name";s:5:"Cache";s:6:"Target";s:6:"/cache";s:7:"Default";s:35:"/mnt/user/appdata/fclones-scheduler";s:4:"Mode";s:2:"rw";s:11:"Description";s:112:"The fclones hash cache and the last-scan record, which keep rescans fast and the schedule stable across restarts";s:4:"Type";s:4:"Path";s:7:"Display";s:6:"always";s:8:"Required";s:4:"true";s:4:"Mask";s:5:"false";}s:5:"value";s:35:"/mnt/user/appdata/fclones-scheduler";}i:2;a:2:{s:11:"@attributes";a:9:{s:4:"Name";s:6:"Action";s:6:"Target";s:14:"FCLONES_ACTION";s:7:"Default";s:5:"group";s:4:"Mode";s:0:"";s:11:"Description";s:180:"What to do with duplicates: group reports only, link replaces them with hardlinks, remove deletes them and dedupe makes copy-on-write clones. Anything but group modifies your files";s:4:"Type";s:8:"Variable";s:7:"Display";s:6:"always";s:8:"Required";s:5:"false";s:4:"Mask";s:5:"false";}s:5:"value";s:5:"group";}i:3;a:2:{s:11:"@attributes";a:9:{s:4:"Name";s:13:"Scan interval";s:6:"Target";s:13:"SCAN_INTERVAL";s:7:"Default";s:2:"3h";s:4:"Mode";s:0:"";s:11:"Description";s:147:"Time between scans as a Go duration such as 3h, 12h or 24h. off turns the schedule off so you trigger scans yourself, and 0 runs one scan and exits";s:4:"Type";s:8:"Variable";s:7:"Display";s:6:"always";s:8:"Required";s:5:"false";s:4:"Mask";s:5:"false";}s:5:"value";s:2:"3h";}i:4;a:2:{s:11:"@attributes";a:9:{s:4:"Name";s:10:"Scan paths";s:6:"Target";s:18:"FCLONES_SCAN_PATHS";s:7:"Default";s:8:"/scandir";s:4:"Mode";s:0:"";s:11:"Description";s:125:"Container paths to scan, separated by spaces. Each needs its own path mapping. Leave at /scandir unless you add more mappings";s:4:"Type";s:8:"Variable";s:7:"Display";s:8:"advanced";s:8:"Required";s:5:"false";s:4:"Mask";s:5:"false";}s:5:"value";s:8:"/scandir";}i:5;a:2:{s:11:"@attributes";a:9:{s:4:"Name";s:14:"Scan arguments";s:6:"Target";s:12:"FCLONES_ARGS";s:7:"Default";s:0:"";s:4:"Mode";s:0:"";s:11:"Description";s:132:"Extra flags for the fclones group phase, the scan, such as --name '*.mkv' --name '*.mp4' or --rf-over 1. Flags and their values only";s:4:"Type";s:8:"Variable";s:7:"Display";s:8:"advanced";s:8:"Required";s:5:"false";s:4:"Mask";s:5:"false";}s:5:"value";s:0:"";}i:6;a:2:{s:11:"@attributes";a:9:{s:4:"Name";s:16:"Action arguments";s:6:"Target";s:19:"FCLONES_ACTION_ARGS";s:7:"Default";s:0:"";s:4:"Mode";s:0:"";s:11:"Description";s:113:"Extra flags for the action phase, such as --priority bottom. --dry-run previews the action without changing files";s:4:"Type";s:8:"Variable";s:7:"Display";s:8:"advanced";s:8:"Required";s:5:"false";s:4:"Mask";s:5:"false";}s:5:"value";s:0:"";}i:7;a:2:{s:11:"@attributes";a:9:{s:4:"Name";s:12:"Scan timeout";s:6:"Target";s:12:"SCAN_TIMEOUT";s:7:"Default";s:3:"12h";s:4:"Mode";s:0:"";s:11:"Description";s:112:"Timeout for each phase as a Go duration. Raise it when a first scan of a large share exceeds 12h. 0 turns it off";s:4:"Type";s:8:"Variable";s:7:"Display";s:8:"advanced";s:8:"Required";s:5:"false";s:4:"Mask";s:5:"false";}s:5:"value";s:3:"12h";}i:8;a:2:{s:11:"@attributes";a:9:{s:4:"Name";s:9:"Log level";s:6:"Target";s:9:"LOG_LEVEL";s:7:"Default";s:4:"info";s:4:"Mode";s:0:"";s:11:"Description";s:45:"Minimum log level: debug, info, warn or error";s:4:"Type";s:8:"Variable";s:7:"Display";s:8:"advanced";s:8:"Required";s:5:"false";s:4:"Mask";s:5:"false";}s:5:"value";s:4:"info";}i:9;a:2:{s:11:"@attributes";a:9:{s:4:"Name";s:22:"Allow unsafe arguments";s:6:"Target";s:17:"ALLOW_UNSAFE_ARGS";s:7:"Default";s:5:"false";s:4:"Mode";s:0:"";s:11:"Description";s:106:"Set to true to allow the --transform, --in-place and --no-copy fclones flags, which are refused by default";s:4:"Type";s:8:"Variable";s:7:"Display";s:8:"advanced";s:8:"Required";s:5:"false";s:4:"Mask";s:5:"false";}s:5:"value";s:5:"false";}}s:12:"TemplatePath";s:51:"/tmp/GitHub/AppFeed/templates/fclones-scheduler.xml";s:4:"Repo";s:21:"cplieger's Repository";s:12:"CategoryList";a:1:{i:0;s:15:"Tools-Utilities";}s:9:"downloads";i:26719;s:13:"downloadtrend";a:2:{i:0;i:19017;i:1;i:26719;}s:6:"trends";a:1:{i:0;d:28.826;}s:10:"trendsDate";a:1:{i:0;i:1792262791;}s:9:"FirstSeen";i:1789615119;s:10:"LastUpdate";i:1791723294;s:14:"LastUpdateScan";i:1792262791;s:8:"Category";s:15:"Tools:Utilities";s:2:"ID";i:1790;s:11:"Displayable";b:1;s:6:"Author";s:8:"cplieger";s:13:"DockerHubName";s:17:"fclones-scheduler";s:8:"RepoName";s:21:"cplieger's Repository";s:10:"SortAuthor";s:8:"cplieger";s:8:"SortName";s:17:"fclones scheduler";s:6:"random";i:1813659343;s:9:"Blacklist";b:0;s:6:"MinVer";s:3:"6.0";s:4:"Path";s:119:"/tmp/community.applications/tempFiles/templates-community-apps/cpliegersRepository/cplieger-fclonesscheduler-latest.xml";s:4:"Date";N;s:11:"BrandNewApp";b:1;s:10:"Deprecated";b:0;s:10:"Compatible";b:1;s:16:"ModeratorComment";N;}i:1791;a:43:{s:4:"Name";s:13:"plex-exporter";s:10:"Repository";s:29:"cplieger/plex-exporter:latest";s:8:"Registry";s:48:"https://hub.docker.com/r/cplieger/plex-exporter/";s:7:"Network";s:6:"bridge";s:10:"Privileged";s:5:"false";s:7:"Support";s:48:"https://github.com/cplieger/plex-exporter/issues";s:7:"Project";s:41:"https://github.com/cplieger/plex-exporter";s:6:"ReadMe";s:71:"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/cplieger/plex-exporter/main/README.md";s:8:"Overview";s:534:"Puts your Plex server's streams, transcodes, bandwidth and library sizes into Prometheus, so you can watch them in Grafana and get alerts.

Shows who is watching what, on which device, and whether it plays directly or is transcoded. Tracks each stream's bandwidth and bitrate, counts the items, length and disk space of each library, and adds host CPU, memory and total bandwidth on a server with Plex Pass. A Grafana dashboard and nine alert rules ship in the project repository. It only reads from Plex and has no web UI of its own.";s:5:"WebUI";s:31:"http://[IP]:[PORT:9594]/metrics";s:4:"Icon";s:88:"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/cplieger/unraid-templates/main/icons/plex-exporter.png";s:11:"TemplateURL";s:92:"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/cplieger/unraid-templates/main/templates/plex-exporter.xml";s:7:"License";s:16:"GPL-3.0-or-later";s:16:"ExtraSearchTerms";s:51:"plex prometheus grafana metrics exporter monitoring";s:8:"Requires";s:641:"Needs a Prometheus-compatible scraper (Prometheus, Grafana Alloy, VictoriaMetrics) pointed at port 9594 and Grafana to show the dashboard. Neither is included.<br>Plex URL: the full URL of your Plex server including scheme and port, for example http://192.0.2.100:32400.<br>Plex Token: the server administrator's token. Plex's guide Finding an authentication token shows where to find it: https://support.plex.tv/articles/204059436-finding-an-authentication-token-x-plex-token/<br>Host CPU, memory and bandwidth metrics require Plex Pass. Everything else works without it.<br>The metrics endpoint has no login, so keep port 9594 on your LAN.";s:6:"Config";a:4:{i:0;a:2:{s:11:"@attributes";a:9:{s:4:"Name";s:8:"Plex URL";s:6:"Target";s:8:"PLEX_URL";s:7:"Default";s:0:"";s:4:"Mode";s:0:"";s:11:"Description";s:98:"Full URL of your Plex Media Server including scheme and port, for example http://192.0.2.100:32400";s:4:"Type";s:8:"Variable";s:7:"Display";s:6:"always";s:8:"Required";s:4:"true";s:4:"Mask";s:5:"false";}s:5:"value";s:0:"";}i:1;a:2:{s:11:"@attributes";a:9:{s:4:"Name";s:10:"Plex Token";s:6:"Target";s:10:"PLEX_TOKEN";s:7:"Default";s:0:"";s:4:"Mode";s:0:"";s:11:"Description";s:157:"Plex authentication token of the server administrator. Plex's guide: https://support.plex.tv/articles/204059436-finding-an-authentication-token-x-plex-token/";s:4:"Type";s:8:"Variable";s:7:"Display";s:6:"always";s:8:"Required";s:4:"true";s:4:"Mask";s:4:"true";}s:5:"value";s:0:"";}i:2;a:2:{s:11:"@attributes";a:9:{s:4:"Name";s:12:"Metrics port";s:6:"Target";s:4:"9594";s:7:"Default";s:4:"9594";s:4:"Mode";s:3:"tcp";s:11:"Description";s:56:"Prometheus metrics at /metrics and health at /api/health";s:4:"Type";s:4:"Port";s:7:"Display";s:6:"always";s:8:"Required";s:4:"true";s:4:"Mask";s:5:"false";}s:5:"value";s:4:"9594";}i:3;a:2:{s:11:"@attributes";a:9:{s:4:"Name";s:24:"Plex CA certificate path";s:6:"Target";s:17:"PLEX_CA_CERT_PATH";s:7:"Default";s:0:"";s:4:"Mode";s:0:"";s:11:"Description";s:151:"Only for an https Plex URL with a self-signed or private-CA certificate. The path of the CA PEM file inside the container, with a matching path mapping";s:4:"Type";s:8:"Variable";s:7:"Display";s:8:"advanced";s:8:"Required";s:5:"false";s:4:"Mask";s:5:"false";}s:5:"value";s:0:"";}}s:12:"TemplatePath";s:47:"/tmp/GitHub/AppFeed/templates/plex-exporter.xml";s:4:"Repo";s:21:"cplieger's Repository";s:12:"CategoryList";a:2:{i:0;s:15:"Tools-Utilities";i:1;s:14:"MediaApp-Video";}s:9:"downloads";i:29711;s:13:"downloadtrend";a:2:{i:0;i:20305;i:1;i:29711;}s:6:"trends";a:1:{i:0;d:31.658;}s:10:"trendsDate";a:1:{i:0;i:1792262791;}s:9:"FirstSeen";i:1789615119;s:10:"LastUpdate";i:1791722040;s:14:"LastUpdateScan";i:1792262791;s:8:"Category";s:30:"Tools:Utilities MediaApp:Video";s:2:"ID";i:1791;s:11:"Displayable";b:1;s:6:"Author";s:8:"cplieger";s:13:"DockerHubName";s:13:"plex-exporter";s:8:"RepoName";s:21:"cplieger's Repository";s:10:"SortAuthor";s:8:"cplieger";s:8:"SortName";s:13:"plex exporter";s:6:"random";i:188228007;s:9:"Blacklist";b:0;s:6:"MinVer";s:3:"6.0";s:4:"Path";s:115:"/tmp/community.applications/tempFiles/templates-community-apps/cpliegersRepository/cplieger-plexexporter-latest.xml";s:4:"Date";N;s:11:"BrandNewApp";b:1;s:10:"Deprecated";b:0;s:10:"Compatible";b:1;s:16:"ModeratorComment";N;}i:1792;a:43:{s:4:"Name";s:18:"plex-language-sync";s:10:"Repository";s:34:"cplieger/plex-language-sync:latest";s:8:"Registry";s:53:"https://hub.docker.com/r/cplieger/plex-language-sync/";s:7:"Network";s:6:"bridge";s:10:"Privileged";s:5:"false";s:7:"Support";s:53:"https://github.com/cplieger/plex-language-sync/issues";s:7:"Project";s:46:"https://github.com/cplieger/plex-language-sync";s:6:"ReadMe";s:76:"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/cplieger/plex-language-sync/main/README.md";s:8:"Overview";s:475:"Remembers the audio and subtitle languages you pick for each TV show in Plex and sets them on every other episode, for each user of your server.

Sets your choice on the rest of the show as soon as you pick it on one episode, and gives new episodes the same tracks when Plex adds them. It learns which subtitles you pair with each audio language and sets them on new shows. It chooses between the tracks your files already have and downloads nothing. No web UI, no open port.";s:4:"Icon";s:93:"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/cplieger/unraid-templates/main/icons/plex-language-sync.png";s:11:"TemplateURL";s:97:"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/cplieger/unraid-templates/main/templates/plex-language-sync.xml";s:7:"License";s:16:"GPL-3.0-or-later";s:16:"ExtraSearchTerms";s:49:"plex audio subtitle language track auto-languages";s:8:"Requires";s:597:"Plex URL: the full URL of your Plex server including scheme and port, for example http://192.0.2.100:32400. Use the server's LAN IP, not a container name.<br>Plex Token: the server administrator's token. Plex's guide Finding an authentication token shows where to find it: https://support.plex.tv/articles/204059436-finding-an-authentication-token-x-plex-token/<br>Multi-user support fetches shared user tokens from plex.tv, so the container needs internet access.<br>Raise the Docker stop time-out to 20 seconds or more (Settings, Docker, advanced view) so the final cache save completes on stop.";s:11:"ExtraParams";s:13:"--user 99:100";s:6:"Config";a:14:{i:0;a:2:{s:11:"@attributes";a:9:{s:4:"Name";s:8:"Plex URL";s:6:"Target";s:8:"PLEX_URL";s:7:"Default";s:0:"";s:4:"Mode";s:0:"";s:11:"Description";s:98:"Full URL of your Plex Media Server including scheme and port, for example http://192.0.2.100:32400";s:4:"Type";s:8:"Variable";s:7:"Display";s:6:"always";s:8:"Required";s:4:"true";s:4:"Mask";s:5:"false";}s:5:"value";s:0:"";}i:1;a:2:{s:11:"@attributes";a:9:{s:4:"Name";s:10:"Plex Token";s:6:"Target";s:10:"PLEX_TOKEN";s:7:"Default";s:0:"";s:4:"Mode";s:0:"";s:11:"Description";s:157:"Plex authentication token of the server administrator. Plex's guide: https://support.plex.tv/articles/204059436-finding-an-authentication-token-x-plex-token/";s:4:"Type";s:8:"Variable";s:7:"Display";s:6:"always";s:8:"Required";s:4:"true";s:4:"Mask";s:4:"true";}s:5:"value";s:0:"";}i:2;a:2:{s:11:"@attributes";a:9:{s:4:"Name";s:6:"Config";s:6:"Target";s:7:"/config";s:7:"Default";s:36:"/mnt/user/appdata/plex-language-sync";s:4:"Mode";s:2:"rw";s:11:"Description";s:80:"Persistent cache of learned language profiles, shared-user tokens and sync state";s:4:"Type";s:4:"Path";s:7:"Display";s:6:"always";s:8:"Required";s:4:"true";s:4:"Mask";s:5:"false";}s:5:"value";s:36:"/mnt/user/appdata/plex-language-sync";}i:3;a:2:{s:11:"@attributes";a:9:{s:4:"Name";s:12:"Update level";s:6:"Target";s:12:"UPDATE_LEVEL";s:7:"Default";s:4:"show";s:4:"Mode";s:0:"";s:11:"Description";s:106:"Scope of language propagation: show applies to all episodes of the show, season only to the current season";s:4:"Type";s:8:"Variable";s:7:"Display";s:8:"advanced";s:8:"Required";s:5:"false";s:4:"Mask";s:5:"false";}s:5:"value";s:4:"show";}i:4;a:2:{s:11:"@attributes";a:9:{s:4:"Name";s:15:"Update strategy";s:6:"Target";s:15:"UPDATE_STRATEGY";s:7:"Default";s:3:"all";s:4:"Mode";s:0:"";s:11:"Description";s:111:"Which episodes to update: all updates every episode in scope, next only the episodes after the one being played";s:4:"Type";s:8:"Variable";s:7:"Display";s:8:"advanced";s:8:"Required";s:5:"false";s:4:"Mask";s:5:"false";}s:5:"value";s:3:"all";}i:5;a:2:{s:11:"@attributes";a:9:{s:4:"Name";s:15:"Trigger on play";s:6:"Target";s:15:"TRIGGER_ON_PLAY";s:7:"Default";s:4:"true";s:4:"Mode";s:0:"";s:11:"Description";s:77:"React to playback events: playing an episode propagates its language settings";s:4:"Type";s:8:"Variable";s:7:"Display";s:8:"advanced";s:8:"Required";s:5:"false";s:4:"Mask";s:5:"false";}s:5:"value";s:4:"true";}i:6;a:2:{s:11:"@attributes";a:9:{s:4:"Name";s:15:"Trigger on scan";s:6:"Target";s:15:"TRIGGER_ON_SCAN";s:7:"Default";s:4:"true";s:4:"Mode";s:0:"";s:11:"Description";s:103:"React to library scans: newly added or updated episodes get each user's recorded selection for the show";s:4:"Type";s:8:"Variable";s:7:"Display";s:8:"advanced";s:8:"Required";s:5:"false";s:4:"Mask";s:5:"false";}s:5:"value";s:4:"true";}i:7;a:2:{s:11:"@attributes";a:9:{s:4:"Name";s:23:"Learn language profiles";s:6:"Target";s:23:"LEARN_LANGUAGE_PROFILES";s:7:"Default";s:4:"true";s:4:"Mode";s:0:"";s:11:"Description";s:108:"Learn audio-to-subtitle language pairs from playback and apply them to brand new shows with no watch history";s:4:"Type";s:8:"Variable";s:7:"Display";s:8:"advanced";s:8:"Required";s:5:"false";s:4:"Mask";s:5:"false";}s:5:"value";s:4:"true";}i:8;a:2:{s:11:"@attributes";a:9:{s:4:"Name";s:19:"Subtitle match tier";s:6:"Target";s:19:"SUBTITLE_MATCH_TIER";s:7:"Default";s:12:"other-region";s:4:"Mode";s:0:"";s:11:"Description";s:164:"How far a subtitle substitution may reach when no exact language match exists: identical, same-language, other-region, other-script, intelligible or shared-literacy";s:4:"Type";s:8:"Variable";s:7:"Display";s:8:"advanced";s:8:"Required";s:5:"false";s:4:"Mask";s:5:"false";}s:5:"value";s:12:"other-region";}i:9;a:2:{s:11:"@attributes";a:9:{s:4:"Name";s:18:"Deep scan interval";s:6:"Target";s:18:"DEEP_SCAN_INTERVAL";s:7:"Default";s:3:"24h";s:4:"Mode";s:0:"";s:11:"Description";s:94:"How often the deep-scan safety net runs, as a Go duration such as 24h or 12h. off turns it off";s:4:"Type";s:8:"Variable";s:7:"Display";s:8:"advanced";s:8:"Required";s:5:"false";s:4:"Mask";s:5:"false";}s:5:"value";s:3:"24h";}i:10;a:2:{s:11:"@attributes";a:9:{s:4:"Name";s:13:"Ignore labels";s:6:"Target";s:13:"IGNORE_LABELS";s:7:"Default";s:21:"PAL_IGNORE,PLS_IGNORE";s:4:"Mode";s:0:"";s:11:"Description";s:144:"Comma-separated Plex labels that exclude a show from language sync. Matching is exact and case-sensitive, and setting this replaces the defaults";s:4:"Type";s:8:"Variable";s:7:"Display";s:8:"advanced";s:8:"Required";s:5:"false";s:4:"Mask";s:5:"false";}s:5:"value";s:21:"PAL_IGNORE,PLS_IGNORE";}i:11;a:2:{s:11:"@attributes";a:9:{s:4:"Name";s:16:"Ignore libraries";s:6:"Target";s:16:"IGNORE_LIBRARIES";s:7:"Default";s:0:"";s:4:"Mode";s:0:"";s:11:"Description";s:92:"Comma-separated Plex library names to exclude entirely. Matching is exact and case-sensitive";s:4:"Type";s:8:"Variable";s:7:"Display";s:8:"advanced";s:8:"Required";s:5:"false";s:4:"Mask";s:5:"false";}s:5:"value";s:0:"";}i:12;a:2:{s:11:"@attributes";a:9:{s:4:"Name";s:9:"Log level";s:6:"Target";s:9:"LOG_LEVEL";s:7:"Default";s:4:"info";s:4:"Mode";s:0:"";s:11:"Description";s:114:"Minimum log level: debug, info, warn or error. debug shows why each event was skipped and how streams were matched";s:4:"Type";s:8:"Variable";s:7:"Display";s:8:"advanced";s:8:"Required";s:5:"false";s:4:"Mask";s:5:"false";}s:5:"value";s:4:"info";}i:13;a:2:{s:11:"@attributes";a:9:{s:4:"Name";s:24:"Plex CA certificate path";s:6:"Target";s:17:"PLEX_CA_CERT_PATH";s:7:"Default";s:0:"";s:4:"Mode";s:0:"";s:11:"Description";s:151:"Only for an https Plex URL with a self-signed or private-CA certificate. The path of the CA PEM file inside the container, with a matching path mapping";s:4:"Type";s:8:"Variable";s:7:"Display";s:8:"advanced";s:8:"Required";s:5:"false";s:4:"Mask";s:5:"false";}s:5:"value";s:0:"";}}s:12:"TemplatePath";s:52:"/tmp/GitHub/AppFeed/templates/plex-language-sync.xml";s:4:"Repo";s:21:"cplieger's Repository";s:12:"CategoryList";a:2:{i:0;s:14:"MediaApp-Video";i:1;s:15:"Tools-Utilities";}s:9:"downloads";i:26116;s:13:"downloadtrend";a:2:{i:0;i:19351;i:1;i:26116;}s:6:"trends";a:1:{i:0;d:25.904;}s:10:"trendsDate";a:1:{i:0;i:1792262791;}s:9:"FirstSeen";i:1789615119;s:10:"LastUpdate";i:1791724202;s:14:"LastUpdateScan";i:1792262791;s:8:"Category";s:30:"MediaApp:Video Tools:Utilities";s:2:"ID";i:1792;s:11:"Displayable";b:1;s:6:"Author";s:8:"cplieger";s:13:"DockerHubName";s:18:"plex-language-sync";s:8:"RepoName";s:21:"cplieger's Repository";s:10:"SortAuthor";s:8:"cplieger";s:8:"SortName";s:18:"plex language sync";s:6:"random";i:1013318844;s:9:"Blacklist";b:0;s:6:"MinVer";s:3:"6.0";s:4:"Path";s:119:"/tmp/community.applications/tempFiles/templates-community-apps/cpliegersRepository/cplieger-plexlanguagesync-latest.xml";s:4:"Date";N;s:11:"BrandNewApp";b:1;s:10:"Deprecated";b:0;s:10:"Compatible";b:1;s:16:"ModeratorComment";N;}i:1793;a:43:{s:4:"Name";s:12:"seadex-scout";s:10:"Repository";s:28:"cplieger/seadex-scout:latest";s:8:"Registry";s:47:"https://hub.docker.com/r/cplieger/seadex-scout/";s:7:"Network";s:6:"bridge";s:10:"Privileged";s:5:"false";s:7:"Support";s:47:"https://github.com/cplieger/seadex-scout/issues";s:7:"Project";s:40:"https://github.com/cplieger/seadex-scout";s:6:"ReadMe";s:70:"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/cplieger/seadex-scout/main/README.md";s:8:"Overview";s:450:"Keeps your Sonarr and Radarr anime library in sync with the best releases on SeaDex, the community list of the best release for each show.

Tells you when SeaDex lists a better release than yours, or a newer v2 or REPACK of it, and writes an on-demand report comparing each season you have with SeaDex. It leaves downloads to Sonarr and Radarr. It can also offer SeaDex's picks to them as a Torznab indexer, so they download under your quality rules.";s:4:"Icon";s:87:"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/cplieger/unraid-templates/main/icons/seadex-scout.png";s:11:"TemplateURL";s:91:"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/cplieger/unraid-templates/main/templates/seadex-scout.xml";s:7:"License";s:16:"GPL-3.0-or-later";s:16:"ExtraSearchTerms";s:58:"seadex seadex.moe releases.moe anime sonarr radarr torznab";s:8:"Requires";s:989:"Sonarr URL and Sonarr API key are enough to start. Fill them in and the first start writes /config/config.yaml, reads your values from these fields and begins comparing. Leave Radarr empty if you only run Sonarr.<br><br>A finding is a warning line in the container log, never a download. Read the log from the Docker tab.<br><br>For a full season-by-season report, run this from an Unraid terminal (Tools, then Terminal) while the container is up: docker exec seadex-scout /seadex-scout report<br>It writes a timestamped Markdown and JSON pair into /config/reports. The container is distroless, so the Console button in the Docker tab does not work.<br><br>Everything else is tuned in /config/config.yaml, which is annotated. The container reads it once at start, so restart it after an edit.<br><br>The Torznab port is only bound when a Torznab URL is set in config.yaml. Leave the port mapping alone otherwise. Keep that feed on your LAN, because its AnimeBytes links carry your passkey.";s:11:"ExtraParams";s:13:"--user 99:100";s:6:"Config";a:6:{i:0;a:2:{s:11:"@attributes";a:9:{s:4:"Name";s:10:"Sonarr URL";s:6:"Target";s:10:"SONARR_URL";s:7:"Default";s:0:"";s:4:"Mode";s:0:"";s:11:"Description";s:144:"Where seadex-scout reaches Sonarr, including scheme and port, for example http://192.0.2.100:8989. Use the 