 processing mode. artist downloads albums listed directly under that artist. discography downloads albums listed under that artist plus albums where that artist appears as a contributor or featured artist. Recommended: artist for tighter libraries; discography for the broadest collection.";s:4:"Type";s:8:"Variable";s:7:"Display";s:6:"always";s:8:"Required";s:4:"true";s:4:"Mask";s:5:"false";}s:5:"value";s:6:"artist";}i:4;a:2:{s:11:"@attributes";a:9:{s:4:"Name";s:22:"MusicBrainz Enrichment";s:6:"Target";s:19:"MUSICBRAINZ_ENABLED";s:7:"Default";s:5:"false";s:4:"Mode";s:0:"";s:11:"Description";s:215:"Optional MusicBrainz enrichment. false uses the standard Deezer/Bambanah workflow. true enables the MusicBrainz-enriched workflow. This variable overrides the legacy /config/run_alternate marker. Recommended: false.";s:4:"Type";s:8:"Variable";s:7:"Display";s:8:"advanced";s:8:"Required";s:5:"false";s:4:"Mask";s:5:"false";}s:5:"value";s:5:"false";}i:5;a:2:{s:11:"@attributes";a:9:{s:4:"Name";s:9:"ARL Token";s:6:"Target";s:9:"ARL_TOKEN";s:7:"Default";s:0:"";s:4:"Mode";s:0:"";s:11:"Description";s:193:"Deezer ARL token used by Deemix Direct. Recommended login method for new Direct-mode installs. Keep private. If left blank, Deemix Direct must be able to read /deemix-config/login.json instead.";s:4:"Type";s:8:"Variable";s:7:"Display";s:6:"always";s:8:"Required";s:5:"false";s:4:"Mask";s:4:"true";}s:5:"value";s:0:"";}i:6;a:2:{s:11:"@attributes";a:9:{s:4:"Name";s:9:"Autostart";s:6:"Target";s:9:"AUTOSTART";s:7:"Default";s:5:"false";s:4:"Mode";s:0:"";s:11:"Description";s:164:"true = run AMA automatically on container startup and repeat using Script Interval. false = manual runs only. Recommended: false until your configuration is tested.";s:4:"Type";s:8:"Variable";s:7:"Display";s:6:"always";s:8:"Required";s:4:"true";s:4:"Mask";s:5:"false";}s:5:"value";s:5:"false";}i:7;a:2:{s:11:"@attributes";a:9:{s:4:"Name";s:15:"Script Interval";s:6:"Target";s:14:"SCRIPTINTERVAL";s:7:"Default";s:2:"7d";s:4:"Mode";s:0:"";s:11:"Description";s:78:"Time between automatic runs when Autostart is true. Examples: 15m, 1h, 1d, 7d.";s:4:"Type";s:8:"Variable";s:7:"Display";s:6:"always";s:8:"Required";s:5:"false";s:4:"Mask";s:5:"false";}s:5:"value";s:2:"7d";}i:8;a:2:{s:11:"@attributes";a:9:{s:4:"Name";s:21:"Retain Partial Albums";s:6:"Target";s:21:"RETAIN_PARTIAL_ALBUMS";s:7:"Default";s:5:"false";s:4:"Mode";s:0:"";s:11:"Description";s:343:"Deemix Direct: true keeps available tracks when an album is incomplete and records missing tracks under /config/partial-albums. false preserves the existing policy of rejecting new partial downloads. Existing retained music and pending records are preserved when disabled. Enable this together with Retry Missing Tracks for automatic recovery.";s:4:"Type";s:8:"Variable";s:7:"Display";s:6:"always";s:8:"Required";s:5:"false";s:4:"Mask";s:5:"false";}s:5:"value";s:5:"false";}i:9;a:2:{s:11:"@attributes";a:9:{s:4:"Name";s:20:"Retry Missing Tracks";s:6:"Target";s:20:"RETRY_MISSING_TRACKS";s:7:"Default";s:4:"true";s:4:"Mode";s:0:"";s:11:"Description";s:257:"Deemix Direct: retry only missing tracks from retained partial albums when Retain Partial Albums is also true. false pauses retries without deleting music or pending records. Due retries run during subsequent AMA scans; enable Autostart for automatic scans.";s:4:"Type";s:8:"Variable";s:7:"Display";s:6:"always";s:8:"Required";s:5:"false";s:4:"Mask";s:5:"false";}s:5:"value";s:4:"true";}i:10;a:2:{s:11:"@attributes";a:9:{s:4:"Name";s:36:"Partial Album Retry Interval (Hours)";s:6:"Target";s:19:"PARTIAL_RETRY_HOURS";s:7:"Default";s:2:"24";s:4:"Mode";s:0:"";s:11:"Description";s:285:"Minimum hours between missing-track attempts. Use a positive whole number of at least 1; invalid values fall back to 24. A retry runs on the next AMA scan after it becomes due, not at an exact scheduled time. Used only when Retain Partial Albums and Retry Missing Tracks are both true.";s:4:"Type";s:8:"Variable";s:7:"Display";s:6:"always";s:8:"Required";s:5:"false";s:4:"Mask";s:5:"false";}s:5:"value";s:2:"24";}i:11;a:2:{s:11:"@attributes";a:9:{s:4:"Name";s:6:"Format";s:6:"Target";s:6:"FORMAT";s:7:"Default";s:4:"FLAC";s:4:"Mode";s:0:"";s:11:"Description";s:198:"Preferred final audio format. Supported values: FLAC, ALAC, AAC, MP3, OPUS. FLAC is recommended for best quality. ALAC, AAC, MP3, and OPUS may trigger post-download conversion from FLAC when needed.";s:4:"Type";s:8:"Variable";s:7:"Display";s:6:"always";s:8:"Required";s:4:"true";s:4:"Mask";s:5:"false";}s:5:"value";s:4:"FLAC";}i:12;a:2:{s:11:"@attributes";a:9:{s:4:"Name";s:7:"Bitrate";s:6:"Target";s:7:"BITRATE";s:7:"Default";s:3:"320";s:4:"Mode";s:0:"";s:11:"Description";s:135:"Lossy bitrate used for MP3, AAC, and OPUS conversion paths. Examples: 128, 192, 256, 320. Only matters for lossy formats or conversion.";s:4:"Type";s:8:"Variable";s:7:"Display";s:8:"advanced";s:8:"Required";s:5:"false";s:4:"Mask";s:5:"false";}s:5:"value";s:3:"320";}i:13;a:2:{s:11:"@attributes";a:9:{s:4:"Name";s:13:"Force Convert";s:6:"Target";s:12:"FORCECONVERT";s:7:"Default";s:5:"false";s:4:"Mode";s:0:"";s:11:"Description";s:213:"Force conversion to the requested Format when supported. Recommended: false to avoid unnecessary lossy-to-lossy conversion. Set true only when you intentionally want the final library to match the selected Format.";s:4:"Type";s:8:"Variable";s:7:"Display";s:8:"advanced";s:8:"Required";s:5:"false";s:4:"Mask";s:5:"false";}s:5:"value";s:5:"false";}i:14;a:2:{s:11:"@attributes";a:9:{s:4:"Name";s:20:"Post Process Threads";s:6:"Target";s:18:"POSTPROCESSTHREADS";s:7:"Default";s:1:"8";s:4:"Mode";s:0:"";s:11:"Description";s:140:"Number of threads used for conversion and post-processing tasks. Lower this on slower systems; raise it only if the server has CPU headroom.";s:4:"Type";s:8:"Variable";s:7:"Display";s:8:"advanced";s:8:"Required";s:5:"false";s:4:"Mask";s:5:"false";}s:5:"value";s:1:"8";}i:15;a:2:{s:11:"@attributes";a:9:{s:4:"Name";s:15:"Require Quality";s:6:"Target";s:15:"REQUIRE_QUALITY";s:7:"Default";s:5:"false";s:4:"Mode";s:0:"";s:11:"Description";s:201:"Strict quality check after download. false lets AMA continue when Deemix fallback provides another available format. true is stricter and can skip or fail items that do not match the requested quality.";s:4:"Type";s:8:"Variable";s:7:"Display";s:8:"advanced";s:8:"Required";s:5:"false";s:4:"Mask";s:5:"false";}s:5:"value";s:5:"false";}i:16;a:2:{s:11:"@attributes";a:9:{s:4:"Name";s:23:"Deemix Fallback Bitrate";s:6:"Target";s:23:"DEEMIX_FALLBACK_BITRATE";s:7:"Default";s:4:"true";s:4:"Mode";s:0:"";s:11:"Description";s:210:"Allow Deemix Direct to fall back to another available bitrate or format when the requested quality is unavailable. Recommended: true so albums can complete when FLAC is missing. Set false for stricter behavior.";s:4:"Type";s:8:"Variable";s:7:"Display";s:8:"advanced";s:8:"Required";s:5:"false";s:4:"Mask";s:5:"false";}s:5:"value";s:4:"true";}i:17;a:2:{s:11:"@attributes";a:9:{s:4:"Name";s:31:"Deemix Direct Queue Concurrency";s:6:"Target";s:24:"DEEMIX_QUEUE_CONCURRENCY";s:7:"Default";s:1:"1";s:4:"Mode";s:0:"";s:11:"Description";s:143:"Internal Deemix Direct queue and download concurrency. Recommended: 1 because AMA uses one shared /downloads-ama/temp working folder per album.";s:4:"Type";s:8:"Variable";s:7:"Display";s:8:"advanced";s:8:"Required";s:5:"false";s:4:"Mask";s:5:"false";}s:5:"value";s:1:"1";}i:18;a:2:{s:11:"@attributes";a:9:{s:4:"Name";s:28:"Deemix Embedded Artwork Size";s:6:"Target";s:28:"DEEMIX_EMBEDDED_ARTWORK_SIZE";s:7:"Default";s:4:"1400";s:4:"Mode";s:0:"";s:11:"Description";s:137:"Artwork size embedded into audio files by Deemix Direct. Recommended: 1400 for high-quality album art without very large embedded images.";s:4:"Type";s:8:"Variable";s:7:"Display";s:8:"advanced";s:8:"Required";s:5:"false";s:4:"Mask";s:5:"false";}s:5:"value";s:4:"1400";}i:19;a:2:{s:11:"@attributes";a:9:{s:4:"Name";s:25:"Deemix Local Artwork Size";s:6:"Target";s:25:"DEEMIX_LOCAL_ARTWORK_SIZE";s:7:"Default";s:4:"1400";s:4:"Mode";s:0:"";s:11:"Description";s:77:"Artwork size used for local cover files such as cover.jpg. Recommended: 1400.";s:4:"Type";s:8:"Variable";s:7:"Display";s:8:"advanced";s:8:"Required";s:5:"false";s:4:"Mask";s:5:"false";}s:5:"value";s:4:"1400";}i:20;a:2:{s:11:"@attributes";a:9:{s:4:"Name";s:25:"Deemix JPEG Image Quality";s:6:"Target";s:25:"DEEMIX_JPEG_IMAGE_QUALITY";s:7:"Default";s:3:"100";s:4:"Mode";s:0:"";s:11:"Description";s:131:"JPEG quality used by Deemix Direct for saved and embedded artwork. Recommended: 100. Falls back to Embedded Cover Quality if unset.";s:4:"Type";s:8:"Variable";s:7:"Display";s:8:"advanced";s:8:"Required";s:5:"false";s:4:"Mask";s:5:"false";}s:5:"value";s:3:"100";}i:21;a:2:{s:11:"@attributes";a:9:{s:4:"Name";s:22:"Embedded Cover Quality";s:6:"Target";s:22:"EMBEDDED_COVER_QUALITY";s:7:"Default";s:3:"100";s:4:"Mode";s:0:"";s:11:"Description";s:161:"Legacy and fallback artwork quality variable. Deemix Direct prefers Deemix JPEG Image Quality, but this remains available for compatibility with older AMA paths.";s:4:"Type";s:8:"Variable";s:7:"Display";s:8:"advanced";s:8:"Required";s:5:"false";s:4:"Mask";s:5:"false";}s:5:"value";s:3:"100";}i:22;a:2:{s:11:"@attributes";a:9:{s:4:"Name";s:17:"Album Type Filter";s:6:"Target";s:17:"ALBUM_TYPE_FILTER";s:7:"Default";s:7:"COMPILE";s:4:"Mode";s:0:"";s:11:"Description";s:180:"Comma-separated Deezer album record types to skip. Common values: COMPILE, SINGLE, ALBUM, EP. Default COMPILE skips compilation albums. Leave blank to disable album type filtering.";s:4:"Type";s:8:"Variable";s:7:"Display";s:8:"advanced";s:8:"Required";s:5:"false";s:4:"Mask";s:5:"false";}s:5:"value";s:7:"COMPILE";}i:23;a:2:{s:11:"@attributes";a:9:{s:4:"Name";s:25:"Maximum Albums Per Artist";s:6:"Target";s:21:"MAX_ALBUMS_PER_ARTIST";s:7:"Default";s:0:"";s:4:"Mode";s:0:"";s:11:"Description";s:219:"Optional maximum number of albums selected per artist during di