oggle from LOG_LEVEL and is off by default. Useful when debugging missing keys, locale resolution misses, or broken locale files.";s:4:"Type";s:8:"Variable";s:7:"Display";s:8:"advanced";s:8:"Required";s:5:"false";s:4:"Mask";s:5:"false";}s:5:"value";s:5:"false";}i:8;a:2:{s:11:"@attributes";a:9:{s:4:"Name";s:18:"Settings Passwords";s:6:"Target";s:25:"DEGOOG_SETTINGS_PASSWORDS";s:7:"Default";s:0:"";s:4:"Mode";s:0:"";s:11:"Description";s:182:"Optional. Comma-separated list of passwords for the Settings page. If set, users must enter one of these to access Settings (unless a middleware plugin is used as the settings gate).";s:4:"Type";s:8:"Variable";s:7:"Display";s:8:"advanced";s:8:"Required";s:5:"false";s:4:"Mask";s:4:"true";}s:5:"value";s:0:"";}i:9;a:2:{s:11:"@attributes";a:9:{s:4:"Name";s:13:"Settings Path";s:6:"Target";s:20:"DEGOOG_SETTINGS_PATH";s:7:"Default";s:0:"";s:4:"Mode";s:0:"";s:11:"Description";s:348:"Optional. Custom path for the admin settings panel. Defaults to /admin on public instances and /settings on private ones. Set to a hard-to-guess string to make the panel undiscoverable (e.g. my-secret-panel-abc123). Leading slashes are stripped automatically. Note: on public instances this path only works if DEGOOG_SETTINGS_PASSWORDS is also set.";s:4:"Type";s:8:"Variable";s:7:"Display";s:8:"advanced";s:8:"Required";s:5:"false";s:4:"Mask";s:5:"false";}s:5:"value";s:0:"";}i:10;a:2:{s:11:"@attributes";a:9:{s:4:"Name";s:15:"Public Instance";s:6:"Target";s:22:"DEGOOG_PUBLIC_INSTANCE";s:7:"Default";s:0:"";s:4:"Mode";s:0:"";s:11:"Description";s:194:"Optional. When set to a truthy value (e.g. true, 1), the instance runs in read-only mode: settings show only theme and engine toggles, no tabs; all server-side mutation APIs return Unauthorized.";s:4:"Type";s:8:"Variable";s:7:"Display";s:8:"advanced";s:8:"Required";s:5:"false";s:4:"Mask";s:5:"false";}s:5:"value";s:0:"";}i:11;a:2:{s:11:"@attributes";a:9:{s:4:"Name";s:14:"Distrust Proxy";s:6:"Target";s:21:"DEGOOG_DISTRUST_PROXY";s:7:"Default";s:3:"1|0";s:4:"Mode";s:0:"";s:11:"Description";s:505:"Optional. Controls whether Degoog trusts X-Forwarded-For, X-Real-IP and X-Forwarded-Proto headers for client IP, rate limiting, IP banning and HTTPS detection. Defaults to 1 (distrust), which is the safe choice when Degoog is exposed directly to the internet, since trusting these headers lets any client spoof their source IP and protocol. Set to 0 only when Degoog sits behind a reverse proxy (nginx, caddy, traefik, etc.) that you control and that strips or rewrites these headers on incoming requests.";s:4:"Type";s:8:"Variable";s:7:"Display";s:8:"advanced";s:8:"Required";s:5:"false";s:4:"Mask";s:5:"false";}s:5:"value";s:1:"1";}i:12;a:2:{s:11:"@attributes";a:9:{s:4:"Name";s:23:"Default Search Language";s:6:"Target";s:30:"DEGOOG_DEFAULT_SEARCH_LANGUAGE";s:7:"Default";s:5:"en-US";s:4:"Mode";s:0:"";s:11:"Description";s:115:"Default ISO 639-1 language code applied to all searches when no language is selected by the user (e.g. en, de, it).";s:4:"Type";s:8:"Variable";s:7:"Display";s:8:"advanced";s:8:"Required";s:5:"false";s:4:"Mask";s:5:"false";}s:5:"value";s:5:"en-US";}i:13;a:2:{s:11:"@attributes";a:9:{s:4:"Name";s:16:"UI Locale (i18n)";s:6:"Target";s:11:"DEGOOG_I18N";s:7:"Default";s:0:"";s:4:"Mode";s:0:"";s:11:"Description";s:148:"Optional. Forces the UI locale for all requests, overriding the Accept-Language header (e.g. en-US, fr-FR). Unset or empty: Accept-Language is used.";s:4:"Type";s:8:"Variable";s:7:"Display";s:8:"advanced";s:8:"Required";s:5:"false";s:4:"Mask";s:5:"false";}s:5:"value";s:0:"";}i:14;a:2:{s:11:"@attributes";a:9:{s:4:"Name";s:11:"Plugins Dir";s:6:"Target";s:18:"DEGOOG_PLUGINS_DIR";s:7:"Default";s:12:"data/plugins";s:4:"Mode";s:0:"";s:11:"Description";s:65:"Optional. Directory to load custom command and slot plugins from.";s:4:"Type";s:8:"Variable";s:7:"Display";s:8:"advanced";s:8:"Required";s:5:"false";s:4:"Mask";s:5:"false";}s:5:"value";s:0:"";}i:15;a:2:{s:11:"@attributes";a:9