SolidCraft features and upstream changes: https://github.com/bherbruck/solidcraft.[br][br]
Additional features provided by this Unraid integration:[br]
- Container packaging and Unraid template with persistent server files and resource/security limits.[br]
- Authenticated HTTP MCP gateway for local AI clients, with independent CAD sessions, bounded capacity and mandatory project selection into fixed real project folders; existing files remain in place.[br]
- Protected live file and session dashboard at /workspace: server-push updates, collapsed project folders and virtual groups for legacy root files, saved model details, PNG thumbnails, original icons, search, filters and downloads; selected projects, opened files, unsaved changes and new drafts.[br]
- Optional remembered browser login for 7 days, 30 days or until logout, independently of MCP authentication; the token is not retained in browser storage.[br]
- Shared-file revision checks to reject stale saves and accidental overwrites by parallel clients.[br]
- Operational logs for authentication and session allocation/release, with Unraid category colors, icons and the token file location.[br]
- Independent hosting of the upstream browser CAD app, with a protected shortcut to open saved models as independent browser copies; browser edits are not automatically written back to server files or MCP sessions.[br][br]
Linux amd64 only. Experimental software: latest contains the newest container build that passed modelling, persistence and web checks. Server designs and exports persist under /data/files. The dashboard uses the existing MCP token; it does not edit models.[br][br]
