:"Registry";s:44:"https://hub.docker.com/r/koenkk/zigbee2mqtt/";s:11:"TemplateURL";s:89:"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/digiblur/unraid-docker-templates/master/zigbee2mqtt.xml";s:5:"WebUI";s:24:"http://[IP]:[PORT:8080]/";s:7:"Network";s:6:"bridge";s:10:"Privileged";s:5:"false";s:7:"Support";s:83:"https://forums.unraid.net/topic/72033-support-digiblurs-docker-template-repository/";s:7:"Project";s:37:"https://github.com/koenkk/zigbee2mqtt";s:8:"Overview";s:1031:"Zigbee to MQTT bridge allows you to use your Zigbee devices without the vendors bridge or gateway. This template has the port 9442 forwarded for the front end on 8080 and does NOT require a USB passthrough to accomodate POE based adapters.

* All users MUST edit the configuration.yaml file in the appdata zigbee2mqtt folder to specify the serial port (or tcp port) for the zigbee adapter.  If you are using a USB adapter add it via dev serial ID and point it to /dev/zigbee for ease of use.  Example value: /dev/serial/by-id/usb-1a86_USB_Serial-if00-port0:/dev/zigbee		

