HOW IT WORKS
• Everyone on your Plex (or Jellyfin/Emby) server signs in and gets a "For You"-style Keep feed — a screenful of titles at a time, weighted toward the biggest space-hogs, so decisions happen a few at a time instead of all at once.
• For each title: Keep, "I don't care", or — for titles they requested via Seerr — "OK to delete" (the requester signing off).
• Keeps are protective: if anyone keeps a title, it's safe.
• The Big Picture dashboard shows what's reclaimable, what nobody has watched, and per-quality storage breakdowns.

NOTHING GETS DELETED
Unlike rule-based cleanup tools (e.g. Maintainerr), Keeparr never deletes anything — it crowdsources the human decisions and hands you the report; you delete in your media server or Sonarr/Radarr.

INTEGRATIONS (ALL OPTIONAL)
Tautulli watch history, Overseerr/Jellyseerr requests, and any number of Sonarr/Radarr instances for quality/tag data and match health.

SETUP
No required config beyond the port and appdata path — secrets are auto-generated on first start. The first user to sign in becomes the admin, so complete first-run setup on your trusted LAN before exposing Keeparr to the internet.";s:7:"Support";s:82:"https://forums.unraid.net/topic/199756-keeparr-decide-what-media-to-keep-together/";s:7:"Project";s:34:"https://github.com/drohack/Keeparr";s:11:"TemplateURL";s:75:"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/drohack/unraid-templates/main/keeparr.xml";s:6:"ReadMe";s:41:"https://github.com/drohack/Keeparr#readme";s:16:"ExtraSearchTerms";s:82:"plex jellyfin emby cleanup reclaim keep delete maintainerr overseerr sonarr radarr";s:6:"Config";a:7:{i:0;a:2:{s:11:"@attributes";a:9:{s:4:"Name";s:10:"WebUI Port";s:6:"Target";s:4:"3000";s:7:"Default";s:4:"8767";s:4:"Mode";s:3:"tcp";s:11:"Description";s:33:"Host port for the Keeparr web UI.";s:4:"Type";s:4:"Port";s:7:"Display";s:6:"always";s:8:"Required";s:4:"true";s:4:"Mask";s:5:"false";}s:5:"value";s:4:"8767";}i:1;a:2:{s:11:"@attributes";a:9:{s:4:"Name";s:7:"Appdata";s:6:"Target";s:5:"/data";s:7:"Default";s:25:"/mnt/user/appdata/keeparr";s:4:"Mode";s:2:"rw";s:11:"Description";s:45:"Keeparr's database, poster cache and backups.";s:4:"Type";s:4:"Path";s:7:"Display";s:6:"always";s:8:"Required";s:4:"true";s:4:"Mask";s:5:"false";}s:5:"value";s:25:"/mnt/user/appdata/keeparr";}i:2;a:2:{s:11:"@attributes";a:8:{s:4:"Name";s:14:"SESSION_SECRET";s:6:"Target";s:14:"SESSION_SECRET";s:7:"Default";s:0:"";s:11:"Description";s:369:"Optional — leave EMPTY and Keeparr auto-generates a secret on first start (stored in appdata as .session-secret). Set it only to manage the secret yourself; if you do, use a HIGH-ENTROPY value (e.g. `openssl rand -hex 32`) — it signs sessions AND encrypts your stored Plex/Tautulli/Seerr/Sonarr/Radarr tokens, so a weak value is unsafe. Never change it once in use.";s:4:"Type";s:8:"Variable";s:7:"Display";s:8:"advanced";s:8:"Required";s:5:"false";s:4:"Mask";s:4:"true";}s:5:"value