    Builds and installs the rtw88 A-series chip modules that Unraid ships disabled
    (CONFIG_RTW88_8821AU is not set), plus their firmware, giving you a wlan0
    interface you configure in Settings -> Network Settings. Because rtw88 is a
    mac80211 driver, [b]WPA3-SAE / PMF work[/b] (verified on RTL8811AU). Modules are
    rebuilt automatically per Unraid kernel release.[br][br]

    [b]Supported chipsets[/b][br]
    - RTL8811AU / RTL8821AU (AC600)[br]
    - RTL8812AU (AC1200)[br]
    - RTL8814AU (AC1900)[br][br]

    [b]Known adapters[/b] (non-exhaustive; the driver binds by USB ID)[br]
    RTL8811AU/8821AU: TP-Link Archer T2U Nano / T2U Plus / T2U v3, D-Link DWA-171,
    Edimax EW-7811UAC / EW-7811UTC, Netgear A6100, ASUS USB-AC51.[br]
    RTL8812AU: TP-Link Archer T4U / T4UH, ASUS USB-AC56, Alfa AWUS036AC / AWUS036ACH,
    D-Link DWA-182, Netgear A6210, Edimax EW-7822UAC, Tenda U12.[br]
    RTL8814AU: TP-Link Archer T9UH, ASUS USB-AC68, Alfa AWUS1900, D-Link DWA-192,
    Netgear A7000.[br][br]

