s:7:"Project";s:38:"https://github.com/flizzy27/Correctarr";s:7:"Network";s:6:"bridge";s:5:"Shell";s:2:"sh";s:10:"Privileged";s:5:"false";s:5:"WebUI";s:24:"http://[IP]:[PORT:8099]/";s:4:"Icon";s:72:"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/flizzy27/Correctarr/main/docs/icon.png";s:16:"ExtraSearchTerms";s:63:"radarr sonarr sabnzbd prowlarr automation cleanup import repair";s:8:"Overview";s:2669:"Correctarr finds and fixes the problems Radarr, Sonarr, SABnzbd and Prowlarr leave
    lying around because nobody is looking: wrongly matched releases, downloads that
    break today's profile rules, stuck imports, files that cannot be matched to a
    title, and leftover debris in the download folders.
    
    It works three ways at once: in real time through webhooks, on a short schedule
    for the queue, and on a full pass for the library and the indexers. 37 rules, and
    you decide per rule what happens when one of them finds something — from
    reporting it to blocklisting, importing, searching again or deleting. Conditions
    such as "wait six hours first" or "nothing over 20 GB" narrow that down further.
    
    It also builds quality profiles. Six questions — which resolutions,
    how good the sound, which languages and whether they are compulsory, which
    codec, what size, may a file be replaced — and it writes the profile
    and every custom format behind it into Radarr and Sonarr, showing you the
    whole plan first. Those profiles cannot cause a download loop: they never
    upgrade on score, only up the resolution ladder, which is finite. Ten ready
    presets cover the usual cases, and every profile comes with an estimate of
    the room it will take, measured on your own files, and of when the disk is
    full at the pace the library has been growing.
    
    A dry run switch stops every change at once, and it is ON after a fresh
    install: everything is found and reported, nothing is touched, until you have
    seen the findings and turned it off yourself.
    
    Guiding principle: when in doubt, do nothing. A rule that is not sure only
    reports. Better one finding left alone than one good file thrown away.
    
    SETUP
    Open the web interface after the first start and create an account (username and
    password). A setup assistant then walks you through connecting Radarr, Sonarr,
    SABnzbd and Prowlarr, testing each one as you go, and checking the paths.
    
    IMPORTANT, ABOUT THE PATHS
    The paths have to be the same inside this container as the ones Radarr and Sonarr
    see. Mount the download folders exactly the way you mounted them there. The
    overview page tells you whether that worked.
    
    LANGUAGES
    The interface is available in English and German and follows your browser by
    default.
    
    SECURITY
    The interface has its own login. If you already run Authelia, Authentik or basic
    auth in a reverse proxy in front of it, you can turn it off with AUTH=off. Without
    one of the two, the port does not belong on the open internet.";s:6:"Config";a:21:{i:0;a:2:{s:11:"@attributes";a:8:{s:4:"Name";s:13:"Web interface";s:6:"Target";s:4:"8099";s:7:"Default";s:4:"8099";s:4:"Mode";s:3:"tcp";s:4:"Type";s:4:"Port";s:7:"Display";s:6:"always";s:8:"Required";s:4:"true";s:11:"Description";s:151:"The port the interface is reachable on in a browser. If it clashes with something, put a different number here; the WebUI button follows automatically.";}s:5:"value";s:4:"8099";}i:1;a:2:{s:11:"@attributes";a:8:{s:4:"Name";s:25:"Configuration and history";s:6:"Target";s:7:"/config";s:7:"Default";s:28:"/mnt/user/appdata/correctarr";s:4:"Mode";s:2:"rw";s:4:"Type";s:4:"Path";s:7:"Display";s:6:"always";s:8:"Required";s:4:"true";s:11:"Description";s:131:"Holds the database, the settings, the services and the history. This directory survives a container update and must not be deleted.";}s:5:"value";s:28:"/mnt/user/appdata/correctarr";}i:2;a:2:{s:11:"@attributes";a:8:{s:4:"Name";s:18:"Finished downloads";s:6:"Target";s:10:"/downloads";s:7:"Default";s:0:"";s:4:"Mode";s:2:"rw";s:4:"Type";s:4:"Path";s:7:"Display";s:6:"always";s:8:"Required";s:4:"true";s:11:"Description";s:175:"The folder SABnzbd puts finished downloads in. This MUST be the same one Radarr and Sonarr see, otherwise Correctarr cannot find the files. Write access is needed for cleanup.";}s:5:"value";s:0:"";}i:3;a:2:{s:11:"@attributes";a:8:{s:4:"Name";s:20:"Incomplete downloads";s:6:"Target";s:11:"/incomplete";s:7:"Default";s:0:"";s:4:"Mode";s:2:"rw";s:4:"Type";s:4:"Path";s:7:"Display";s:6:"always";s:8:"Required";s:5:"false";s:11:"Description";s:71:"The working folder of SABnzbd. Leave empty if there is no separate one.";}s:5:"value";s:0:"";}i:4;a:2:{s:11:"@attributes";a:8:{s:4:"Name";s:6:"Movies";s:6:"Target";s:7:"/movies";s:7:"Default";s:0:"";s:4:"Mode";s:2:"ro";s:4:"Type";s:4:"Path";s:7:"Display";s:6:"always";s:8:"Required";s:5:"false";s:11:"Description";s:98:"The movie library. Read only. Opti