    It adds a second audio track, "Censored - English" by default, with the swearing silenced. The original is untouched and stays the default — in Plex or Jellyfin you pick the clean one from the audio menu. One file, two tracks, not two copies.
    
    Built for a household with a small child in the room, so when anything is uncertain the word gets muted.";s:10:"Screenshot";a:2:{i:0;s:75:"https://github.com/geoguy89/censarr/blob/main/docs/images/home.jpg?raw=true";i:1;s:78:"https://github.com/geoguy89/censarr/blob/main/docs/images/details.jpg?raw=true";}s:5:"WebUI";s:24:"http://[IP]:[PORT:8477]/";s:11:"TemplateURL";s:76:"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/geoguy89/unraid-templates/main/censarr.xml";s:4:"Icon";s:68:"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/geoguy89/censarr/main/web/icon.png";s:11:"ExtraParams";s:24:"--restart=unless-stopped";s:4:"Date";s:10:"2026-09-26";s:8:"Requires";s:156:"<br>&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Sonarr and Radarr, Plex, or Jellyfin, with the media mounted at the paths it reports. An NVIDIA GPU and Ollama are optional.<br>";s:6:"Config";a:5:{i:0;a:2:{s:11:"@attributes";a:9:{s:4:"Name";s:5:"WebUI";s:6:"Target";s:4:"8477";s:7:"Default";s:4:"8477";s:4:"Mode";s:3:"tcp";s:11:"Description";s:26:"The Censarr web interface.";s:4:"Type";s:4:"Port";s:7:"Display";s:6:"always";s:8:"Required";s:4:"true";s:4:"Mask";s:5:"false";}s:5:"value";s:4:"8477";}i:1;a:2:{s:11:"@attributes";a:9:{s:4:"Name";s:6:"Config";s:6:"Target";s:7:"/config";s:7:"Default";s:25:"/mnt/user/appdata/censarr";s:4:"Mode";s:2:"rw";s:11:"Description";s:54:"Settings, the job database and the cached transcripts.";s:4:"Type";s:4:"Path";s:7:"Display";s:6:"always";s:8:"Required";s:4:"true";s:4:"Mask";s:5:"false";}s:5:"value";s:25:"/mnt/user/appdata/censarr";}i:2;a:2:{s:11:"@attributes";a:9:{s:4:"Name";s:5:"Media";s:6:"Target";s:5:"/data";s:7:"Default";s:14:"/mnt/user/data";s:4:"Mode";s:2:"rw";s:11:"Description";s:217:"The CONTAINER PATH must be what your library reports. Sonarr, Radarr and Plex in containers usually report /data/media/..., so /data is right for them. Censarr opens those paths unchanged - there is no path rewriting.";s:4:"Type";s:4:"Path";s:7:"Display";s:6:"always";s:8:"Required";s:4:"true";s:4:"Mask";s:5:"false";}s:5:"value";s:14:"/mnt/user/data";}i:3;a:2:{s:11:"@attributes";a:9:{s:4:"Name";s:22:"NVIDIA_VISIBLE_DEVICES";s:6:"Target";s:22:"NVIDIA_VISIBLE_DEVICES";s:7:"Default";s:3:"all";s:4:"Mode";s:0:"";s:11:"Description";s:125:"NVIDIA only: the GPU used to transcribe. 'all', or a GPU UUID from nvidia-smi -L. Needs --runtime=nvidia in Extra Parameters.";s:4:"Type";s:8:"Variable";s:7:"Display";s:6:"always";s:8:"Required";s:5:"false";s:4:"Mask";s:5:"false";}s:5:"value";s:3:"all";}i:4;a:2:{s:11:"@attributes";a:9:{s:4:"Name";s:26:"NVIDIA_DRIVER_CAPABILITIES";s:6:"Target";s:26:"NVIDIA_DRIVER_CAPABILITIES";s:7:"Default";s:15:"compute,utility";s:4:"Mode";s:0:"";s:11:"Description";s:55:"NVIDIA only: what the container may use the driver for.";s:4:"Type";s:8:"Variable";s:7:"Display";s:8:"advanced";s:8:"Required";s:5:"false";s:4:"Mask";s:5:"false";}s:5:"value";s:15:"compute,utility";}}s:12:"TemplatePath";s:31:"/tmp/GitHub/AppFeed/censarr.xml";s:4:"Repo";s:21:"Geoguy89's Repository";s:12:"CategoryList";a:2:{i:0;s:14:"MediaApp-Video";i:1;s:15:"Tools-Utilities";}s:16:"ChangeLogPresent";s:1:"1";s:9:"downloads";i:54;s:9:"FirstSeen";i:1790698417;s:10:"LastUpdate";i:1790642896;s:14:"LastUpdateScan";i:1790698417;s:8:"Category";s:30:"MediaApp:Video Tools:Utilities";s:2:"ID";i:2139;s:11:"Displayable";b:1;s:6:"Author";s:8:"geoguy89";s:13:"DockerHubName";s:8:"cens-arr";s:8:"RepoName";s:21:"Geoguy89's Repository";s:10:"SortAuthor";s:8:"geoguy89";s:8:"SortName";s:8:"Cens Arr";s:6:"random";i:1833833398;s:9:"Blacklist";b:0;s:6:"MinVer";s:3:"6.0";s:4:"Path";s:110:"/tmp/community.applications/tempFiles/templates-community-apps/Geoguy89sRepository/geoguy89-CensArr-latest.xml";s:10:"Deprecated";b:0;s:10:"Compatible";b:1;s:16:"ModeratorComment";N;}i:2140;a:38:{s:4:"Name";s:9:"clockspan";s:10:"Repository";s:35:"ghcr.io/geransmith/clockspan:latest";s:8:"Registry";s:64:"https://github.com/geransmith/clockspan/pkgs/container/clockspan";s:7:"Network";s:6:"bridge";s:5:"Shell";s:2:"sh";s:10:"Privileged";s:5:"false";s:7:"Support";s:46:"https://github.com/geransmith/clockspan/issues";s:7:"Project";s:39:"https://github.com/geransmith/clockspan";s:8:"Overview";s:794:"Clockspan is a self-hosted, single-day focus sheet for getting through a workday with ADHD. One page: a punch-style timeclock that works out when lunch is due and when the day ends, a short list of the day's priorities, a focus timer that logs what you did, and a retrospective that puts the plan next to what happened. Every day is saved, and alarms fire as deadlines approach. It works on phones and installs to the Home Screen.

The default sign-in mode, none, has no login: anyone who can reach the port can use it. Keep it for a LAN you trust, or behind a reverse proxy that signs people in itself, with the port reachable from the internet only through that proxy; set App URL when the proxy serves it on a domain. Otherwise pick local or oidc before you expose Clockspan to the internet.";s:16:"ExtraSearchTerms";s:72:"adhd timeclock punch clock focus timer pomodoro priorities time tracking";s:5:"WebUI";s:24:"http://[IP]:[PORT:8080]/";s:11:"TemplateURL";s:80:"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/geransmith/clockspan/main/unraid/clockspan.xml";s:4:"Icon";s:92:"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/geransmith/clockspan/main/client/public/icons/icon-512.png";s:7:"License";s:3:"MIT";s:10:"Screenshot";a:3:{i:0;s:97:"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/geransmith/clockspan/main/docs/screenshots/sheet-phone-dark.png";i:1;s:94:"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/geransmith/clockspan/main/docs/screenshots/sheet-desktop.png";i:2;s:88:"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/geransmith/clockspan/main/docs/screenshots/history.png";}s:6:"Config";a:15:{i:0;a:2:{s:11:"@attributes";a:9:{s:4:"Name";s:11:"Web UI port";s:6:"Target";s:4:"8080";s:7:"Default";s:4:"8080";s:4:"Mode";s:3:"tcp";s:11:"Description";s:20:"Port for the web UI.";s:4:"Type";s:4:"Port";s:7:"Display";s:6:"always";s:8:"Required";s:4:"true";s:4:"Mask";s:5:"false";}s:5:"value";s:4:"8080";}i:1;a:2:{s:11:"@attributes";a:9:{s:4:"Name";s:4:"Data";s:6:"Target";s:5:"/data";s:7:"Default";s:27:"/mnt/user/appdata/clockspan";s:4:"Mode";s:2:"rw";s:11:"Description";s:85:"Folder for the database (focus.db). The container takes ownership of it as PUID:PGID.";s:4:"Type";s:4:"Path";s:7:"Display";s:6:"always";s:8:"Required";s:4:"true";s:4:"Mask";s:5:"false";}s:5:"value";s:27:"/mnt/user/appdata/clockspan";}i:2;a:2:{s:11:"@attributes";a:8:{s:4:"Name";s:12:"Sign-in mode";s:6:"Target";s:9:"AUTH_MODE";s:7:"Default";s:15:"none|local|oidc";s:11:"Description";s:289:"none: no sign-in (LAN, or behind your proxy's own auth). local: the first visit creates the admin account, using the setup code in the container's log, and the admin adds users in Settings. oidc: sign in with Authentik or another OpenID Connect provider; needs App URL and the OIDC fields.";s:4:"Type";s:8:"Variable";s:7:"Display";s:6:"always";s:8:"Required";s:4:"true";s:4:"Mask";s:5:"false";}s:5:"value";s:4:"none";}i:3;a:2:{s:11:"@attributes";a:8:{s:4:"Name";s:7:"App URL";s:6:"Target";s:7:"APP_URL";s:7:"Default";s:0:"";s:11:"Description";s:321:"Public URL of the app, scheme and host only, e.g. https://focus.example.com (a path is ignored with a warning). Required for oidc, and recommended whenever you reach the app through a domain. With https the session cookie is Secure and HSTS is on. Your provider's redirect URI must be this URL followed by /auth/callback.";s:4:"Type";s:8:"Variable";s:7:"Display";s:6:"always";s:8:"Required";s:5:"false";s:4:"Mask";s:5:"false";}s:5:"value";s:0:"";}i:4;a:2:{s:11:"@attributes";a:8:{s:4:"Name";s:18:"Allowed host names";s:6:"Target";s:13:"ALLOWED_HOSTS";s:7:"Default";s:0:"";s:11:"Description";s:350:"With sign-in mode none: other names the app answers to, comma-separated (focus.example.com, or .lan for every name under it). IP addresses, localhost, one-word names like tower, .localhost, .local, .home.arpa and .internal names and App URL's always work. Any other name is refused, which keeps a web page from reaching the app through DNS rebinding.";s:4:"Type";s:8:"Variable";s:7:"Display";s:8:"advanced";s:8:"Required";s:5:"false";s:4:"Mask";s:5:"false";}s:5:"value";s:0:"";}i:5;a:2:{s:11:"@attributes";a:8:{s:4:"Name";s:15:"Trusted proxies";s:6:"Target";s:11:"TRUST_PROXY";s:7:"Default";s:0:"";s:11:"Description";s:240:"Behind a reverse proxy (Nginx Proxy Manager, SWAG, Traefik): the number of proxies between the internet and the container, usually 1. Blank: none. Never true, which trusts any X-Forwarded-For a client sends and defeats the login rate limit.";s:4:"Type";s:8:"Variable";s:7:"Display";s:8:"advanced";s:8:"Required";s:5:"false";s:4:"Mask";s:5:"false";}s:5:"value";s:0:"";}i:6;a:2:{s:11:"@attributes";a:8:{s:4:"Name";s:13:"Secure cookie";s:6:"Target";s:13:"COOKIE_SECURE";s:7:"Default";s:0:"";s:11:"Description";s:101:"true or false forces the session cookie's Secure flag and HSTS. Blank: both on when App URL is https.";s:4:"Type";s:8:"Variable";s:7:"Display";s:8:"advanced";s:8:"Required";s:5:"false";s:4:"Mask";s:5:"false";}s:5:"value";s:0:"";}i:7;a:2:{s:11:"@attributes";a:8:{s:4:"Name";s:12:"Session days";s:6:"Target";s:16:"SESSION_TTL_DAYS";s:7:"Default";s:2:"30";s:11:"Description";s:33:"Sliding session lifetime in days.";s:4:"Type";s:8:"Variable";s:7:"Display";s:8:"advanced";s:8:"Required";s:5:"false";s:4:"Mask";s:5:"false";}s:5:"value";s:2:"30";}i:8;a:2:{s:11:"@attributes";a:8:{s:4:"Name";s:9:"Keep days";s:6:"Target";s:14:"RETENTION_DAYS";s:7:"Default";s:0:"";s:11:"Description";s:240:"Server-wide ceiling on history, in days (30 to 3650; any other value stops the app with a message in the log): every user's older days are deleted every few hours. Blank keeps everything; users can pick a shorter limit in Settings → Data.";s:4:"Type";s:8:"Variable";s:7:"Display";s:8:"advanced";s:8:"Required";s:5:"false";s:4:"Mask";s:5:"false";}s:5:"value";s:0:"";}i:9;a:2:{s:11:"@attributes";a:8:{s:4:"Name";s:11:"OIDC issuer";s:6:"Target";s:11:"OIDC_ISSUER";s:7:"Default";s:0:"";s:11:"Description";s:98:"For oidc, an https:// URL. Authentik: Providers → your provider → OpenID Configuration Issuer.";s:4:"Type";s:8:"Variable";s:7:"Display";s:8:"advanced";s:8:"Required";s:5:"false";s:4:"Mask";s:5:"false";}s:5:"value";s:0:"";}i:10;a:2:{s:11:"@attributes";a:8:{s:4:"Name";s:14:"OIDC client ID";s:6:"Target";s:14:"OIDC_CLIENT_ID";s:7:"Default";s:0:"";s:11:"Description";s:43:"For oidc: the client ID from your provider.";s:4:"Type";s:8:"Variable";s:7:"Display";s:8:"advanced";s:8:"Required";s:5:"false";s:4:"Mask";s:5:"false";}s:5:"value";s:0:"";}i:11;a:2:{s:11:"@attributes";a:8:{s:4:"Name";s:18:"OIDC client secret";s:6:"Target";s:18:"OIDC_CLIENT_SECRET";s:7:"Default";s:0:"";s:11:"Description";s:47:"For oidc: the client secret from your provider.";s:4:"Type";s:8:"Variable";s:7:"Display";s:8:"advanced";s:8:"Required";s:5:"false";s:4:"Mask";s:4:"true";}s:5:"value";s:0:"";}i:12;a:2:{s:11:"@attributes";a:8:{s:4:"Name";s:11:"OIDC scopes";s:6:"Target";s:11:"OIDC_SCOPES";s:7:"Default";s:20:"openid profile email";s:11:"Description";s:32:"For oidc: the scopes to request.";s:4:"Type";s:8:"Variable";s:7:"Display";s:8:"advanced";s:8:"Required";s:5:"false";s:4:"Mask";s:5:"false";}s:5:"value";s:20:"openid profile email";}i:13;a:2:{s:11:"@attributes";a:8:{s:4:"Name";s:4:"PUID";s:6:"Target";s:4:"PUID";s:7:"Default";s:2:"99";s:11:"Description";s:88:"User ID that owns the data folder and runs the app. 99 is Unraid's nobody; 0 keeps root.";s:4:"Type";s:8:"Variable";s:7:"Display";s:8:"advanced";s:8:"Required";s:5:"false";s:4:"Mask";s:5:"false";}s:5:"value";s:2:"99";}i:14;a:2:{s:11:"@attributes";a:8:{s:4:"Name";s:4:"PGID";s:6:"Target";s:4:"PGID";s:7:"Default";s:3:"100";s:11:"Description";s:45:"Group ID for the same. 100 is Unraid's users.";s:4:"Type";s:8:"Variable";s:7:"Display";s:8:"advanced";s:8:"Required";s:5:"false";s:4:"Mask";s:5:"false";}s:5:"value";s:3:"100";}}s:12:"TemplatePath";s:40:"/tmp/GitHub/AppFeed/unraid/clockspan.xml";s:4:"Repo";s:23:"geransmith's Repository";s:12:"CategoryList";a:2:{i:0;s:12:"Productivity";i:1;s:15:"Tools-Utilities";}s:16:"ChangeLogPresent";s:1:"1";s:9:"FirstSeen";i:1790280948;s:8:"Category";s:29:"Productivity: Tools:Utilities";s:2:"ID";i:2140;s:11:"Displayable";b:1;s:6:"Author";s:10:"geransmith";s:13:"DockerHubName";s:9:"clockspan";s:8:"RepoName";s:23:"geransmith's Repository";s:10:"SortAuthor";s:10:"geransmith";s:8:"SortName";s:9:"clockspan";s:6:"random";i:1561890043;s:9:"Blacklist";b:0;s:6:"MinVer";s:3:"6.0";s:4:"Path";s:116:"/tmp/community.applications/tempFiles/templates-community-apps/geransmithsRepository/geransmith-clockspan-latest.xml";s:4:"Date";N;s:11:"BrandNewApp";b:1;s:10:"Deprecated";b:0;s:10:"Compatible";b:1;s:16:"ModeratorComment";N;}i:2141;a:39:{s:4:"Name";s:26:"Unraid Docker Page Speedup";s:8:"Overview";s:1118:"Makes the Docker page load faster and controls refresh rate on your server. Unraid's Docker page calls getTemplateValue() around nine times per container, and each call re-parses every container template XML from the flash drive, so the work grows with containers multiplied by templates. This plugin adds two in-request caches to DockerClient.php so each template is read once per request, which on a server with well over a hundred containers took a cold page load from roughly 38 seconds to 4. It also lets you throttle the live stats refresh, which by default runs docker stats against every container once per second and repaints the whole table each time. Both changes are made to the copy of the webGUI that runs in RAM, never to the flash drive. The template patch only applies if four exact code anchors match, so it cleanly does nothing on an Unraid build it does not recognise, and the result is checked with php -l and rolled back automatically if it does not lint. A stock backup of each file is kept, the settings page can disable either change at any time, and uninstalling restores both files to stock.";s:9:"PluginURL";s:96:"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/ghzgod/unraid-docker-page-speedup/main/docker.page.speedup.plg";s:12:"PluginAuthor";s:6:"ghzgod";s:7:"Project";s:52:"https://github.com/ghzgod/unraid-docker-page-speedup";s:6:"ReadMe";s:82:"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/ghzgod/unraid-docker-page-speedup/main/README.md";s:4:"Icon";s:81:"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/ghzgod/unraid-docker-page-speedup/main/icon.png";s:6:"IconFA";s:4:"bolt";s:7:"License";s:3:"MIT";s:11:"TemplateURL";s:97:"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/ghzgod/unraid-ca-templates/main/plugins/docker.page.speedup.xml";s:12:"TemplatePath";s:51:"/tmp/GitHub/AppFe