s:5:"false";s:7:"Support";s:45:"https://github.com/halvar20000/fiefdom/issues";s:7:"Project";s:38:"https://github.com/halvar20000/fiefdom";s:8:"Overview";s:1125:"An isometric castle-builder in the spirit of Stronghold Crusader, played in the browser. Build a settlement in the desert, run the food, ale and weapon chains, raise a garrison and hold your ground against an enemy lord who builds his own economy under the same rules you do.

⚔ Multiplayer: two to four players on one map, allied or every lord for himself, with AI lords to fill the empty seats. Players register on your server with a name, an email and a password — nothing to configure, no mail server, no external login.

⚙ Nothing to set up: no database, no API keys. Set the port, keep the Saves path on appdata, start it, open the WebUI.

💾 Saved games, custom maps and accounts are stored on the server under /data — map it to appdata and they survive updates and are the same in every browser. (Leave it unmapped and the game falls back to per-browser storage and nobody can register.)

The simulation runs in the browser, even in a match: the container serves the files, keeps the saves and passes messages between players, so it uses almost no CPU or memory. A WebGL-capable browser is required.";s:5:"WebUI";s:21:"http://[IP]:[PORT:80]";s:11:"TemplateURL";s:80:"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/halvar20000/fiefdom/main/templates/fiefdom.xml";s:4:"Icon";s:67:"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/halvar20000/fiefdom/main/icon.png";s:8:"Requires";s:277:"Nothing. A browser with WebGL support is all that is needed on the client side. For players outside your network to join a match, the game needs to be reachable from outside — a Cloudflare Tunnel or a reverse proxy will do, as long as it passes WebSocket connections through.";s:6:"Config";a:2:{i:0;a:2:{s:11:"@attributes";a:9:{s:4:"Name";s:10:"WebUI Port";s:6:"Target";s:2:"80";s:7:"Default";s:4:"8080";s:4:"Mode";s:3:"tcp";s:11:"Description";s:28:"Port the game is reached on.";s:4:"Type";s:4:"Port";s:7:"Display";s:6:"always";s:8:"Required";s:4:"true";s:4:"Mask";s:5:"false";}s:5:"value";s:4:"8080";}i:1;a:2:{s:11:"@attributes";a:9:{s:4:"Name";s:5:"Saves";s:6:"Target";s:5:"/data";s:7:"Default";s:25:"/mnt/user/appdata/fiefdom";s:4:"Mode";s:2:"rw";s:11:"Description";s:202:"Where saved games, custom maps and player accounts are kept. Leave it on appdata: this folder holds the accounts and the key that signs their sign-ins, so losing it means everyone has to register again.";s:4:"Type";s:4:"Path";s:7:"Display";s:6:"always";s:8:"Required";s:4:"true";s:4:"Mask";s:5:"false";}s:5:"value";s:25:"/mnt/user/appdata/fiefdom";}}s:12:"TemplatePath";s:41:"/tmp/GitHub/AppFeed/templates/fiefdom.xml";s:4:"Repo";s:35:"fiefdom_castlebuilding's Repository";s:12:"CategoryList";a:2:{i:0;s:11:"GameServers";i:1;s:14:"MediaApp-Other";}s:9:"FirstSeen";i:1787313925;s:8:"Category";s:27:"GameServers: MediaApp:Other";s:2:"ID";i:2167;s:11:"Displayable";b:1;s:6:"Author";s:11:"halvar20000";s:13:"DockerHubName";s:7:"fiefdom";s:8:"RepoName";s:35:"f