nd";a:3:{i:0;i:2099549;i:1;i:2131730;i:2;i:2266398;}s:8:"trending";d:5.942;s:6:"trends";a:2:{i:0;d:1.51;i:1;d:5.942;}s:10:"trendsDate";a:2:{i:0;i:1788523586;i:1;i:1791953108;}s:9:"FirstSeen";i:1785928030;s:10:"LastUpdate";i:1791779030;s:14:"LastUpdateScan";i:1791953108;s:8:"Category";s:29:"HomeAutomation: Productivity:";s:2:"ID";i:2186;s:11:"Displayable";b:0;s:6:"Author";s:9:"karsten13";s:13:"DockerHubName";s:11:"magicmirror";s:8:"RepoName";s:24:"magicmirror's Repository";s:10:"SortAuthor";s:9:"karsten13";s:8:"SortName";s:11:"MagicMirror";s:6:"random";i:1897165243;s:9:"Blacklist";b:0;s:4:"Path";s:71:"/tmp/community.applications/tempFiles/templates-community-apps/2186.xml";s:10:"Deprecated";b:0;s:10:"trendDelta";d:4.432;s:12:"trendAverage";d:3.726;s:10:"BranchName";s:13:"debian-server";s:17:"BranchDescription";s:251:"Debian 13 based, server-only mode. Largest image, but the broadest compatibility for modules that compile native dependencies, and the only variant shipping /bin/bash. Change the template's Console Shell Command from sh to bash if you select this one.";s:11:"Description";N;s:10:"Compatible";b:1;s:16:"ModeratorComment";N;}i:2187;a:55:{s:4:"Name";s:11:"MagicMirror";s:10:"Repository";s:28:"karsten13/magicmirror:alpine";s:8:"Registry";s:46:"https://hub.docker.com/r/karsten13/magicmirror";s:7:"Network";s:6:"bridge";s:5:"Shell";s:2:"sh";s:10:"Privileged";s:5:"false";s:11:"ExtraParams";s:13:"--user 99:100";s:4:"Icon";s:75:"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/heckpiet/magicmirror-unraid/main/icon.svg";s:5:"WebUI";s:24:"http://[IP]:[PORT:8080]/";s:8:"Overview";s:1701:"MagicMirror² is an open source modular smart mirror platform. It turns a display behind a two-way mirror, a wall tablet or simply a browser tab into a personal dashboard showing clock, calendar, weather, news and hundreds of community modules.[br][br]This template runs MagicMirror² in server-only mode, the correct mode for a headless Unraid server: the interface is served over HTTP and rendered in any browser or on a separate client device such as a Raspberry Pi. The electron scenario, which draws to a locally attached display, will not work on Unraid and is deliberately not offered.[br][br][b]No setup is required.[/b] Install it, open the WebUI, done. On first start the image writes a working config.js that listens on all interfaces and already permits the usual private network ranges, including 10.x, 172.16-31.x and 192.168.x. The template also runs the container as user 99:100 so that everything it writes into appdata is owned nobody:users like the rest of your Unraid shares.[br][br]That same config.js is where you enable modules and change the layout, at /mnt/user/appdata/magicmirror/config/config.js. Third party modules go into the modules directory. See https://docs.magicmirror.builders and https://modules.magicmirror.builders.[br][br][b]Security note.[/b] MagicMirror² has no built-in authentication. Anyone who can reach the port sees your calendar and whatever else you configure. Keep it on a trusted network and do not forward the port. Use a VPN or an authenticated HTTPS reverse proxy for remote access.[br][br]The container image is built and maintained by Karsten Hassel at https://gitlab.com/khassel/magicmirror. This template provides only the Unraid packaging.";s:7:"Support";s:53:"https://github.com/heckpiet/magicmirror-unraid/issues";s:7:"Project";s:38:"https://khassel.gitlab.io/magicmirror/";s:11:"TemplateURL";s:92:"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/heckpiet/magicmirror-unraid/main/templates/magicmirror.xml";s:6:"ReadMe";s:76:"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/heckpiet/magicmirror-unraid/main/README.md";s:16:"ExtraSearchTerms";s:112:"magicmirror magic mirror smart mirror smartmirror dashboard kiosk wall display calendar weather news modules mm2";s:8:"Requires";s:284:"No manual setup. The container runs as user 99:100 through Extra Parameters so that files it writes into appdata are owned nobody:users; leave that setting in place. MagicMirror² is unau