as changes land, for testing new features before release";s:11:"Description";N;s:10:"Compatible";b:1;s:16:"ModeratorComment";N;}i:2196;a:35:{s:4:"Name";s:9:"DiscVault";s:10:"Repository";s:41:"ghcr.io/helmerznl/discvault-launcher:beta";s:8:"Registry";s:15:"https://ghcr.io";s:7:"Network";s:6:"bridge";s:5:"Shell";s:2:"sh";s:10:"Privileged";s:5:"false";s:7:"Support";s:90:"https://forums.unraid.net/topic/198808-support-discvault-physical-disc-collection-manager/";s:7:"Project";s:47:"https://github.com/helmerzNL/DiscVault-Launcher";s:8:"Overview";s:621:"DiscVault launcher for Unraid Community Apps. It updates and manages the PostgreSQL-backed DiscVault 26 stack while reusing the existing DiscVault beta appdata directory for migration.

There are two channels. Use ghcr.io/helmerznl/discvault-launcher:latest for the production release, or ghcr.io/helmerznl/discvault-launcher:beta for the beta release.

If your Repository is still set to discvault-launcher:v26-beta or :v26, those tags keep working as aliases of :beta and :latest for now, but switch to the new names when convenient. The :dev, :stable and :legacy tags are no longer published; move to :latest or :beta.";s:5:"WebUI";s:21:"http://[IP]:[PORT:80]";s:4:"Icon";s:87:"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/helmerzNL/DiscVault/main/app/frontend/favicon-192.png";s:6:"Config";a:23:{i:0;a:2:{s:11:"@attributes";a:9:{s:4:"Name";s:17:"DiscVault Channel";s:6:"Target";s:17:"DISCVAULT_CHANNEL";s:7:"Default";s:23:"auto|latest|beta|manual";s:4:"Mode";s:0:"";s:11:"Description";s:343:"Which DiscVault release to run. auto follows the channel built into this launcher image (matching the Repository above). latest deploys discvault:latest, beta deploys discvault:beta. manual deploys whatever you put in DiscVault Image below - if that reference does not exist, the launcher falls back to discvault:latest and says so in the log.";s:4:"Type";s:8:"Variable";s:7:"Display";s:6:"always";s:8:"Required";s:4:"true";s:4:"Mask";s:5:"false";}s:5:"value";s:4:"auto";}i:1;a:2:{s:11:"@attributes";a:9:{s:4:"Name";s:37:"DiscVault Image (manual channel only)";s:6:"Target";s:15:"DISCVAULT_IMAGE";s:7:"Default";s:4:"auto";s:4:"Mode";s:0:"";s:11:"Description";s:357:"Only used when DiscVault Channel is set to manual; ignored otherwise. Accepts any DiscVault tag name such as latest, stable, v26, beta, v26-beta, dev or v26.7.7, or a full image reference. Digest pinning is supported, for example ghcr.io/helmerznl/discvault:beta@sha256:digest - note that a pinned digest disables automatic updates until you change it back.";s:4:"Type";s:8:"Variable";s:7:"Display";s:6:"always";s:8:"Required";s:5:"false";s:4:"Mask";s:5:"false";}s:5:"value";s:4:"auto";}i:2;a:2:{s:11:"@attributes";a:9:{s:4:"Name";s:11:"Web UI Port";s:6:"Target";s:2:"80";s:7:"Default";s:4:"6080";s:4:"Mode";s:3:"tcp";s:11:"Description";s:85:"DiscVault web interface. The launcher proxies this port to the DiscVault Next API/UI.";s:4:"Type";s:4:"Port";s:7:"Display";s:6:"always";s:8:"Required";s:4:"true";s:4:"Mask";s:5:"false";}s:5:"value";s:4:"6080";}i:3;a:2:{s:11:"@attributes";a:9:{s:4:"Name";s:9:"Data Path";s:6:"Target";s:5:"/data";s:7:"Default";s:27:"/mnt/user/appdata/discvault";s:4:"Mode";s:2:"rw";s:11:"Description";s:102:"Existing DiscVault beta appdata path. Kept for compatibility with the current beta container template.";s:4:"Type";s:4:"Path";s:7:"Display";s:6:"always";s:8:"Required";s:4:"true";s:4:"Mask";s:5:"false";}s:5:"value";s:27:"/mnt/user/appdata/discvault";}i:4;a:2:{s:11:"@attributes";a:9:{s:4:"Name";s:33:"Existing DiscVault Host Data Path";s:6:"Target";s:23:"DISCVAULT_DATA_DIR_HOST";s:7:"Default";s:27:"/mnt/user/appdata/discvault";s:4:"Mode";s:0:"";s:11:"Description";s:143:"Host path of the existing DiscVault beta appdata. Must match Data Path above so the managed stack can mount the same data from the Docker host.";s:4:"Type";s:8:"Variable";s:7:"Display";s:6:"always";s:8:"Required";s:4:"true";s:4:"Mask";s:5:"false";}s:5:"value";s:27:"/mnt/user/appdata/discvault";}i:5;a:2:{s:11:"@attributes";a:9:{s:4:"Name";s:20:"PostgreSQL Data Path";s:6:"Target";s:32:"DISCVAULT_POSTGRES_DATA_DIR_HOST";s:7:"Default";s:36:"/mnt/user/appdata/discvault-postgres";s:4:"Mode";s:0:"";s:11:"Description";s:229:"Host path where the launcher stores PostgreSQL data. Use a directory of its own: PostgreSQL only reads the password when it first initialises this directory, so reusing one from another install keeps that install&apos;s password.";s:4:"Type";s:8:"Variable";s:7:"Display";s:6:"always";s:8:"Required";s:4:"true";s:4:"Mask";s:5:"false";}s:5:"value";s:36:"/mnt/user/appdata/discvault-postgres";}i:6;a:2:{s:11:"@attributes";a:9:{s:4:"Name";s:20:"Launcher Config Path";s:6:"Target";s:7:"/config";s:7:"Default";s:36:"/mnt/user/appdata/discvault-launcher";s:4:"Mode";s:2:"rw";s:11:"Description";s:72:"Launcher state, generated Compose file, generated secrets and boot logs.";s:4:"Ty