isper-asr-webservice/issues";s:7:"Project";s:51:"https://github.com/ahmetoner/whisper-asr-webservice";s:8:"Overview";s:916:"CPU-ONLY Whisper ASR Webservice (no NVIDIA GPU required). Same faster-whisper HTTP API with word-level timestamps, but transcription runs on the CPU + system RAM. It WORKS but is MUCH slower than GPU - expect roughly 5-15x longer (a 50-min episode can take well over an hour). This uses the SAME image as the GPU template on purpose, so WhisperX and the SubSyncarr multilingual patch are guaranteed compatible; it simply never requests a GPU and sets ASR_DEVICE=cpu. (The image carries CUDA libraries it won't use - it still runs fine on a GPU-less box. Advanced users can swap the Repository tag to onerahmet/openai-whisper-asr-webservice:latest for a smaller CPU image, but then verify the patch files still match.) NOTE: WhisperX word-alignment on CPU is extremely slow, so SubSyncarr skips or down-scopes alignment on CPU-only setups. Leave the two "SubSyncarr patch" mappings empty if you do not use SubSyncarr.";s:5:"WebUI";s:28:"http://[IP]:[PORT:9000]/docs";s:11:"TemplateURL";s:97:"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/hernandito/docker-templates/master/hernando/whisper-asr-cpu.xml";s:4:"Icon";s:93:"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/hernandito/docker-templates/master/hernando/whisper-asr.png";s:11:"ExtraParams";s:12:"--memory=12g";s:8:"Requires";s:352:"No GPU and no Nvidia Driver plugin needed. Give it plenty of RAM (large-v3 int8 on CPU wants ~6-10 GB; the --memory cap in Extra Parameters is a safety ceiling - adjust to taste). First start downloads the model (large-v3 ~3 GB) to the Models path below. If you also run the GPU container, change this one's host PORT (e.g. 9001) so they don't collide.";s:6:"Config";a:11:{i:0;a:2:{s:11:"@attributes";a:9:{s:4:"Name";s:16:"WebUI / API Port";s:6:"Target";s:4:"9000";s:7:"Default";s:4:"9000";s:4:"Mode";s:3:"tcp";s:11:"Description";s:115:"HTTP API + Swagger docs (http://host:9000/docs). Change the host port if a GPU Whisper container already uses 9000.";s:4:"Type";s:4:"Port";s:7:"Display";s:6:"always";s:8:"Required";s:4:"true";s:4:"Mask";s:5:"false";}s:5:"value";s:4:"9000";}i:1;a:2:{s:11:"@attributes";a:9:{s:4:"Name";s:10:"ASR_ENGINE";s:6:"Target";s:10:"ASR_ENGINE";s:7:"Default";s:14:"faster_whisper";s:4:"Mode";s:0:"";s:11:"Description";s:85:"Use faster_whisper (supports SubSyncarr's multilingual=true). Do NOT set to whisperx.";s:4:"Type";s:8:"Variable";s:7:"Display";s:6:"always";s:8:"Required";s:4:"true";s:4:"Mask";s:5:"false";}s:5:"value";s:14:"faster_whisper";}i:2;a:2:{s:11:"@attributes";a:9:{s:4:"Name";s:9:"ASR_MODEL";s:6:"Target";s:9:"ASR_MODEL";s:7:"Default";s:8:"large-v3";s:4:"Mode";s:0:"";s:11:"Description";s:113:"Model: tiny, base, small, medium, large-v3. On a weak CPU, 'medium' or 'small' trade accuracy for a big speed-up.";s:4:"Type";s:8:"Variable";s:7:"Display";s:6:"always";s:8:"Required";s:4:"true";s:4:"Mask";s:5:"false";}s:5:"value";s:8:"large-v3";}i:3;a:2:{s:11:"@attributes";a:9:{s:4:"Name";s:16:"ASR_QUANTIZATION";s:6:"Target";s:16:"ASR_QUANTIZATION";s:7:"Default";s:4:"int8";s:4:"Mode";s:0:"";s:11:"Description";s:82:"int8 = smallest + fastest on CPU. (float32/float16 are slower and heavier on CPU.)";s:4:"Type";s:8:"Variable";s:7:"Display";s:6:"always";s:8:"Required";s:4:"true";s:4:"Mask";s:5:"false";}s:5:"value";s:4:"int8";}i:4;a:2:{s:11:"@attributes";a:9:{s:4:"Name";s:14:"ASR_MODEL_PATH";s:6:"Target";s:14:"ASR_MODEL_PATH";s:7:"Default";s:13:"/data/whisper";s:4:"Mode";s:0:"";s:11:"Description";s:92:"Where models are stored INSIDE the container. Must match the Models host-path mapping below.";s:4:"Type";s:8:"Variable";s:7:"Display";s:6:"always";s:8:"Required";s:4:"true";s:4:"Mask";s:5:"false";}s:5:"value";s:13:"/data/whisper";}i:5;a:2:{s:11:"@attributes";a:9:{s:4:"Name";s:10:"ASR_DEVICE";s:6:"Target";s:10:"ASR_DEVICE";s:7:"Default";s:3:"cpu";s:4:"Mode";s:0:"";s:11:"Description";s:63:"cpu = run entirely on the processor + RAM. No GPU is requested.";s:4:"Type";s