;s:10:"Deprecated";b:0;s:10:"BranchName";s:4:"beta";s:17:"BranchDescription";s:82:"Beta - jeweils aktuellster Stand von main, ungetestet fuer den produktiven Einsatz";s:11:"Description";N;s:10:"Compatible";b:1;s:16:"ModeratorComment";N;}i:2324;a:36:{s:4:"Name";s:11:"Backblaze64";s:10:"Repository";s:45:"ghcr.io/iamfoz/backblaze-personal-wine:latest";s:8:"Registry";s:101:"https://github.com/iamfoz/backblaze-64-personal-wine-container/pkgs/container/backblaze-personal-wine";s:11:"TemplateURL";s:122:"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/iamfoz/backblaze-64-personal-wine-container/main/templates/backblaze-personal-backup.xml";s:7:"Network";s:6:"bridge";s:5:"Shell";s:4:"bash";s:10:"Privileged";s:5:"false";s:7:"Support";s:108:"https://forums.unraid.net/topic/199284-support-backblaze-64-backblaze-personal-backup-10x-64-bit-under-wine/";s:7:"Project";s:62:"https://github.com/iamfoz/backblaze-64-personal-wine-container";s:8:"Overview";s:899:"Backblaze Personal Backup running under Wine (64-bit Windows environment) on Ubuntu 24.04. Provides a web-based GUI via browser or VNC, and keeps Backblaze updated to the latest version on each restart. Includes a live upload dashboard (bb-monitor, run from the container console), backup-aware health status on this Docker page, optional automatic recovery from stalled backups, and built-in diagnostic tools (bb-doctor, bb-report, bb-version).

Note on the beta tag: the :beta image carries two patches to Wine's socket code that are not in the stable images. One is submitted upstream. The other is a workaround that deliberately differs from how Windows behaves, is not being submitted, and will be removed once the proper fix lands in Wine. It is there because it roughly triples upload throughput on high-latency connections. Use the stable tags unless upload speed is the reason you are here.";s:5:"WebUI";s:24:"http://[IP]:[PORT:5800]/";s:4:"Icon";s:59:"https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/gh/selfhst/icons/png/backblaze.png";s:6:"Config";a:14:{i:0;a:2:{s:11:"@attributes";a:9:{s:4:"Name";s:11:"Web UI Port";s:6:"Target";s:4:"5800";s:7:"Default";s:4:"5800";s:4:"Mode";s:3:"tcp";s:11:"Description";s:38:"Port for the browser-based GUI (HTTP).";s:4:"Type";s:4:"Port";s:7:"Display";s:6:"always";s:8:"Required";s:4:"true";s:4:"Mask";s:5:"false";}s:5:"value";s:4:"5800";}i:1;a:2:{s:11:"@attributes";a:9:{s:4:"Name";s:8:"VNC Port";s:6:"Target";s:4:"5900";s:7:"Default";s:4:"5900";s:4:"Mode";s:3:"tcp";s:11:"Description";s:34:"Port for direct VNC client access.";s:4:"Type";s:4:"Port";s:7:"Display";s:6:"always";s:8:"Required";s:5:"false";s:4:"Mask";s:5:"false";}s:5:"value";s:4:"5900";}i:2;a:2:{s:11:"@attributes";a:9:{s:4:"Name";s:6:"Config";s:6:"Target";s:7:"/config";s:7:"Default";s:29:"/mnt/user/appdata/Backblaze64";s:4:"Mode";s:2:"rw";s:11:"Description";s:100:"Persistent storage for the Wine prefix and Backblaze configuration. Must survive container restarts.";s:4:"Type";s:4:"Path";s:7:"Display";s:6:"always";s:8:"Required";s:4:"true";s:4:"Mask";s:5:"false";}s:5:"value";s:29:"/mnt/user/appdata/Backblaze64";}i:3;a:2:{s:11:"@attributes";a:9:{s:4:"Name";s:23:"Backup Source (Drive D)";s:6:"Target";s:9:"/drive_d/";s:7:"Default";s:0:"";s:4:"Mode";s:2:"rw";s:11:"Description";s:212:"Optional: map a host path to back up as drive D. Must be read-write: Backblaze creates a .bzvol folder in the drive's root to track and back it up. Repeat with /drive_e/, /drive_f/, etc. for additional locations.";s:4:"Type";s:4:"Path";s:7:"Display";s:6:"always";s:8:"Required";s:5:"false";s:4:"Mask";s:5:"false";}s:5:"value";s:0:"";}i:4;a:2:{s:11:"@attributes";a:8:{s:4:"Name";s:8:"Timezone";s:6:"Target";s:2:"TZ";s:7:"Default";s:7:"Etc/UTC";s:11:"Description";s:104:"Timezone string, e.g. America/New_York. See https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/List_of_tz_database_time_zones";s:4:"Type";s:8:"Variable";s:7:"Display";s:6:"always";s:8:"Required";s:5:"false";s:4:"Mask";s:5:"false";}s:5:"value";s:7:"Etc/UTC";}i:5;a:2:{s:11:"@attributes";a:8:{s:4:"Name";s:7:"User ID";s:6:"Target";s:7:"USER_ID";s:7:"Default";s:2:"99";s:11:"Description";s:274:"UID the app runs as. On Unraid this is normally 99 (nobody), which matches user-share ownership. The app must own the files it backs up, since Backblaze writes a .bzvol folder into each drive's root. Change only if your data is owned by a different user (check with: id -u).";s:4:"Type";s:8:"Variable";s:7:"Display";s:8:"advanced";s:8:"Required";s:5:"false";s:4:"Mask";s:5:"false";}s:5:"value";s:2:"99";}i:6;a:2:{s:11:"@attributes";a:8:{s:4:"Name";s:8:"Group ID";s:6:"Target";s:8:"GROUP_ID";s:7:"Default";s:3:"100";s:11:"Description";s:167:"GID the app runs as. On Unraid this is normally 100 (users), matching user-share ownership. Change only if your data is owned by a different group (check with: id -g).";s:4:"Type";s:8:"Variable";s:7:"Display";s:8:"advanced";s:8:"Required";s:5:"false";s:4:"Mask";s:5:"false";}s:5:"value";s:3:"100";}i:7;a:2:{s:11:"@attributes";a:8:{s:4:"Name";s:19:"Force Latest Update";s:6:"Target";s:19:"FORCE_LATEST_UPDATE";s:7:"Default";s:4:"true";s:11:"Description";s:168:"When true (the default), the container downloads the newest Backblaze client on each start. Set to false to keep the installed client version and skip the update check.";s:4:"Type";s:8:"Variable";s:7:"Display";s:8:"advanced";s:8:"Required";s:5:"false";s:4:"Mask";s:5:"false";}s:5:"value";s:4:"true";}i:8;a:2:{s:11:"@attributes";a:8:{s:4:"Name";s:17:"Backblaze Version";s:6:"Target";s:17:"BACKBLAZE_VERSION";s:7:"Default";s:0:"";s:11:"Description";s:410:"Pin the Backblaze client to one exact version, for example 10.0.1.1069: on each start the container installs that version if a different one is installed, newer or older, and skips the update check. Leave empty to use the image's default: the stable image pins 10.0.1.1069 because 10.0.3.1075 completes no backup pass under its Wine, and the beta, whose Wine carries the fix, follows Backblaze's newest client.";s:4:"Type";s:8:"Variable";s:7:"Display";s:8:"advanced";s:8:"Required";s:5:"false";s:4:"Mask";s:5:"false";}s:5:"value";s:0:"";}i:9;a:2:{s:11:"@attributes";a:8:{s:4:"Name";s:15:"Enable Watchdog";s:6:"Target";s:15:"ENABLE_WATCHDOG";s:7:"Default";s:5:"false";s:11:"Description";s:435:"Set to true to let the container recover automatically when a backup stalls: it clears a stale four-hour lock left behind by an out-of-memory kill or an unclean restart, and stops a pass stuck on a lost upload child so the service starts a fresh one. Actions are written to the container log. Off by default because it deletes a lock file and kills processes. The beta's Settings tab has a switch that overrides this without a restart.";s:4:"Type";s:8:"Variable";s:7:"Display";s:8:"advanced";s:8:"Required";s:5:"false";s:4:"Mask";s:5:"false";}s:5:"value";s:5:"false";}i:10;a:2:{s:11:"@attributes";a:8:{s:4:"Name";s:19:"Disable Auto-Update";s:6:"Target";s:18:"DISABLE_AUTOUPDATE";s:7:"Default";s:5:"false";s:11:"Description";s:96:"Set to true to skip the Backblaze version check on startup (faster boot, but won't auto-update).";s:4:"Type";s:8:"Variable";s:7:"Display";s:8:"advanced";s:8:"Required";s:5:"false";s:4:"Mask";s:5:"false";}s:5:"value";s:5:"false";}i:11;a:2:{s:11:"@attributes";a:8:{s:4:"Name";s:23:"Disable Virtual Desktop";s:6:"Target";s:23:"DISABLE_VIRTUAL_DESKTOP";s:7:"Default";s:5:"false";s:11:"Description";s:51:"Set to true to disable Wine's virtual desktop mod