s:10:"Privileged";s:5:"false";s:7:"Support";s:50:"https://github.com/indyone/unraid-templates/issues";s:7:"Project";s:40:"https://github.com/luskaner/ageLANServer";s:6:"ReadMe";s:89:"https://github.com/indyone/unraid-templates/blob/main/ageLANServer-BattleServer/README.md";s:8:"Overview";s:516:"ageLANServer with a BattleServer included: LAN server emulator for Age of Empires: DE (AoE1),
    Age of Empires II: DE (AoE2), Age of Empires III: DE (AoE3), Age of Empires IV (AoE4), and
    Age of Mythology: Retold (AoM). It runs the game's own BattleServer.exe (which you provide)
    inside the container, which AoE4 and AoM require. It includes Wine, so the download is about 1.3 GB.
    If you only play AoE, AoE II or AoE III, the ageLANServer template is enough.
    Each container instance serves one game.";s:11:"TemplateURL";s:103:"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/indyone/unraid-templates/main/templates/ageLANServer-BattleServer.xml";s:4:"Icon";s:98:"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/indyone/unraid-templates/main/ageLANServer-BattleServer/icon.png";s:11:"ExtraParams";s:24:"--restart=unless-stopped";s:8:"Requires";s:838:"<br>&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;BattleServer.exe from your own game install (see the BattleServer Folder setting). Required for age4 and athens.<br>&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Port 443 and TCP ports 27012, 27112 and 27212 must be free on the host IP used by this container.<br>&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;For a single game: host networking is the simplest option (the ports must be free on the host).<br>&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;For multiple games: create an ipvlan L2 custom network (Settings > Docker > Docker custom networks)<br>&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;and assign each container a unique LAN IP — this avoids the port conflicts that occur when multiple<br>&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;containers share the same host network stack. ipvlan is preferred over macvlan as it does not require<br>&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;promiscuous mode on the host NIC.<br>";s:6:"Config";a:5:{i:0;a:2:{s:11:"@attributes";a:9:{s:4:"Name";s:17:"Certificates Path";s:6:"Target";s:27:"/app/resources/certificates";s:7:"Default";s:56:"/mnt/user/appdata/agelanserver-battleserver/certificates";s:4:"Mode";s:2:"rw";s:11:"Description";s:184:"Persistent storage for the server's SSL certificates. Generated automatically on first run; keep this mounted so the certificates survive restarts and clients keep trusting the server.";s:4:"Type";s:4:"Path";s:7:"Display";s:6:"always";s:8:"Required";s:4:"true";s:4:"Mask";s:5:"false";}s:5:"value";s:56:"/mnt/user/appdata/agelanserver-battleserver/certificates";}i:1;a:2:{s:11:"@attributes";a:9:{s:4:"Name";s:11:"Config Path";s:6:"Target";s:21:"/app/resources/config";s:7:"Default";s:50:"/mnt/user/appdata/agelanserver-battleserver/config";s:4:"Mode";s:2:"rw";s:11:"Description";s:268:"Server configuration. On first run the per-game folders (do not delete them) and a fully commented config.toml.example are placed here. Rename the example to config.toml and edit it to change authentication, announce settings, etc. Restart the container after editing.";s:4:"Type";s:4:"Path";s:7:"Display";s:6:"always";s:8:"Required";s:5:"false";s:4:"Mask";s:5:"false";}s:5:"value";s:50:"/mnt/user/appdata/agelanserver-battleserver/config";}i:2;a:2:{s:11:"@attributes";a:9:{s:4:"Name";s:19:"BattleServer Folder";s:6:"Target";s:17:"/app/battleserver";s:7:"Default";s:56:"/mnt/user/appdata/agelanserver-battleserver/battleserver";s:4:"Mode";s:2:"ro";s:11:"Description";s:328:"Folder containing BattleServer.exe from your game install, from the game this container serves (AoE IV ships none and AoM's is buggy: for age4 and athens use the one from AoE II: DE). It is started automatically inside the container. Required for age4 and athens; for the other games an empty folder runs without a BattleServer.";s:4:"Type";s:4:"Path";s:7:"Display";s:6:"always";s:8:"Required";s:4:"true";s:4:"Mask";s:5:"false";}s:5:"value";s:56:"/mnt/user/appdata/agelanserver-battleserver/battleserver";}i:3;a:2:{s:11:"@attributes";a:9:{s:4:"Name";s:9:"Logs Path";s:6:"Target";s:9:"/app/logs";s:7:"Default";s:48:"/mnt/user/appdata/agelanserver-battleserver/logs";s:4:"Mode";s:2:"rw";s:11:"Description";s:140:"Server and BattleServer log files. Detailed server file logging is off by default; add --log to Post Arguments (Advanced View) to enable it.";s:4:"Type";s:4:"Path";s:7:"Display";s:6:"always";s:8:"Required";s:5:"false";s:4:"Mask";s:5:"false";}s:5:"value";s:48:"/mnt/user/appdata/agelanserver-battleserver/logs";}i:4;a:2:{s:11:"@attributes";a:8:{s:4:"Name";s:4:"Game";s:6:"Target";s:5:"GAMES";s:7:"Default";s:26:"age2|age1|age3|age4|athens";s:11:"Description";s:324:"The single game this container serves: age2 (AoE II: DE), age1 (AoE: DE), age3 (AoE III: DE), age4 (AoE IV) or athens (AoM: Retold). age4 and athens will not start without BattleServer.exe in the BattleServer Folder. To serve another game, run a second container with its own IP (ipvlan network) and its own appdata folders.";s:4:"Type";s:8:"Variable";s:7:"Display";s:6:"always";s:8:"Required";s:4:"true";s:4:"Mask";s:5:"false";}s:5:"value";s:4:"age2";}}s:12:"TemplatePath";s:59:"/tmp/GitHub/AppFeed/templates/ageLANServer-BattleServer.xml";s:4:"Repo";s:20:"indyone's Repository";s:12:"CategoryList";a:1:{i:0;s:11:"GameServers";}s:9:"FirstSeen";i:1792123733;s:8:"Category";s:12:"GameServers:";s:2:"ID";i:2592;s:11:"Displayable";b:1;s:6:"Author";s:7:"indyone";s:13:"DockerHubName";s:25:"agelanserver-battleserver";s:8:"RepoName";s:20:"indyone's Repository";s:10:"SortAuthor";s:7:"indyone";s:8:"SortName";s:25:"ageLANServer BattleServer";s:6:"random";i:128473648;s:9:"Blacklist";b:0;s:6:"MinVer";s:3:"6.0";s:4:"Path";s:125:"/tmp/community.applications/tempFiles/templates-community-apps/indyonesRepository/indyone-ageLANServerBattleServer-latest.xml";s:4:"Date";N;s:11:"BrandNewApp";b:1;s:10:"Deprecated";b:0;s:10:"Compatible";b:1;s:16:"ModeratorComment";N;}i:2593;a:36:{s:4:"Name";s:12:"ageLANServer";s:10:"Repository";s:35:"ghcr.io/indyone/agelanserver:latest";s:8:"Registry";s:15:"https://ghcr.io";s:7:"Network";s:4:"host";s:5:"Shell";s:2:"sh";s:10:"Privileged";s:5:"false";s:7:"Support";s:50:"https://github.com/indyone/unraid-templates/issues";s:7:"Project";s:40:"https://github.com/luskaner/ageLANServer";s:6:"ReadMe";s:76:"https://github.com/indyone/unraid-templates/blob/main/ageLANServer/README.md";s:8:"Overview";s:754:"LAN server emulator for Age of Empires: DE (AoE1), Age of Empires II: DE (AoE2) and
    Age of Empires III: DE (AoE3). Play multiplayer over your local network without an internet connection.
    Each container instance serves one game. To support multiple titles simultaneously, run one
    container per game — but switch from host networking to an ipvlan network so each container
    gets its own LAN IP and can independently bind port 443 and the UDP discovery port.
    When you create a lobby, choose Use Local Lan Server in the game's Server list.
    SSL certificates are generated automatically on the first start and reused on subsequent runs.
    For Age of Empires IV or Age of Mythology: Retold use the ageLANServer-BattleServer template.";s:11:"TemplateURL";s:90:"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/indyone/unraid-templates/main/templates/ageLANServer.xml";s:4:"Icon";s:85:"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/indyone/unraid-templates/main/ageLANServer/icon.png";s:11:"ExtraParams";s:24:"--restart=unless-stopped";s:8:"Requires";s:678:"<br>&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Port 443 must be free on the host IP used by this container.<br>&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;For a single game: host networking is the simplest option (port 443 must be free on the host).<br>&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;For multiple games: create an ipvlan L2 custom network (Settings > Docker > Docker custom networks)<br>&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;and assign each container a unique LAN IP — this avoids the port 443 and UDP 31978 conflicts that<br>&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;occur when multiple containers share the same host network stack. ipvlan is preferred over macvlan<br>&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;as it does not require promiscuous mode on the host NIC.<br>";s:6:"Config";a:4:{i:0;a:2:{s:11:"@attributes";a:9:{s:4:"Name";s:17:"Certificates Path";s:6:"Target";s:27:"/app/resources/certificates";s:7:"Default";s:43:"/mnt/user/appdata/agelanserver/certificates";s:4:"Mode";s:2:"rw";s:11:"Description";s:184:"Persistent storage for the server's SSL certificates. Generated automatically on first run; keep this mounted so the certificates survive restarts and clients keep trusting the server.";s:4:"Type";s:4:"Path";s:7:"Display";s:6:"always";s:8:"Required";s:4:"true";s:4:"Mask";s:5:"false";}s:5:"value";s:43:"/mnt/user/appdata/agelanserver/certificates";}i:1;a:2:{s:11:"@attributes";a:9:{s:4:"Name";s:11:"Config Path";s:6:"Target";s:21:"/app/resources/config";s:7:"Default";s:37:"/mnt/user/appdata/agelanserver/config";s:4:"Mode";s:2:"rw";s:11:"Description";s:283:"Server configuration. On first run the per-game folders (do not delete them) and a fully commented config.toml.example are p