50682328;s:9:"Blacklist";b:0;s:6:"MinVer";s:3:"6.0";s:4:"Path";s:105:"/tmp/community.applications/tempFiles/templates-community-apps/sp00ksRepository/lakker-Pulsarr-latest.xml";s:4:"Date";N;s:11:"BrandNewApp";b:1;s:10:"Deprecated";b:0;s:10:"trendDelta";d:3.577;s:12:"trendAverage";d:15.5784;s:10:"Compatible";b:1;s:16:"ModeratorComment";N;}i:2615;a:44:{s:4:"Name";s:13:"BorgWarehouse";s:10:"Repository";s:27:"borgwarehouse/borgwarehouse";s:8:"Registry";s:52:"https://hub.docker.com/r/borgwarehouse/borgwarehouse";s:7:"Network";s:6:"bridge";s:5:"Shell";s:4:"bash";s:10:"Privileged";s:5:"false";s:7:"Support";s:60:"https://forums.unraid.net/topic/200915-plugin-borgwarehouse/";s:7:"Project";s:25:"https://borgwarehouse.com";s:6:"ReadMe";s:62:"https://github.com/jamesfreeman959/unraid-borgwarehouse#readme";s:8:"Overview";s:973:"BorgWarehouse is a fast, modern web interface for running a BorgBackup server. It turns your Unraid server into a central destination for Borg backups from your other machines: create and manage repositories, assign SSH keys, set quotas, monitor backup status and storage use, and get alerts by email or Apprise when a backup is late. Clients back up over SSH using borg, Vorta or borgmatic.

Before installing: generate two secrets for BETTER_AUTH_SECRET and CRONJOB_KEY (for example with "openssl rand -base64 32" in the Unraid terminal), and set SSH_SERVER_PORT to the same value as the SSH host port. Unraid's own SSH already uses port 22, so the default here is 2222.

Status and storage checks run on a schedule outside the container. Install the User Scripts plugin and add the script from the support page to keep the dashboard up to date.

