t user; the appdata data path must remain writable by the container (default on Unraid). Single-tenant design: any authenticated user (owner or viewer) can see all financial data — roles limit actions, not data visibility. Do not expose to untrusted users or the public internet. If you reach Tally through a reverse proxy, tunnel, or custom domain, set ALLOWED_ORIGINS.";s:5:"WebUI";s:23:"http://[IP]:[PORT:8091]";s:11:"TemplateURL";s:79:"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/jaydenroberts/unraid-templates/main/tally.xml";s:4:"Icon";s:101:"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/jaydenroberts/tally/main/frontend/public/android-chrome-512x512.png";s:10:"Networking";a:1:{s:4:"Mode";s:6:"bridge";}s:6:"Config";a:18:{i:0;a:2:{s:11:"@attributes";a:9:{s:4:"Name";s:11:"Web UI Port";s:6:"Target";s:4:"8091";s:7:"Default";s:4:"8092";s:4:"Mode";s:3:"tcp";s:11:"Description";s:170:"Host port Tally is reached on. Access the app at http://[serverIP]:[this port]. Tally listens on 8091 inside the container; only change the host side unless you know why.";s:4:"Type";s:4:"Port";s:7:"Display";s:6:"always";s:8:"Required";s:4:"true";s:4:"Mask";s:5:"false";}s:5:"value";s:4:"8092";}i:1;a:2:{s:11:"@attributes";a:9:{s:4:"Name";s:11:"Data Volume";s:6:"Target";s:5:"/data";s:7:"Default";s:28:"/mnt/user/appdata/tally/data";s:4:"Mode";s:2:"rw";s:11:"Description";s:285:"SQLite database storage. Must be a persistent path on the host. The container runs as a non-root user, so this path must be writable by the container (the default /mnt/user/appdata location on Unraid already is). Tally fails to create its database on first start if it is not writable.";s:4:"Type";s:4:"Path";s:7:"Display";s:6:"always";s:8:"Required";s:4:"true";s:4:"Mask";s:5:"false";}s:5:"value";s:28:"/mnt/user/appdata/tally/data";}i:2;a:2:{s:11:"@attributes";a:9:{s:4:"Name";s:10:"SECRET_KEY";s:6:"Target";s:10:"SECRET_KEY";s:7:"Default";s:0:"";s:4:"Mode";s:0:"";s:11:"Description";s:52:"JWT signing key. Generate with: openssl rand -hex 32";s:4:"Type";s:8:"Variable";s:7:"Display";s:6:"always";s:8:"Required";s:4:"true";s:4:"Mask";s:4:"true";}s:5:"value";s:0:"";}i:3;a:2:{s:11:"@attributes";a:9:{s:4:"Name";s:24:"ACCESS_TOKEN_EXPIRE_DAYS";s:6:"Target";s:24:"ACCESS_TOKEN_EXPIRE_DAYS";s:7:"Default";s:2:"30";s:4:"Mode";s:0:"";s:11:"Description";s:27:"JWT token lifetime in days.";s:4:"Type";s:8:"Variable";s:7:"Display";s:8:"advanced";s:8:"Required";s:5:"false";s:4:"Mask";s:5:"false";}s:5:"value";s:2:"30";}i:4;a:2:{s:11:"@attributes";a:9:{s:4:"Name";s:15:"ALLOWED_ORIGINS";s:6:"Target";s:15:"ALLOWED_ORIGINS";s:7:"Default";s:0:"";s:4:"Mode";s:0:"";s:11:"Description";s:333:"Comma-separated allow-list of browser origins permitted to call the app (CORS). Leave blank to allow only the local origin. If you reach Tally through a reverse proxy, tunnel, or custom domain/hostname, you MUST list that origin here or the browser app will break. Example: https://tally.example.com,https://tally.example.duckdns.org";s:4:"Type";s:8:"Variable";s:7:"Display";s:8:"advanced";s:8:"Required";s:5:"false";s:4:"Mask";s:5:"false";}s:5:"value";s:0:"";}i:5;a:2:{s:11:"@attributes";a:9:{s:4:"Name";s:16:"MAX_UPLOAD_BYTES";s:6:"Target";s:16:"MAX_UPLOAD_BYTES";s:7:"Default";s:8:"10485760";s:4:"Mode";s:0:"";s:11:"Description";s:150:"Maximum size in bytes for an uploaded bank statement file (CSV/PDF). Default 10485760 (10 MB). Increase only if you import unusually large statements.";s:4:"Type";s:8:"Variable";s:7:"Display";s:8:"advanced";s:8:"Required";s:5:"false";s:4:"Mask";s:5:"false";}s:5:"value";s:8:"10485760";}i:6;a:2:{s:11:"@attributes";a:9:{s:4:"Name";s:24:"FIRST_RUN_OWNER_USERNAME";s:6:"Target";s:24:"FIRST_RUN_OWNER_USERNAME";s:7:"Default";s:0:"";s:4:"Mode";s:0:"";s:11:"Description";s:91:"Auto-creates the first owner account on startup. Leave blank to use the setup page instead.";s:4:"Type";s:8:"Variable";s:7:"Display";s:8:"advanced";s:8:"Required";s:5:"false";s:4:"Mask";s:5:"false";}s:5:"value";s:0:"";}i:7;a:2:{s:11:"@attributes";a:9:{s:4:"Name";s:24:"FIRST_RUN_OWNER_PASSWORD";s:6:"Target";s:24:"FIRST_RUN_OWNER_PASSWORD";s:7:"Default";s:0:"";s:4:"Mode";s:0:"";s:11:"Description";s:44:"Required if FIRST_RUN_OWNER_USERNAME is set.";s:4:"Type";s:8:"Variable";s:7:"Display";s:8:"advanced";s:8:"Required";s:5:"false";s:4:"Mask";s:4:"true";}s:5:"value";s:0:"";}i:8;a:2:{s:11:"@attributes";a:9:{s:4:"Name";s:14:"RECOVERY_TOKEN";s:6:"Target";s:14:"RECOVERY_TOKEN";s:7:"Default";s:0:"";s:4:"Mode";s:0:"";s:11:"Description";s:189:"Emergency owner password reset token. Set to any strong random value (openssl rand -hex 32), call POST /api/auth/recover, then remove this variable and restart. Leave blank when not in use.";s:4:"Type";s:8:"Variable";s:7:"Display";s:8:"advanced";s:8:"Required";s:5:"false";s:4:"Mask";s:4:"true";}s:5:"value";s:0:"";}i:9;a:2:{s:11:"@attributes";a:9:{s:4:"Name";s:10:"BACKUP_DIR";s:6:"Target";s:10:"BACKUP_DIR";s:7:"Default";s:0:"";s:4:"Mode";s:0:"";s:11:"Description";s:178:"Directory where automatic pre-upgrade database snapshots are written. Leave blank to use a backups folder beside the database — /data/backups with the shipped Data Volume path.";s:4:"Type";s:8:"Variable";s:7:"Display";s:8:"advanced";s:8:"Required";s:5:"false";s:4:"Mask";s:5:"false";}s:5:"value";s:0:"";}i:10;a:2:{s:11:"@attributes";a:9:{s:4:"Name";s:11:"BACKUP_KEEP";s:6:"Target";s:11:"BACKUP_KEEP";s:7:"Default";s:1:"5";s:4:"Mode";s:0:"";s:11:"Description";s:116:"How many automatic pre-upgrade snapshots to keep. Older snapshots are deleted after a new one is written. Minimum 1.";s:4:"Type";s:8:"Variable";s:7:"Display";s:8:"advanced";s:8:"Required";s:5:"false";s:4:"Mask";s:5:"false";}s:5:"value";s:1:"5";}i:11;a:2:{s:11:"@attributes";a:9:{s:4:"Name";s:20:"PRE_MIGRATION_BACKUP";s:6:"Target";s:20:"PRE_MIGRATION_BACKUP";s:7:"Default";s:2:"on";s:4:"Mode";s:0:"";s:11:"Description";s:176:"Set to off to skip the automatic verified snapshot Tally takes before an upgrade changes the database. Leave on unless you run your own backup process and want faster upgrades.";s:4:"Type";s:8:"Variable";s:7:"Display";s:8:"advanced";s:8:"Required";s:5:"false";s:4:"Mask";s:5:"false";}s:5:"value";s:2:"on";}i:12;a:2:{s:11:"@attributes";a:9:{s:4:"Name";s:11:"AI_PROVIDER";s:6:"Target";s:11:"AI_PROVIDER";s:7:"Default";s:9:"anthropic";s:4:"Mode";s:0:"";s:11:"Description";s:524:"AI provider for the chat feature: anthropic, openai, or ollama (any OpenAI-compatible endpoint). AI is entirely optional — the rest of Tally works fully without it, and with no API key set no request is ever made. Note that clearing this field does NOT turn the feature off and does NOT hide the AI Coach page: the page stays visible in the sidebar and opens normally, but shows an error if you try to send a message without an API key. Leave this set to a real provider name; control whether AI is active with AI_API_KEY.";s:4:"Type";s:8:"Variable";s:7:"Display";s:8:"advanced";s:8:"Required";s:5:"false";s:4:"Mask";s:5:"false";}s:5:"value";s:9:"anthropic";}i:13;a:2:{s:11:"@attributes";a:9:{s:4:"Name";s:10:"AI_API_KEY";s:6:"Target";s:10:"AI_API_KEY";s:7:"Default";s:0:"";s:4:"Mode";s:0:"";s:11:"Description";s:68:"API key for the selected AI provider. Not required for local Ollama.";s:4:"Type";s:8:"Variable";s:7:"Display";s:8:"advanced";s:8:"Required";s:5:"false";s:4:"Mask";s:4:"true";}s:5:"value";s:0:"";}i:14;a:2:{s:11:"@attributes";a:9:{s:4:"Name";s:8:"AI_MODEL";s:6:"Target";s:8:"AI_MODEL";s:7:"Default";s:0:"";s:4:"Mode";s:0:"";s:11:"Description";s:103:"Model name to use (e.g. claude-sonnet-4-6, gpt-4o, llama3). Defaults to provider default if left blank.";s:4:"Type";s:8:"Variable";s:7:"Display";s:8:"advanced";s:8:"Required";s:5:"false";s:4:"Mask";s:5:"false";}s:5:"value";s:0:"";}i:15;a:2:{s:11:"@attributes";a:9:{s:4:"Name";s:11:"AI_BASE_URL";s:6:"Target";s:11:"AI_BASE_URL";s:7:"Default";s:0:"";s:4:"Mode";s:0:"";s:11:"Description";s:129:"Base URL for OpenAI-compatible endpoints (e.g. http://ollama:11434/v1). Required for Ollama; leave blank for Anthropic or O