my work please consider sponsoring.";s:10:"DonateLink";s:28:"https://jbrio.net/unbalanced";s:10:"Compatible";b:1;s:16:"ModeratorComment";N;}i:2633;a:37:{s:4:"Name";s:25:"crowdsec-mikrotik-bouncer";s:10:"Repository";s:43:"ghcr.io/funkolab/cs-mikrotik-bouncer:latest";s:8:"Registry";s:82:"https://github.com/funkolab/cs-mikrotik-bouncer/pkgs/container/cs-mikrotik-bouncer";s:7:"Network";s:6:"bridge";s:5:"Shell";s:2:"sh";s:10:"Privileged";s:5:"false";s:7:"Support";s:82:"https://github.com/funkolab/cs-mikrotik-bouncer/pkgs/container/cs-mikrotik-bouncer";s:7:"Project";s:87:"https://app.crowdsec.net/hub/author/funkolab/remediation-components/cs-mikrotik-bouncer";s:8:"Overview";s:202:"This repository aim to implement a CrowdSec bouncer for the router Mikrotik to block malicious IP to access your services. For this it leverages Mikrotik API to populate a dynamic Firewall Address List.";s:11:"TemplateURL";s:122:"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/jcesclapez/unraid-templates/main/crowdsec-mikrotik-bouncer/crowdsec-mikrotik-bouncer.xml";s:4:"Icon";s:130:"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/jcesclapez/unraid-templates/refs/heads/main/crowdsec-mikrotik-bouncer/crowdsec_mikrotik_logo.png";s:8:"Requires";s:1666:"Prerequisites:<br>Generate a bouncer API key following CrowdSec documentation https://doc.crowdsec.net/docs/cscli/cscli_bouncers_add/<br>cscli bouncers add Mikrotik-0<br>Activate API in mikrotik<br>IP -> Service -> Enable api and apply security<br><br>Procedure:<br>1&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Get a bouncer API key from your CrowdSec with command cscli bouncers add mikrotik-bouncer<br>2&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Copy the API key printed. You WON'T be able the get it again.<br>3&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Paste this API key as the value for bouncer environment variable CROWDSEC_BOUNCER_API_KEY, instead of &quot;MyApiKey&quot;<br>4&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Start bouncer with docker-compose up bouncer in the example directory<br>5&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Create IP drop Filter Rules in input and forward Chain with the crowdsec Source Address List<br>6&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Create IPv6 drop Filter Rules in input and forward Chain with the crowdsec Source Address List (if IPv6 used)<br><br>/ip/firewall/filter/<br>add action=drop src-address-list=crowdsec chain=input  in-interface=your-wan-interface place-before=0 comment=&quot;crowdsec input drop rules&quot;<br>add action=drop src-address-list=crowdsec chain=forward in-interface=your-wan-interface place-before=0 comment=&quot;crowdsec forward drop rules&quot;<br><br>/ipv6/firewall/filter/<br>add action=drop src-address-list=crowdsec chain=input  in-interface=your-wan-interface place-before=0 comment=&quot;crowdsec input drop rules&quot;<br>add action=drop src-address-list=crowdsec chain=forward in-interface=your-wan-interface place-before=0 comment=&quot;crowdsec forward drop rules&quot;";s:6:"Config";a:9:{i:0;a:2:{s:11:"@attributes";a:9:{s:4:"Name";s:24:"CROWDSEC BOUNCER API KEY";s:6:"Target";s:24:"CROWDSEC_BOUNCER_API_KEY";s:7:"Default";s:12:"your-api-key";s:4:"Mode";s:0:"";s:11:"Description";s:0:"";s:4:"Type";s:8:"Variable";s:7:"Display";s:6:"always";s:8:"Required";s:4:"true";s:4:"Mask";s:5:"false";}s:5:"value";s:12:"your-api-key";}i:1;a:2:{s:11:"@attributes";a:9:{s:4:"Name";s:12:"CROWDSEC URL";s:6:"Target";s:12:"CROWDSEC_URL";s:7:"Default";s:21:"http://crowdsec:8080/";s:4:"Mode";s:0:"";s:11:"Description";s:0:"";s:4:"Type";s:8:"Variable";s:7:"Display";s:6:"always";s:8:"Required";s:4:"true";s:4:"Mask";s:5:"false";}s:5:"value";s:21:"http://crowdsec:8080/";}i:2;a:2:{s:11:"@attributes";a:9:{s:4:"Name";s:13:"MIKROTIK HOST";s:6:"Target";s:13:"MIKROTIK_HOST";s:7:"Default";s:21:"your-ip-mikrotik:8728";s:4:"Mode";s:0:"";s:11:"Description";s:0:"";s:4:"Type";s:8:"Variable";s:7:"Display";s:6:"always";s:8:"Required";s:4:"true";s:4:"Mask";s:5:"false";}s:5:"value";s:21:"your-ip-mikrotik:8728";}i:3;a:2:{s:11:"@attributes";a:9:{s:4:"Name";s:13:"MIKROTIK USER";s:6:"Target";s:13:"MIKROTIK_USER";s:7:"Defa