s/container/chatgpt-community-docker";s:7:"Network";s:6:"bridge";s:5:"Shell";s:4:"bash";s:10:"Privileged";s:5:"false";s:7:"Support";s:66:"https://github.com/jeffreymooiweer/ChatGPT-Community-Docker/issues";s:7:"Project";s:59:"https://github.com/jeffreymooiweer/ChatGPT-Community-Docker";s:6:"ReadMe";s:66:"https://github.com/jeffreymooiweer/ChatGPT-Community-Docker#readme";s:8:"Overview";s:340:"Docker packaging for the upstream ChatGPT Community app. Standard: just the app, with persistent appdata. Optional: map selected folders or enable GPU acceleration. Advanced: optional SSH access for server administration; follow the setup steps under Additional Requirements below. WebUI login is optional; keep access on a trusted LAN/VPN.";s:8:"Requires";s:1658:"No extra requirements for normal app use. SSH is OPTIONAL.<br><br>**Optional SSH setup for Unraid**<br><br>1. On your Unraid server, open Settings → Management Access. Set Use SSH to Yes and note the SSH port (normally 22). Apply only if changed. Keep SSH on your trusted LAN/VPN; do not forward it to the internet.<br><br>2. Switch this container form to Advanced View. Set Advanced: provision host SSH to true, SSH host to your server's reachable LAN IP/hostname (not localhost), SSH user to root, and SSH port to the port above.<br><br>3. Finish any active app tasks, then click Apply. This recreates the container and interrupts its running sessions. Setup creates missing keys/config only; it does not grant access yet.<br><br>4. Open this container's Logs from the Docker tab. Copy the complete public-key line beginning with ssh-ed25519. Under Users → root → SSH authorized keys, add it on a NEW line without removing existing keys, then Save. Never copy or share the private key.<br><br>5. Verify the server's SSH host-key fingerprint as explained in the guide below. Open this container's Console and test: su -s /bin/sh abc -c &quot;ssh server 'hostname; id'&quot;. A successful check shows your server's name and uid=0(root).<br><br>**Important:** authorizing root gives the app full control of your server. Privileged mode and the Docker socket are not needed. Existing SSH config/keys are preserved; changing these fields does not replace an existing connection, and setting provisioning back to false does not revoke access. Older configs may use the alias unraid instead of server.<br><br>Full SSH guide, verification and troubleshooting";s:5:"WebUI";s:25:"https://[IP]:[PORT:3001]/";s:4:"Icon";s:90:"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/ilysenko/codex-desktop-linux/main/assets/codex-linux.png";s:11:"ExtraParams";s:42:"--shm-size=1g --hostname=ChatGPT-Community";s:6:"Config";a:14:{i:0;a:2:{s:11:"@attributes";a:9:{s:4:"Name";s:11:"WebUI HTTPS";s:6:"Target";s:4:"3001";s:7:"Default";s:5:"33443";s:4:"Mode";s:3:"tcp";s:11:"Description";s:30:"ChatGPT application over HTTPS";s:4:"Type";s:4:"Port";s:7:"Display";s:6:"always";s:8:"Required";s:4:"true";s:4:"Mask";s:5:"false";}s:5:"value";s:5:"33443";}i:1;a:2:{s:11:"@attributes";a:9:{s:4:"Name";s:7:"Appdata";s:6:"Target";s:7:"/config";s:7:"Default";s:35:"/mnt/user/appdata/chatgpt-community";s:4:"Mode";s:2:"rw";s:11:"Description";s:62:"Keep the existing path to preserve login, pairing and SSH keys";s:4:"Type";s:4:"Path";s:7:"Display";s:6:"always";s:8:"Required";s:4:"true";s:4:"Mask";s:5:"false";}s:5:"value";s:35:"/mnt/user/appdata/chatgpt-community";}i:2;a:2:{s:11:"@attributes";a:9:{s:4:"Name";s:23:"Optional: shared folder";s:6:"Target";s:16:"/workspace/files";s:7:"Default";s:0:"";s:4:"Mode";s:2:"ro";s:11:"Description";s:185:"Leave blank for app-only mode. Select one folder to make it available at /workspace/files (read-only by default). Change Access Mode to Read/Write only if the app may edit/delete files.";s:4:"Type";s:4:"Path";s:7:"Display";s:6:"always";s:8:"Required";s:5:"false";s:4:"Mask";s:5:"false";}s:5:"value";s:0:"";}i:3;a:2:{s:11:"@attributes";a:9:{s:4:"Name";s:25:"WebUI username (optional)";s:6:"Target";s:11:"CUSTOM_USER";s:7:"Default";s:3:"abc";s:4