sed by the web terminal.";s:4:"Type";s:8:"Variable";s:7:"Display";s:8:"advanced";s:8:"Required";s:5:"False";s:4:"Mask";s:5:"False";}s:5:"value";s:0:"";}i:18;a:2:{s:11:"@attributes";a:9:{s:4:"Name";s:18:"Web Authentication";s:6:"Target";s:18:"WEB_AUTHENTICATION";s:7:"Default";s:1:"0";s:4:"Mode";s:0:"";s:11:"Description";s:181:"When set to `1`, protects the application's GUI with a login page when accessed via a web browser. Access is granted only with valid credentials. Requires secure web access (HTTPS).";s:4:"Type";s:8:"Variable";s:7:"Display";s:8:"advanced";s:8:"Required";s:5:"False";s:4:"Mask";s:5:"False";}s:5:"value";s:0:"";}i:19;a:2:{s:11:"@attributes";a:9:{s:4:"Name";s:33:"Web Authentication Allow Insecure";s:6:"Target";s:33:"WEB_AUTHENTICATION_ALLOW_INSECURE";s:7:"Default";s:1:"0";s:4:"Mode";s:0:"";s:11:"Description";s:138:"When set to `1`, allows web authentication without secure connection (HTTPS). NOT RECOMMENDED. Use only if you fully understand the risks.";s:4:"Type";s:8:"Variable";s:7:"Display";s:8:"advanced";s:8:"Required";s:5:"False";s:4:"Mask";s:5:"False";}s:5:"value";s:0:"";}i:20;a:2:{s:11:"@attributes";a:9:{s:4:"Name";s:38:"Web Authentication Token Validity Time";s:6:"Target";s:38:"WEB_AUTHENTICATION_TOKEN_VALIDITY_TIME";s:7:"Default";s:2:"24";s:4:"Mode";s:0:"";s:11:"Description";s:244:"Lifetime of a token, in hours. A token is assigned to the user after successful login. As long as the token is valid, the user can access the application's GUI without logging in again. Once the token expires, the login page is displayed again.";s:4:"Type";s:8:"Variable";s:7:"Display";s:8:"advanced";s:8:"Required";s:5:"False";s:4:"Mask";s:5:"False";}s:5:"value";s:0:"";}i:21;a:2:{s:11:"@attributes";a:9:{s:4:"Name";s:27:"Web Authentication Username";s:6:"Target";s:27:"WEB_AUTHENTICATION_USERNAME";s:7:"Default";s:0:"";s:4:"Mode";s:0:"";s:11:"Description";s:187:"Optional username for web authentication. Provides a quick and easy way to configure credentials for a single