board-driven interface with extensive customization options, making it the perfect personal dashboard for power users. Based on the excellent ThinkDashboard.

Key features:
• Keyboard-driven navigation for fast access to all your bookmarks
• Extensive theme and layout customization, with a look studio beside the dashboard and a theme editor
• Inbox to collect new links fast: triage them, or keep them under Bookmarks → Unsorted and file whole groups later
• Bookmarks view with Health built in: finds broken, stale and duplicate links, with uptime monitoring and downtime alerts
• Video bookmarks marked in the list, and played in the hover card without leaving the dashboard
• Widgets beside your bookmarks: 36 built-in kinds (uptime, feeds, weather, calendar, disks, containers and more) plus a Custom widget for any JSON API
• Your media stack on the dashboard: Jellyfin, Sonarr, Radarr, Seerr, qBittorrent and SABnzbd, with the posters from your own library
• Finds the web apps in your Docker containers and offers them as bookmarks, with an icon and a status check (needs the Docker socket below)
• Your Unraid server on the dashboard: seven widgets for the array, parity, shares, VMs, the UPS and notifications, with alerts
• Web search in the search panel through your own SearXNG or the Brave Search API
• Six interface languages: English, Dutch, German, French, Spanish and Chinese
• Lightweight and fast, no heavy dependencies
• Actively maintained with regular releases

Links:
• Website: https://www.nextdash.cc
• Source code and releases: https://github.com/jordibrouwer/nextdash
• Changelog: https://github.com/jordibrouwer/nextdash/releases
• Devlog / release updates: https://www.nextdash.cc/news
• Also available on GHCR: ghcr.io/jordibrouwer/nextdash:latest
• User manual: https://github.com/jordibrouwer/nextdash/blob/main/MANUAL.md

The host widgets (Processor, Memory, Disks, Containers) are off until you fill in the optional paths and variables below — they are hidden under Show more settings. Section 15.4 of the manual explains what each one reads.

