ot, and load them on demand. Adds a Parking tab and a Boot Packages tab to the Plugins page, and a Park button on each row of the Installed Plugins list. Shows what each plugin cost at boot and what it does on its own (schedules, background services, array hooks), checks for a newer version when you load a parked plugin, and manages the packages in /boot/extra too, including offering to park what a package needs after checking nothing else does. Removing it asks whether to move everything parked back or keep it parked.";s:9:"PluginURL";s:88:"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/joshmans/unraid-plugin-parking/main/plugin-parking.plg";s:12:"PluginAuthor";s:6:"shwa87";s:4:"Icon";s:93:"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/joshmans/unraid-plugin-parking/main/icon/plugin-parking.png";s:7:"Support";s:56:"https://github.com/joshmans/unraid-plugin-parking/issues";s:7:"Project";s:49:"https://github.com/joshmans/unraid-plugin-parking";s:6:"MinVer";s:5:"7.0.0";s:11:"TemplateURL";s:79:"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/joshmans/unraid-tools/main/plugin-parking.xml";s:12:"TemplatePath";s:38:"/tmp/GitHub/AppFeed/plugin-parking.xml";s:4:"Repo";s:20:"shwa87-'s Repository";s:10:"Repository";s:88:"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/joshmans/unraid-plugin-parking/main/plugin-parking.plg";s:12:"CategoryList";a:2:{i:0;s:15:"Tools-Utilities";i:1;s:7:"Plugins";}s:6:"Plugin";b:1;s:13:"pluginVersion";s:11:"2026.10.13a";s:6:"Author";s:6:"shwa87";s:9:"downloads";i:41;s:9:"FirstSeen";i:1790647059;s:14:"LastUpdateScan";i:1792383193;s:11:"pluginStats";a:13:{i:10;i:17;i:11;i:0;i:12;i:0;s:2:"01";i:0;s:2:"02";i:0;s:2:"03";i:0;s:2:"04";i:0;s:2:"05";i:0;s:2:"06";i:0;s:2:"07";i:0;s:2:"08";i:0;s:2:"09";i:24;s:1:"T";i:41;}s:8:"Category";s:24:"Tools:Utilities Plugins:";s:2:"ID";i:2736;s:11:"Displayable";b:1;s:13:"DockerHubName";s:14:"plugin parking";s:8:"RepoName";s:20:"shwa87-'s Repository";s:10:"SortAuthor";s:6:"shwa87";s:8:"SortName";s:14:"Plugin Parking";s:6:"random";i:1542617418;s:9:"Blacklist";b:0;s:4:"Path";s:188:"/tmp/community.applications/tempFiles/templates-community-apps/shwa87sRepository/shwa87-PluginParking-//raw.githubusercontent.com/joshmans/unraid-plugin-parking/main/plugin-parking.plg.xml";s:4:"Date";N;s:11:"BrandNewApp";b:1;s:10:"Deprecated";b:0;s:10:"Compatible";b:1;s:16:"ModeratorComment";N;}i:2737;a:35:{s:4:"Name";s:31:"SCSI Enclosure Monitor Extended";s:8:"Overview";s:758:"Monitor SES-capable SCSI enclosures (JBODs, disk shelves) with sesmon and get an Unraid notification when a fan, power supply, temperature sensor or drive bay reports a problem. Choose the enclosures from the ones found on your server instead of typing SAS addresses, and set poll, back-off and notification options from dropdowns; the configuration files stay editable. The Enclosure Devices page shows what each enclosure reports in plain words (Friendly view, or Raw), names every bay by the drive in it (Unraid disk, model, size, temperature) and shows an HBA's virtual enclosure as ports with the HBA firmware; alerts name the affected disks. A fork of the SCSI Enclosure Monitor plugin by desertwitch; it cannot be installed together with the original.";s:9:"PluginURL";s:85:"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/joshmans/unraid-sesmon-extended/main/sesmon-ext.plg";s:12:"PluginAuthor";s:6:"shwa87";s:4:"Icon";s:95:"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/joshmans/unraid-sesmon-extended/main/icon/sesmon-extended.png";s:7:"Support";s:57:"https://github.com/joshmans/unraid-sesmon-extended/issues";s:7:"Project";s:50:"https://github.com/joshmans/unraid-sesmon-extended";s:6:"MinVer";s:3:"7.0";s:11:"TemplateURL";s:75:"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/joshmans/unraid-tools/main/sesmon-ext.xml";s:12:"TemplatePath";s:34:"/tmp/GitHub/AppFeed/sesmon-ext.xml";s:4:"Repo";s:20:"shwa87-'s Repository";s:10:"Repository";s:85:"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/joshmans/unraid-sesmon-extended/main/sesmon-ext.plg";s:12:"CategoryList";a:2:{i:0;s:12:"Tools-System";i:1;s:7:"Plugins";}s:6:"Plugin";b:1;s:13:"pluginVersion