ma-separated list of file extensions to treat as video. Empty uses the built-in default list (mkv, mp4, avi, mov, wmv, and more).";s:4:"Type";s:8:"Variable";s:7:"Display";s:8:"advanced";s:8:"Required";s:5:"false";s:4:"Mask";s:5:"false";}s:5:"value";s:0:"";}i:22;a:2:{s:11:"@attributes";a:9:{s:4:"Name";s:60:"Ignore Directories (AUTOMATED_CONVERSION_IGNORE_DIRECTORIES)";s:6:"Target";s:39:"AUTOMATED_CONVERSION_IGNORE_DIRECTORIES";s:7:"Default";s:0:"";s:4:"Mode";s:0:"";s:11:"Description";s:144:"Optional. Space-separated directory names (e.g. sync-client metadata folders) pruned from every watch-folder scan, matched anywhere in the tree.";s:4:"Type";s:8:"Variable";s:7:"Display";s:8:"advanced";s:8:"Required";s:5:"false";s:4:"Mask";s:5:"false";}s:5:"value";s:0:"";}i:23;a:2:{s:11:"@attributes";a:9:{s:4:"Name";s:48:"Active Hours (AUTOMATED_CONVERSION_ACTIVE_HOURS)";s:6:"Target";s:33:"AUTOMATED_CONVERSION_ACTIVE_HOURS";s:7:"Default";s:0:"";s:4:"Mode";s:0:"";s:11:"Description";s:162:"Optional. Restrict automated conversion to a daily window, HH-HH in 24h clock (e.g. 22-06 for overnight only). Empty means always active. Uses the container's TZ.";s:4:"Type";s:8:"Variable";s:7:"Display";s:8:"advanced";s:8:"Required";s:5:"false";s:4:"Mask";s:5:"false";}s:5:"value";s:0:"";}i:24;a:2:{s:11:"@attributes";a:9:{s:4:"Name";s:52:"Staging Directory (AUTOMATED_CONVERSION_STAGING_DIR)";s:6:"Target";s:32:"AUTOMATED_CONVERSION_STAGING_DIR";s:7:"Default";s:0:"";s:4:"Mode";s:0:"";s:11:"Description";s:217:"Optional. Where in-progress conversions are written. Empty means a hidden folder under the output root. Set to /staging (map that path above to a cache pool) to keep the array out of the write path during a transcode.";s:4:"Type";s:8:"Variable";s:7:"Display";s:8:"advanced";s:8:"Required";s:5:"false";s:4:"Mask";s:5:"false";}s:5:"value";s:0:"";}i:25;a:2:{s:11:"@attributes";a:9:{s:4:"Name";s:60:"Source Stable Time (AUTOMATED_CONVERSION_SOURCE_STABLE_TIME)";s:6:"Target";s:39:"AUTOMATED_CONVERSION_SOURCE_STABLE_TIME";s:7:"Default";s:1:"5";s:4:"Mode";s:0:"";s:11:"Description";s:129:"Seconds a source file must stop changing (size + mtime) before it is picked up, so a file still being copied in is never touched.";s:4:"Type";s:8:"Variable";s:7:"Display";s:8:"advanced";s:8:"Required";s:5:"false";s:4:"Mask";s:5:"false";}s:5:"value";s:1:"5";}i:26;a:2:{s:11:"@attributes";a:9:{s:4:"Name";s:52:"Check Interval (AUTOMATED_CONVERSION_CHECK_INTERVAL)";s:6:"Target";s:35:"AUTOMATED_CONVERSION_CHECK_INTERVAL";s:7:"Default";s:1:"5";s:4:"Mode";s:0:"";s:11:"Description";s:35:"Seconds between watch-folder scans.";s:4:"Type";s:8:"Variable";s:7:"Display";s:8:"advanced";s:8:"Required";s:5:"false";s:4:"Mask";s:5:"false";}s:5:"value";s:1:"5";}i:27;a:2:{s:11:"@attributes";a:9:{s:4:"Name";s:58:"Max Watch Folders (AUTOMATED_CONVERSION_MAX_WATCH_FOLDERS)";s:6:"Target";s:38:"AUTOMATED_CONVERSION_MAX_WATCH_FOLDERS";s:7:"Default";s:1:"5";s:4:"Mode";s:0:"";s:11:"Description";s:93:"How many numbered watch folders (/watch..N) to scan when the watch directory is left at AUTO.";s:4:"Type";s:8:"Variable";s:7:"Display";s:8:"advanced";s:8:"Required";s:5:"false";s:4:"Mask";s:5:"false";}s:5:"value";s:1:"5";}i:28;a:2:{s:11:"@attributes";a:9:{s:4:"Name";s:69:"Custom HandBrakeCLI Args (AUTOMATED_CONVERSION_HANDBRAKE_CUSTOM_ARGS)";s:6:"Target";s:42:"AUTOMATED_CONVERSION_HANDBRAKE_CUSTOM_ARGS";s:7:"Default";s:0:"";s:4:"Mode";s:0:"";s:11:"Description";s:124:"Optional. Extra HandBrakeCLI arguments appended to every automated job, e.g. --encoder nvenc_h265 for HEVC instead of H.264.";s:4:"Type";s:8:"Variable";s:7:"Display";s:8:"advanced";s:8:"Required";s:5:"false";s:4:"Mask";s:5:"false";}s:5:"value";s:0:"";}i:29;a:2:{s:11:"@attributes";a:9:{s:4:"Name";s:35:"Web File Manager (WEB_FILE_MANAGER)";s:6:"Target";s:16:"WEB_FILE_MANAGER";s:7:"Default";s:3:"1|0";s:4:"Mode";s:0:"";s:11:"Description";s:137:"1 = browse, upload and download the watch/output/storage folders at https://host:3001/files/ (default). 0 disables the endpoint entirely.";s:4:"Type";s:8:"Variable";s:7:"Display";s:6:"always";s:8:"Required";s:5:"false";s:4:"Mask";s:5:"false";}s:5:"value";s:1:"1";}i:30;a:2:{s:11:"@attributes";a:9:{s:4:"Name";s:59:"File Manager Allowed Paths (WEB_FILE_MANAGER_ALLOWED_PATHS)";s:6:"Target";s:30:"WEB_FILE_MANAGER_ALLOWED_PATHS";s:7:"Default";s:4:"AUTO";s:4:"Mode";s:0:"";s:11:"Description";s:205:"AUTO publishes the watch folders, the output folder and /storage, whichever exist. Otherwise a comma-separated list of absolute paths. /config is always refused, since it holds the WebUI's TLS private key.";s:4:"Type";s:8:"Variable";s:7:"Display";s:8:"advanced";s:8:"Required";s:5:"false";s:4:"Mask";s:5:"false";}s:5:"value";s:4:"AUTO";}i:31;a:2:{s:11:"@attributes";a:9:{s:4:"Name";s:57:"File Manager Denied Paths (WEB_FILE_MANAGER_DENIED_PATHS)";s:6:"Target";s:29:"WEB_FILE_MANAGER_DENIED_PATHS";s:7:"Default";s:0:"";s:4:"Mode";s:0:"";s:11:"Description";s:104:"Optional. Comma-separated paths inside the allowed ones that must answer 403 instead of being browsable.";s:4:"Type";s:8:"Variable";s:7:"Display";s:8:"advanced";s:8:"Required";s:5:"false";s:4:"Mask";s:5:"false";}s:5:"value";s:0:"";}i:32;a:2:{s:11:"@attributes";a:9:{s:4:"Name";s:27:"Web Terminal (WEB_TERMINAL)";s:6:"Target";s:12:"WEB_TERMINAL";s:7:"Default";s:3:"0|1";s:4:"Mode";s:0:"";s:11:"Description";s:118:"1 enables a terminal on the web desktop with Ctrl+Alt+T. 0 (default) disables every terminal program in the container.";s:4:"Type";s:8:"Variable";s:7:"Display";s:8:"advanced";s:8:"Required";s:5:"false";s:4:"Mask";s:5:"false";}s:5:"value";s:1:"0";}i:33;a:2:{s:11:"@attributes";a:9:{s:4:"Name";s:44:"Web Terminal Shell (WEB_TERMINAL_SHELL_PATH)";s:6:"Target";s:23:"WEB_TERMINAL_SHELL_PATH";s:7:"Default";s:9:"/bin/bash";s:4:"Mode";s:0:"";s:11:"Description";s:33:"The shell the web terminal opens.";s:4:"Type";s:8:"Variable";s:7:"Display";s:8:"advanced";s:8:"Required";s:5:"false";s:4:"Mask";s:5:"false";}s:5:"value";s:9:"/bin/bash";}i:34;a:2:{s:11:"@attributes";a:9:{s:4:"Name";s:40:"Desktop Notifications (WEB_NOTIFICATION)";s:6:"Target";s:16:"WEB_NOTIFICATION";s:7:"Default";s:3:"0|1";s:4:"Mode";s:0:"";s:11:"Description";s:91:"1 shows a popup on the web desktop when a conversion finishes or fails. 0 (default) is off.";s:4:"Type";s:8:"Variable";s:7:"Display";s:8:"advanced";s:8:"Required";s:5:"false";s:4:"Mask";s:5:"false";}s:5:"value";s:1:"0";}i:35;a:2:{s:11:"@attributes";a:9:{s:4:"Name";s:50:"Optical Drive Permissions (ATTACHED_DEVICES_PERMS)";s:6:"Target";s:22:"ATTACHED_DEVICES_PERMS";s:7:"Default";s:8:"/dev/sr*";s:4:"Mode";s:0:"";s:11:"Description";s:239:"Device glob the container is granted group access to for optical-drive ripping, e.g. /dev/sr*. Also pass the device itself under Extra Parameters, e.g. --device /dev/sr0. Unverified: no optical drive was available to test a rip end to end.";s:4:"Type";s:8:"Variable";s:7:"Display";s:8:"advanced";s:8:"Required";s:5:"false";s:4:"Mask";s:5:"false";}s:5:"value";s:8:"/dev/sr*";}i:36;a:2:{s:11:"@attributes";a:9:{s:4:"Name";s:54:"Build libdvdcss for encrypted DVDs (INSTALL_LIBDVDCSS)";s:6:"Target";s:17:"INSTALL_LIBDVDCSS";s:7:"Default";s:10:"false|true";s:4:"Mode";s:0:"";s:11:"Description";s:594:"false (default) leaves the container as it is: a commercially encrypted DVD ends at 'No Title Found' because no decryption library is present. true makes the container download the libdvdcss source from VideoLAN's own mirror on its first start, check it against a pinned checksum and compile it here. The library is never shipped inside the image. The first start with it takes about 15 seconds and needs internet; the result is cached under /config so later starts take about a second. Whether decrypting a disc you own is lawful depends on where you live, which is why this is off by default.";s:4:"Type";s:8:"Variable";s:7:"Display";s:8:"advanced";s:8:"Required";s:5:"false";s:4:"Mask";s:5:"false";}s:5:"value";s:5:"false";}i:37;a:2:{s:11:"@attributes";a:9:{s:4:"Name";s:14:"WebU