ame";s:13:"Cookie Domain";s:6:"Target";s:13:"COOKIE_DOMAIN";s:7:"Default";s:0:"";s:4:"Mode";s:0:"";s:11:"Description";s:278:"Bare domain only. No https://, no trailing slash, no path. Example: standardnotesserver.mydomain.tld. Wrong: https://standardnotesserver.mydomain.tld. A URL here breaks session cookies. The Custom Sync Server URL entered into clients is a separate value and is a full HTTPS URL.";s:4:"Type";s:8:"Variable";s:7:"Display";s:6:"always";s:8:"Required";s:5:"false";s:4:"Mask";s:5:"false";}s:5:"value";s:0:"";}}s:12:"TemplatePath";s:65:"/tmp/GitHub/AppFeed/standardnotes-server/standardnotes-server.xml";s:4:"Repo";s:29:"junkerderprovinz's Repository";s:12:"CategoryList";a:3:{i:0;s:12:"Productivity";i:1;s:5:"Cloud";i:2;s:8:"Security";}s:5:"stars";i:3;s:9:"downloads";i:443355;s:13:"downloadtrend";a:5:{i:0;i:323353;i:1;i:347274;i:2;i:369857;i:3;i:393989;i:4;i:443355;}s:8:"trending";d:11.135;s:6:"trends";a:4:{i:0;d:6.888;i:1;d:6.106;i:2;d:6.125;i:3;d:11.135;}s:10:"trendsDate";a:4:{i:0;i:1783627457;i:1;i:1786368799;i:2;i:1788966671;i:3;i:1791745164;}s:9:"FirstSeen";i:1781028981;s:10:"LastUpdate";i:1790011321;s:14:"LastUpdateScan";i:1791745164;s:11:"topTrending";d:4.247;s:8:"Category";s:30:"Productivity: Cloud: Security:";s:2:"ID";i:2791;s:11:"Displayable";b:1;s:6:"Author";s:13:"standardnotes";s:13:"DockerHubName";s:20:"standardnotes-server";s:8:"RepoName";s:29:"junkerderprovinz's Repository";s:10:"SortAuthor";s:13:"standardnotes";s:8:"SortName";s:20:"StandardNotes Server";s:6:"random";i:592943126;s:9:"Blacklist";b:0;s:6:"MinVer";s:3:"6.0";s:4:"Path";s:135:"/tmp/community.applications/tempFiles/templates-community-apps/junkerderprovinzsRepository/standardnotes-StandardNotesServer-latest.xml";s:4:"Date";N;s:11:"BrandNewApp";b:1;s:10:"Deprecated";b:0;s:10:"trendDelta";d:4.247;s:12:"trendAverage";d:7.5635;s:10:"Compatible";b:1;s:16:"ModeratorComment";N;}i:2792;a:49:{s:4:"Name";s:19:"StandardNotes-WebUI";s:10:"Repository";s:24:"standardnotes/web:latest";s:8:"Registry";s:42:"https://hub.docker.com/r/standardnotes/web";s:7:"Network";s:6:"bridge";s:5:"Shell";s:2:"sh";s:10:"Privileged";s:5:"false";s:7:"Support";s:76:"https://forums.unraid.net/topic/198811-support-junkerderprovinz-unraid-apps/";s:7:"Project";s:25:"https://standardnotes.com";s:6:"ReadMe";s:87:"https://github.com/junkerderprovinz/unraid-apps/blob/main/standardnotes-webui/README.md";s:8:"Overview";s:2911:"Standard Notes: browser web client for Unraid (community template).
    Runs the official standardnotes/web image as a static-served web app
    on port 80 inside the container, exposed on host port 3001 by default
    to avoid clashing with the Standard Notes server's :3000 API gateway.
    
    IMPORTANT: This template only ships the WEB CLIENT. You still need a
    running Standard Notes backend (see the companion folder
    https://github.com/junkerderprovinz/Unraid-apps/tree/main/standardnotes-server
    in this template repo, container name "StandardNotes-Server").
    The web client itself does not host a sync server. It is just the
    browser UI.
    
    Configuring the sync server:
    The official standardnotes/web image is configured at RUNTIME from
    the browser, not via env vars. After opening the web app, click
    "Advanced options" on the sign-in / sign-up screen and set
    Custom Sync Server = https://standardnotesserver.mydomain.tld (your own
    backend URL). The official Docker docs only document
    "docker run -d -p 3000:80 standardnotes/web", and no sync-server env
    var is exposed, so this template intentionally does not invent one.
    
    Recommended reverse-proxy setup (Nginx Proxy Manager):
    Domain: app.standardnotes.mydomain.tld
    Forward Hostname/IP: this container's Unraid IP
    Forward Port: 3001 (the host port chosen below)
    Force SSL + Let's Encrypt + HTTP/2 ON.
    Then in the web app, set Custom Sync Server =
    https://standardnotesserver.mydomain.tld (the BACKEND domain, not the
    web-app domain).
    
    Notes:
    • UNOFFICIAL community template. Standard Notes does not provide
      support for self-hosted setups beyond the official Docker docs at
      https://standardnotes.com/help/self-hosting/web-app.
    • Self-hosting the web client does NOT unlock paid / subscription
      Standard Notes features. Subscription-only client features
      (extended editors, advanced themes, Files quota, Listed, etc.)
      are gated by Standard Notes' own licensing checks in the official
      clients. This template deploys the upstream image as-is and does
      NOT patch, bypass, or otherwise modify those checks.
    • Always reach the web client through your HTTPS reverse proxy.
      The container serves plain HTTP on port 80 internally, but the
      browser MUST load it over HTTPS, because Standard Notes uses WebCrypto
      (window.crypto.subtle) for account key derivation, and browsers
      only expose it on secure contexts. Opening the web app over
      http://[Unraid-ip]:[port]/ will fail at sign-up with
      "crypto.subtle is undefined". HTTPS also avoids mix-content
      blocks on API calls to the HTTPS backend.
