/200517-support-libredb-libredb-studio/";s:7:"Project";s:41:"https://github.com/libredb/libredb-studio";s:8:"Overview";s:990:"LibreDB Studio is an open source (MIT), self-hosted SQL IDE. Use a clean web UI to connect to forty-one database drivers, browse schemas, write and run queries, and work with your data from any browser on your network. The drivers are PostgreSQL, MySQL, Oracle, Db2 LUW, SQL Server, SQLite, libSQL, DuckDB, Redis, MongoDB, Couchbase, ClickHouse, Apache Druid, Elasticsearch, OpenSearch, Trino, Apache Cassandra, Databend, Prometheus, InfluxDB (InfluxQL), InfluxDB 3 (SQL), Apache Kafka, etcd, Neo4j, Milvus, Qdrant and Oxia, and they reach sixty-eight named engines in all, because twenty-seven further engines speak one of the same wire protocols. Some of the drivers send only read requests. Where an engine cannot edit data, the controls are shown as unsupported instead of failing. It runs as a single container and stores its own settings in an embedded SQLite file under appdata, so there is no extra database to set up just to run it, and your data persists across container updates.";s:5:"WebUI";s:23:"http://[IP]:[PORT:3000]";s:11:"TemplateURL";s:92:"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/libredb/unraid-templates/main/templates/libredb-studio.xml";s:4:"Icon";s:88:"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/libredb/unraid-templates/main/icons/libredb-studio.png";s:6:"Config";a:8:{i:0;a:2:{s:11:"@attributes";a:9:{s:4:"Name";s:10:"WebUI Port";s:6:"Target";s:4:"3000";s:7:"Default";s:4:"3006";s:4:"Mode";s:3:"tcp";s:11:"Description";s:146:"Host port for the LibreDB Studio web UI (maps to container port 3000). Any free host port works; avoid 3000 to prevent a conflict with other apps.";s:4:"Type";s:4:"Port";s:7:"Display";s:6:"always";s:8:"Required";s:4:"true";s:4:"Mask";s:5:"false";}s:5:"value";s:4:"3006";}i:1;a:2:{s:11:"@attributes";a:9:{s:4:"Name";s:8:"App Data";s:6:"Target";s:9:"/app/data";s:7:"Default";s:32:"/mnt/user/appdata/libredb-studio";s:4:"Mode";s:2:"rw";s:11