    background using ffmpeg, tracks results in a dashboard, and never re-encodes the
    same file twice. Lighter-weight than Tdarr / FileFlows / Unmanic.
    
    Setup guide (install, updates, GPU):
    https://gitlab.com/MisterJB/x265-butler/-/blob/main/docs/user/README.md
    
    [!] Images moved to the GitLab registry with v2.54.0. Installs from before
    must change the Repository field to registry.gitlab.com/misterjb/x265-butler:latest
    to keep receiving updates; the old ghcr.io image stays at 2.53.0.
    
    Recent highlights: Stats + Dashboard / UI Redesign /
    Encoder-Benchmark with Pareto-Frontier / Encoder-Profile-Editor / Multi-Share /
    Storage-Analyzer / Auto-Scan-on-Change.
    
    Release notes for every version:
    https://gitlab.com/MisterJB/x265-butler/-/releases
    
    [!] Image tag: we strongly recommend keeping the :latest tag in the Repository
    field. Fixes only ship in new releases,
    older version tags are removed from the registry over time,
    and Unraid shows update notices only for :latest. Read the
    release notes before a major upgrade (v2.x to v3.x). A version tag
    (registry.gitlab.com/misterjb/x265-butler:X.Y.Z) is only a short way back to the
    previous release: back up your AppData folder first and switch back to :latest
