ted reverse proxy and site-management app built on top of Caddy. It gives you a web UI for the routing patterns most people actually need — hosted sites, proxy hosts, redirects, and streaming hosts — with automatic HTTPS certificate management, live DNS/port/TLS/upstream health checks, and detailed access and gateway-event logs. Advanced users can still drop in custom Caddy directives per route when they need something the UI doesn't cover.

Data lives locally in SQLite inside your appdata folder — no external database to run. Three built-in roles (Administrator, Standard, Viewer) let you share access with a team without giving everyone full control.";s:5:"WebUI";s:23:"http://[IP]:[PORT:8080]";s:11:"TemplateURL";s:87:"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/mfwadejr/site-gateway/main/templates/site-gateway.xml";s:4:"Icon";s:69:"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/mfwadejr/site-gateway/main/icon.svg";s:11:"ExtraParams";s:24:"--restart=unless-stopped";s:6:"Config";a:18:{i:0;a:2:{s:11:"@attributes";a:9:{s:4:"Name";s:7:"Appdata";s:6:"Target";s:5:"/data";s:7:"Default";s:30:"/mnt/user/appdata/site-gateway";s:4:"Mode";s:2:"rw";s:11:"Description";s:248:"Where Site Gateway stores its SQLite database, hosted files, backups, and certificates (including private keys). This is real, durable data, not a cache — point it at a protected array or pool location rather than an unprotected cache-only share.";s:4:"Type";s:4:"Path";s:7:"Display";s:6:"always";s:8:"Required";s:4:"true";s:4:"Mask";s:5:"false";}s:5:"value";s:30:"/mnt/user/appdata/site-gateway";}i:1;a:2:{s:11:"@attributes";a:9:{s:4:"Name";s:14:"ADMIN_USERNAME";s:6:"Target";s:14:"ADMIN_USERNAME";s:7:"Default";s:5:"admin";s:4:"Mode";s:0:"";s:11:"Description";s:161:"Login name for the first-run admin account. Pre-filled with admin — used the first time you log in to the dashboard; you can create additional users afterward.";s:4:"Type";s:8:"Variable";s:7:"Display";s:6:"always";s:8:"Required";s:4:"true";s:4:"Mask";s:5:"false";}s:5:"value";s:5:"admin";}i:2;a:2:{s:11:"@attributes";a:9:{s:4:"Name";s:14:"ADMIN_PASSWORD";s:6:"Target";s:14:"ADMIN_PASSWORD";s:7:"Default";s:0:"";s:4:"Mode";s:0:"";s:11:"Description";s:222:"Password for the first-run admin account, used the first time you log in to the dashboard. Pre-filled with changeme as a placeholder — required, and you must replace it with a real password before starting the container.";s:4:"Type";s:8:"Variable";s:7:"Display";s:6:"always";s:8:"Required";s:4:"true";s:4:"Mask";s:4:"true";}s:5:"value";s:8:"changeme";}i:3;a:2:{s:11:"@attributes";a:9:{s:4:"Name";s:14:"SESSION_SECRET";s:6:"Target";s:14:"SESSION_SECRET";s:7:"Default";s:0:"";s:4:"Mode";s:0:"";s:11:"Description";s:194:"Required. A random secret (at least 32 characters recommended) used to sign login sessions — it is not a password and is never used to log in. Changing it later signs every logged-in user out.";s:4:"Type";s:8:"Variable";s:7:"Display";s:6:"always";s:8:"Required";s:4:"true";s:4:"Mask";s:4:"true";}s:5:"value";s:12:"changeme-too";}i:4;a:2:{s:11:"@attributes";a:9:{s:4:"Name";s:15:"BACKUP_PASSWORD";s:6:"Target";s:15:"BACKUP_PASSWORD";s:7:"Default";s:0:"";s:4:"Mode";s:0:"";s:11:"Description";s:117:"Encryption password used only when encrypted scheduled backups are enabled. Leave blank to disable backup encryption.";s:4:"Type";s:8:"Variable";s:7:"Display";s:8:"advanced";s:8:"Required";s:5:"false";s:4:"Mask";s:4:"true";}s:5:"value";s:0:"";}i:5;a:2:{s:11:"@attributes";a:9:{s:4:"Name";s:10:"ACME_EMAIL";s:6:"Target";s:10:"ACME_EMAIL";s:7:"Default";s:0:"";s:4:"Mode";s:0:"";s:11:"Description";s:176:"Optional, but recommended. Let's Encrypt uses this address to warn you if a certificate renewal is failing — without it you won't be notified until a site actually goes down.";s:4:"Type";s:8:"Variable";s:7:"Display";s:8:"advanced";s:8:"Required";s:5:"false";s:4:"Mask";s:5:"false";}s:5:"value";s:0:"";}i:6;a:2:{s:11:"@attributes";a:9:{s:4:"Name";s:10:"ADMIN_PORT";s:6:"Target";s:10:"ADMIN_PORT";s:7:"Default";s:4:"8080";s:4:"Mode";s:0:"";s:11:"Description";s:106:"Internal port the admin dashboard listens on. Must match the WebUI port mapping's target below if changed.";s:4:"Type";s:8:"Variable";s:7:"Display";s:8:"advanced";s:8:"Required";s:4:"true";s:4:"Mask";s:5:"false";}s:5:"value";s:4:"8080";}i:7;a:2:{s:11:"@attributes";a:9:{s:4:"Name";s:13:"SITE_PORT_MIN";s:6:"Target";s:13:"SITE_PORT_MIN";s:7:"Default";s:4:"9000";s:4:"Mode";s:0:"";s:11:"