;b:1;s:16:"ModeratorComment";N;}i:3409;a:56:{s:4:"Name";s:21:"ComfyUI-Nvidia-Docker";s:10:"Repository";s:55:"mmartial/comfyui-nvidia-docker:ubuntu24_cuda12.8-latest";s:8:"Registry";s:55:"https://hub.docker.com/r/mmartial/comfyui-nvidia-docker";s:7:"Support";s:69:"https://forums.unraid.net/topic/172874-support-comfyui-nvidia-docker/";s:7:"Project";s:49:"https://github.com/mmartial/ComfyUI-Nvidia-Docker";s:11:"TemplateURL";s:100:"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/mmartial/unraid-templates/main/templates/ComfyUI-Nvidia-Docker.xml";s:4:"Icon";s:104:"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/mmartial/unraid-templates/main/templates/img/ComfyUI-Nvidia-Docker.png";s:16:"ExtraSearchTerms";s:40:"WebUI images generation Stable Diffusion";s:7:"Network";s:6:"docker";s:8:"Requires";s:24:"**Nvidia Driver plugin**";s:5:"Shell";s:4:"bash";s:10:"Privileged";s:5:"false";s:8:"Overview";s:2380:"ComfyUI WebUI Dockerfile with Nvidia support, installing ComfyUI from GitHub.
Also installs ComfyUI Manager to simplify integration of additional custom nodes.

The "run directory" contains HF, ComfyUI and venv.
The "basedir" contains input, output and custom_nodes.

The ComfyUI "Manager" is installed to simplify integration of additional custom nodes and their updates.
The "Manager" is also used to update ComfyUI to more recent versions.

All those folders will be created with the WANTED_UID and WANTED_GID parameters (by default using Unraid's default of 99:100) allowing the end-user to place directly into the folders their checkpoints, unet, lora and other required models.

The container comes with no weights/models; you need to obtain those and install them in the proper directories under the mount you have selected for the "run directory".

