IN_API_KEY";s:6:"Target";s:18:"EMBY_ADMIN_API_KEY";s:7:"Default";s:0:"";s:11:"Description";s:65:"Emby API key: Emby Dashboard -> Advanced -> Security -> API Keys.";s:4:"Type";s:8:"Variable";s:7:"Display";s:6:"always";s:8:"Required";s:4:"true";s:4:"Mask";s:4:"true";}s:5:"value";s:0:"";}i:4;a:2:{s:11:"@attributes";a:8:{s:4:"Name";s:17:"POSTGRES_PASSWORD";s:6:"Target";s:17:"POSTGRES_PASSWORD";s:7:"Default";s:0:"";s:11:"Description";s:142:"Password for the bundled PostgreSQL database. Set it once on first start and never change it afterwards, or the database becomes inaccessible.";s:4:"Type";s:8:"Variable";s:7:"Display";s:6:"always";s:8:"Required";s:4:"true";s:4:"Mask";s:4:"true";}s:5:"value";s:0:"";}i:5;a:2:{s:11:"@attributes";a:8:{s:4:"Name";s:18:"APP_ENCRYPTION_KEY";s:6:"Target";s:18:"APP_ENCRYPTION_KEY";s:7:"Default";s:0:"";s:11:"Description";s:153:"Generate once with 'openssl rand -base64 32' and keep it stable. Encrypts stored API keys for Seerr/Radarr/Sonarr/TMDB; if lost, those become unreadable.";s:4:"Type";s:8:"Variable";s:7:"Display";s:6:"always";s:8:"Required";s:4:"true";s:4:"Mask";s:4:"true";}s:5:"value";s:0:"";}i:6;a:2:{s:11:"@attributes";a:8:{s:4:"Name";s:13:"COOKIE_SECURE";s:6:"Target";s:13:"COOKIE_SECURE";s:7:"Default";s:4:"true";s:11:"Description";s:244:"Keep true if you access Emby Insights via HTTPS (e.g. behind a reverse proxy). Set to false ONLY if you access it over plain HTTP without TLS - otherwise the browser silently drops the session cookie and the UI looks logged out / shows no data.";s:4:"Type";s:8:"Variable";s:7:"Display";s:6:"always";s:8:"Required";s:5:"false";s:4:"Mask";s:5:"false";}s:5:"value";s:0:"";}i:7;a:2:{s:11:"@attributes";a:8:{s:4:"Name";s:15:"TRUSTED_PROXIES";s:6:"Target";s:15:"TRUSTED_PROXIES";s:7:"Default";s:0:"";s:11:"Description";s:136:"Comma-separated IPs/CIDRs of an upstream reverse proxy allowed to set X-Forwarded-For. Leave empty if the container is reached directly.";s:4:"Type";s:8:"Variable";s:7:"Display";s:8:"advanced";s:8:"Required";s:5:"false";s:4:"Mask";s:5:"false";}s:5:"value";s:0:"";}}s:12:"TemplatePath";s:47:"/tmp/GitHub/AppFeed/templates/emby-insights.xml";s:4:"Repo";s:19:"mrt187's Repository";s:12:"CategoryList";a:1:{i:0;s:14:"MediaApp-Video";}s:7:"Support";s:0:"";s:16:"ChangeLogPresent";s:1:"1";s:9:"FirstSeen";i:1786118681;s:8:"Category";s:14:"MediaApp:Video";s:2:"ID";i:3431;s:11:"Displayable";b:1;s:6:"Author";s:6:"mrt187";s:13:"DockerHubName";s:13:"emby-insights";s:8:"RepoName";s:19:"mrt187's Repository";s:10:"SortAuthor";s:6:"mrt187";s:8:"SortName";s:13:"emby insights";s:6:"random";i:758894992;s:9:"Blacklist";b:0;s:4:"Path";s:111:"/tmp/community.applications/tempFiles/templates-community-apps/mrt187sRepository/mrt187-embyinsights-latest.xml";s:10:"Deprecated";b:0;s:10:"Compatible";b:1;s:16:"ModeratorComment";N;}i:3432;a:38:{s:4:"Name";s:6:"YunKan";s:10:"Repository";s:27:"martin888/yunkan-cpu:latest";s:8:"Registry";s:45:"https://hub.docker.com/r/martin888/yunkan-cpu";s:7:"Network";s:4:"host";s:5:"Shell";s:2:"sh";s:10:"Privileged";s:5:"false";s:7:"Support";s:60:"https://github.com/mrtian2016/yunkan-unraid-templates/issues";s:7:"Project";s:19:"https://yun-kan.com";s:8:"Overview";s:4952:"YunKan (云瞰) — self-hosted, local-first **NVR / VMS** for home and small-business IP cameras, with on-device AI: motion, **person / vehicle / face recognition / license plate (ALPR / LPR) / pose & fall / package / baby-cry detection**. Your video stays on your LAN — nothing is uploaded to any vendor cloud. A privacy-first **Frigate / Shinobi / ZoneMinder / Scrypted / Agent DVR / iSpy / MotionEye** alternative — pre-bundled into a single container so there is no Mosquitto / database / reverse-proxy / model-download wiring to do by hand.

This is the **CPU variant** — runs on any amd64 Unraid host with no special hardware. Best for 1-4 cameras at moderate FPS. Have an Intel iGPU (J4125 / N100 / N305 / N5105 / 12-14th gen Core)? Install "YunKan-OpenVINO" instead for 3-5x faster inference. Have an NVIDIA GPU? Install "YunKan-CUDA" (or "YunKan-TRT" for the highest throughput). All four variants share the same ports — **only one can run at a time**.

**Works with any RTSP or ONVIF camera** — Reolink, Hikvision, Dahua, Amcrest, Annke, Uniview, EZVIZ, Foscam, Lorex, Anpviz, generic Chinese ONVIF, etc. **Tapo, Wyze, Xiaomi, Eufy, Mi Home, Aqara, Imou** and other proprietary-protocol cameras work via a **go2rtc** bridge. **GB/T 28181 cameras & NVRs** (Hikvision / Dahua / Uniview, etc.) register directly into YunKan — import individual channels, including many NVR channels in one batch.

**Built in:** 24/7 continuous recording + motion-event highlights, **NVR-style multi-camera synced timeline playback**, a **Birdseye** all-cameras overview, **PTZ control with presets**, **virtual tripwires (line-crossing)** for accurate entry/exit direction, customizable **video-wall layouts**, a built-in **file manager** for recordings & snapshots, a **people library** for face recognition, **AI scene understanding** that turns each event into a natural-language summary ("an elderly person fell in the living room" — no OpenAI / Gemini / Claude API keys, all inference on-box), bilingual EN ↔ 中文, **WebRTC (WHEP)** sub-second live streaming with HLS fallback, **two-way talkback** (push-to-talk on supported ONVIF cameras), **Apple Home (HomeKit) incl. HomeKit Secure Video — record motion clips to iCloud (Pro)**, **Home Assistant** integration via MQTT auto-discovery (every camera becomes an HA device with motion / person / vehicle / package / fall / baby-cry binary_sensors), Web admin + Android + iOS apps, optional off-site backup to **115 网盘 (115 Pan / 115 Cloud)**.

![Dashboard](https://raw.githubusercontent.com/mrtian2016/yunkan-Unraid-templates/main/screenshots/dashboard.jpg)

![Events timeline](https://raw.githubusercontent.com/mrtian2016/yunkan-Unraid-templates/main/screenshots/events.jpg)

On first launch, open the WebUI to enter the Setup wizard (pick SQLite for the simplest path), create an admin, and add cameras.

Ports (hardcoded inside the image — don't edit them on this page; if you need to change ports use the docker compose path):
- 23406/tcp — web dashboard + app API + streaming (required)
- 23515/udp+tcp — low-latency live video channel (without it live view falls back to HLS)
- 23880/tcp — RTSP for external players on the LAN (optional)
- 24214/tcp — internal streaming service, no need to expose it

Watching from outside your network: enable it in the web interface (Settings, General, HTTPS certificate) — enter your own domain and your DNS provider's API key and a Let's Encrypt certificate is issued and renewed automatically over DNS-01, so port 80 stays closed. Then pick a public port (23443 by default) and forward that single TCP port on your router; with IPv6 nothing needs forwarding at all. See https://yun-kan.com/docs/remote-access

**Keywords:** NVR, VMS, CCTV, surveillance, security camera, video doorbell, RTSP, ONVIF, IP camera, motion detection, person detection, vehicle detection, face recognition, license plate recognition, ALPR, LPR, fall detection, pose detection, two-way audio, talkback, 24/7 recording, continuous recording, timeline playback, WebRTC, HLS, Home Assistant, MQTT, smart home, AI NVR, AI camera, AI scene understanding, natural language event summary, smart event description, on-device AI, edge AI, offline AI, no API key, no cloud, privacy, self-hosted, Frigate alternative, Shinobi alternative, ZoneMinder alternative, Scrypted alternative, Agent DVR alternative, iSpy alternative, MotionEye alternative, BlueIris alternative, Reolink, Hikvision, Dahua, Amcrest, Annke, Uniview, EZVIZ, Foscam, Lorex, Tapo, Wyze, Xiaomi, Eufy, Imou, Aqara, HomeKit, Apple Home, HomeKit Secure Video, HKSV, Siri, GB28181, GB/T 28181, birdseye, virtual tripwire, line crossing, entry exit detection, video wall, PTZ, pan tilt zoom, package detection, parcel detection, baby cry detection, people library, NVR playback, multi-channel playback, go2rtc, 云瞰, 摄像头, 监控, AI 监控, 本地 AI, 自然语言.";s:5:"WebUI";s:25:"http://[IP]:[PORT:23406]/";s:11:"TemplateURL";s:98:"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/mrtian2016/yunkan-unraid-templates/main/templates/yunkan-cpu.xml";s:4:"Icon";s:82:"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/mrtian2016/yunkan-unraid-templates/main/icon.png";s:6:"Config";a:11:{i:0;a:2:{s:11:"@attributes";a:9:{s:4:"Name";s:14:"Time zone (TZ)";s:6:"Target";s:2:"TZ";s:7:"Default";s:7:"Etc/UTC";s:4:"Mode";s:0:"";s:11:"Description";s:65:"Container time zone. Affects log timestamps and quiet-hours cron.";s:4:"Type";s:8:"Variable";s:7:"Display";s:6:"always";s:8:"Required";s:4:"true";s:4:"Mask";s:5:"false";}s:5:"value";s:7:"Etc/UTC";}i:1;a:2:{s:11:"@attributes";a:9:{s:4:"Name";s:31:"Container name (license anchor)";s:6:"Target";s:27:"SKYVIEW_SELF_CONTAINER_NAME";s:7:"Default";s:6:"YunKan";s:4:"Mode";s:0:"";s:11:"Description";s:154:"Must exactly match the 'Name' field above. The license heartbeat uses this to identify the container itself; if you rename the container, change this too.";s:4:"Type";s:8:"Variable";s:7:"Display";s:8:"advanced";s:8:"Required";s:4:"true";s:4:"Mask";s:5:"false";}s:5:"value";s:6:"YunKan";}i:2;a:2:{s:11:"@attributes";a:9:{s:4:"Name";s:35:"Data directory (DB / config / logs)";s:6:"Target";s:9:"/app/data";s:7:"Default";s:29:"/mnt/user/appdata/yunkan/data";s:4:"Mode";s:2:"rw";s:11:"Description";s:216:"Small state: database, config, cookies, logs, upgrade state. Unraid convention is /mnt/user/appdata/app/ (cache pool / SSD recommended). Recordings have their own path entry below — don't size this share for video.";s:4:"Type";s:4:"Path";s:7:"Display";s:6:"always";s:8:"Required";s:4:"true";s:4:"Mask";s:5:"false";}s:5:"value";s:29:"/mnt/user/appdata/yunkan/data";}i:3;a:2:{s:11:"@attributes";a:9:{s:4:"Name";s:20:"Recordings directory";s:6:"Target";s:20:"/app/data/recordings";s:7:"Default";s:40:"/mnt/user/appdata/yunkan/data/recordings";s:4:"Mode";s:2:"rw";s:11:"Description";s:654:"Camera recordings — can grow to TBs. Mounted on top of the data directory (container path /app/data/recordings), so snapshots / exports / face thumbnails follow it automatically. **To put recordings on a big array share or a dedicated pool, change the host path of THIS entry — do not add your own path mapping with a different container path, it will be silently ignored.** If YunKan already ran on this host and you point this at a new location, FIRST move the contents of .../yunkan/data/recordings/ there — otherwise the old recordings become invisible to the app (playback and auto-cleanup can't see them) while still occupying the data share.";s:4:"Type";s:4:"Path";s:7:"Display";s:6:"always";s:8:"Required";s:4:"true";s:4:"Mask";s:5:"false";}s:5:"value";s:40:"/mnt/user/appdata/yunkan/data/recordings";}i:4;a:2:{s:11:"@attributes";a:9:{s:4:"Name";s:41:"machine-id (license hardware fingerprint)";s:6:"Target";s:15:"/etc/machine-id";s:7:"Default";s:15:"/etc/machine-id";s:4:"Mode";s:2:"ro";s:11:"Description";s:255:"The license uses the Unraid host's machine-id as part of its hardware fingerprint. **Without this mount the fingerprint drifts on every container recreate; the license then consumes a new activation slot and eventually fails to activate.** Keep read-only.";s:4:"Type";s:4:"Path";s:7:"Display";s:8:"advanced";s:8:"Required";s:4:"true";s:4:"Mask";s:5:"false";}s:5:"value";s:15:"/etc/machine-id";}i:5;a:2:{s:11:"@attributes";a:9:{s:4:"Name";s:43:"product_uuid (license hardware fingerprint)";s:6:"Target";s:30:"/sys/class/dmi/id/product_uuid";s:7:"Default";s:30:"/sys/class/dmi/id/product_uuid";s:4:"Mode";s:2:"ro";s:11:"Description";s:74:"Second hardware-fingerprint signal (motherboard DMI UUID). Keep read-only.";s:4:"Type";s:4:"Path";s:7:"Display";s:8:"advanced";s:8:"Required";s:4:"true";s:4:"Mask";s:5:"false";}s:5:"value";s:30:"/sys/class/dmi/id/product_uuid";}i:6;a:2:{s:11:"@attributes";a:9:{s:4:"Name";s:53:"docker socket (self-introspection / OTA self-restart)";s:6:"Target";s:20:"/var/run/docker.sock";s:7:"Default";s:20:"/var/run/docker.sock";s:4:"Mode";s:2:"rw";s:11:"Description";s:127:"YunKan uses the docker socket internally for self-identification and OTA self-restart. The default Unraid permissions are fine.";s:4:"Type";s:4:"Path";s:7:"Display";s:8:"advanced";s:8:"Required";s:4:"true";s:4:"Mask";s:5:"false";}s:5:"value";s:20:"/var/run/docker.sock";}i:7;a:2:{s:11:"@attributes";a:9:{s:4:"Name";s:18:"HTTP / API (nginx)";s:6:"Target";s:5:"23406";s:7:"Default";s:5:"23406";s:4:"Mode";s:3:"tcp";s:11:"Description";s:36:"Web dashboard + REST API front door.";s:4:"Type";s:4:"Port";s:7:"Display";s:6:"always";s:8:"Required";s:5:"false";s:4:"Mask";s:5:"false";}s:5:"value";s:5:"23406";}i:8;a:2:{s:11:"@attributes";a:9:{s:4:"Name";s:4:"RTSP";s:6:"Target";s:5:"23880";s:7:"Default";s:5:"23880";s:4:"Mode";s:3:"tcp";s:11:"Description";s:51:"Cameras and external players connect directly here.";s:4:"Type";s:4:"Port";s:7:"Display";s:6:"always";s:8:"Required";s:5:"false";s:4:"Mask";s:5:"false";}s:5:"value";s:5:"23880";}i:9;a:2:{s:11:"@attributes";a:9:{s:4:"Name";s:26:"Internal streaming service";s:6:"Target";s:5:"24214";s:7:"Default";s:5:"24214";s:4:"Mode";s:3:"tcp";s:11:"Description";s:192:"Internal media server (HLS, WebRTC signaling, hooks). Clients never talk to it directly - they go through 23406 with a signed token - so it does not need to be reachable from outside the host.";s:4:"Type";s:4:"Port";s:7:"Display";s:6:"always";s:8:"Required";s:5:"false";s:4:"Mask";s:5:"false";}s:5:"value";s:5:"24214";}i:10;a:2:{s:11:"@attributes";a:9:{s:4:"Name";s:16:"WebRTC ICE media";s:6:"Target";s:5:"23515";s:7:"Default";s:5:"23515";s:4:"Mode";s:3:"udp";s:11:"Description";s:29:"WebRTC ICE media (UDP + TCP).";s:4:"Type";s:4:"Port";s:7:"Display";s:6:"always";s:8:"Required";s:5:"false";s:4:"Mask";s:5:"false";}s:5:"value";s:5:"23515";}}s:12:"TemplatePath";s:44:"/tmp/GitHub/AppFeed/templates/yunkan-cpu.xml";s:4:"Repo";s:22:"田继业's Repository";s:12:"CategoryList";a:3:{i:0;s:14:"HomeAutomation";i:1;s:14:"MediaApp-Video";i:2;s:8:"Security";}s:16:"ChangeLogPresent";s:1:"1";s:9:"downloads";i:3200;s:9:"FirstSeen";i:1780848192;s:10:"LastUpdate";i:1788877567;s:14:"LastUpdateScan";i:1791274300;s:8:"Category";s:40:"HomeAutomation: MediaApp:Video Security:";s:2:"ID";i:3432;s:11:"Displayable";b:1;s:6:"Author";s:9:"martin888";s:13:"DockerHubName";s:6:"yunkan";s:8:"RepoName";s:22:"田继业's Repository";s:10:"SortAuthor";s:9:"martin888";s:8:"SortName";s:6:"YunKan";s:6:"random";i:960289882;s:9:"Blacklist";b:0;s:6:"MinVer";s:3:"6.0";s:4:"Path";s:102:"/tmp/community.applications/tempFiles/templates-community-apps/sRepository/martin888-YunKan-latest.xml";s:4:"Date";N;s:11:"BrandNewApp";b:1;s:10:"Deprecated";b:0;s:10:"Compatible";b:1;s:16:"ModeratorComment";N;}i:3433;a:40:{s:4:"Name";s:11:"YunKan-CUDA";s:10:"Repository";s:28:"martin888/yunkan-cuda:latest";s:8:"Registry";s:46:"https://hub.docker.com/r/martin888/yunkan-cuda";s:7:"Network";s:4:"host";s:5:"Shell";s:2:"sh";s:10:"Privileged";s:5:"false";s:7:"Support";s:60:"https://github.com/mrtian2016/yunkan-unraid-templates/issues";s:7:"Project";s:19:"https://yun-kan.com";s:8:"Overview";s:5055:"YunKan (云瞰) — self-hosted, local-first **NVR / VMS** for home and small-business IP cameras, with on-device AI: motion, **person / vehicle / face recognition / license plate (ALPR / LPR) / pose & fall / package / baby-cry detection**. Your video stays on your LAN — nothing is uploaded to any vendor cloud. A privacy-first **Frigate / Shinobi / ZoneMinder / Scrypted / Agent DVR / iSpy / MotionEye** alternative — pre-bundled into a single container so there is no Mosquitto / database / reverse-proxy / model-download wiring to do by hand.

This is the **CUDA variant** — uses an **NVIDIA GPU** for inference (≥6 GB VRAM recommended; ≥8 GB for many high-resolution cameras). Tested on **RTX 3060 / 3070 / 4060 / 4070 / A2000 / A4000 / Tesla P4 / T4 / Quadro P2000**. Best fit if you already run a GPU in your Unraid box for Plex / Jellyfin transcoding or other AI workloads; for the absolute highest throughput on the same GPU, see "YunKan-TRT" (one-time engine build on first start).

**Prerequisites:**
1. Install the **"NVIDIA Driver"** plugin in Unraid → reboot → `nvidia-smi` works on the host;
2. This template already sets `--runtime=nvidia` and the NVIDIA_* env vars — no extra config needed;
3. The image is ~3-4 GB, so the first pull will take a while.

No NVIDIA GPU? Install "YunKan" (CPU) or "YunKan-OpenVINO" (Intel iGPU). All four variants share the same ports — **only one can run at a time**.

**Works with any RTSP or ONVIF camera** — Reolink, Hikvision, Dahua, Amcrest, Annke, Uniview, EZVIZ, Foscam, Lorex, Anpviz, generic Chinese ONVIF, etc. **Tapo, Wyze, Xiaomi, Eufy, Mi Home, Aqara, Imou** and other proprietary-protocol cameras work via a **go2rtc** bridge. **GB/T 28181 cameras & NVRs** (Hikvision / Dahua / Uniview, etc.) register directly into YunKan — import individual channels, including many NVR channels in one batch.

**Built in:** 24/7 continuous recording + motion-event highlights, **NVR-style multi-camera synced timeline playback**, a **Birdseye** all-cameras overview, **PTZ control with presets**, **virtual tripwires (line-crossing)** for accurate entry/exit direction, customizable **video-wall layouts**, a built-in **file manager** for recordings & snapshots, a **people library** for face recognition, **AI scene understanding** that turns each event into a natural-language summary ("an elderly person fell in the living room" — no OpenAI / Gemini / Claude API keys, all inference on your own GPU), bilingual EN ↔ 中文, **WebRTC (WHEP)** sub-second live streaming with HLS fallback, **two-way talkback** (push-to-talk on supported ONVIF cameras), **Apple Home (HomeKit) incl. HomeKit Secure Video — record motion clips to iCloud (Pro)**, **Home Assistant** integration via MQTT auto-discovery, Web admin + Android + iOS apps, optional off-site backup to **115 网盘 (115 Pan / 115 Cloud)**.

