;s:11:"Description";s:74:"Second hardware-fingerprint signal (motherboard DMI UUID). Keep read-only.";s:4:"Type";s:4:"Path";s:7:"Display";s:8:"advanced";s:8:"Required";s:4:"true";s:4:"Mask";s:5:"false";}s:5:"value";s:30:"/sys/class/dmi/id/product_uuid";}i:8;a:2:{s:11:"@attributes";a:9:{s:4:"Name";s:53:"docker socket (self-introspection / OTA self-restart)";s:6:"Target";s:20:"/var/run/docker.sock";s:7:"Default";s:20:"/var/run/docker.sock";s:4:"Mode";s:2:"rw";s:11:"Description";s:127:"YunKan uses the docker socket internally for self-identification and OTA self-restart. The default Unraid permissions are fine.";s:4:"Type";s:4:"Path";s:7:"Display";s:8:"advanced";s:8:"Required";s:4:"true";s:4:"Mask";s:5:"false";}s:5:"value";s:20:"/var/run/docker.sock";}i:9;a:2:{s:11:"@attributes";a:9:{s:4:"Name";s:18:"HTTP / API (nginx)";s:6:"Target";s:5:"23406";s:7:"Default";s:5:"23406";s:4:"Mode";s:3:"tcp";s:11:"Description";s:36:"Web dashboard + REST API front door.";s:4:"Type";s:4:"Port";s:7:"Display";s:6:"always";s:8:"Required";s:5:"false";s:4:"Mask";s:5:"false";}s:5:"value";s:5:"23406";}i:10;a:2:{s:11:"@attributes";a:9:{s:4:"Name";s:4:"RTSP";s:6:"Target";s:5:"23880";s:7:"Default";s:5:"23880";s:4:"Mode";s:3:"tcp";s:11:"Description";s:51:"Cameras and external players connect directly here.";s:4:"Type";s:4:"Port";s:7:"Display";s:6:"always";s:8:"Required";s:5:"false";s:4:"Mask";s:5:"false";}s:5:"value";s:5:"23880";}i:11;a:2:{s:11:"@attributes";a:9:{s:4:"Name";s:26:"Internal streaming service";s:6:"Target";s:5:"24214";s:7:"Default";s:5:"24214";s:4:"Mode";s:3:"tcp";s:11:"Description";s:192:"Internal media server (HLS, WebRTC signaling, hooks). Clients never talk to it directly - they go through 23406 with a signed token - so it does not need to be reachable from outside the host.";s:4:"Type";s:4:"Port";s:7:"Display";s:6:"always";s:8:"Required";s:5:"false";s:4:"Mask";s:5:"false";}s:5:"value";s:5:"24214";}i:12;a:2:{s:11:"@attributes";a:9:{s:4:"Name";s:16:"WebRTC ICE media";s:6:"Target";s:5:"23515";s:7:"Default";s:5:"23515";s:4:"Mode";s:3:"udp";s:11:"Description";s:29:"WebRTC ICE media (UDP + TCP).";s:4:"Type";s:4:"Port";s:7:"Display";s:6:"always";s:8:"Required";s:5:"false";s:4:"Mask";s:5:"false";}s:5:"value";s:5:"23515";}}s:12:"TemplatePath";s:45:"/tmp/GitHub/AppFeed/templates/yunkan-cuda.xml";s:4:"Repo";s:22:"田继业's Repository";s:12:"CategoryList";a:3:{i:0;s:14:"HomeAutomation";i:1;s:14:"MediaApp-Video";i:2;s:8:"Security";}s:16:"ChangeLogPresent";s:1:"1";s:9:"downloads";i:3520;s:9:"FirstSeen";i:1780848192;s:10:"LastUpdate";i:1788877777;s:14:"LastUpdateScan";i:1791274300;s:8:"Category";s:40:"HomeAutomation: MediaApp:Video Security:";s:2:"ID";i:3433;s:11:"Displayable";b:1;s:6:"Author";s:9:"martin888";s:13:"DockerHubName";s:11:"yunkan-cuda";s:8:"RepoName";s:22:"田继业's Repository";s:10:"SortAuthor";s:9:"martin888";s:8:"SortName";s:11:"YunKan CUDA";s:6:"random";i:1182008701;s:9:"Blacklist";b:0;s:6:"MinVer";s:3:"6.0";s:4:"Path";s:106:"/tmp/community.applications/tempFiles/templates-community-apps/sRepository/martin888-YunKanCUDA-latest.xml";s:4:"Date";N;s:11:"BrandNewApp";b:1;s:10:"Deprecated";b:0;s:10:"Compatible";b:1;s:16:"ModeratorComment";N;}i:3434;a:39:{s:4:"Name";s:15:"YunKan-OpenVINO";s:10:"Repository";s:32:"martin888/yunkan-openvino:latest";s:8:"Registry";s:50:"https://hub.docker.com/r/martin888/yunkan-openvino";s:7:"Network";s:4:"host";s:5:"Shell";s:2:"sh";s:10:"Privileged";s:5:"false";s:7:"Support";s:60:"https://github.com/mrtian2016/yunkan-unraid-templates/issues";s:7:"Project";s:19:"https://yun-kan.com";s:8:"Overview";s:5004:"YunKan (云瞰) — self-hosted, local-first **NVR / VMS** for home and small-business IP cameras, with on-device AI: motion, **person / vehicle / face recognition / license plate (ALPR / LPR) / pose & fall / package / baby-cry detection**. Your video stays on your LAN — nothing is uploaded to any vendor cloud. A privacy-first **Frigate / Shinobi / ZoneMinder / Scrypted / Agent DVR / iSpy / MotionEye** alternative — pre-bundled into a single container so there is no Mosquitto / database / reverse-proxy / model-download wiring to do by hand.

This is the **OpenVINO variant** — uses Intel iGPU acceleration via **OpenVINO + VAAPI hardware decode**. Best fit for low-power mini-PCs and NAS boxes: **N100 / N300 / N305 / N5105 / J4125 / J5040 / 12th-14th gen Core / UHD 6xx / Iris Xe / Arc**. Inference is typically 3-5x faster than the CPU variant; software decode drops from ~80%/core to ~25%/core via VAAPI — perfect for **N100 / N305 Unraid servers** running many cameras.

**Prerequisites:**
1. Install the **"Intel GPU TOP"** plugin in Unraid → reboot → /dev/dri appears on the host;
2. This template already wires /dev/dri through to the container — no extra config needed.

No Intel iGPU? Install "YunKan" (pure CPU). Have an NVIDIA GPU? Install "YunKan-CUDA" or "YunKan-TRT". All four variants share the same ports — **only one can run at a time**.

**Works with any RTSP or ONVIF camera** — Reolink, Hikvision, Dahua, Amcrest, Annke, Uniview, EZVIZ, Foscam, Lorex, Anpviz, generic Chinese ONVIF, etc. **Tapo, Wyze, Xiaomi, Eufy, Mi Home, Aqara, Imou** and other proprietary-protocol cameras work via a **go2rtc** bridge. **GB/T 28181 cameras & NVRs** (Hikvision / Dahua / Uniview, etc.) register directly into YunKan — import individual channels, including many NVR channels in one batch.

**Built in:** 24/7 continuous recording + motion-event highlights, **NVR-style multi-camera synced timeline playback**, a **Birdseye** all-cameras overview, **PTZ control with presets**, **virtual tripwires (line-crossing)** for accurate entry/exit direction, customizable **video-wall layouts**, a built-in **file manager** for recordings & snapshots, a **people library** for face recognition, **AI scene understanding** that turns each event into a natural-language summary ("an elderly person fell in the living room" — no OpenAI / Gemini / Claude API keys, all inference on-box), bilingual EN ↔ 中文, **WebRTC (WHEP)** sub-second live streaming with HLS fallback, **two-way talkback** (push-to-talk on supported ONVIF cameras), **Apple Home (HomeKit) incl. HomeKit Secure Video — record motion clips to iCloud (Pro)**, **Home Assistant** integration via MQTT auto-discovery, Web admin + Android + iOS apps, optional off-site backup to **115 网盘 (115 Pan / 115 Cloud)**.

![Dashboard](https://raw.githubusercontent.com/mrtian2016/yunkan-Unraid-templates/main/screenshots/dashboard.jpg)

![Events timeline](https://raw.githubusercontent.com/mrtian2016/yunkan-Unraid-templates/main/screenshots/events.jpg)

On first launch, open the WebUI to enter the Setup wizard.

Ports (hardcoded): 23406/tcp web dashboard + app API + streaming (required), 23515/udp+tcp low-latency live video, 23880/tcp RTSP for external players (optional), 24214/tcp internal streaming service (no need to expose).
Watching from outside your network: enable it in the web interface (Settings, General, HTTPS certificate) - your own domain plus your DNS provider's API key gets a Let's Encrypt certificate automatically over DNS-01 (port 80 stays closed); then pick a public port (23443 by default) and forward that one TCP port. See https://yun-kan.com/docs/remote-access

