:20:"myTickrs' Repository";s:12:"CategoryList";a:2:{i:0;s:12:"Productivity";i:1;s:15:"Tools-Utilities";}s:8:"Official";b:1;s:9:"FirstSeen";i:1791953108;s:8:"Category";s:29:"Productivity: Tools:Utilities";s:2:"ID";i:3454;s:11:"Displayable";b:1;s:6:"Author";s:8:"mytickrs";s:13:"DockerHubName";s:8:"mytickrs";s:8:"RepoName";s:20:"myTickrs' Repository";s:10:"SortAuthor";s:8:"mytickrs";s:8:"SortName";s:8:"myTickrs";s:6:"random";i:67539304;s:9:"Blacklist";b:0;s:6:"MinVer";s:3:"6.0";s:4:"Path";s:110:"/tmp/community.applications/tempFiles/templates-community-apps/myTickrsRepository/mytickrs-myTickrs-latest.xml";s:4:"Date";N;s:11:"BrandNewApp";b:1;s:10:"Deprecated";b:0;s:10:"DonateText";N;s:10:"DonateLink";N;s:10:"Compatible";b:1;s:16:"ModeratorComment";N;}i:3455;a:39:{s:4:"Name";s:21:"claude-unraid-manager";s:10:"Repository";s:43:"ghcr.io/mygrexit/claude-unraid-manager:beta";s:4:"Beta";s:4:"true";s:8:"Registry";s:86:"https://github.com/mygrexit/claude-unraid-manager/pkgs/container/claude-unraid-manager";s:7:"Network";s:6:"bridge";s:5:"Shell";s:4:"bash";s:10:"Privileged";s:5:"false";s:7:"Support";s:56:"https://github.com/mygrexit/claude-unraid-manager/issues";s:7:"Project";s:49:"https://github.com/mygrexit/claude-unraid-manager";s:6:"ReadMe";s:56:"https://github.com/mygrexit/claude-unraid-manager#readme";s:7:"License";s:3:"MIT";s:8:"Overview";s:2440:"**For experienced Unraid users only. Careful: this app can do serious damage to your server if you don't know what you're doing.**

Claude Code set up as an Unraid administrator, not as a coding tool: an AI assistant that manages containers, storage, VMs, plugins and configuration from the terminal or from your phone via Remote Control. It is meant to ask before it acts; that only holds as long as you keep the permission prompts on and read them.

**What it does**
- Scans your storage (ZFS, btrfs, array), containers, VMs, plugins, User Scripts and network on every start and writes a CLAUDE.md so Claude knows your server.
- Manages containers via the Docker socket and runs host commands through a short-lived helper container. No privileged mode needed.
- Safe defaults: boot drive read-only, no shares mounted. Opt in to more access as needed.
- Risky commands (downloads piped to a shell, network tools, deletes, writes to the flash drive) always ask for your approval with a reason, whatever the mode; disk formatting and wipes are blocked outright.

**Requirements**
An Anthropic account: a claude.ai subscription (also needed for Remote Control) or a Console API key.

**Setup**
1. Apply this template with the default mounts (adjust the two appdata paths if yours is not /mnt/user/appdata).
2. Click the container in the Docker tab, then Console: you are in the Claude session.
3. Log in once (URL in any browser, paste the code back). Leave the session with Ctrl-b, then d; it keeps running.
4. Phone: open the Claude app, tap Code, pick this session. Sessions start in manual mode and ask before acting.
5. Optional: a `claude-Unraid` command in the Unraid terminal. Two lines in /boot/config/go, shown in the guide (step 4); the container does not write to your host for this.
Full walkthrough: https://github.com/mygrexit/claude-Unraid-manager/blob/main/docs/getting-started.md

**Beta**
Tested on the author's two Unraid 7.3.3 servers (ZFS pool-only), not on a range of setups. It is an AI agent: its rules shape what it does, they do not guarantee it.

**Warning**
The Docker socket gives this container root-equivalent access to your server. The guard rails reduce accidents but are not a security boundary. If you would not do the same work yourself on the Unraid command line, do not install this. Review every action before confirming. Keep backups. The author accepts no liability for data loss or misconfiguration.";s:11:"TemplateURL";s:100:"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/mygrexit/unraid-templates/main/templates/claude-unraid-manager.xml";s:4:"Icon";s:97:"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/mygrexit/unraid-templates/main/images/claude-unraid-manager.png";s:11:"ExtraParams";s:32:"--hostname claude-unraid-manager";s:8:"Requires";s:132:"An Anthropic account (claude.ai subscription or Console API key) and access to the Docker socket. For experienced Unraid users only.";s:6:"Config";a:13:{i:0;a:2:{s:11:"@attributes";a:9:{s:4:"Name";s:31:"Data (login, settings, history)";s:6:"Target";s:5:"/root";s:7:"Default";s:44:"/mnt/user/appdata/claude-unraid-manager/home";s:4:"Mode";s:2:"rw";s:11:"Description";s:219:"Persisted home directory. Holds .claude/ (settings, history) and .claude.json (login). Must survive container rebuilds. Tip: a cache-only (exclusive) appdata share avoids FUSE overhead for the many small history writes.";s:4:"Type";s:4:"Path";s:7:"Display";s:6:"always";s:8:"Required";s:4:"true";s:4:"Mask";s:5:"false";}s:5:"value";s:44:"/mnt/user/appdata/claude-unraid-manager/home";}i:1;a:2:{s:11:"@attributes";a:9:{s:4:"Name";s:9:"Workspace";s:6:"Target";s:10:"/workspace";s:7:"Default";s:49:"/mnt/user/appdata/claude-unraid-manager/workspace";s:4:"Mode";s:2:"rw";s:11:"Description";s:67:"Working directory. CLAUDE.md is auto-generated here on every start.";s:4:"Type";s:4:"Path";s:7:"Display";s:6:"always";s:8:"Required";s:4:"true";s:4:"Mask";s:5:"false";}s:5:"value";s:49:"/mnt/user/appdata/claude-unraid-manager/workspace";}i:2;a:2:{s:11:"@attributes";a:9:{s:4:"Name";s:13:"Docker Socket";s:6:"Target";s:20:"/var/run/docker.sock";s:7:"Defa