UGREEN NASync iDX6011 Pro, running natively on Unraid - no UGOS required. Build your own
dashboard pages from a module library, drive the fans, and theme everything from the
Unraid web UI. Model-gated via DMI, so it safely no-ops on other hardware.";s:11:"TemplateURL";s:118:"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/noodlemctwoodle/unraid-ugreen-idx6011-pro/main/community-apps/ugreen-idx6011-pro.xml";s:12:"TemplatePath";s:57:"/tmp/GitHub/AppFeed/community-apps/ugreen-idx6011-pro.xml";s:4:"Repo";s:28:"noodlemctwoodle's Repository";s:10:"Repository";s:103:"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/noodlemctwoodle/unraid-ugreen-idx6011-pro/main/ugreen-idx6011-pro.plg";s:12:"CategoryList";a:2:{i:0;s:12:"Tools-System";i:1;s:7:"Plugins";}s:6:"Plugin";b:1;s:13:"pluginVersion";s:10:"2026.07.25";s:6:"MinVer";s:6:"6.12.0";s:6:"Author";s:15:"noodlemctwoodle";s:16:"ChangeLogPresent";s:1:"1";s:9:"downloads";i:105;s:9:"FirstSeen";i:1784808253;s:14:"LastUpdateScan";i:1792383193;s:11:"pluginStats";a:13:{i:10;i:26;i:11;i:0;i:12;i:0;s:2:"01";i:0;s:2:"02";i:0;s:2:"03";i:0;s:2:"04";i:0;s:2:"05";i:0;s:2:"06";i:0;s:2:"07";i:26;s:2:"08";i:36;s:2:"09";i:17;s:1:"T";i:105;}s:8:"Category";s:21:"Tools:System Plugins:";s:2:"ID";i:3513;s:11:"Displayable";b:1;s:13:"DockerHubName";s:30:"ugreen idx6011 pro front panel";s:8:"RepoName";s:28:"noodlemctwoodle's Repository";s:10:"SortAuthor";s:15:"noodlemctwoodle";s:8:"SortName";s:30:"UGREEN iDX6011 Pro Front Panel";s:6:"random";i:1309147626;s:9:"Blacklist";b:0;s:4:"Path";s:234:"/tmp/community.applications/tempFiles/templates-community-apps/noodlemctwoodlesRepository/noodlemctwoodle-UGREENiDX6011ProFrontPanel-//raw.githubusercontent.com/noodlemctwoodle/unraid-ugreen-idx6011-pro/main/ugreen-idx6011-pro.plg.xml";s:10:"Deprecated";b:0;s:10:"Compatible";b:1;s:16:"ModeratorComment";N;}i:3514;a:37:{s:4:"Name";s:7:"paddock";s:10:"Repository";s:23:"ghcr.io/nordada/paddock";s:8:"Registry";s:57:"https://github.com/nordada/paddock/pkgs/container/paddock";s:7:"Network";s:6:"bridge";s:5:"Shell";s:2:"sh";s:10:"Privileged";s:5:"false";s:7:"Support";s:41:"https://github.com/nordada/paddock/issues";s:7:"Project";s:34:"https://github.com/nordada/paddock";s:8:"Overview";s:972:"Quietly files completed race torrent downloads (autobrr, Transmission, or a manual drop) into a Plex-friendly library layout, renaming them into a standardized "Show - SYYYYEnn - Title - ptNN.ext" scheme. Copies only, never moves or deletes from your download share, so seeding is unaffected. Matching/naming vocabulary is driven by an "event profile" (Settings tab) - Formula 1 and cycling ship built in. See the project's README for full setup: Transmission's script-torrent-done hook, optional Plex partial-scan refresh, optional hot-folder ingestion, optional Discord notifications, and a password-gated web UI for editing show definitions and testing the matcher.

IMPORTANT: on first run, "Config File" below is auto-seeded from the image's own bundled config/events.json (a small starter list) - open the web UI (set WEBUI_PASSWORD below) or edit that file directly to add the shows/events your own tracker covers, since this list is intentionally not exhaustive.";s:5:"WebUI";s:26:"http://[IP]:[PORT:8420]/ui";s:11:"TemplateURL";s:69:"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/nordada/domestique/main/paddock.xml";s:4:"Icon";s:70:"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/nordada/paddock/main/public/icon.png";s:8:"Requires";s:202:"A downloads share (from Transmission or similar) and a Plex media library share. Both are plain host folders you already have - see each Path config's description below for how to find the right values.";s:6:"Config";a:36:{i:0;a:2:{s:11:"@attributes";a:9:{s:4:"Name";s:29:"WebUI / Webhook / Health Port";s:6:"Target";s:4:"8420";s:7:"Default";s:4:"8420";s:4:"Mode";s:3:"tcp";s:11:"Description";s:118:"Port the web UI (/ui), the Transmission webhook (/webhook/torrent-done), and the health check (/health) all listen on.";s:4:"Type";s:4:"Port";s:7:"Display";s:6:"always";s:8:"Required";s:4:"true";s:4:"Mask";s:5:"false";}s:5:"value";s:4:"8420";}i:1;a:2:{s:11:"@attributes";a:9:{s:4:"Name";s:12:"Library Root";s:6:"Target";s:6:"/media";s:7:"Default";s:26:"/mnt/user/media/motorsport";s:4:"Mode";s:2:"rw";s:11:"Description";s:111:"Your Plex media library root - point this at your actual racing library folder. Renamed/copied files land here.";s:4:"Type";s:4:"Path";s:7:"Display";s:6:"always";s:8:"Required";s:4:"true";s:4:"Mask";s:5:"false";}s:5:"value";s:26:"/mnt/user/media/motorsport";}i:2;a:2:{s:11:"@attributes";a:9:{s:4:"Name";s:12:"LIBRARY_ROOT";s:6:"Target";s:12:"LIBRARY_ROOT";s:7:"Default";s:6:"/media";s:4:"Mode";s:0:"";s:11:"Description";s:141:"The container-side path the app uses for the library (must match Library Root's fixed mount point above - you shouldn't need to change this).";s:4:"Type";s:8:"Variable";s:7:"Display";s:8:"advanced";s:8:"Required";s:4:"true";s:4:"Mask";s:5:"false";}s:5:"value";s:6:"/media";}i:3;a:2:{s:11:"@attributes";a:9:{s:4:"Name";s:15:"Downloads Share";s:6:"Target";s:10:"/downloads";s:7:"Default";s:19:"/mnt/user/downloads";s:4:"Mode";s:2:"rw";s:11:"Description";s:660:"The SAME share Transmission's own container maps to /downloads internally - check Transmission's Docker template path mappings to confirm what that is. This is the whole share (not just its 'complete' subfolder). Read-write: the normal ingestion pipeline only ever copies from here, but the Reseed tab's Dedupe feature deletes a torrent's original download-folder copy once it's confirmed hardlinked to the library instead (an explicit, two-click-confirmed action). Set Mode to ro instead if you'd rather keep this share read-only - Dedupe's relink/verify step still works either way, only its optional 'Delete original copy' follow-up needs write access here.";s:4:"Type";s:4:"Path";s:7:"Display";s:6:"always";s:8:"Required";s:4:"true";s:4:"Mask";s:5:"false";}s:5:"value";s:19:"/mnt/user/downloads";}i:4;a:2:{s:11:"@attributes";a:9:{s:4:"Name";s:33:"Hot-folder (read-write, optional)";s:6:"Target";s:18:"/downloads/paddock";s:7:"Default";s:27:"/mnt/user/downloads/paddock";s:4:"Mode";s:2:"rw";s:11:"Description";s:279:"Optional read-write overlay on a 'paddock' subfolder of the share above, for hot-folder ingestion (drop a file/folder here to bypass Transmission entirely). Only takes effect if HOTFOLDER_DIR below is also set to /downloads/paddock; otherwise this is just an unused empty folder.";s:4:"Type";s:4:"Path";s:7:"Display";s:8:"advanced";s:8:"Required";s:5:"false";s:4:"Mask";s:5:"false";}s:5:"value";s:27:"/mnt/user/downloads/paddock";}i:5;a:2:{s:11:"@attributes";a:9:{s:4:"Name";s:11:"Config File";s:6:"Target";s:19:"/config/events.json";s:7:"Default";s:37:"/mnt/user/appdata/paddock/events.json";s:4:"Mode";s:2:"rw";s:11:"Description";s:257:"Persists your show/event definitions across container updates and image upgrades. Auto-created from the image's bundled config/events.json the first time this file doesn't exist yet (see the Overview above) - edit it by hand or through the web UI afterward.";s:4:"Type";s:4:"Path";s:7:"Display";s:6:"always";s:8:"Required";s:4:"true";s:4:"Mask";s:5:"false";}s:5:"value";s:37:"/mnt/user/appdata/paddock/events.json";}i:6;a:2:{s:11:"@attributes";a:9:{s:4:"Name";s:11:"CONFIG_PATH";s:6:"Target";s:11:"CONFIG_PATH";s:7:"Default";s:19:"/config/events.json";s:4:"Mode";s:0:"";s:11:"Description";s:136:"Where the app looks for the config file above, from inside the container. Matches the Config File mount target - no need to change this.";s:4:"Type";s:8:"Variable";s:7:"Display";s:8:"advanced";s:8:"Required";s:4:"true";s:4:"Mask";s:5:"false";}s:5:"value";s:19:"/config/events.json";}i:7;a:2:{s:11:"@attributes";a:9:{s:4:"Name";s:13:"Settings File";s:6:"Target";s:21:"/config/settings.json";s:7:"Default";s:39:"/mnt/user/appdata/paddock/settings.json";s:4:"Mode";s:2:"rw";s:11:"Description";s:526:"Persists your Plex/Discord/hot-folder settings across container updates. Auto-created (seeded from the PLEX_*/DISCORD_*/HOTFOLDER_* variables below) the first time this file doesn't exist yet - edit it live afterward through the web UI's Settings panel instead of these variables. BEFORE FIRST APPLY: from the Unraid terminal, run 'touch /mnt/user/appdata/paddock/settings.json' (or your own path above if changed) - otherwise Docker creates an empty directory there instead of a file, which the app can't clean up on its own.";s:4:"Type";s:4:"Path";s:7:"Display";s:6:"always";s:8:"Required";s:4:"true";s:4:"Mask";s:5:"false";}s:5:"value";s:39:"/mnt/user/appdata/paddock/settings.json";}i:8;a:2:{s:11:"@attributes";a:9:{s:4:"Name";s:13:"SETTINGS_PATH";s:6:"Target";s:13:"SETTINGS_PATH";s:7:"Default";s:21:"/config/settings.json";s:4:"Mode";s:0:"";s:11:"Description";s:140:"Where the app looks for the settings file above, from inside the container. Matches the Settings File mount target - no need to change this.";s:4:"Type";s:8:"Variable";s:7:"Display";s:8:"advanced";s:8:"Required";s:4:"true";s:4:"Mask";s:5:"false";}s:5:"value";s:21:"/config/settings.json";}i:9;a:2:{s:11:"@attributes";a:9:{s:4:"Name";s:12:"Activity Log";s:6:"Target";s:21:"/config/activity.json";s:7:"Default";s:39:"/mnt/user/appdata/paddock/activity.json";s:4:"Mode";s:2:"rw";s:11:"Description";s:389:"Persists the web UI's recent-activity log across container updates and restarts. Auto-created empty the first time this file doesn't exist yet. BEFORE FIRST APPLY: from the Unraid terminal, run 'touch /mnt/user/appdata/paddock/activity.json' (or your own path above if changed) - otherwise Docker creates an empty directory there instead of a file, which the app can't clean up on its own.";s:4:"Type";s:4:"Path";s:7:"Display";s:8:"advanced";s:8:"Required";s:4:"true";s:4:"Mask";s:5:"false";}s:5:"value";s:39:"/mnt/user/appdata/paddock/activity.json";}i:10;a:2:{s:11:"@attributes";a:9:{s:4:"Name";s:13:"ACTIVITY_PATH";s:6:"Target";s:13:"ACTIVITY_PATH";s:7:"Default";s:21:"/config/activity.json";s:4:"Mode";s:0:"";s:11:"Description";s:138:"Where the app looks for the activity log above, from inside the container. Matches the Activity Log mount target - no need to change this.";s:4:"Type";s:8:"Variable";s:7:"Display";s:8:"advanced";s:8:"Required";s:4:"true";s:4:"Mask";s:5:"false";}s:5:"value";s:21:"/config/activity.json";}i:11;a:2:{s:11:"@attributes";a:9:{s:4:"Name";s:12:"Dedupe State";s:6:"Target";s:25:"/config/dedupe-state.json";s:7:"Default";s:43:"/mnt/user/appdata/paddock/dedupe-state.json";s:4:"Mode";s:2:"rw";s:11:"Description";s:557:"Records where a deduped torrent's data lived before the Reseed tab's Dedupe feature relinked it to your library - Transmission itself forgets a torrent's previous location once relocated, so this is the app's own persisted memory of it instead. Auto-created empty the first time this file doesn't exist yet. BEFORE FIRST APPLY: from the Unraid terminal, run