e first time this file doesn't exist yet. BEFORE FIRST APPLY: from the Unraid terminal, run 'touch /mnt/user/appdata/paddock/archive-state.json' (or your own path above if changed) - otherwise Docker creates an empty directory there instead of a file, which the app can't clean up on its own.";s:4:"Type";s:4:"Path";s:7:"Display";s:8:"advanced";s:8:"Required";s:4:"true";s:4:"Mask";s:5:"false";}s:5:"value";s:44:"/mnt/user/appdata/paddock/archive-state.json";}i:18;a:2:{s:11:"@attributes";a:9:{s:4:"Name";s:18:"ARCHIVE_STATE_PATH";s:6:"Target";s:18:"ARCHIVE_STATE_PATH";s:7:"Default";s:26:"/config/archive-state.json";s:4:"Mode";s:0:"";s:11:"Description";s:145:"Where the app looks for the archive-state file above, from inside the container. Matches the Archive State mount target - no need to change this.";s:4:"Type";s:8:"Variable";s:7:"Display";s:8:"advanced";s:8:"Required";s:4:"true";s:4:"Mask";s:5:"false";}s:5:"value";s:26:"/config/archive-state.json";}i:19;a:2:{s:11:"@attributes";a:9:{s:4:"Name";s:16:"Torrent Registry";s:6:"Target";s:24:"/config/torrent-registry";s:7:"Default";s:42:"/mnt/user/appdata/paddock/torrent-registry";s:4:"Mode";s:2:"rw";s:11:"Description";s:429:"A durable copy of every .torrent Paddock has a record of (staged through the Index tab, or synced in from Transmission's own torrents directory below), keyed by info-hash - lets you download any of them back later or skip re-processing an already-registered one on a repeat batch drop. A directory mount - unlike the file mounts above, there's no first-run empty-directory gotcha here, since a directory is exactly what's wanted.";s:4:"Type";s:4:"Path";s:7:"Display";s:8:"advanced";s:8:"Required";s:4:"true";s:4:"Mask";s:5:"false";}s:5:"value";s:42:"/mnt/user/appdata/paddock/torrent-registry";}i:20;a:2:{s:11:"@attributes";a:9:{s:4:"Name";s:20:"TORRENT_REGISTRY_DIR";s:6:"Target";s:20:"TORRENT_REGISTRY_DIR";s:7:"Default";s:24:"/config/torrent-registry";s:4:"Mode";s:0:"";s:11:"Description";s:146:"Where the app looks for the torrent registry above, from inside the container. Matches the Torrent Registry mount target - no need to change this.";s:4:"Type";s:8:"Variable";s:7:"Display";s:8:"advanced";s:8:"Required";s:4:"true";s:4:"Mask";s:5:"false";}s:5:"value";s:24:"/config/torrent-registry";}i:21;a:2:{s:11:"@attributes";a:9:{s:4:"Name";s:53:"Transmission's own torrents dir (read-only, optional)";s:6:"Target";s:22:"/transmission-torrents";s:7:"Default";s:39:"/mnt/user/appdata/transmission/torrents";s:4:"Mode";s:2:"ro";s:11:"Description";s:563:"Optional: Transmission's OWN .torrent-storage directory (its config dir's 'torrents' subfolder, next to its own settings.json/resume/ - check Transmission's Docker template path mappings to find its config directory's host path). When set AND TRANSMISSION_TORRENTS_DIR below is also set to /transmission-torrents, every .torrent Transmission has ever been handed - including anything autobrr added directly, never touching Paddock - gets synced into the Torrent Registry above automatically. Leave blank to disable; this share is only ever read, never written to.";s:4:"Type";s:4:"Path";s:7:"Display";s:8:"advanced";s:8:"Required";s:5:"false";s:4:"Mask";s:5:"false";}s:5:"value";s:0:"";}i:22;a:2:{s:11:"@attributes";a:9:{s:4:"Name";s:25:"TRANSMISSION_TORRENTS_DIR";s:6:"Target";s:25:"TRANSMISSION_TORRENTS_DIR";s:7:"Default";s:0:"";s:4:"Mode";s:0:"";s:11:"Description";s:193:"Set to /transmission-torrents (matching the mount target above) to enable the sync described there. Leave blank to disable, same as leaving the mount above blank - both need to be set together.";s:4:"Type";s:8:"Variable";s:7:"Display";s:8:"advanced";s:8:"Required";s:5:"false";s:4:"Mask";s:5:"false";}s:5:"value";s:0:"";}i:23;a:2:{s:11:"@attributes";a:9:{s:4:"Name";s:8:"PLEX_URL";s:6:"Target";s:8:"PLEX_URL";s:7:"Default";s:0:"";s:4:"Mode";s:0:"";s:11:"Description";s:242:"One-time seed only: used to create Settings File above if it doesn't exist yet, then ignored - edit Plex settings live afterward via the web UI. Enables a Plex partial-scan refresh after each successful archive. e.g. http://192.168.1.10:32400";s:4:"Type";s:8:"Variable";s:7:"Display";s:6:"always";s:8:"Required";s:5:"false";s:4:"Mask";s:5:"false";}s:5:"value";s:0:"";}i:24;a:2:{s:11:"@attributes";a:9:{s:4:"Name";s:10:"PLEX_TOKEN";s:6:"Target";s:10:"PLEX_TOKEN";s:7:"Default";s:0:"";s:4:"Mode";s:0:"";s:11:"Description";s:141:"One-time seed only (see PLEX_URL above). Your Plex auth token, required if PLEX_URL is set. See the README's Plex section for how to find it.";s:4:"Type";s:8:"Variable";s:7:"Display";s:6:"always";s:8:"Required";s:5:"false";s:4:"Mask";s:4:"true";}s:5:"value";s:0:"";}i:25;a:2:{s:11:"@attributes";a:9:{s:4:"Name";s:15:"PLEX_SECTION_ID";s:6:"Target";s:15:"PLEX_SECTION_ID";s:7:"Default";s:0:"";s:4:"Mode";s:0:"";s:11:"Description";s:107:"One-time seed only (see PLEX_URL above). The racing library's Plex section id, required if PLEX_URL is set.";s:4:"Type";s:8:"Variable";s:7:"Display";s:6:"always";s:8:"Required";s:5:"false";s:4:"Mask";s:5:"false";}s:5:"value";s:0:"";}i:26;a:2:{s:11:"@attributes";a:9:{s:4:"Name";s:17:"PLEX_LIBRARY_ROOT";s:6:"Target";s:17:"PLEX_LIBRARY_ROOT";s:7:"Default";s:0:"";s:4:"Mode";s:0:"";s:11:"Description";s:208:"One-time seed only (see PLEX_URL above). Only needed if Plex's own container sees this library at a different internal path than Library Root above (the same category of issue as the Downloads Share mapping).";s:4:"Type";s:8:"Variable";s:7:"Display";s:8:"advanced";s:8:"Required";s:5:"false";s:4:"Mask";s:5:"false";}s:5:"value";s:0:"";}i:27;a:2:{s:11:"@attributes";a:9:{s:4:"Name";s:13:"HOTFOLDER_DIR";s:6:"Target";s:13:"HOTFOLDER_DIR";s:7:"Default";s:0:"";s:4:"Mode";s:0:"";s:11:"Description";s:269:"One-time seed only: used to create Settings File above if it doesn't exist yet, then ignored - edit hot-folder settings live afterward via the web UI. Set to /downloads/paddock to enable hot-folder ingestion (matches the read-write mount above). Leave unset to disable.";s:4:"Type";s:8:"Variable";s:7:"Display";s:6:"always";s:8:"Required";s:5:"false";s:4:"Mask";s:5:"false";}s:5:"value";s:0:"";}i:28;a:2:{s:11:"@attributes";a:9:{s:4:"Name";s:26:"HOTFOLDER_POLL_INTERVAL_MS";s:6:"Target";s:26:"HOTFOLDER_POLL_INTERVAL_MS";s:7:"Default";s:5:"60000";s:4:"Mode";s:0:"";s:11:"Description";s:142:"One-time seed only (see HOTFOLDER_DIR above). Tuning: how often (ms) to check a hot-folder drop for size/mtime stability before processing it.";s:4:"Type";s:8:"Variable";s:7:"Display";s:8:"advanced";s:8:"Required";s:5:"false";s:4:"Mask";s:5:"false";}s:5:"value";s:0:"";}i:29;a:2:{s:11:"@attributes";a:9:{s:4:"Name";s:22:"HOTFOLDER_STABLE_POLLS";s:6:"Target";s:22:"HOTFOLDER_STABLE_POLLS";s:7:"Default";s:1:"3";s:4:"Mode";s:0:"";s:11:"Description";s:132:"One-time seed only (see HOTFOLDER_DIR above). Tuning: consecutive stable polls required before a hot-folder drop is treated as done.";s:4:"Type";s:8:"Variable";s:7:"Display";s:8:"advanced";s:8:"Required";s:5:"false";s:4:"Mask";s:5:"false";}s:5:"value";s:0:"";}i:30;a:2:{s:11:"@attributes";a:9:{s:4:"Name";s:19:"DISCORD_WEBHOOK_URL";s:6:"Target";s:19:"DISCORD_WEBHOOK_URL";s:7:"Default";s:0:"";s:4:"Mode";s:0:"";s:11:"Description";s:294:"One-time seed only: used to create Settings File above if it doesn't exist yet, then ignored - edit Discord settings live afterward via the web UI. Posts a summary message to a Discord channel after every torrent-done event. Create one via the target channel's Settings, Integrations, Webhooks.";s:4:"Type";s:8:"Variable";s:7:"Display";s:6:"always";s:8:"Required";s:5:"false";s:4:"Mask";s:4:"true";}s:5:"value";s:0:"";}i:31;a:2:{s:11:"@attributes";a:9:{s:4:"Name";s:23:"DISCORD_MENTION_USER_ID";s:6:"Target";s:23:"DISCORD_MENTION_USER_ID";s:7:"Default";s:0:"";s:4:"Mode";s:0:"";s:11:"Description";s:225:"One-time seed only (see DISCORD_WEBHOOK_URL above). A Discord user id to @mention, but only on review-worthy notifications (auto-created shows, warnings, errors). Leave unset to have every notification post without a mention.";s:4:"Type";s:8:"Variable";s:7:"Display";s:8:"advanced";s:8:"Required";s:5:"false";s:4:"Mask";s:5:"false";}s:5:"value";s:0:"";}i:32;a:2:{s:11:"@attributes";a:9:{s:4:"Name";s:14:"WEBUI_PASSWORD";s:6:"Target";s:14:"WEBUI_PASSWORD";s:7:"Default";s:0:"";s:4:"Mode";s:0:"";s:11:"Description";s:223:"Set this to enable the web UI at /ui (events editor, match tester, upload, activity log). Fails CLOSED, not open: leaving this unset keeps /ui and /api/* returning 503, since that surface can read and overwrite your config.";s:4:"Type";s:8:"Variable";s:7:"Display";s:6:"always";s:8:"Required";s:5:"false";s:4:"Mask";s:4:"true";}s:5:"value";s:0:"";}i:33;a:2:{s:11:"@attributes";a:9:{s:4:"Name";s:10:"WEBUI_USER";s:6:"Target";s:10:"WEBUI_USER";s:7:"Default";s:0:"";s:4:"Mode";s:0:"";s:11:"Description";s:150:"Optional: also require this exact username (HTTP Basic Auth) alongside WEBUI_PASSWORD. Leave unset to accept any username, checking only the password.";s:4:"Type";s:8:"Variable";s:7:"Display";s:8:"advanced";s:8:"Required";s:5:"false";s:4:"Mask";s:5:"false";}s:5:"value";s:0:"";}i:34;a:2:{s:11:"@attributes";a:9:{s:4:"Name";s:4:"PUID";s:6:"Target";s:4:"PUID";s:7:"Default";s:2:"99";s:4:"Mode";s:0:"";s:11:"Description";s:412:"Run the app as this user id instead of root (99 = Unraid's 'nobody', the same user most containers including Transmission run as). The container fixes ownership of its two config files automatically; the Library Root (and hot-folder, if used) must be writable by this user - on a default Unraid share that's already true, otherwise run once from the terminal: chown -R 99:100 on those paths. Blank = run as root.";s:4:"Type";s:8:"Variable";s:7:"Display";s:6:"always";s:8:"Required";s:5:"false";s:4:"Mask";s:5:"false";}s:5:"value";s:2:"99";}i:35;a:2:{s:11:"@attributes";a:9:{s:4:"Name";s:4:"PGID";s:6:"Target";s:4:"PGID";s:7:"Default";s:3:"100";s:4:"Mode";s:0:"";s:11:"Description";s:98:"Group id to run as (100 = Unraid's 'users' group, paired with PUID 99 above). Blank = run as root.";s:4:"Type";s:8:"Variable";s:7:"Display";s:6:"always";s:8:"Required";s:5:"false";s:4:"Mask";s:5:"false";}s:5:"value";s:3:"100";}}s:12:"TemplatePath";s:31:"/tmp/GitHub/AppFeed/paddock.xml";s:4:"Repo";s:20:"nordada's Repository";s:12:"CategoryList";a:3:{i:0;s:15:"Tools-Utilities";i:1;s:14:"MediaApp-Video";i:2;s:11:"Downloaders";}s:9:"FirstSeen";i:1785743710;s:8:"Category";s:43:"Tools:Utilities MediaApp:Video Downloaders:";s:2:"ID";i:3514;s:11:"Displayable";b:1;s:6:"Author";s:7:"nordada";s:13:"DockerHubName";s:7:"paddock";s:8:"RepoName";s:20:"nordada's Repository";s:10:"SortAuthor";s:7:"nordada";s:8:"SortName";s:7:"paddock";s:6:"random";i:1622611873;s:9:"Blacklist";b:0;s:6:"MinVer";s:3:"6.0";s:4:"Path";s:108:"/tmp/community.applications/tempFiles/templates-community-apps/nordadasRepository/nordada-paddock-latest.xml";s:4:"Date";N;s:11:"BrandNewApp";b:1;s:10:"Deprecated";b:0;s:13:"BranchDefault";N;s:8:"BranchID";a:1:{i:0;i:3515;}s:10:"Compatible";b:1;s:16:"ModeratorComment";N;}i:3515;a:38:{s:4:"Name";s:7:"paddock";s:10:"Repository";s:137:"ghcr.io/nordada/paddock:latest: current main branch. Version tags (e.g. v0.1.035) are also published if you want to pin a specific build.";s:8:"Registry";s:57:"https://github.com/nordada/paddock/pkgs/container/paddock";s:7:"Network";s:6:"bridge";s:5:"Shell";s:2:"sh";s:10:"Privileged";s:5:"false";s:7:"Support";s:41:"https://github.com/nordada/paddock/issues";s:7:"Project";s:34:"https://github.com/nordada/paddock";s:8:"Overview";s:972:"Quietly files completed race torrent downloads (autobrr, Transmission, or a manual drop) into a Plex-friendly library layout, renaming them into a standardized "Show - SYYYYEnn - Title - ptNN.ext" scheme. Copies only, never moves or deletes from your download share, so seeding is unaffected. Matching/naming vocabulary is driven by an "event profile" (Settings tab) - Formula 1 and cycling ship built in. See the project's README for full setup: Transmission's script-torrent-done hook, optional Plex partial-scan refresh, optional hot-folder ingestion, optional Discord notifications, and a password-gated web UI for editing show definitions and testing the matcher.

IMPORTANT: on first run, "Config File" below is auto-seeded from the image's own bundled config/events.json (a small starter list) - open the web UI (set WEBUI_PASSWORD below) or edit that file directly to add the shows/events your own tracker covers, since this list is intentionally not exhaustive.";s:5:"WebUI";s:26:"http://[IP]:[PORT:8420]/ui";s:11:"TemplateURL";s:69:"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/nordada/domestique/main/paddock.xml";s:4:"Icon";s:70:"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/nordada/paddock/main/public/icon.png";s:8:"Requires";s:202:"A downloads share (from Transmission or similar) and a Plex media library share. Both are plain host folders you already have - see each Path config's description below for how to find the right values.";s:6:"Config";a:36:{i:0;a:2:{s:11:"@attributes";a:9:{s:4:"Name";s:29:"WebUI / Webhook / Health Port";s:6:"Target";s:4:"8420";s:7:"Default";s:4:"8420";s:4:"Mode";s:3:"tcp";s:11:"Description";s:118:"Port the web UI (/ui), the Transmission webhook (/webhook/torrent-done), and the health check (/health) all listen on.";s:4:"Type";s:4:"Port";s:7:"Display";s:6:"always";s:8:"Required";s:4:"true";s:4:"Mask";s:5:"false";}s:5:"value";s:4:"8420";}i:1;a:2:{s:11:"@attributes";a:9:{s:4:"Name";s:12:"Library Root";s:6:"Target";s:6:"/media";s:7:"Default";s:26:"/mnt/user/media/motorsport";s:4:"Mode";s:2:"rw";s:11:"Description";s:111:"Your Plex media library root - point this at your actual racing library folder. Renamed/copied files land here.";s:4:"Type";s:4:"Path";s:7:"Display";s:6:"always";s:8:"Required";s:4:"true";s:4:"Mask";s:5:"false";}s:5:"value";s:26:"/mnt/user/media/motorsport";}i:2;a:2:{s:11:"@attributes";a:9:{s:4:"Name";s:12:"LIBRARY_ROOT";s:6:"Target";s:12:"LIBRARY_ROOT";s:7:"Default";s:6:"/media";s:4:"Mode";s:0:"";s:11:"Description";s:141:"The container-side path the app uses for the library (must match Library Root's fixed mount point above - you shouldn't need to change this).";s:4:"Type";s:8:"Variable";s:7:"Display";s:8:"advanced";s:8:"Required";s:4:"true";s:4:"Mask";s:5:"false";}s:5:"value";s:6:"/media";}i:3;a:2:{s:11:"@attributes";a:9:{s:4:"Name";s:15:"Downloads Share";s:6:"Target";s:10:"/downloads";s:7:"Default";s:19:"/mnt/user/downloads";s:4:"Mode";s:2:"rw";s:11:"Description";s:660:"The SAME share Transmission's own container maps to /downloads internally - check Transmission's Docker template path mappings to confirm what that is. This is the whole share (not just its 'complete' subfolder). Read-write: the normal ingestion pipeline only ever copies from here, but the Reseed tab's Dedupe feature deletes a torrent's original download-folder copy once it's confirmed hardlinked to the library instead (an explicit, two-click-confirmed action). Set Mode to ro instead if you'd rather keep this share read-only - Dedupe's relink/verify step still works either way, only its optional 'Delete original copy' follow-up needs write access here.";s:4:"Type";s:4:"Path";s:7:"Display";s:6:"always";s:8:"Required";s:4:"true";s:4:"Mask";s:5:"false";}s:5:"value";s:19:"/mnt/user/downloads";}i:4;a:2:{s:11:"@attributes";a:9:{s:4:"Name";s:33:"Hot-folder (read-write, optional)";s:6:"Target";s:18:"/downloads/paddock";s:7:"Default";s:27:"/mnt/user/downloads/paddock";s:4:"Mode";s:2:"rw";s:11:"Description";s:279:"Optional read-write overlay on a 'paddock' subfolder of the share above, for hot-folder ingestion (drop a file/folder here to bypass Transmission entirely). Only takes effect if HOTFOLDER_DIR below is also set to /downloads/paddock; otherwise this is just an unused empty folder.";s:4:"Type";s:4:"Path";s:7:"Display";s:8:"advanced";s:8:"Required";s:5:"false";s:4:"Mask";s:5:"false";}s:5:"value";s:27:"/mnt/user/downloads/paddock";}i:5;a:2:{s:11:"@attributes";a:9:{s:4:"Name";s:11:"Config File";s:6:"Target";s:19:"/config/events.json";s:7:"Default";s:37:"/mnt/user/appdata/paddock/events.json";s:4:"Mode";s:2:"rw";s:11:"Description";s:257:"Persists your show/event definitions across container updates and image upgrades. Auto-created from the image's bundled config/events.json the first time this file doesn't exist yet (see the Overview above) - edit it by hand or through the web UI afterward.";s:4:"Type";s:4:"Path";s:7:"Display";s:6:"always";s:8:"Required";s:4:"true";s:4:"Mask";s:5:"false";}s:5:"value";s:37:"/mnt/user/appdata/paddock/events.json";}i:6;a:2:{s:11:"@attributes";a:9:{s:4:"Name";s:11:"CONFIG_PATH";s:6:"Target";s:11:"CONFIG_PATH";s:7:"Default";s:19:"/config/events.json";s:4:"Mode";s:0:"";s:11:"Description";s:136:"Where the app looks for the config file above, from inside the container. Matches the Config File mount target - no need to change this.";s:4:"Type";s:8:"Variable";s:7:"Display";s:8:"advanced";s:8:"Required";s:4:"true";s:4:"Mask";s:5:"false";}s:5:"value";s:19:"/config/events.json";}i:7;a:2:{s:11:"@attributes";a:9:{s:4:"Name";s:13:"Settings File";s:6:"Target";s:21:"/config/settings.json";s:7:"Default";s:39:"/mnt/user/appdata/paddock/settings.json";s:4:"Mode";s:2:"rw";s:11:"Description";s:526:"Persists your Plex/Discord/hot-folder settings across container updates. Auto-created (seeded from the PLEX_*/DISCORD_*/HOTFOLDER_* variables below) the first time this file doesn't exist yet - edit it live afterward through the web UI's Settings panel instead of these variables. BEFORE FIRST APPLY: from the Unraid terminal, run 'touch /mnt/user/appdata/paddock/settings.json' (or your own path above if changed) - otherwise Docker creates an empty directory there instead of a file, which the app can't clean up on its own.";s:4:"Type";s:4:"Path";s:7:"Display";s:6:"always";s:8:"Required";s:4:"true";s:4:"Mask";s:5:"false";}s:5:"value";s:39:"/mnt/user/appdata/paddock/settings.json";}i:8;a:2:{s:11:"@attributes";a:9:{s:4:"Name";s:13:"SETTINGS_PATH";s:6:"Target";s:13:"SETTINGS_PATH";s:7:"Default";s:21:"/config/settings.json";s:4:"Mode";s:0:"";s:11:"Description";s:140:"Where the app looks for the settings file above, from inside the container. Matches the Settings File mount target - no need to change this.";s:4:"Type";s:8:"Variable";s:7:"Display";s:8:"advanced";s:8:"Required";s:4:"true";s:4:"Mask";s:5:"false";}s:5:"value";s:21:"/config/settings.json";}i:9;a:2:{s:11:"@attributes";a:9:{s:4:"Name";s:12:"Activity Log";s:6:"Target";s:21:"/config/activity.json";s:7:"Default";s:39:"/mnt/user/appdata/paddock/activity.json";s:4:"Mode";s:2:"rw";s:11:"Description";s:389:"Persists the web UI's recent-activity log across container updates and restarts. Auto-created empty the first time this file doesn't exist yet. BEFORE FIRST APPLY: from the Unraid terminal, run 'touch /mnt/user/appdata/paddock/activity.json' (or your own path above if changed) - otherwise Docker creates an empty directory there instead of a file, which the app can't clean up on its own.";s:4:"Type";s:4:"Path";s:7:"Display";s:8:"advanced";s:8:"Required";s:4:"true";s:4:"Mask";s:5:"false";}s:5:"value";s:39:"/mnt/user/appdata/paddock/activity.json";}i:10;a:2:{s:11:"@attributes";a:9:{s:4:"Name";s:13:"ACTIVITY_PATH";s:6:"Target";s:13:"ACTIVITY_PATH";s:7:"Default";s:21:"/config/activity.json";s:4:"Mode";s:0:"";s:11:"Description";s:138:"Where the app looks for the activity log above, from inside the container. Matches the Activity Log mount target - no need to change this.";s:4:"Type";s:8:"Variable";s:7:"Display";s:8:"advanced";s:8:"Required";s:4:"true";s:4:"Mask";s:5:"false";}s:5:"value";s:21:"/config/activity.json";}i:11;a:2:{s:11:"@attributes";a:9:{s:4:"Name";s:12:"Dedupe State";s:6:"Target";s:25:"/config/dedupe-state.json";s:7:"Default";s:43:"/mnt/user/appdata/paddock/dedupe-state.json";s:4:"Mode";s:2:"rw";s:11:"Description";s:557:"Records where a deduped torrent's data lived before the Reseed tab's Dedupe feature relinked it to your library - Transmission itself forgets a torrent's previous location once relocated, so this is the app's own persisted memory of it instead. Auto-created empty the first time this file doesn't exist yet. BEFORE FIRST APPLY: from the Unraid terminal, run 'touch /mnt/user/appdata/paddock/dedupe-state.json' (or your own path above if changed) - otherwise Docker creates an empty directory there instead of a file, which the app can't clean up on its own.";s:4:"Type";s:4:"Path";s:7:"Display";s:8:"advanced";s:8:"Required";s:4:"true";s:4:"Mask";s:5:"false";}s:5:"value";s:43:"/mnt/user/appdata/paddock/dedupe-state.json";}i:12;a:2:{s:11:"@attributes";a:9:{s:4:"Name";s:17:"DEDUPE_STATE_PATH";s:6:"Target";s:17:"DEDUPE_STATE_PATH";s:7:"Default";s:25:"/config/dedupe-state.json";s:4:"Mode";s:0:"";s:11:"Description";s:143:"Where the app looks for the dedupe-state file above, from inside the container. Matches the Dedupe State mount target - no need to change this.";s:4:"Type";s:8:"Variable";s:7:"Display";s:8:"advanced";s:8:"Required";s:4:"true";s:4:"Mask";s:5:"false";}s:5:"value";s:25:"/config/dedupe-state.json";}i:13;a:2:{s:11:"@attributes";a:9:{s:4:"Name";s:12:"Verify State";s:6:"Target";s:25:"/config/verify-state.json";s:7:"Default";s:43:"/mnt/user/appdata/paddock/verify-state.json";s:4:"Mode";s:2:"rw";s:11:"Description";s:401:"Persists the Index tab's 'Verify data' integrity-check results across container updates. Auto-created empty the first time this file doesn't exist yet. BEFORE FIRST APPLY: from the Unraid terminal, run 'touch /mnt/user/appdata/paddock/verify-state.json' (or your own path above if changed) - otherwise Docker creates an empty directory there instead of a file, which the app can't clean up on its own.";s:4:"Type";s:4:"Path";s:7:"Display";s:8:"advanced";s:8:"Required";s:4:"true";s:4:"Mask";s:5:"false";}s:5:"value";s:43:"/mnt/user/appdata/paddock/verify-state.json";}i:14;a:2:{s:11:"@attributes";a:9:{s:4:"Name";s:17:"VERIFY_STATE_PATH";s:6:"Target";s:17:"VERIFY_STATE_PATH";s:7:"Default";s:25:"/config/verify-state.json";s:4:"Mode";s:0:"";s:11:"Description";s:143:"Where the app looks for the verify-state file above, from inside the container. Matches the Verify State mount target - no need to change this.";s:4:"Type";s:8:"Variable";s:7:"Display";s:8:"advanced";s:8:"Required";s:4:"true";s:4:"Mask";s:5:"false";}s:5:"value";s:25:"/config/verify-state.json";}i:15;a:2:{s:11:"@attributes";a:9:{s:4:"Name";s:15:"Match Overrides";s:6:"Target";s:28:"/config/match-overrides.json";s:7:"Default";s:46:"/mnt/user/appdata/paddock/match-overrides.json";s:4:"Mode";s:2:"rw";s:11:"Description";s:512:"Persists a human's own picks from the Index tab's 'Resolve ambiguous files' modal across container updates - without this, a resolved pick silently reverts to 'ambiguous' again on the next update. Auto-created empty the first time this file doesn't exist yet. BEFORE FIRST APPLY: from the Unraid terminal, run 'touch /mnt/user/appdata/paddock/match-overrides.json' (or your own path above if changed) - otherwise Docker creates an empty directory there instead of a file, which the app can't clean up on its own.";s:4:"Type";s:4:"Path";s:7:"Display";s:8:"advanced";s:8:"Required";s:4:"true";s:4:"Mask";s:5:"false";}s:5:"value";s:46:"/mnt/user/appdata/paddock/match-overrides.json";}i:16;a:2:{s:11:"@attributes";a:9:{s:4:"Name";s:20:"MATCH_OVERRIDES_PATH";s:6:"Target";s:20:"MATCH_OVERRIDES_PATH";s:7:"Default";s:28:"/config/match-overrides.json";s:4:"Mode";s:0:"";s:11:"Description";s:149:"Where the app looks for the match-overrides file above, from inside the container. Matches the Match Overrides mount target - no need to change this.";s:4:"Type";s:8:"Variable";s:7:"Display";s:8:"advanced";s:8:"Required";s:4:"true";s:4:"Mask";s:5:"false";}s:5:"value";s:28:"/config/match-overrides.json";}i:17;a:2:{s:11:"@attributes";a:9:{s:4:"Name";s:13:"Archive State";s:6:"Target";s:26:"/config/archive-state.json";s:7:"Default";s:44:"/mnt/user/appdata/paddock/archive-state.json";s:4:"Mode";s:2:"rw";s:11:"Description";s:494:"Persists which torrents you've archived from the Index tab (hidden from the list without deleting anything - see the Settings tab's Archive panel to undo) across container updates. Auto-created empty the first time this file doesn't exist yet. BEFORE FIRST APPLY: from the Unraid terminal, run 'touch /mnt/user/appdata/paddock/archive-state.json' (or your own path above if changed) - otherwise Docker creates an empty directory there instead of a file, which the app can't clean up on its own.";s:4:"Type";s:4:"Path";s:7:"Display";s:8:"advanced";s:8:"Required";s:4:"true";s:4:"Mask";s:5:"false";}s:5:"value";s:44:"/mnt/user/appdata/paddock/archive-state.json";}i:18;a:2:{s:11:"@attributes";a:9:{s:4:"Name";s:18:"ARCHIVE_STATE_PATH";s:6:"Target";s:18:"ARCHIVE_STATE_PATH";s:7:"Default";s:26:"/config/archive-state.json";s:4:"Mode";s:0:"";s:11:"Description";s:145:"Where the app looks for the archive-state file above, from inside the container. Matches the Archive State mount target - no need to change this.";s:4:"Type";s:8:"Variable";s:7:"Display";s:8:"advanced";s:8:"Required";s:4:"true";s:4:"Mask";s:5:"false";}s:5:"value";s:26:"/config/archive-state.json";}i:19;a:2:{s:11:"@attributes";a:9:{s:4:"Name";s:16:"Torrent Registry";s:6:"Target";s:24:"/config/torrent-registry";s:7:"Default";s:42:"/mnt/user/appdata/paddock/torrent-registry";s:4:"Mode";s:2:"rw";s:11:"Description";s:429:"A durable copy of every .torrent Paddock has a record of (staged through the Index tab, or synced in from Transmission's own torrents directory below), keyed by info-hash - lets you download any of them back later or skip re-processing an already-registered one on a repeat batch drop. A directory mount - unlike the file mounts above, there's no first-run empty-directory gotcha here, since a directory is exactly what's wanted.";s:4:"Type";s:4:"Path";s:7:"Display";s:8:"advanced";s:8:"Required";s:4:"true";s:4:"Mask";s:5:"false";}s:5:"value";s:42:"/mnt/user/appdata/paddock/torrent-registry";}i:20;a:2:{s:11:"@attributes";a:9:{s:4:"Name";s:20:"TORRENT_REGISTRY_DIR";s:6:"Target";s:20:"TORRENT_REGISTRY_DIR";s:7:"Default";s:24:"/config/torrent-registry";s:4:"Mode";s:0:"";s:11:"Description";s:146:"Where the app looks for the torrent registry above, from inside the container. Matches the Torrent Registry mount target - no need to change this.";s:4:"Type";s:8:"Variable";s:7:"Display";s:8:"advanced";s:8:"Required";s:4:"true";s:4:"Mask";s:5:"false";}s:5:"value";s:24:"/config/torrent-registry";}i:21;a:2:{s:11:"@attributes";a:9:{s:4:"Name";s:53:"Transmission's own torrents dir (read-only, optional)";s:6:"Target";s:22:"/transmission-torrents";s:7:"Default";s:39:"/mnt/user/appdata/transmission/torrents";s:4:"Mode";s:2:"ro";s:11:"Description";s:563:"Optional: Transmission's OWN .torrent-storage directory (its config dir's 'torrents' subfolder, next to its own settings.json/resume/ - check Transmission's Docker template path mappings to find its config directory's host path). When set AND TRANSMISSION_TORRENTS_DIR below is also set to /transmission-torrents, every .torrent Transmission has ever been handed - including anything autobrr added directly, never touching Paddock - gets synced into the Torrent Registry above automatically. Leave blank to disable; this share is only ever read, never written to.";s:4:"Type";s:4:"Path";s:7:"Display";s:8:"advanced";s:8:"Required";s:5:"false";s:4:"Mask";s:5:"false";}s:5:"value";s:0:"";}i:22;a:2:{s:11:"@attributes";a:9:{s:4:"Name";s:25:"TRANSMISSION_TORRENTS_DIR";s:6:"Target";s:25:"TRANSMISSION_TORRENTS_DIR";s:7:"Default";s:0:"";s:4:"Mode";s:0:"";s:11:"Description";s:193:"Set to /transmission-torrents (matching the mount target above) to enable the sync described there. Leave blank to disable, same as leaving the mount above blank - both need to be set together.";s:4:"Type";s:8:"Variable";s:7:"Display";s:8:"advanced";s:8:"Required";s:5:"false";s:4:"Mask";s:5:"false";}s:5:"value";s:0:"";}i:23;a:2:{s:11:"@attributes";a:9:{s:4:"Name";s:8:"PLEX_URL";s:6:"Target";s:8:"PLEX_URL";s:7:"Default";s:0:"";s:4:"Mode";s:0:"";s:11:"Description";s:242:"One-time seed only: used to create Settings File above if it doesn't exist yet, then ignored - edit Plex settings live afterward via the web UI. Enables a Plex partial-scan refresh after each successful archive. e.g. http://192.168.1.10:32400";s:4:"Type";s:8:"Variable";s:7:"Display";s:6:"always";s:8:"Required";s:5:"false";s:4:"Mask";s:5:"false";}s:5:"value";s:0:"";}i:24;a:2:{s:11:"@attributes";a:9:{s:4:"Name";s:10:"PLEX_TOKEN";s:6:"Target";s:10:"PLEX_TOKEN";s:7:"Default";s:0:"";s:4:"Mode";s:0:"";s:11:"Description";s:141:"One-time seed only (see PLEX_URL above). Your Plex auth token, required if PLEX_URL is set. See the README's Plex section for how to find it.";s:4:"Type";s:8:"Variable";s:7:"Display";s:6:"always";s:8:"Required";s:5:"false";s:4:"Mask";s:4:"true";}s:5:"value";s:0:"";}i:25;a:2:{s:11:"@attributes";a:9:{s:4:"Name";s:15:"PLEX_SECTION_ID";s:6:"Target";s:15:"PLEX_SECTION_ID";s:7:"Default";s:0:"";s:4:"Mode";s:0:"";s:11:"Description";s:107:"One-time seed only (see PLEX_URL above). The racing library's Plex section id, required if PLEX_URL is set.";s:4:"Type";s:8:"Variable";s:7:"Display";s:6:"always";s:8:"Required";s:5:"false";s:4:"Mask";s:5:"false";}s:5:"value";s:0:"";}i:26;a:2:{s:11:"@attributes";a:9:{s:4:"Name";s:17:"PLEX_LIBRARY_ROOT";s:6:"Target";s:17:"PLEX_LIBRARY_ROOT";s:7:"Default";s:0:"";s:4:"Mode";s:0:"";s:11:"Description";s:208:"One-time seed only (see PLEX_URL above). Only needed if Plex's own container sees this library at a different internal path than Library Root above (the same category of issue as the Downloads Share mapping).";s:4:"Type";s:8:"Variable";s:7:"Display";s:8:"advanced";s:8:"Required";s:5:"false";s:4:"Mask";s:5:"false";}s:5:"value";s:0:"";}i:27;a:2:{s:11:"@attributes";a:9:{s:4:"Name";s:13:"HOTFOLDER_DIR";s:6:"Target";s:13:"HOTFOLDER_DIR";s:7:"Default";s:0:"";s:4:"Mode";s:0:"";s:11:"Description";s:269:"One-time seed only: used to create Settings File above if it doesn't exist yet, then ignored - edit hot-folder settings live afterward via the web UI. Set to /downloads/paddock to enable hot-folder ingestion (matches the read-write mount above). Leave unset to disable.";s:4:"Type";s:8:"Variable";s:7:"Display";s:6:"always";s:8:"Required";s:5:"false";s:4:"Mask";s:5:"false";}s:5:"value";s:0:"";}i:28;a:2:{s:11:"@attributes";a:9:{s:4:"Name";s:26:"HOTFOLDER_POLL_INTERVAL_MS";s:6:"Target";s:26:"HOTFOLDER_POLL_INTERVAL_MS";s:7:"Default";s:5:"60000";s:4:"Mode";s:0:"";s:11:"Description";s:142:"One-time seed only (see HOTFOLDER_DIR above). Tuning: how often (ms) to check a hot-folder drop for size/mtime stability before processing it.";s:4:"Type";s:8:"Variable";s:7:"Display";s:8:"advanced";s:8:"Required";s:5:"false";s:4:"Mask";s:5:"false";}s:5:"value";s:0:"";}i:29;a:2:{s:11:"@attributes";a:9:{s:4:"Name";s:22:"HOTFOLDER_STABLE_POLLS";s:6:"Target";s:22:"HOTFOLDER_STABLE_POLLS";s:7:"Default";s:1:"3";s:4:"Mode";s:0:"";s:11:"Description";s:132:"One-time seed only (see HOTFOLDER_DIR above). Tuning: consecutive stable polls required before a hot-folder drop is treated as done.";s:4:"Type";s:8:"Variable";s:7:"Display";s:8:"advanced";s:8:"Required";s:5:"false";s:4:"Mask";s:5:"false";}s:5:"value";s:0:"";}i:30;a:2:{s:11:"@attributes";a:9:{s:4:"Name";s:19:"DISCORD_WEBHOOK_URL";s:6:"Target";s:19:"DISCORD_WEBHOOK_URL";s:7:"Default";s:0:"";s:4:"Mode";s:0:"";s:11:"Description";s:294:"One-time seed only: used to create Settings File above if it doesn't exist yet, then ignored - edit Discord settings live afterward via the web UI. Posts a summary message to a Discord channel after every torrent-done event. Create one via the target channel's Settings, Integrations, Webhooks.";s:4:"Type";s:8:"Variable";s:7:"Display";s:6:"always";s:8:"Required";s:5:"false";s:4:"Mask";s:4:"true";}s:5:"value";s:0:"";}i:31;a:2:{s:11:"@attributes";a:9:{s:4:"Name";s:23:"DISCORD_MENTION_USER_ID";s:6:"Target";s:23:"DISCORD_MENTION_USER_ID";s:7:"Default";s:0:"";s:4:"Mode";s:0:"";s:11:"Description";s:225:"One-time seed only (see DISCORD_WEBHOOK_URL above). A Discord user id to @mention, but only on review-worthy notifications (auto-created shows, warnings, errors). Leave unset to have every notification post without a mention.";s:4:"Type";s:8:"Variable";s:7:"Display";s:8:"advanced";s:8:"Required";s:5:"false";s:4:"Mask";s:5:"false";}s:5:"value";s:0:"";}i:32;a:2:{s:11:"@attributes";a:9:{s:4:"Name";s:14:"WEBUI_PASSWORD";s:6:"Target";s:14:"WEBUI_PASSWORD";s:7:"Default";s:0:"";s:4:"Mode";s:0:"";s:11:"Description";s:223:"Set this to enable the web UI at /ui (events editor, match tester, upload, activity log). Fails CLOSED, not open: leaving this unset keeps /ui and /api/* returning 503, since that surface can read and overwrite your config.";s:4:"Type";s:8:"Variable";s:7:"Display";s:6:"always";s:8:"Required";s:5:"false";s:4:"Mask";s:4:"true";}s:5:"value";s:0:"";}i:33;a:2:{s:11:"@attributes";a:9:{s:4:"Name";s:10:"WEBUI_USER";s:6:"Target";s:10:"WEBUI_USER";s:7:"Default";s:0:"";s:4:"Mode";s:0:"";s:11:"Description";s:150:"Optional: also require this exact username (HTTP Basic Auth) alongside WEBUI_PASSWORD. Leave unset to accept any username, checking only the password.";s:4:"Type";s:8:"Variable";s:7:"Display";s:8:"advanced";s:8:"Required";s:5:"false";s:4:"Mask";s:5:"false";}s:5:"value";s:0:"";}i:34;a:2:{s:11:"@attributes";a:9:{s:4:"Name";s:4:"PUID";s:6:"Target";s:4:"PUID";s:7:"Default";s:2:"99";s:4:"Mode";s:0:"";s:11:"Description";s:412:"Run the app as this user id instead of root (99 = Unraid's 'nobody', the same user most containers including Transmission run as). The container fixes ownership of its two config files automatically; the Library Root (and hot-folder, if used) must be writable by this user - on a default Unraid share that's already true, otherwise run once from the terminal: chown -R 99:100 on those paths. Blank = run as root.";s:4:"Type";s:8:"Variable";s:7:"Display";s:6:"always";s:8:"Required";s:5:"false";s:4:"Mask";s:5:"false";}s:5:"value";s:2:"99";}i:35;a:2:{s:11:"@attributes";a:9:{s:4:"Name";s:4:"PGID";s:6:"Target";s:4:"PGID";s:7:"Default";s:3:"100";s:4:"Mode";s:0:"";s:11:"Description";s:98:"Group id to run as (100 = Unraid's 'users' group, paired with PUID 99 above). Blank = run as root.";s:4:"Type";s:8:"Variable";s:7:"Display";s:6:"always";s:8:"Required";s:5:"false";s:4:"Mask";s:5:"false";}s:5:"value";s:3:"100";}}s:12:"TemplatePath";s:31:"/tmp/GitHub/AppFeed/paddock.xml";s:4:"Repo";s:20:"nordada's Repository";s:12:"CategoryList";a:3:{i:0;s:15:"Tools-Utilities";i:1;s:14:"MediaApp-Video";i:2;s:11:"Downloaders";}s:9:"FirstSeen";i:1785743710;s:8:"Category";s:43:"Tools:Utilities MediaApp:Video Downloaders:";s:2:"ID";i:3515;s:11:"Displayable";b:0;s:6:"Author";s:7:"nordada";s:13:"DockerHubName";s:7:"paddock";s:8:"RepoName";s:20:"nordada's Repository";s:10:"SortAuthor";s:7:"nordada";s:8:"SortName";s:7:"paddock";s:6:"random";i:1622611873;s:9:"Blacklist";b:0;s:6:"MinVer";s:3:"6.0";s:4:"Path";s:71:"/tmp/community.applications/tempFiles/templates-community-apps/3515.xml";s:4:"Date";N;s:11:"BrandNewApp";b:1;s:10:"Deprecated";b:0;s:10:"BranchName";s:113:"latest: current main branch. Version tags (e.g. v0.1.035) are also published if you want to pin a specific build.";s:17:"BranchDescription";s:113:"latest: current main branch. Version tags (e.g. v0.1.035) are also published if you want to pin a specific build.";s:11:"Description";N;s:10:"Compatible";b:1;s:16:"ModeratorComment";N;}i:3516;a:37:{s:4:"Name";s:7:"paddock";s:10:"Repository";s:23:"ghcr.io/nordada/paddock";s:8:"Registry";s:57:"https://github.com/nordada/paddock/pkgs/container/paddock";s:7:"Network";s:6:"bridge";s:5:"Shell";s:2:"sh";s:10:"Privileged";s:5:"false";s:7:"Support";s:41:"https://github.com/nordada/paddock/issues";s:7:"Project";s:34:"https://github.com/nordada/paddock";s:8:"Overview";s:972:"Quietly files completed race torrent downloads (autobrr, Transmission, or a manual drop) into a Plex-friendly library layout, renaming them into a standardized "Show - SYYYYEnn - Title - ptNN.ext" scheme. Copies only, never moves or deletes from your download share, so seeding is unaffected. Matching/naming vocabulary is driven by an "event profile" (Settings tab) - Formula 1 and cycling ship built in. See the project's README for full setup: Transmission's script-torrent-done hook, optional Plex partial-scan refresh, optional hot-folder ingestion, optional Discord notifications, and a password-gated web UI for editing show definitions and testing the matcher.

IMPORTANT: on first run, "Config File" below is auto-seeded from the image's own bundled config/events.json (a small starter list) - open the web UI (set WEBUI_PASSWORD below) or edit that file directly to add the shows/events your own tracker covers, since this list is intentionally not exhaustive.";s:5:"WebUI";s:26:"http://[IP]:[PORT:8420]/ui";s:11:"TemplateURL";s:74:"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/nordada/paddock/main/unraid-template.xml";s:4:"Icon";s:70:"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/nordada/paddock/main/public/icon.png";s:8:"Requires";s:202:"A downloads share (from Transmission or similar) and a Plex media library share. Both are plain host folders you already have - see each Path config's description below for how to find the right values.";s:6:"Config";a:36:{i:0;a:2:{s:11:"@attributes";a:9:{s:4:"Name";s:29:"WebUI / Webhook / Health Port";s:6:"Target";s:4:"8420";s:7:"Default";s:4:"8420";s:4:"Mode";s:3:"tcp";s:11:"Description";s:118:"Port the web UI (/ui), the Transmission webhook (/webhook/torrent-done), and the health check (/health) all listen on.";s:4:"Type";s:4:"Port";s:7:"Display";s:6:"always";s:8:"Required";s:4:"true";s:4:"Mask";s:5:"false";}s:5:"value";s:4:"8420";}i:1;a:2:{s:11:"@attributes";a:9:{s:4:"Name";s:12:"Library Root";s:6:"Target";s:6:"/media";s:7:"Default";s:26:"/mnt/user/media/motorsport";s:4:"Mode";s:2:"rw";s:11:"Description";s:111:"Your Plex media library root - point this at your actual racing library folder. Renamed/copied files land here.";s:4:"Type";s:4:"Path";s:7:"Display";s:6:"always";s:8:"Required";s:4:"true";s:4:"Mask";s:5:"false";}s:5:"value";s:26:"/mnt/user/media/motorsport";}i:2;a:2:{s:11:"@attributes";a:9:{s:4:"Name";s:12:"LIBRARY_ROOT";s:6:"Target";s:12:"LIBRARY_ROOT";s:7:"Default";s:6:"/media";s:4:"Mode";s:0:"";s:11:"Description";s:141:"The container-side path the app uses for the library (must match Library Root's fixed mount point above - you shouldn't need to change this).";s:4:"Type";s:8:"Variable";s:7:"Display";s:8:"advanced";s:8:"Required";s:4:"true";s:4:"Mask";s:5:"false";}s:5:"value";s:6:"/media";}i:3;a:2:{s:11:"@attributes";a:9:{s:4:"Name";s:15:"Downloads Share";s:6:"Target";s:10:"/downloads";s:7:"Default";s:19:"/mnt/user/downloads";s:4:"Mode";s:2:"rw";s:11:"Description";s:660:"The SAME share Transmission's own container maps to /downloads internally - check Transmission's Docker template path mappings to confirm what that is. This is the whole share (not just its 'complete' subfolder). Read-write: the normal ingestion pipeline only ever copies from here, but the Reseed tab's Dedupe feature deletes a torrent's original download-folder copy once it's confirmed hardlinked to the library instead (an explicit, two-click-confirmed action). Set Mode to ro instead if you'd rather keep this share read-only - Dedupe's relink/verify step still works either way, only its optional 'Delete original copy' follow-up needs write access here.";s:4:"Type";s:4:"Path";s:7:"Display";s:6:"always";s:8:"Required";s:4:"true";s:4:"Mask";s:5:"false";}s:5:"value";s:19:"/mnt/user/downloads";}i:4;a:2:{s:11:"@attributes";a:9:{s:4:"Name";s:33:"Hot-folder (read-write, optional)";s:6:"Target";s:18:"/downloads/paddock";s:7:"Default";s:27:"/mnt/user/downloads/paddock";s:4:"Mode";s:2:"rw";s:11:"Description";s:279:"Optional read-write overlay on a 'paddock' subfolder of the share above, for hot-folder ingestion (drop a file/folder here to bypass Transmission entirely). Only takes effect if HOTFOLDER_DIR below is also set to /downloads/paddock; otherwise this is just an unused empty folder.";s:4:"Type";s:4:"Path";s:7:"Display";s:8:"advanced";s:8:"Required";s:5:"false";s:4:"Mask";s:5:"false";}s:5:"value";s:27:"/mnt/user/downloads/paddock";}i:5;a:2:{s:11:"@attributes";a:9:{s:4:"Name";s:11:"Config File";s:6:"Target";s:19:"/config/events.json";s:7:"Default";s:37:"/mnt/user/appdata/paddock/events.json";s:4:"Mode";s:2:"rw";s:11:"Description";s:257:"Persists your show/event definitions across container updates and image upgrades. Auto-created from the image's bundled config/events.json the first time this file doesn't exist yet (see the Overview above) - edit it by hand or through the web UI afterward.";s:4:"Type";s:4:"Path";s:7:"Display";s:6:"always";s:8:"Required";s:4:"true";s:4:"Mask";s:5:"false";}s:5:"value";s:37:"/mnt/user/appdata/paddock/events.json";}i:6;a:2:{s:11:"@attributes";a:9:{s:4:"Name";s:11:"CONFIG_PATH";s:6:"Target";s:11:"CONFIG_PATH";s:7:"Default";s:19:"/config/events.json";s:4:"Mode";s:0:"";s:11:"Description";s:136:"Where the app looks for the config file above, from inside the container. Matches the Config File mount target - no need to change this.";s:4:"Type";s:8:"Variable";s:7:"Display";s:8:"advanced";s:8:"Required";s:4:"true";s:4:"Mask";s:5:"false";}s:5:"value";s:19:"/config/events.json";}i:7;a:2:{s:11:"@attributes";a:9:{s:4:"Name";s:13:"Settings File";s:6:"Target";s:21:"/config/settings.json";s:7:"Default";s:39:"/mnt/user/appdata/paddock/settings.json";s:4:"Mode";s:2:"rw";s:11:"Description";s:526:"Persists your Plex/Discord/hot-folder settings across container updates. Auto-created (seeded from the PLEX_*/DISCORD_*/HOTFOLDER_* variables below) the first time this file doesn't exist yet - edit it live afterward through the web UI's Settings panel instead of these variables. BEFORE FIRST APPLY: from the Unraid terminal, run 'touch /mnt/user/appdata/paddock/settings.json' (or your own path above if changed) - otherwise Docker creates an empty directory there instead of a file, which the app can't clean up on its own.";s:4:"Type";s:4:"Path";s:7:"Display";s:6:"always";s:8:"Required";s:4:"true";s:4:"Mask";s:5:"false";}s:5:"value";s:39:"/mnt/user/appdata/paddock/settings.json";}i:8;a:2:{s:11:"@attributes";a:9:{s:4:"Name";s:13:"SETTINGS_PATH";s:6:"Target";s:13:"SETTINGS_PATH";s:7:"Default";s:21:"/config/settings.json";s:4:"Mode";s:0:"";s:11:"Description";s:140:"Where the app looks for the settings file above, from inside the container. Matches the Settings File mount target - no need to change this.";s:4:"Type";s:8:"Variable";s:7:"Display";s:8:"advanced";s:8:"Required";s:4:"true";s:4:"Mask";s:5:"false";}s:5:"value";s:21:"/config/settings.json";}i:9;a:2:{s:11:"@attributes";a:9:{s:4:"Name";s:12:"Activity Log";s:6:"Target";s:21:"/config/activity.json";s:7:"Default";s:39:"/mnt/user/appdata/paddock/activity.json";s:4:"Mode";s:2:"rw";s:11:"Description";s:389:"Persists the web UI's recent-activity log across container updates and restarts. Auto-created empty the first time this file doesn't exist yet. BEFORE FIRST APPLY: from the Unraid terminal, run 'touch /mnt/user/appdata/paddock/activity.json' (or your own path above if changed) - otherwise Docker creates an empty directory there instead of a file, which the app can't clean up on its own.";s:4:"Type";s:4:"Path";s:7:"Display";s:8:"advanced";s:8:"Required";s:4:"true";s:4:"Mask";s:5:"false";}s:5:"value";s:39:"/mnt/user/appdata/paddock/activity.json";}i:10;a:2:{s:11:"@attributes";a:9:{s:4:"Name";s:13:"ACTIVITY_PATH";s:6:"Target";s:13:"ACTIVITY_PATH";s:7:"Default";s:21:"/config/activity.json";s:4:"Mode";s:0:"";s:11:"Description";s:138:"Where the app looks for the activity log above, from inside the container. Matches the Activity Log mount target - no need to change this.";s:4:"Type";s:8:"Variable";s:7:"Display";s:8:"advanced";s:8:"Required";s:4:"true";s:4:"Mask";s:5:"false";}s:5:"value";s:21:"/config/activity.json";}i:11;a:2:{s:11:"@attributes";a:9:{s:4:"Name";s:12:"Dedupe State";s:6:"Target";s:25:"/config/dedupe-state.json";s:7:"Default";s:43:"/mnt/user/appdata/paddock/dedupe-state.json";s:4:"Mode";s:2:"rw";s:11:"Description";s:557:"Records where a deduped torrent's data lived before the Reseed tab's Dedupe feature relinked it to your library - Transmission itself forgets a torrent's previous location once relocated, so this is the app's own persisted memory of it instead. Auto-created empty the first time this file doesn't exist yet. BEFORE FIRST APPLY: from the Unraid terminal, run 'touch /mnt/user/appdata/paddock/dedupe-state.json' (or your own path above if changed) - otherwise Docker creates an empty directory there instead of a file, which the app can't clean up on its own.";s:4:"Type";s:4:"Path";s:7:"Display";s:8:"advanced";s:8:"Required";s:4:"true";s:4:"Mask";s:5:"false";}s:5:"value";s:43:"/mnt/user/appdata/paddock/dedupe-state.json";}i:12;a:2:{s:11:"@attributes";a:9:{s:4:"Name";s:17:"DEDUPE_STATE_PATH";s:6:"Target";s:17:"DEDUPE_STATE_PATH";s:7:"Default";s:25:"/config/dedupe-state.json";s:4:"Mode";s:0:"";s:11:"Description";s:143:"Where the app looks for the dedupe-state file above, from inside the container. Matches the Dedupe State mount target - no need to change this.";s:4:"Type";s:8:"Variable";s:7:"Display";s:8:"advanced";s:8:"Required";s:4:"true";s:4:"Mask";s:5:"false";}s:5:"value";s:25:"/config/dedupe-state.json";}i:13;a:2:{s:11:"@attributes";a:9:{s:4:"Name";s:12:"Verify State";s:6:"Target";s:25:"/config/verify-state.json";s:7:"Default";s:43:"/mnt/user/appdata/paddock/verify-state.json";s:4:"Mode";s:2:"rw";s:11:"Description";s:401:"Persists the Index tab's 'Verify data' integrity-check results across container updates. Auto-created empty the first time this file doesn't exist yet. BEFORE FIRST APPLY: from the Unraid terminal, run 'touch /mnt/user/appdata/paddock/verify-state.json' (or your own path above if changed) - otherwise Docker creates an empty directory there instead of a file, which the app can't clean up on its own.";s:4:"Type";s:4:"Path";s:7:"Display";s:8:"advanced";s:8:"Required";s:4:"true";s:4:"Mask";s:5:"false";}s:5:"value";s:43:"/mnt/user/appdata/paddock/verify-state.json";}i:14;a:2:{s:11:"@attributes";a:9:{s:4:"Name";s:17:"VERIFY_STATE_PATH";s:6:"Target";s:17:"VERIFY_STATE_PATH";s:7:"Default";s:25:"/config/verify-state.json";s:4:"Mode";s:0:"";s:11:"Description";s:143:"Where the app looks for the verify-state file above, from inside the container. Matches the Verify State mount target - no need to change this.";s:4:"Type";s:8:"Variable";s:7:"Display";s:8:"advanced";s:8:"Required";s:4:"true";s:4:"Mask";s:5:"false";}s:5:"value";s:25:"/config/verify-state.json";}i:15;a:2:{s:11:"@attributes";a:9:{s:4:"Name";s:15:"Match Overrides";s:6:"Target";s:28:"/config/match-overrides.json";s:7:"Default";s:46:"/mnt/user/appdata/paddock/match-overrides.json";s:4:"Mode";s:2:"rw";s:11:"Description";s:512:"Persists a human's own picks from the Index tab's 'Resolve ambiguous files' modal across container updates - without this, a resolved pick silently reverts to 'ambiguous' again on the next update. Auto-created empty the first time this file doesn't exist yet. BEFORE FIRST APPLY: from the Unraid terminal, run 'touch /mnt/user/appdata/paddock/match-overrides.json' (or your own path above if changed) - otherwise Docker creates an empty directory there instead of a file, which the app can't clean up on its own.";s:4:"Type";s:4:"Path";s:7:"Display";s:8:"advanced";s:8:"Required";s:4:"true";s:4:"Mask";s:5:"false";}s:5:"value";s:46:"/mnt/user/appdata/paddock/match-overrides.json";}i:16;a:2:{s:11:"@attributes";a:9:{s:4:"Name";s:20:"MATCH_OVERRIDES_PATH";s:6:"Target";s:20:"MATCH_OVERRIDES_PATH";s:7:"Default";s:28:"/config/match-overrides.json";s:4:"Mode";s:0:"";s:11:"Description";s:149:"Where the app looks for the match-overrides file above, from inside the container. Matches the Match Overrides mount target - no need to change this.";s:4:"Type";s:8:"Variable";s:7:"Display";s:8:"advanced";s:8:"Required";s:4:"true";s:4:"Mask";s:5:"false";}s:5:"value";s:28:"/config/match-overrides.json";}i:17;a:2:{s:11:"@attributes";a:9:{s:4:"Name";s:13:"Archive State";s:6:"Target";s:26:"/config/archive-state.json";s:7:"Default";s:44:"/mnt/user/appdata/paddock/archive-state.json";s:4:"Mode";s:2:"rw";s:11:"Description";s:494:"Persists which torrents you've archived from the Index tab (hidden from the list without deleting anything - see the Settings tab's Archive panel to undo) across container updates. Auto-created empty the first time this file doesn't exist yet. BEFORE FIRST APPLY: from the Unraid terminal, run 'touch /mnt/user/appdata/paddock/archive-state.json' (or your own path above if changed) - otherwise Docker creates an empty directory there instead of a file, which the app can't clean up on its own.";s:4:"Type";s:4:"Path";s:7:"Display";s:8:"advanced";s:8:"Required";s:4:"true";s:4:"Mask";s:5:"false";}s:5:"value";s:44:"/mnt/user/appdata/paddock/archive-state.json";}i:18;a:2:{s:11:"@attributes";a:9:{s:4:"Name";s:18:"ARCHIVE_STATE_PATH";s:6:"Target";s:18:"ARCHIVE_STATE_PATH";s:7:"Default";s:26:"/config/archive-state.json";s:4:"Mode";s:0:"";s:11:"Description";s:145:"Where the app looks for the archive-state file above, from inside the container. Matches the Archive State mount target - no need to change this.";s:4:"Type";s:8:"Variable";s:7:"Display";s:8:"advanced";s:8:"Required";s:4:"true";s:4:"Mask";s:5:"false";}s:5:"value";s:26:"/config/archive-state.json";}i:19;a:2:{s:11:"@attributes";a:9:{s:4:"Name";s:16:"Torrent Registry";s:6:"Target";s:24:"/config/torrent-registry";s:7:"Default";s:42:"/mnt/user/appdata/paddock/torrent-registry";s:4:"Mode";s:2:"rw";s:11:"Description";s:429:"A durable copy of every .torrent Paddock has a record of (staged through the Index tab, or synced in from Transmission's own torrents directory below), keyed by info-hash - lets you download any of them back later or skip re-processing an already-registered one on a repeat batch drop. A directory mount - unlike the file mounts above, there's no first-run empty-directory gotcha here, since a directory is exactly what's wanted.";s:4:"Type";s:4:"Path";s:7:"Display";s:8:"advanced";s:8:"Required";s:4:"true";s:4:"Mask";s:5:"false";}s:5:"value";s:42:"/mnt/user/appdata/paddock/torrent-registry";}i:20;a:2:{s:11:"@attributes";a:9:{s:4:"Name";s:20:"TORRENT_REGISTRY_DIR";s:6:"Target";s:20:"TORRENT_REGISTRY_DIR";s:7:"Default";s:24:"/config/torrent-registry";s:4:"Mode";s:0:"";s:11:"Description";s:146:"Where the app looks for the torrent registry above, from inside the container. Matches the Torrent Registry mount target - no need to change this.";s:4:"Type";s:8:"Variable";s:7:"Display";s:8:"advanced";s:8:"Required";s:4:"true";s:4:"Mask";s:5:"false";}s:5:"value";s:24:"/config/torrent-registry";}i:21;a:2:{s:11:"@attributes";a:9:{s:4:"Name";s:53:"Transmission's own torrents dir (read-only, optional)";s:6:"Target";s:22:"/transmission-torrents";s:7:"Default";s:39:"/mnt/user/appdata/transmission/torrents";s:4:"Mode";s:2:"ro";s:11:"Description";s:563:"Optional: Transmission's OWN .torrent-storage directory (its config dir's 'torrents' subfolder, next to its own settings.json/resume/ - check Transmission's Docker template path mappings to find its config directory's host path). When set AND TRANSMISSION_TORRENTS_DIR below is also set to /transmission-torrents, every .torrent Transmission has ever been handed - including anything autobrr added directly, never touching Paddock - gets synced into the Torrent Registry above automatically. Leave blank to disable; this share is only ever read, never written to.";s:4:"Type";s:4:"Path";s:7:"Display";s:8:"advanced";s:8:"Required";s:5:"false";s:4:"Mask";s:5:"false";}s:5:"value";s:0:"";}i:22;a:2:{s:11:"@attributes";a:9:{s:4:"Name";s:25:"TRANSMISSION_TORRENTS_DIR";s:6:"Target";s:25:"TRANSMISSION_TORRENTS_DIR";s:7:"Default";s:0:"";s:4:"Mode";s:0:"";s:11:"Description";s:193:"Set to /transmission-torrents (matching the mount target above) to enable the sync described there. Leave blank to disable, same as leaving the mount above blank - both need to be set together.";s:4:"Type";s:8:"Variable";s:7:"Display";s:8:"advanced";s:8:"Required";s:5:"false";s:4:"Mask";s:5:"false";}s:5:"value";s:0:"";}i:23;a:2:{s:11:"@attributes";a:9:{s:4:"Name";s:8:"PLEX_URL";s:6:"Target";s:8:"PLEX_URL";s:7:"Default";s:0:"";s:4:"Mode";s:0:"";s:11:"Description";s:242:"One-time seed only: used to create Settings File above if it doesn't exist yet, then ignored - edit Plex settings live afterward via the web UI. Enables a Plex partial-scan refresh after each successful archive. e.g. http://192.168.1.10:32400";s:4:"Type";s:8:"Variable";s:7:"Display";s:6:"always";s:8:"Required";s:5:"false";s:4:"Mask";s:5:"false";}s:5:"value";s:0:"";}i:24;a:2:{s:11:"@attributes";a:9:{s:4:"Name";s:10:"PLEX_TOKEN";s:6:"Target";s:10:"PLEX_TOKEN";s:7:"Default";s:0:"";s:4:"Mode";s:0:"";s:11:"Description";s:141:"One-time seed only (see PLEX_URL above). Your Plex auth token, required if PLEX_URL is set. See the README's Plex section for how to find it.";s:4:"Type";s:8:"Variable";s:7:"Display";s:6:"always";s:8:"Required";s:5:"false";s:4:"Mask";s:4:"true";}s:5:"value";s:0:"";}i:25;a:2:{s:11:"@attributes";a:9:{s:4:"Name";s:15:"PLEX_SECTION_ID";s:6:"Target";s:15:"PLEX_SECTION_ID";s:7:"Default";s:0:"";s:4:"Mode";s:0:"";s:11:"Description";s:107:"One-time seed only (see PLEX_URL above). The racing library's Plex section id, required if PLEX_URL is set.";s:4:"Type";s:8:"Variable";s:7:"Display";s:6:"always";s:8:"Required";s:5:"false";s:4:"Mask";s:5:"false";}s:5:"value";s:0:"";}i:26;a:2:{s:11:"@attributes";a:9:{s:4:"Name";s:17:"PLEX_LIBRARY_ROOT";s:6:"Target";s:17:"PLEX_LIBRARY_ROOT";s:7:"Default";s:0:"";s:4:"Mode";s:0:"";s:11:"Description";s:208:"One-time seed only (see PLEX_URL above). Only needed if Plex's own container sees this library at a different internal path than Library Root above (the same category of issue as the Downloads Share mapping).";s:4:"Type";s:8:"Variable";s:7:"Display";s:8:"advanced";s:8:"Required";s:5:"false";s:4:"Mask";s:5:"false";}s:5:"value";s:0:"";}i:27;a:2:{s:11:"@attributes";a:9:{s:4:"Name";s:13:"HOTFOLDER_DIR";s:6:"Target";s:13:"HOTFOLDER_DIR";s:7:"Default";s:0:"";s:4:"Mode";s:0:"";s:11:"Description";s:269:"One-time seed only: used to create Settings File above if it doesn't exist yet, then ignored - edit hot-folder settings live afterward via the web UI. Set to /downloads/paddock to enable hot-folder ingestion (matches the read-write mount above). Leave unset to disable.";s:4:"Type";s:8:"Variable";s:7:"Display";s:6:"always";s:8:"Required";s:5:"false";s:4:"Mask";s:5:"false";}s:5:"value";s:0:"";}i:28;a:2:{s:11:"@attributes";a:9:{s:4:"Name";s:26:"HOTFOLDER_POLL_INTERVAL_MS";s:6:"Target";s:26:"HOTFOLDER_POLL_INTERVAL_MS";s:7:"Default";s:5:"60000";s:4:"Mode";s:0:"";s:11:"Description";s:142:"One-time seed only (see HOTFOLDER_DIR above). Tuning: how often (ms) to check a hot-folder drop for size/mtime stability before processing it.";s:4:"Type";s:8:"Variable";s:7:"Display";s:8:"advanced";s:8:"Required";s:5:"false";s:4:"Mask";s:5:"false";}s:5:"value";s:0:"";}i:29;a:2:{s:11:"@attributes";a:9:{s:4:"Name";s:22:"HOTFOLDER_STABLE_POLLS";s:6:"Target";s:22:"HOTFOLDER_STABLE_POLLS";s:7:"Default";s:1:"3";s:4:"Mode";s:0:"";s:11:"Description";s:132:"One-time seed only (see HOTFOLDER_DIR above). Tuning: consecutive stable polls required before a hot-folder drop is treated as done.";s:4:"Type";s:8:"Variable";s:7:"Display";s:8:"advanced";s:8:"Required";s:5:"false";s:4:"Mask";s:5:"false";}s:5:"value";s:0:"";}i:30;a:2:{s:11:"@attributes";a:9:{s:4:"Name";s:19:"DISCORD_WEBHOOK_URL";s:6:"Target";s:19:"DISCORD_WEBHOOK_URL";s:7:"Default";s:0:"";s:4:"Mode";s:0:"";s:11:"Description";s:294:"One-time seed only: used to create Settings File above if it doesn't exist yet, then ignored - edit Discord settings live afterward via the web UI. Posts a summary message to a Discord channel after every torrent-done event. Create one via the target channel's Settings, Integrations, Webhooks.";s:4:"Type";s:8:"Variable";s:7:"Display";s:6:"always";s:8:"Required";s:5:"false";s:4:"Mask";s:4:"true";}s:5:"value";s:0:"";}i:31;a:2:{s:11:"@attributes";a:9:{s:4:"Name";s:23:"DISCORD_MENTION_USER_ID";s:6:"Target";s:23:"DISCORD_MENTION_USER_ID";s:7:"Default";s:0:"";s:4:"Mode";s:0:"";s:11:"Description";s:225:"One-time seed only (see DISCORD_WEBHOOK_URL above). A Discord user id to @mention, but only on review-worthy notifications (auto-created shows, warnings, errors). Leave unset to have every notification post without a mention.";s:4:"Type";s:8:"Variable";s:7:"Display";s:8:"advanced";s:8:"Required";s:5:"false";s:4:"Mask";s:5:"false";}s:5:"value";s:0:"";}i:32;a:2:{s:11:"@attributes";a:9:{s:4:"Name";s:14:"WEBUI_PASSWORD";s:6:"Target";s:14:"WEBUI_PASSWORD";s:7:"Default";s:0:"";s:4:"Mode";s:0:"";s:11:"Description";s:223:"Set this to enable the web UI at /ui (events editor, match tester, upload, activity log). Fails CLOSED, not open: leaving this unset keeps /ui and /api/* returning 503, since that surface can read and overwrite your config.";s:4:"Type";s:8:"Variable";s:7:"Display";s:6:"always";s:8:"Required";s:5:"false";s:4:"Mask";s:4:"true";}s:5:"value";s:0:"";}i:33;a:2:{s:11:"@attributes";a:9:{s:4:"Name";s:10:"WEBUI_USER";s:6:"Target";s:10:"WEBUI_USER";s:7:"Default";s:0:"";s:4:"Mode";s:0:"";s:11:"Description";s:150:"Optional: also require this exact username (HTTP Basic Auth) alongside WEBUI_PASSWORD. Leave unset to accept any username, checking only the password.";s:4:"Type";s:8:"Variable";s:7:"Display";s:8:"advanced";s:8:"Required";s:5:"false";s:4:"Mask";s:5:"false";}s:5:"value";s:0:"";}i:34;a:2:{s:11:"@attributes";a:9:{s:4:"Name";s:4:"PUID";s:6:"Target";s:4:"PUID";s:7:"Default";s:2:"99";s:4:"Mode";s:0:"";s:11:"Description";s:412:"Run the app as this user id instead of root (99 = Unraid's 'nobody', the same user most containers including Transmission run as). The container fixes ownership of its two config files automatically; the Library Root (and hot-folder, if used) must be writable by this user - on a default Unraid share that's already true, otherwise run once from the terminal: chown -R 99:100 on those paths. Blank = run as root.";s:4:"Type";s:8:"Variable";s:7:"Display";s:6:"always";s:8:"Required";s:5:"false";s:4:"Mask";s:5:"false";}s:5:"value";s:2:"99";}i:35;a:2:{s:11:"@attributes";a:9:{s:4:"Name";s:4:"PGID";s:6:"Target";s:4:"PGID";s:7:"Default";s:3:"100";s:4:"Mode";s:0:"";s:11:"Description";s:98:"Group id to run as (100 = Unraid's 'users' group, paired with PUID 99 above). Blank = run as root.";s:4:"Type";s:8:"Variable";s:7:"Display";s:6:"always";s:8:"Required";s:5:"false";s:4:"Mask";s:5:"false";}s:5:"value";s:3:"100";}}s:12:"TemplatePath";s:39:"/tmp/GitHub/AppFeed/unraid-template.xml";s:4:"Repo";s:20:"Paddock's Repository";s:12:"CategoryList";a:3:{i:0;s:15:"Tools-Utilities";i:1;s:14:"MediaApp-Video";i:2;s:11:"Downloaders";}s:9:"FirstSeen";i:1785743710;s:8:"Category";s:43:"Tools:Utilities MediaApp:Video Downloaders:";s:2:"ID";i:3516;s:11:"Displayable";b:1;s:6:"Author";s:7:"nordada";s:13:"DockerHubName";s:7:"paddock";s:8:"RepoName";s:20:"Paddock's Repository";s:10:"SortAuthor";s:7:"nordada";s:8:"SortName";s:7:"paddock";s:6:"random";i:1549347503;s:9:"Blacklist";b:0;s:6:"MinVer";s:3:"6.0";s:4:"Path";s:108:"/tmp/community.applications/tempFiles/templates-community-apps/PaddocksRepository/nordada-paddock-latest.xml";s:4:"Date";N;s:11:"BrandNewApp";b:1;s:10:"Deprecated";b:0;s:13:"BranchDefault";N;s:8:"BranchID";a:1:{i:0;i:3517;}s:10:"Compatible";b:1;s:16:"ModeratorComment";N;}i:3517;a:38:{s:4:"Name";s:7:"paddock";s:10:"Repository";s:137:"ghcr.io/nordada/paddock:latest: current main branch. Version tags (e.g. v0.1.035) are also published if you want to pin a specific build.";s:8:"Registry";s:57:"https://github.com/nordada/paddock/pkgs/container/paddock";s:7:"Network";s:6:"bridge";s:5:"Shell";s:2:"sh";s:10:"Privileged";s:5:"false";s:7:"Support";s:41:"https://github.com/nordada/paddock/issues";s:7:"Project";s:34:"https://github.com/nordada/paddock";s:8:"Overview";s:972:"Quietly files completed race torrent downloads (autobrr, Transmission, or a manual drop) into a Plex-friendly library layout, renaming them into a standardized "Show - SYYYYEnn - Title - ptNN.ext" scheme. Copies only, never moves or deletes from your download share, so seeding is unaffected. Matching/naming vocabulary is driven by an "event profile" (Settings tab) - Formula 1 and cycling ship built in. See the project's README for full setup: Transmission's script-torrent-done hook, optional Plex partial-scan refresh, optional hot-folder ingestion, optional Discord notifications, and a password-gated web UI for editing show definitions and testing the matcher.

IMPORTANT: on first run, "Config File" below is auto-seeded from the image's own bundled config/events.json (a small starter list) - open the web UI (set WEBUI_PASSWORD below) or edit that file directly to add the shows/events your own tracker covers, since this list is intentionally not exhaustive.";s:5:"WebUI";s:26:"http://[IP]:[PORT:8420]/ui";s:11:"TemplateURL";s:74:"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/nordada/paddock/main/unraid-template.xml";s:4:"Icon";s:70:"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/nordada/paddock/main/public/icon.png";s:8:"Requires";s:202:"A downloads share (from Transmission or similar) and a Plex media library share. Both are plain host folders you already have - see each Path config's description below for how to find the right values.";s:6:"Config";a:36:{i:0;a:2:{s:11:"@attributes";a:9:{s:4:"Name";s:29:"WebUI / Webhook / Health Port";s:6:"Target";s:4:"8420";s:7:"Default";s:4:"8420";s:4:"Mode";s:3:"tcp";s:11:"Description";s:118:"Port the web UI (/ui), the Transmission webhook (/webhook/torrent-done), and the health check (/health) all listen on.";s:4:"Type";s:4:"Port";s:7:"Display";s:6:"always";s:8:"Required";s:4:"true";s:4:"Mask";s:5:"false";}s:5:"value";s:4:"8420";}i:1;a:2:{s:11:"@attributes";a:9:{s:4:"Name";s:12:"Library Root";s:6:"Target";s:6:"/media";s:7:"Default";s:26:"/mnt/user/media/motorsport";s:4:"Mode";s:2:"rw";s:11:"Description";s:111:"Your Plex media library root - point this at your actual racing library folder. Renamed/copied files land here.";s:4:"Type";s:4:"Path";s:7:"Display";s:6:"always";s:8:"Required";s:4:"true";s:4:"Mask";s:5:"false";}s:5:"value";s:26:"/mnt/user/media/motorsport";}i:2;a:2:{s:11:"@attributes";a:9:{s:4:"Name";s:12:"LIBRARY_ROOT";s:6:"Target";s:12:"LIBRARY_ROOT";s:7:"Default";s:6:"/media";s:4:"Mode";s:0:"";s:11:"Description";s:141:"The container-side path the app uses for the library (must match Library Root's fixed mount point above - you shouldn't need to change this).";s:4:"Type";s:8:"Variable";s:7:"Display";s:8:"advanced";s:8:"Required";s:4:"true";s:4:"Mask";s:5:"false";}s:5:"value";s:6:"/media";}i:3;a:2:{s:11:"@attributes";a:9:{s:4:"Name";s:15:"Downloads Share";s:6:"Target";s:10:"/downloads";s:7:"Default";s:19:"/mnt/user/downloads";s:4:"Mode";s:2:"rw";s:11:"Description";s:660:"The SAME share Transmission's own container maps to /downloads internally - check Transmission's Docker template path mappings to confirm what that is. This is the whole share (not just its 'complete' subfolder). Read-write: the normal ingestion pipeline only ever copies from here, but the Reseed tab's Dedupe feature deletes a torrent's original download-folder copy once it's confirmed hardlinked to the library instead (an explicit, two-click-confirmed action). Set Mode to ro instead if you'd rather keep this share read-only - Dedupe's relink/verify step still works either way, only its optional 'Delete original copy' follow-up needs write access here.";s:4:"Type";s:4:"Path";s:7:"Display";s:6:"always";s:8:"Required";s:4:"true";s:4:"Mask";s:5:"false";}s:5:"value";s:19:"/mnt/user/downloads";}i:4;a:2:{s:11:"@attributes";a:9:{s:4:"Name";s:33:"Hot-folder (read-write, optional)";s:6:"Target";s:18:"/downloads/paddock";s:7:"Default";s:27:"/mnt/user/downloads/paddock";s:4:"Mode";s:2:"rw";s:11:"Description";s:279:"Optional read-write overlay on a 'paddock' subfolder of the share above, for hot-folder ingestion (drop a file/folder here to bypass Transmission entirely). Only takes effect if HOTFOLDER_DIR below is also set to /downloads/paddock; otherwise this is just an unused empty folder.";s:4:"Type";s:4:"Path";s:7:"Display";s:8:"advanced";s:8:"Required";s:5:"false";s:4:"Mask";s:5:"false";}s:5:"value";s:27:"/mnt/user/downloads/paddock";}i:5;a:2:{s:11:"@attributes";a:9:{s:4:"Name";s:11:"Config File";s:6:"Target";s:19:"/config/events.json";s:7:"Default";s:37:"/mnt/user/appdata/paddock/events.json";s:4:"Mode";s:2:"rw";s:11:"Description";s:257:"Persists your show/event definitions across container updates and image upgrades. Auto-created from the image's bundled config/events.json the first time this file doesn't exist yet (see the Overview above) - edit it by hand or through the web UI afterward.";s:4:"Type";s:4:"Path";s:7:"Display";s:6:"always";s:8:"Required";s:4:"true";s:4:"Mask";s:5:"false";}s:5:"value";s:37:"/mnt/user/appdata/paddock/events.json";}i:6;a:2:{s:11:"@attributes";a:9:{s:4:"Name";s:11:"CONFIG_PATH";s:6:"Target";s:11:"CONFIG_PATH";s:7:"Default";s:19:"/config/events.json";s:4:"Mode";s:0:"";s:11:"Description";s:136:"Where the app looks for the config file above, from inside the container. Matches the Config File mount target - no need to change this.";s:4:"Type";s:8:"Variable";s:7:"Display";s:8:"advanced";s:8:"Required";s:4:"true";s:4:"Mask";s:5:"false";}s:5:"value";s:19:"/config/events.json";}i:7;a:2:{s:11:"@attributes";a:9:{s:4:"Name";s:13:"Settings File";s:6:"Target";s:21:"/config/settings.json";s:7:"Default";s:39:"/mnt/user/appdata/paddock/settings.json";s:4:"Mode";s:2:"rw";s:11:"Description";s:526:"Persists your Plex/Discord/hot-folder settings across container updates. Auto-created (seeded from the PLEX_*/DISCORD_*/HOTFOLDER_* variables below) the first time this file doesn't exist yet - edit it live afterward through the web UI's Settings panel instead of these variables. BEFORE FIRST APPLY: from the Unraid terminal, run 'touch /mnt/user/appdata/paddock/settings.json' (or your own path above if changed) - otherwise Docker creates an empty directory there instead of a file, which the app can't clean up on its own.";s:4:"Type";s:4:"Path";s:7:"Display";s:6:"always";s:8:"Required";s:4:"true";s:4:"Mask";s:5:"false";}s:5:"value";s:39:"/mnt/user/appdata/paddock/settings.json";}i:8;a:2:{s:11:"@attributes";a:9:{s:4:"Name";s:13:"SETTINGS_PATH";s:6:"Target";s:13:"SETTINGS_PATH";s:7:"Default";s:21:"/config/settings.json";s:4:"Mode";s:0:"";s:11:"Description";s:140:"Where the app looks for the settings file above, from inside the container. Matches the Settings File mount target - no need to change this.";s:4:"Type";s:8:"Variable";s:7:"Display";s:8:"advanced";s:8:"Required";s:4:"true";s:4:"Mask";s:5:"false";}s:5:"value";s:21:"/config/settings.json";}i:9;a:2:{s:11:"@attributes";a:9:{s:4:"Name";s:12:"Activity Log";s:6:"Target";s:21:"/config/activity.json";s:7:"Default";s:39:"/mnt/user/appdata/paddock/activity.json";s:4:"Mode";s:2:"rw";s:11:"Description";s:389:"Persists the web UI's recent-activity log across container updates and restarts. Auto-created empty the first time this file doesn't exist yet. BEFORE FIRST APPLY: from the Unraid terminal, run 'touch /mnt/user/appdata/paddock/activity.json' (or your own path above if changed) - otherwise Docker creates an empty directory there instead of a file, which the app can't clean up on its own.";s:4:"Type";s:4:"Path";s:7:"Display";s:8:"advanced";s:8:"Required";s:4:"true";s:4:"Mask";s:5:"false";}s:5:"value";s:39:"/mnt/user/appdata/paddock/activity.json";}i:10;a:2:{s:11:"@attributes";a:9:{s:4:"Name";s:13:"ACTIVITY_PATH";s:6:"Target";s:13:"ACTIVITY_PATH";s:7:"Default";s:21:"/config/activity.json";s:4:"Mode";s:0:"";s:11:"Description";s:138:"Where the app looks for the activity log above, from inside the container. Matches the Activity Log mount target - no need to change this.";s:4:"Type";s:8:"Variable";s:7:"Display";s:8:"advanced";s:8:"Required";s:4:"true";s:4:"Mask";s:5:"false";}s:5:"value";s:21:"/config/activity.json";}i:11;a:2:{s:11:"@attributes";a:9:{s:4:"Name";s:12:"Dedupe State";s:6:"Target";s:25:"/config/dedupe-state.json";s:7:"Default";s:43:"/mnt/user/appdata/paddock/dedupe-state.json";s:4:"Mode";s:2:"rw";s:11:"Description";s:557:"Records where a deduped torrent's data lived before the Reseed tab's Dedupe feature relinked it to your library - Transmission itself forgets a torrent's previous location once relocated, so this is the app's own persisted memory of it instead. Auto-created empty the first time this file doesn't exist yet. BEFORE FIRST APPLY: from the Unraid terminal, run 'touch /mnt/user/appdata/paddock/dedupe-state.json' (or your own path above if changed) - otherwise Docker creates an empty directory there instead of a file, which the app can't clean up on its own.";s:4:"Type";s:4:"Path";s:7:"Display";s:8:"advanced";s:8:"Required";s:4:"true";s:4:"Mask";s:5:"false";}s:5:"value";s:43:"/mnt/user/appdata/paddock/dedupe-state.json";}i:12;a:2:{s:11:"@attributes";a:9:{s:4:"Name";s:17:"DEDUPE_STATE_PATH";s:6:"Target";s:17:"DEDUPE_STATE_PATH";s:7:"Default";s:25:"/config/dedupe-state.json";s:4:"Mode";s:0:"";s:11:"Description";s:143:"Where the app looks for the dedupe-state file above, from inside the container. Matches the Dedupe State mount target - no need to change this.";s:4:"Type";s:8:"Variable";s:7:"Display";s:8:"advanced";s:8:"Required";s:4:"true";s:4:"Mask";s:5:"false";}s:5:"value";s:25:"/config/dedupe-state.json";}i:13;a:2:{s:11:"@attributes";a:9:{s:4:"Name";s:12:"Verify State";s:6:"Target";s:25:"/config/verify-state.json";s:7:"Default";s:43:"/mnt/user/appdata/paddock/verify-state.json";s:4:"Mode";s:2:"rw";s:11:"Description";s:401:"Persists the Index tab's 'Verify data' integrity-check results across container updates. Auto-created empty the first time this file doesn't exist yet. BEFORE FIRST APPLY: from the Unraid terminal, run 'touch /mnt/user/appdata/paddock/verify-state.json' (or your own path above if changed) - otherwise Docker creates an empty directory there instead of a file, which the app can't clean up on its own.";s:4:"Type";s:4:"Path";s:7:"Display";s:8:"advanced";s:8:"Required";s:4:"true";s:4:"Mask";s:5:"false";}s:5:"value";s:43:"/mnt/user/appdata/paddock/verify-state.json";}i:14;a:2:{s:11:"@attributes";a:9:{s:4:"Name";s:17:"VERIFY_STATE_PATH";s:6:"Target";s:17:"VERIFY_STATE_PATH";s:7:"Default";s:25:"/config/verify-state.json";s:4:"Mode";s:0:"";s:11:"Description";s:143:"Where the app looks for the verify-state file above, from inside the container. Matches the Verify State mount target - no need to change this.";s:4:"Type";s:8:"Variable";s:7:"Display";s:8:"advanced";s:8:"Required";s:4:"true";s:4:"Mask";s:5:"false";}s:5:"value";s:25:"/config/verify-state.json";}i:15;a:2:{s:11:"@attributes";a:9:{s:4:"Name";s:15:"Match Overrides";s:6:"Target";s:28:"/config/match-overrides.json";s:7:"Default";s:46:"/mnt/user/appdata/paddock/match-overrides.json";s:4:"Mode";s:2:"rw";s:11:"Description";s:512:"Persists a human's own picks from the Index tab's 'Resolve ambiguous files' modal across container updates - without this, a resolved pick silently reverts to 'ambiguous' again on the next update. Auto-created empty the first time this file doesn't exist yet. BEFORE FIRST APPLY: from the Unraid terminal, run 'touch /mnt/user/appdata/paddock/match-overrides.json' (or your own path above if changed) - otherwise Docker creates an empty directory there instead of a file, which the app can't clean up on its own.";s:4:"Type";s:4:"Path";s:7:"Display";s:8:"advanced";s:8:"Required";s:4:"true";s:4:"Mask";s:5:"false";}s:5:"value";s:46:"/mnt/user/appdata/paddock/match-overrides.json";}i:16;a:2:{s:11:"@attributes";a:9:{s:4:"Name";s:20:"MATCH_OVERRIDES_PATH";s:6:"Target";s:20:"MATCH_OVERRIDES_PATH";s:7:"Default";s:28:"/config/match-overrides.json";s:4:"Mode";s:0:"";s:11:"Description";s:149:"Where the app looks for the match-overrides file above, from inside the container. Matches the Match Overrides mount target - no need to change this.";s:4:"Type";s:8:"Variable";s:7:"Display";s:8:"advanced";s:8:"Required";s:4:"true";s:4:"Mask";s:5:"false";}s:5:"value";s:28:"/config/match-overrides.json";}i:17;a:2:{s:11:"@attributes";a:9:{s:4:"Name";s:13:"Archive State";s:6:"Target";s:26:"/config/archive-state.json";s:7:"Default";s:44:"/mnt/user/appdata/paddock/archive-state.json";s:4:"Mode";s:2:"rw";s:11:"Description";s:494:"Persists which torrents you've archived from the Index tab (hidden from the list without deleting anything - see the Settings tab's Archive panel to undo) across container updates. Auto-created empty the first time this file doesn't exist yet. BEFORE FIRST APPLY: from the Unraid terminal, run 'touch /mnt/user/appdata/paddock/archive-state.json' (or your own path above if changed) - otherwise Docker creates an empty directory there instead of a file, which the app can't clean up on its own.";s:4:"Type";s:4:"Path";s:7:"Display";s:8:"advanced";s:8:"Required";s:4:"true";s:4:"Mask";s:5:"false";}s:5:"value";s:44:"/mnt/user/appdata/paddock/archive-state.json";}i:18;a:2:{s:11:"@attributes";a:9:{s:4:"Name";s:18:"ARCHIVE_STATE_PATH";s:6:"Target";s:18:"ARCHIVE_STATE_PATH";s:7:"Default";s:26:"/config/archive-state.json";s:4:"Mode";s:0:"";s:11:"Description";s:145:"Where the app looks for the archive-state file above, from inside the container. Matches the Archive State mount target - no need to change this.";s:4:"Type";s:8:"Variable";s:7:"Display";s:8:"advanced";s:8:"Required";s:4:"true";s:4:"Mask";s:5:"false";}s:5:"value";s:26:"/config/archive-state.json";}i:19;a:2:{s:11:"@attributes";a:9:{s:4:"Name";s:16:"Torrent Registry";s:6:"Target";s:24:"/config/torrent-registry";s:7:"Default";s:42:"/mnt/user/appdata/paddock/torrent-registry";s:4:"Mode";s:2:"rw";s:11:"Description";s:429:"A durable copy of every .torrent Paddock has a record of (staged through the Index tab, or synced in from Transmission's own torrents directory below), keyed by info-hash - lets you download any of them back later or skip re-processing an already-registered one on a repeat batch drop. A directory mount - unlike the file mounts above, there's no first-run empty-directory gotcha here, since a directory is exactly what's wanted.";s:4:"Type";s:4:"Path";s:7:"Display";s:8:"advanced";s:8:"Required";s:4:"true";s:4:"Mask";s:5:"false";}s:5:"value";s:42:"/mnt/user/appdata/paddock/torrent-registry";}i:20;a:2:{s:11:"@attributes";a:9:{s:4:"Name";s:20:"TORRENT_REGISTRY_DIR";s:6:"Target";s:20:"TORRENT_REGISTRY_DIR";s:7:"Default";s:24:"/config/torrent-registry";s:4:"Mode";s:0:"";s:11:"Description";s:146:"Where the app looks for the torrent registry above, from inside the container. Matches the Torrent Registry mount target - no need to change this.";s:4:"Type";s:8:"Variable";s:7:"Display";s:8:"advanced";s:8:"Required";s:4:"true";s:4:"Mask";s:5:"false";}s:5:"value";s:24:"/config/torrent-registry";}i:21;a:2:{s:11:"@attributes";a:9:{s:4:"Name";s:53:"Transmission's own torrents dir (read-only, optional)";s:6:"Target";s:22:"/transmission-torrents";s:7:"Default";s:39:"/mnt/user/appdata/transmission/torrents";s:4:"Mode";s:2:"ro";s:11:"Description";s:563:"Optional: Transmission's OWN .torrent-storage directory (its config dir's 'torrents' subfolder, next to its own settings.json/resume/ - check Transmission's Docker template path mappings to find its config directory's host path). When set AND TRANSMISSION_TORRENTS_DIR below is also set to /transmission-torrents, every .torrent Transmission has ever been handed - including anything autobrr added directly, never touching Paddock - gets synced into the Torrent Registry above automatically. Leave blank to disable; this share is only ever read, never written to.";s:4:"Type";s:4:"Path";s:7:"Display";s:8:"advanced";s:8:"Required";s:5:"false";s:4:"Mask";s:5:"false";}s:5:"value";s:0:"";}i:22;a:2:{s:11:"@attributes";a:9:{s:4:"Name";s:25:"TRANSMISSION_TORRENTS_DIR";s:6:"Target";s:25:"TRANSMISSION_TORRENTS_DIR";s:7:"Default";s:0:"";s:4:"Mode";s:0:"";s:11:"Description";s:193:"Set to /transmission-torrents (matching the mount target above) to enable the sync described there. Leave blank to disable, same as leaving the mount above blank - both need to be set together.";s:4:"Type";s:8:"Variable";s:7:"Display";s:8:"advanced";s:8:"Required";s:5:"false";s:4:"Mask";s:5:"false";}s:5:"value";s:0:"";}i:23;a:2:{s:11:"@attributes";a:9:{s:4:"Name";s:8:"PLEX_URL";s:6:"Target";s:8:"PLEX_URL";s:7:"Default";s:0:"";s:4:"Mode";s:0:"";s:11:"Description";s:242:"One-time seed only: used to create Settings File above if it doesn't exist yet, then ignored - edit Plex settings live afterward via the web UI. Enables a Plex partial-scan refresh after each successful archive. e.g. http://192.168.1.10:32400";s:4:"Type";s:8:"Variable";s:7:"Display";s:6:"always";s:8:"Required";s:5:"false";s:4:"Mask";s:5:"false";}s:5:"value";s:0:"";}i:24;a:2:{s:11:"@attributes";a:9:{s:4:"Name";s:10:"PLEX_TOKEN";s:6:"Target";s:10:"PLEX_TOKEN";s:7:"Default";s:0:"";s:4:"Mode";s:0:"";s:11:"Description";s:141:"One-time seed only (see PLEX_URL above). Your Plex auth token, required if PLEX_URL is set. See the README's Plex section for how to find it.";s:4:"Type";s:8:"Variable";s:7:"Display";s:6:"always";s:8:"Required";s:5:"false";s:4:"Mask";s:4:"true";}s:5:"value";s:0:"";}i:25;a:2:{s:11:"@attributes";a:9:{s:4:"Name";s:15:"PLEX_SECTION_ID";s:6:"Target";s:15:"PLEX_SECTION_ID";s:7:"Default";s:0:"";s:4:"Mode";s:0:"";s:11:"Description";s:107:"One-time seed only (see PLEX_URL above). The racing library's Plex section id, required if PLEX_URL is set.";s:4:"Type";s:8:"Variable";s:7:"Display";s:6:"always";s:8:"Required";s:5:"false";s:4:"Mask";s:5:"false";}s:5:"value";s:0:"";}i:26;a:2:{s:11:"@attributes";a:9:{s:4:"Name";s:17:"PLEX_LIBRARY_ROOT";s:6:"Target";s:17:"PLEX_LIBRARY_ROOT";s:7:"Default";s:0:"";s:4:"Mode";s:0:"";s:11:"Description";s:208:"One-time seed only (see PLEX_URL above). Only needed if Plex's own container sees this library at a different internal path than Library Root above (the same category of issue as the Downloads Share mapping).";s:4:"Type";s:8:"Variable";s:7:"Display";s:8:"advanced";s:8:"Required";s:5:"false";s:4:"Mask";s:5:"false";}s:5:"value";s:0:"";}i:27;a:2:{s:11:"@attributes";a:9:{s:4:"Name";s:13:"HOTFOLDER_DIR";s:6:"Target";s:13:"HOTFOLDER_DIR";s:7:"Default";s:0:"";s:4:"Mode";s:0:"";s:11:"Description";s:269:"One-time seed only: used to create Settings File above if it doesn't exist yet, then ignored - edit hot-folder settings live afterward via the web UI. Set to /downloads/paddock to enable hot-folder ingestion (matches the read-write mount above). Leave unset to disable.";s:4:"Type";s:8:"Variable";s:7:"Display";s:6:"always";s:8:"Required";s:5:"false";s:4:"Mask";s:5:"false";}s:5:"value";s:0:"";}i:28;a:2:{s:11:"@attributes";a:9:{s:4:"Name";s:26:"HOTFOLDER_POLL_INTERVAL_MS";s:6:"Target";s:26:"HOTFOLDER_POLL_INTERVAL_MS";s:7:"Default";s:5:"60000";s:4:"Mode";s:0:"";s:11:"Description";s:142:"One-time seed only (see HOTFOLDER_DIR above). Tuning: how often (ms) to check a hot-folder drop for size/mtime stability before processing it.";s:4:"Type";s:8:"Variable";s:7:"Display";s:8:"advanced";s:8:"Required";s:5:"false";s:4:"Mask";s:5:"false";}s:5:"value";s:0:"";}i:29;a:2:{s:11:"@attributes";a:9:{s:4:"Name";s:22:"HOTFOLDER_STABLE_POLLS";s:6:"Target";s:22:"HOTFOLDER_STABLE_POLLS";s:7:"Default";s:1:"3";s:4:"Mode";s:0:"";s:11:"Description";s:132:"One-time seed only (see HOTFOLDER_DIR above). Tuning: consecutive stable polls required before a hot-folder drop is treated as done.";s:4:"Type";s:8:"Variable";s:7:"Display";s:8:"advanced";s:8:"Required";s:5:"false";s:4:"Mask";s:5:"false";}s:5:"value";s:0:"";}i:30;a:2:{s:11:"@attributes";a:9:{s:4:"Name";s:19:"DISCORD_WEBHOOK_URL";s:6:"Target";s:19:"DISCORD_WEBHOOK_URL";s:7:"Default";s:0:"";s:4:"Mode";s:0:"";s:11:"Description";s:294:"One-time seed only: used to create Settings File above if it doesn't exist yet, then ignored - edit Discord settings live afterward via the web UI. Posts a summary message to a Discord channel after every torrent-done event. Create one via the target channel's Settings, Integrations, Webhooks.";s:4:"Type";s:8:"Variable";s:7:"Display";s:6:"always";s:8:"Required";s:5:"false";s:4:"Mask";s:4:"true";}s:5:"value";s:0:"";}i:31;a:2:{s:11:"@attributes";a:9:{s:4:"Name";s:23:"DISCORD_MENTION_USER_ID";s:6:"Target";s:23:"DISCORD_MENTION_USER_ID";s:7:"Default";s:0:"";s:4:"Mode";s:0:"";s:11:"Description";s:225:"One-time seed only (see DISCORD_WEBHOOK_URL above). A Discord user id to @mention, but only on review-worthy notifications (auto-created shows, warnings, errors). Leave unset to have every notification post without a mention.";s:4:"Type";s:8:"Variable";s:7:"Display";s:8:"advanced";s:8:"Required";s:5:"false";s:4:"Mask";s:5:"false";}s:5:"value";s:0:"";}i:32;a:2:{s:11:"@attributes";a:9:{s:4:"Name";s:14:"WEBUI_PASSWORD";s:6:"Target";s:14:"WEBUI_PASSWORD";s:7:"Default";s:0:"";s:4:"Mode";s:0:"";s:11:"Description";s:223:"Set this to enable the web UI at /ui (events editor, match tester, upload, activity log). Fails CLOSED, not open: leaving this unset keeps /ui and /api/* returning 503, since that surface can read and overwrite your config.";s:4:"Type";s:8:"Variable";s:7:"Display";s:6:"always";s:8:"Required";s:5:"false";s:4:"Mask";s:4:"true";}s:5:"value";s:0:"";}i:33;a:2:{s:11:"@attributes";a:9:{s:4:"Name";s:10:"WEBUI_USER";s:6:"Target";s:10:"WEBUI_USER";s:7:"Default";s:0:"";s:4:"Mode";s:0:"";s:11:"Description";s:150:"Optional: also require this exact username (HTTP Basic Auth) alongside WEBUI_PASSWORD. Leave unset to accept any username, checking only the password.";s:4:"Type";s:8:"Variable";s:7:"Display";s:8:"advanced";s:8:"Required";s:5:"false";s:4:"Mask";s:5:"false";}s:5:"value";s:0:"";}i:34;a:2:{s:11:"@attributes";a:9:{s:4:"Name";s:4:"PUID";s:6:"Target";s:4:"PUID";s:7:"Default";s:2:"99";s:4:"Mode";s:0:"";s:11:"Description";s:412:"Run the app as this user id instead of root (99 = Unraid's 'nobody', the same user most containers including Transmission run as). The container fixes ownership of its two config files automatically; the Library Root (and hot-folder, if used) must be writable by this user - on a default Unraid share that's already true, otherwise run once from the terminal: chown -R 99:100 on those paths. Blank = run as root.";s:4:"Type";s:8:"Variable";s:7:"Display";s:6:"always";s:8:"Required";s:5:"false";s:4:"Mask";s:5:"false";}s:5:"value";s:2:"99";}i:35;a:2:{s:11:"@attributes";a:9:{s:4:"Name";s:4:"PGID";s:6:"Target";s:4:"PGID";s:7:"Default";s:3:"100";s:4:"Mode";s:0:"";s:11:"Description";s:98:"Group id to run as (100 = Unraid's 'users' group, paired with PUID 99 above). Blank = run as root.";s:4:"Type";s:8:"Variable";s:7:"Display";s:6:"always";s:8:"Required";s:5:"false";s:4:"Mask";s:5:"false";}s:5:"value";s:3:"100";}}s:12:"TemplatePath";s:39:"/tmp/GitHub/AppFeed/unraid-template.xml";s:4:"Repo";s:20:"Paddock's Repository";s:12:"CategoryList";a:3:{i:0;s:15:"Tools-Utilities";i:1;s:14:"MediaApp-Video";i:2;s:11:"Downloaders";}s:9:"FirstSeen";i:1785743710;s:8:"Category";s:43:"Tools:Utilities MediaApp:Video Downloaders:";s:2:"ID";i:3517;s:11:"Displayable";b:0;s:6:"Author";s:7:"nordada";s:13:"DockerHubName";s:7:"paddock";s:8:"RepoName";s:20:"Paddock's Repository";s:10:"SortAuthor";s:7:"nordada";s:8:"SortName";s:7:"paddock";s:6:"random";i:1549347503;s:9:"Blacklist";b:0;s:6:"MinVer";s:3:"6.0";s:4:"Path";s:71:"/tmp/community.applications/tempFiles/templates-community-apps/3517.xml";s:4:"Date";N;s:11:"BrandNewApp";b:1;s:10:"Deprecated";b:0;s:10:"BranchName";s:113:"latest: current main branch. Version tags (e.g. v0.1.035) are also published if you want to pin a specific build.";s:17:"BranchDescription";s:113:"latest: current main branch. Version tags (e.g. v0.1.035) are also published if you want to pin a specific build.";s:11:"Description";N;s:10:"Compatible";b:1;s:16:"ModeratorComment";N;}i:3518;a:37:{s:4:"Name";s:10:"domestique";s:10:"Repository";s:26:"ghcr.io/nordada/domestique";s:8:"Registry";s:63:"https://github.com/nordada/domestique/pkgs/container/domestique";s:7:"Network";s:6:"bridge";s:5:"Shell";s:2:"sh";s:10:"Privileged";s:5:"false";s:7:"Support";s:44:"https://github.com/nordada/domestique/issues";s:7:"Project";s:37:"https://github.com/nordada/domestique";s:8:"Overview";s:988:"Quietly files completed bike-race torrent downloads (autobrr, Transmission, or a manual drop) into a Plex-friendly library layout, renaming them into a standardized "Show - SYYYYEnn - Title - ptNN.ext" scheme. Copies only, never moves or deletes from your download share, so seeding is unaffected. See the project's README for full setup: Transmission's script-torrent-done hook, optional Plex partial-scan refresh, optional hot-folder ingestion, optional Discord notifications, and a password-gated web UI for editing show definitions and testing the matcher.

IMPORTANT: on first run, "Config File" below is auto-seeded from the image's own bundled config/events.json (a curated starter list of major/well-known professional races - Grand Tours, Monuments, Worlds, Olympics, top stage races and classics) - open the web UI (set WEBUI_PASSWORD below) or edit that file directly to add the smaller/regional races your own tracker covers, since this list is intentionally not exhaustive.";s:5:"WebUI";s:26:"http://[IP]:[PORT:8420]/ui";s:11:"TemplateURL";s:77:"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/nordada/domestique/main/unraid-template.xml";s:4:"Icon";s:73:"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/nordada/domestique/main/public/icon.png";s:8:"Requires";s:202:"A downloads share (from Transmission or similar) and a Plex media library share. Both are plain host folders you already have - see each Path config's description below for how to find the right values.";s:6:"Config";a:36:{i:0;a:2:{s:11:"@attributes";a:9:{s:4:"Name";s:29:"WebUI / Webhook / Health Port";s:6:"Target";s:4:"8420";s:7:"Default";s:4:"8420";s:4:"Mode";s:3:"tcp";s:11:"Description";s:118:"Port the web UI (/ui), the Transmission webhook (/webhook/torrent-done), and the health check (/health) all listen on.";s:4:"Type";s:4:"Port";s:7:"Display";s:6:"always";s:8:"Required";s:4:"true";s:4:"Mask";s:5:"false";}s:5:"value";s:4:"8420";}i:1;a:2:{s:11:"@attributes";a:9:{s:4:"Name";s:12:"Library Root";s:6:"Target";s:6:"/media";s:7:"Default";s:27:"/mnt/user/media/bike-racing";s:4:"Mode";s:2:"rw";s:11:"Description";s:111:"Your Plex media library root - point this at your actual racing library folder. Renamed/copied files land here.";s:4:"Type";s:4:"Path";s:7:"Display";s:6:"always";s:8:"Required";s:4:"true";s:4:"Mask";s:5:"false";}s:5:"value";s:27:"/mnt/user/media/bike-racing";}i:2;a:2:{s:11:"@attributes";a:9:{s:4:"Name";s:12:"LIBRARY_ROOT";s:6:"Target";s:12:"LIBRARY_ROOT";s:7:"Default";s:6:"/media";s:4:"Mode";s:0:"";s:11:"Description";s:141:"The container-side path the app uses for the library (must match Library Root's fixed mount point above - you shouldn't need to change this).";s:4:"Type";s:8:"Variable";s:7:"Display";s:8:"advanced";s:8:"Required";s:4:"true";s:4:"Mask";s:5:"false";}s:5:"value";s:6:"/media";}i:3;a:2:{s:11:"@attributes";a:9:{s:4:"Name";s:15:"Downloads Share";s:6:"Target";s:10:"/downloads";s:7:"Default";s:19:"/mnt/user/downloads";s:4:"Mode";s:2:"rw";s:11:"Description";s:660:"The SAME share Transmission's own container maps to /downloads internally - check Transmission's Docker template path mappings to confirm what that is. This is the whole share (not just its 'complete' subfolder). Read-write: the normal ingestion pipeline only ever copies from here, but the Reseed tab's Dedupe feature deletes a torrent's original download-folder copy once it's confirmed hardlinked to the library instead (an explicit, two-click-confirmed action). Set Mode to ro instead if you'd rather keep this share read-only - Dedupe's relink/verify step still works either way, only its optional 'Delete original copy' follow-up needs write access here.";s:4:"Type";s:4:"Path";s:7:"Display";s:6:"always";s:8:"Required";s:4:"true";s:4:"Mask";s:5:"false";}s:5:"value";s:19:"/mnt/user/downloads";}i:4;a:2:{s:11:"@attributes";a:9:{s:4:"Name";s:33:"Hot-folder (read-write, optional)";s:6:"Target";s:21:"/downloads/domestique";s:7:"Default";s:30:"/mnt/user/downloads/domestique";s:4:"Mode";s:2:"rw";s:11:"Description";s:285:"Optional read-write overlay on a 'domestique' subfolder of the share above, for hot-folder ingestion (drop a file/folder here to bypass Transmission entirely). Only takes effect if HOTFOLDER_DIR below is also set to /downloads/domestique; otherwise this is just an unused empty folder.";s:4:"Type";s:4:"Path";s:7:"Display";s:8:"advanced";s:8:"Required";s:5:"false";s:4:"Mask";s:5:"false";}s:5:"value";s:30:"/mnt/user/downloads/domestique";}i:5;a:2:{s:11:"@attributes";a:9:{s:4:"Name";s:11:"Config File";s:6:"Target";s:19:"/config/events.json";s:7:"Default";s:40:"/mnt/user/appdata/domestique/events.json";s:4:"Mode";s:2:"rw";s:11:"Description";s:257:"Persists your show/event definitions across container updates and image upgrades. Auto-created from the image's bundled config/events.json the first time this file doesn't exist yet (see the Overview above) - edit it by hand or through the web UI afterward.";s:4:"Type";s:4:"Path";s:7:"Display";s:6:"always";s:8:"Required";s:4:"true";s:4:"Mask";s:5:"false";}s:5:"value";s:40:"/mnt/user/appdata/domestique/events.json";}i:6;a:2:{s:11:"@attributes";a:9:{s:4:"Name";s:11:"CONFIG_PATH";s:6:"Target";s:11:"CONFIG_PATH";s:7:"Default";s:19:"/config/events.json";s:4:"Mode";s:0:"";s:11:"Description";s:136:"Where the app looks for the config file above, from inside the container. Matches the Config File mount target - no need to change this.";s:4:"Type";s:8:"Variable";s:7:"Display";s:8:"advanced";s:8:"Required";s:4:"true";s:4:"Mask";s:5:"false";}s:5:"value";s:19:"/config/events.json";}i:7;a:2:{s:11:"@attributes";a:9:{s:4:"Name";s:13:"Settings File";s:6:"Target";s:21:"/config/settings.json";s:7:"Default";s:42:"/mnt/user/appdata/domestique/settings.json";s:4:"Mode";s:2:"rw";s:11:"Description";s:529:"Persists your Plex/Discord/hot-folder settings across container updates. Auto-created (seeded from the PLEX_*/DISCORD_*/HOTFOLDER_* variables below) the first time this file doesn't exist yet - edit it live afterward through the web UI's Settings panel instead of these variables. BEFORE FIRST APPLY: from the Unraid terminal, run 'touch /mnt/user/appdata/domestique/settings.json' (or your own path above if changed) - otherwise Docker creates an empty directory there instead of a file, which the app can't clean up on its own.";s:4:"Type";s:4:"Path";s:7:"Display";s:6:"always";s:8:"Required";s:4:"true";s:4:"Mask";s:5:"false";}s:5:"value";s:42:"/mnt/user/appdata/domestique/settings.json";}i:8;a:2:{s:11:"@attributes";a:9:{s:4:"Name";s:13:"SETTINGS_PATH";s:6:"Target";s:13:"SETTINGS_PATH";s:7:"Default";s:21:"/config/settings.json";s:4:"Mode";s:0:"";s:11:"Description";s:140:"Where the app looks for the settings file above, from inside the container. Matches the Settings File mount target - no need to change this.";s:4:"Type";s:8:"Variable";s:7:"Display";s:8:"advanced";s:8:"Required";s:4:"true";s:4:"Mask";s:5:"false";}s:5:"value";s:21:"/config/settings.json";}i:9;a:2:{s:11:"@attributes";a:9:{s:4:"Name";s:12:"Activity Log";s:6:"Target";s:21:"/config/activity.json";s:7:"Default";s:42:"/mnt/user/appdata/domestique/activity.json";s:4:"Mode";s:2:"rw";s:11:"Description";s:392:"Persists the web UI's recent-activity log across container updates and restarts. Auto-created empty the first time this file doesn't exist yet. BEFORE FIRST APPLY: from the Unraid terminal, run 'touch /mnt/user/appdata/domestique/activity.json' (or your own path above if changed) - otherwise Docker creates an empty directory there instead of a file, which the app can't clean up on its own.";s:4:"Type";s:4:"Path";s:7:"Display";s:8:"advanced";s:8:"Required";s:4:"true";s:4:"Mask";s:5:"false";}s:5:"value";s:42:"/mnt/user/appdata/domestique/activity.json";}i:10;a:2:{s:11:"@attributes";a:9:{s:4:"Name";s:13:"ACTIVITY_PATH";s:6:"Target";s:13:"ACTIVITY_PATH";s:7:"Default";s:21:"/config/activity.json";s:4:"Mode";s:0:"";s:11:"Description";s:138:"Where the app looks for the activity log above, from inside the container. Matches the Activity Log mount target - no need to change this.";s:4:"Type";s:8:"Variable";s:7:"Display";s:8:"advanced";s:8:"Required";s:4:"true";s:4:"Mask";s:5:"false";}s:5:"value";s:21:"/config/activity.json";}i:11;a:2:{s:11:"@attributes";a:9:{s:4:"Name";s:12:"Dedupe State";s:6:"Target";s:25:"/config/dedupe-state.json";s:7:"Default";s:46:"/mnt/user/appdata/domestique/dedupe-state.json";s:4:"Mode";s:2:"rw";s:11:"Description";s:560:"Records where a deduped torrent's data lived before the Reseed tab's Dedupe feature relinked it to your library - Transmission itself forgets a torrent's previous location once relocated, so this is the app's own persisted memory of it instead. Auto-created empty the first time this file doesn't exist yet. BEFORE FIRST APPLY: from the Unraid terminal, run 'touch /mnt/user/appdata/domestique/dedupe-state.json' (or your own path above if changed) - otherwise Docker creates an empty directory there instead of a file, which the app can't clean up on its own.";s:4:"Type";s:4:"Path";s:7:"Display";s:8:"advanced";s:8:"Required";s:4:"true";s:4:"Mask";s:5:"false";}s:5:"value";s:46:"/mnt/user/appdata/domestique/dedupe-state.json";}i:12;a:2:{s:11:"@attributes";a:9:{s:4:"Name";s:17:"DEDUPE_STATE_PATH";s:6:"Target";s:17:"DEDUPE_STATE_PATH";s:7:"Default";s:25:"/config/dedupe-state.json";s:4:"Mode";s:0:"";s:11:"Description";s:143:"Where the app looks for the dedupe-state file above, from inside the container. Matches the Dedupe State mount target - no need to change this.";s:4:"Type";s:8:"Variable";s:7:"Display";s:8:"advanced";s:8:"Required";s:4:"true";s:4:"Mask";s:5:"false";}s:5:"value";s:25:"/config/dedupe-state.json";}i:13;a:2:{s:11:"@attributes";a:9:{s:4:"Name";s:12:"Verify State";s:6:"Target";s:25:"/config/verify-state.json";s:7:"Default";s:46:"/mnt/user/appdata/domestique/verify-state.json";s:4:"Mode";s:2:"rw";s:11:"Description";s:404:"Persists the Index tab's 'Verify data' integrity-check results across container updates. Auto-created empty the first time this file doesn't exist yet. BEFORE FIRST APPLY: from the Unraid terminal, run 'touch /mnt/user/appdata/domestique/verify-state.json' (or your own path above if changed) - otherwise Docker creates an empty directory there instead of a file, which the app can't clean up on its own.";s:4:"Type";s:4:"Path";s:7:"Display";s:8:"advanced";s:8:"Required";s:4:"true";s:4:"Mask";s:5:"false";}s:5:"value";s:46:"/mnt/user/appdata/domestique/verify-state.json";}i:14;a:2:{s:11:"@attributes";a:9:{s:4:"Name";s:17:"VERIFY_STATE_PATH";s:6:"Target";s:17:"VERIFY_STATE_PATH";s:7:"Default";s:25:"/config/verify-state.json";s:4:"Mode";s:0:"";s:11:"Description";s:143:"Where the app looks for the verify-state file above, from inside the container. Matches the Verify State mount target - no need to change this.";s:4:"Type";s:8:"Variable";s:7:"Display";s:8:"advanced";s:8:"Required";s:4:"true";s:4:"Mask";s:5:"false";}s:5:"value";s:25:"/config/verify-state.json";}i:15;a:2:{s:11:"@attributes";a:9:{s:4:"Name";s:15:"Match Overrides";s:6:"Target";s:28:"/config/match-overrides.json";s:7:"Default";s:49:"/mnt/user/appdata/domestique/match-overrides.json";s:4:"Mode";s:2:"rw";s:11:"Description";s:515:"Persists a human's own picks from the Index tab's 'Resolve ambiguous files' modal across container updates - without this, a resolved pick silently reverts to 'ambiguous' again on the next update. Auto-created empty the first time this file doesn't exist yet. BEFORE FIRST APPLY: from the Unraid terminal, run 'touch /mnt/user/appdata/domestique/match-overrides.json' (or your own path above if changed) - otherwise Docker creates an empty directory there instead of a file, which the app can't clean up on its own.";s:4:"Type";s:4:"Path";s:7:"Display";s:8:"advanced";s:8:"Required";s:4:"true";s:4:"Mask";s:5:"false";}s:5:"value";s:49:"/mnt/user/appdata/domestique/match-overrides.json";}i:16;a:2:{s:11:"@attributes";a:9:{s:4:"Name";s:20:"MATCH_OVERRIDES_PATH";s:6:"Target";s:20:"MATCH_OVERRIDES_PATH";s:7:"Default";s:28:"/config/match-overrides.json";s:4:"Mode";s:0:"";s:11:"Description";s:149:"Where the app looks for the match-overrides file above, from inside the container. Matches the Match Overrides mount target - no need to change this.";s:4:"Type";s:8:"Variable";s:7:"Display";s:8:"advanced";s:8:"Required";s:4:"true";s:4:"Mask";s:5:"false";}s:5:"value";s:28:"/config/match-overrides.json";}i:17;a:2:{s:11:"@attributes";a:9:{s:4:"Name";s:13:"Archive State";s:6:"Target";s:26:"/config/archive-state.json";s:7:"Default";s:47:"/mnt/user/appdata/domestique/archive-state.json";s:4:"Mode";s:2:"rw";s:11:"Description";s:497:"Persists which torrents you've archived from the Index tab (hidden from the list without deleting anything - see the Settings tab's Archive panel to undo) across container updates. Auto-created empty the first time this file doesn't exist yet. BEFORE FIRST APPLY: from the Unraid terminal, run 'touch /mnt/user/appdata/domestique/archive-state.json' (or your own path above if changed) - otherwise Docker creates an empty directory there instead of a file, which the app can't clean up on its own.";s:4:"Type";s:4:"Path";s:7:"Display";s:8:"advanced";s:8:"Required";s:4:"true";s:4:"Mask";s:5:"false";}s:5:"value";s:47:"/mnt/user/appdata/domestique/archive-state.json";}i:18;a:2:{s:11:"@attributes";a:9:{s:4:"Name";s:18:"ARCHIVE_STATE_PATH";s:6:"Target";s:18:"ARCHIVE_STATE_PATH";s:7:"Default";s:26:"/config/archive-state.json";s:4:"Mode";s:0:"";s:11:"Description";s:145:"Where the app looks for the archive-state file above, from inside the container. Matches the Archive State mount target - no need to change this.";s:4:"Type";s:8:"Variable";s:7:"Display";s:8:"advanced";s:8:"Required";s:4:"true";s:4:"Mask";s:5:"false";}s:5:"value";s:26:"/config/archive-state.json";}i:19;a:2:{s:11:"@attributes";a:9:{s:4:"Name";s:16:"Torrent Registry";s:6:"Target";s:24:"/config/torrent-registry";s:7:"Default";s:45:"/mnt/user/appdata/domestique/torrent-registry";s:4:"Mode";s:2:"rw";s:11:"Description";s:432:"A durable copy of every .torrent Domestique has a record of (staged through the Index tab, or synced in from Transmission's own torrents directory below), keyed by info-hash - lets you download any of them back later or skip re-processing an already-registered one on a repeat batch drop. A directory mount - unlike the file mounts above, there's no first-run empty-directory gotcha here, since a directory is exactly what's wanted.";s:4:"Type";s:4:"Path";s:7:"Display";s:8:"advanced";s:8:"Required";s:4:"true";s:4:"Mask";s:5:"false";}s:5:"value";s:45:"/mnt/user/appdata/domestique/torrent-registry";}i:20;a:2:{s:11:"@attributes";a:9:{s:4:"Name";s:20:"TORRENT_REGISTRY_DIR";s:6:"Target";s:20:"TORRENT_REGISTRY_DIR";s:7:"Default";s:24:"/config/torrent-registry";s:4:"Mode";s:0:"";s:11:"Description";s:146:"Where the app looks for the torrent registry above, from inside the container. Matches the Torrent Registry mount target - no need to change this.";s:4:"Type";s:8:"Variable";s:7:"Display";s:8:"advanced";s:8:"Required";s:4:"true";s:4:"Mask";s:5:"false";}s:5:"value";s:24:"/config/torrent-registry";}i:21;a:2:{s:11:"@attributes";a:9:{s:4:"Name";s:53:"Transmission's own torrents dir (read-only, optional)";s:6:"Target";s:22:"/transmission-torrents";s:7:"Default";s:39:"/mnt/user/appdata/transmission/torrents";s:4:"Mode";s:2:"ro";s:11:"Description";s:566:"Optional: Transmission's OWN .torrent-storage directory (its config dir's 'torrents' subfolder, next to its own settings.json/resume/ - check Transmission's Docker template path mappings to find its config directory's host path). When set AND TRANSMISSION_TORRENTS_DIR below is also set to /transmission-torrents, every .torrent Transmission has ever been handed - including anything autobrr added directly, never touching Domestique - gets synced into the Torrent Registry above automatically. Leave blank to disable; this share is only ever read, never written to.";s:4:"Type";s:4:"Path";s:7:"Display";s:8:"advanced";s:8:"Required";s:5:"false";s:4:"Mask";s:5:"false";}s:5:"value";s:0:"";}i:22;a:2:{s:11:"@attributes";a:9:{s:4:"Name";s:25:"TRANSMISSION_TORRENTS_DIR";s:6:"Target";s:25:"TRANSMISSION_TORRENTS_DIR";s:7:"Default";s:0:"";s:4:"Mode";s:0:"";s:11:"Description";s:193:"Set to /transmission-torrents (matching the mount target above) to enable the sync described there. Leave blank to disable, same as leaving the mount above blank - both need to be set together.";s:4:"Type";s:8:"Variable";s:7:"Display";s:8:"advanced";s:8:"Required";s:5:"false";s:4:"Mask";s:5:"false";}s:5:"value";s:0:"";}i:23;a:2:{s:11:"@attributes";a:9:{s:4:"Name";s:8:"PLEX_URL";s:6:"Target";s:8:"PLEX_URL";s:7:"Default";s:0:"";s:4:"Mode";s:0:"";s:11:"Description";s:242:"One-time seed only: used to create Settings File above if it doesn't exist yet, then ignored - edit Plex settings live afterward via the web UI. Enables a Plex partial-scan refresh after each successful archive. e.g. http://192.168.1.10:32400";s:4:"Type";s:8:"Variable";s:7:"Display";s:6:"always";s:8:"Required";s:5:"false";s:4:"Mask";s:5:"false";}s:5:"value";s:0:"";}i:24;a:2:{s:11:"@attributes";a:9:{s:4:"Name";s:10:"PLEX_TOKEN";s:6:"Target";s:10:"PLEX_TOKEN";s:7:"Default";s:0:"";s:4:"Mode";s:0:"";s:11:"Description";s:141:"One-time seed only (see PLEX_URL above). Your Plex auth token, required if PLEX_URL is set. See the README's Plex section for how to find it.";s:4:"Type";s:8:"Variable";s:7:"Display";s:6:"always";s:8:"Required";s:5:"false";s:4:"Mask";s:4:"true";}s:5:"value";s:0:"";}i:25;a:2:{s:11:"@attributes";a:9:{s:4:"Name";s:15:"PLEX_SECTION_ID";s:6:"Target";s:15:"PLEX_SECTION_ID";s:7:"Default";s:0:"";s:4:"Mode";s:0:"";s:11:"Description";s:107:"One-time seed only (see PLEX_URL above). The racing library's Plex section id, required if PLEX_URL is set.";s:4:"Type";s:8:"Variable";s:7:"Display";s:6:"always";s:8:"Required";s:5:"false";s:4:"Mask";s:5:"false";}s:5:"value";s:0:"";}i:26;a:2:{s:11:"@attributes";a:9:{s:4:"Name";s:17:"PLEX_LIBRARY_ROOT";s:6:"Target";s:17:"PLEX_LIBRARY_ROOT";s:7:"Default";s:0:"";s:4:"Mode";s:0:"";s:11:"Description";s:208:"One-time seed only (see PLEX_URL above). Only needed if Plex's own container sees this library at a different internal path than Library Root above (the same category of issue as the Downloads Share mapping).";s:4:"Type";s:8:"Variable";s:7:"Display";s:8:"advanced";s:8:"Required";s:5:"false";s:4:"Mask";s:5:"false";}s:5:"value";s:0:"";}i:27;a:2:{s:11:"@attributes";a:9:{s:4:"Name";s:13:"HOTFOLDER_DIR";s:6:"Target";s:13:"HOTFOLDER_DIR";s:7:"Default";s:0:"";s:4:"Mode";s:0:"";s:11:"Description";s:272:"One-time seed only: used to create Settings File above if it doesn't exist yet, then ignored - edit hot-folder settings live afterward via the web UI. Set to /downloads/domestique to enable hot-folder ingestion (matches the read-write mount above). Leave unset to disable.";s:4:"Type";s:8:"Variable";s:7:"Display";s:6:"always";s:8:"Required";s:5:"false";s:4:"Mask";s:5:"false";}s:5:"value";s:0:"";}i:28;a:2:{s:11:"@attributes";a:9:{s:4:"Name";s:26:"HOTFOLDER_POLL_INTERVAL_MS";s:6:"Target";s:26:"HOTFOLDER_POLL_INTERVAL_MS";s:7:"Default";s:5:"60000";s:4:"Mode";s:0:"";s:11:"Description";s:142:"One-time seed only (see HOTFOLDER_DIR above). Tuning: how often (ms) to check a hot-folder drop for size/mtime stability before processing it.";s:4:"Type";s:8:"Variable";s:7:"Display";s:8:"advanced";s:8:"Required";s:5:"false";s:4:"Mask";s:5:"false";}s:5:"value";s:0:"";}i:29;a:2:{s:11:"@attributes";a:9:{s:4:"Name";s:22:"HOTFOLDER_STABLE_POLLS";s:6:"Target";s:22:"HOTFOLDER_STABLE_POLLS";s:7:"Default";s:1:"3";s:4:"Mode";s:0:"";s:11:"Description";s:132:"One-time seed only (see HOTFOLDER_DIR above). Tuning: consecutive stable polls required before a hot-folder drop is treated as done.";s:4:"Type";s:8:"Variable";s:7:"Display";s:8:"advanced";s:8:"Required";s:5:"false";s:4:"Mask";s:5:"false";}s:5:"value";s:0:"";}i:30;a:2:{s:11:"@attributes";a:9:{s:4:"Name";s:19:"DISCORD_WEBHOOK_URL";s:6:"Target";s:19:"DISCORD_WEBHOOK_URL";s:7:"Default";s:0:"";s:4:"Mode";s:0:"";s:11:"Description";s:294:"One-time seed only: used to create Settings File above if it doesn't exist yet, then ignored - edit Discord settings live afterward via the web UI. Posts a summary message to a Discord channel after every torrent-done event. Create one via the target channel's Settings, Integrations, Webhooks.";s:4:"Type";s:8:"Variable";s:7:"Display";s:6:"always";s:8:"Required";s:5:"false";s:4:"Mask";s:4:"true";}s:5:"value";s:0:"";}i:31;a:2:{s:11:"@attributes";a:9:{s:4:"Name";s:23:"DISCORD_MENTION_USER_ID";s:6:"Target";s:23:"DISCORD_MENTION_USER_ID";s:7:"Default";s:0:"";s:4:"Mode";s:0:"";s:11:"Description";s:225:"One-time seed only (see DISCORD_WEBHOOK_URL above). A Discord user id to @mention, but only on review-worthy notifications (auto-created shows, warnings, errors). Leave unset to have every notification post without a mention.";s:4:"Type";s:8:"Variable";s:7:"Display";s:8:"advanced";s:8:"Required";s:5:"false";s:4:"Mask";s:5:"false";}s:5:"value";s:0:"";}i:32;a:2:{s:11:"@attributes";a:9:{s:4:"Name";s:14:"WEBUI_PASSWORD";s:6:"Target";s:14:"WEBUI_PASSWORD";s:7:"Default";s:0:"";s:4:"Mode";s:0:"";s:11:"Description";s:223:"Set this to enable the web UI at /ui (events editor, match tester, upload, activity log). Fails CLOSED, not open: leaving this unset keeps /ui and /api/* returning 503, since that surface can read and overwrite your config.";s:4:"Type";s:8:"Variable";s:7:"Display";s:6:"always";s:8:"Required";s:5:"false";s:4:"Mask";s:4:"true";}s:5:"value";s:0:"";}i:33;a:2:{s:11:"@attributes";a:9:{s:4:"Name";s:10:"WEBUI_USER";s:6:"Target";s:10:"WEBUI_USER";s:7:"Default";s:0:"";s:4:"Mode";s:0:"";s:11:"Description";s:150:"Optional: also require this exact username (HTTP Basic Auth) alongside WEBUI_PASSWORD. Leave unset to accept any username, checking only the password.";s:4:"Type";s:8:"Variable";s:7:"Display";s:8:"advanced";s:8:"Required";s:5:"false";s:4:"Mask";s:5:"false";}s:5:"value";s:0:"";}i:34;a:2:{s:11:"@attributes";a:9:{s:4:"Name";s:4:"PUID";s:6:"Target";s:4:"PUID";s:7:"Default";s:2:"99";s:4:"Mode";s:0:"";s:11:"Description";s:412:"Run the app as this user id instead of root (99 = Unraid's 'nobody', the same user most containers including Transmission run as). The container fixes ownership of its two config files automatically; the Library Root (and hot-folder, if used) must be writable by this user - on a default Unraid share that's already true, otherwise run once from the terminal: chown -R 99:100 on those paths. Blank = run as root.";s:4:"Type";s:8:"Variable";s:7:"Display";s:6:"always";s:8:"Required";s:5:"false";s:4:"Mask";s:5:"false";}s:5:"value";s:2:"99";}i:35;a:2:{s:11:"@attributes";a:9:{s:4:"Name";s:4:"PGID";s:6:"Target";s:4:"PGID";s:7:"Default";s:3:"100";s:4:"Mode";s:0:"";s:11:"Description";s:98:"Group id to run as (100 = Unraid's 'users' group, paired with PUID 99 above). Blank = run as root.";s:4:"Type";s:8:"Variable";s:7:"Display";s:6:"always";s:8:"Required";s:5:"false";s:4:"Mask";s:5:"false";}s:5:"value";s:3:"100";}}s:12:"TemplatePath";s:39:"/tmp/GitHub/AppFeed/unraid-template.xml";s:4:"Repo";s:20:"nordada's Repository";s:12:"CategoryList";a:3:{i:0;s:15:"Tools-Utilities";i:1;s:14:"MediaApp-Video";i:2;s:11:"Downloaders";}s:9:"FirstSeen";i:1785248890;s:8:"Category";s:43:"Tools:Utilities MediaApp:Video Downloaders:";s:2:"ID";i:3518;s:11:"Displayable";b:1;s:6:"Author";s:7:"nordada";s:13:"DockerHubName";s:10:"domestique";s:8:"RepoName";s:20:"nordada's Repository";s:10:"SortAuthor";s:7:"nordada";s:8:"SortName";s:10:"domestique";s:6:"random";i:1181916350;s:9:"Blacklist";b:0;s:6:"MinVer";s:3:"6.0";s:4:"Path";s:111:"/tmp/community.applications/tempFiles/templates-community-apps/nordadasRepository/nordada-domestique-latest.xml";s:4:"Date";N;s:11:"BrandNewApp";b:1;s:10:"Deprecated";b:0;s:13:"BranchDefault";N;s:8:"BranchID";a:1:{i:0;i:3519;}s:10:"Compatible";b:1;s:16:"ModeratorComment";N;}i:3519;a:38:{s:4:"Name";s:10:"domestique";s:10:"Repository";s:140:"ghcr.io/nordada/domestique:latest: current main branch. Version tags (e.g. v0.1.035) are also published if you want to pin a specific build.";s:8:"Registry";s:63:"https://github.com/nordada/domestique/pkgs/container/domestique";s:7:"Network";s:6:"bridge";s:5:"Shell";s:2:"sh";s:10:"Privileged";s:5:"false";s:7:"Support";s:44:"https://github.com/nordada/domestique/issues";s:7:"Project";s:37:"https://github.com/nordada/domestique";s:8:"Overview";s:988:"Quietly files completed bike-race torrent downloads (autobrr, Transmission, or a manual drop) into a Plex-friendly library layout, renaming them into a standardized "Show - SYYYYEnn - Title - ptNN.ext" scheme. Copies only, never moves or deletes from your download share, so seeding is unaffected. See the project's README for full setup: Transmission's script-torrent-done hook, optional Plex partial-scan refresh, optional hot-folder ingestion, optional Discord notifications, and a password-gated web UI for editing show definitions and testing the matcher.

IMPORTANT: on first run, "Config File" below is auto-seeded from the image's own bundled config/events.json (a curated starter list of major/well-known professional races - Grand Tours, Monuments, Worlds, Olympics, top stage races and classics) - open the web UI (set WEBUI_PASSWORD below) or edit that file directly to add the smaller/regional races your own tracker covers, since this list is intentionally not exhaustive.";s:5:"WebUI";s:26:"http://[IP]:[PORT:8420]/ui";s:11:"TemplateURL";s:77:"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/nordada/domestique/main/unraid-template.xml";s:4:"Icon";s:73:"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/nordada/domestique/main/public/icon.png";s:8:"Requires";s:202:"A downloads share (from Transmission or similar) and a Plex media library share. Both are plain host folders you already have - see each Path config's description below for how to find the right values.";s:6:"Config";a:36:{i:0;a:2:{s:11:"@attributes";a:9:{s:4:"Name";s:29:"WebUI / Webhook / Health Port";s:6:"Target";s:4:"8420";s:7:"Default";s:4:"8420";s:4:"Mode";s:3:"tcp";s:11:"Description";s:118:"Port the web UI (/ui), the Transmission webhook (/webhook/torrent-done), and the health check (/health) all listen on.";s:4:"Type";s:4:"Port";s:7:"Display";s:6:"always";s:8:"Required";s:4:"true";s:4:"Mask";s:5:"false";}s:5:"value";s:4:"8420";}i:1;a:2:{s:11:"@attributes";a:9:{s:4:"Name";s:12:"Library Root";s:6:"Target";s:6:"/media";s:7:"Default";s:27:"/mnt/user/media/bike-racing";s:4:"Mode";s:2:"rw";s:11:"Description";s:111:"Your Plex media library root - point this at your actual racing library folder. Renamed/copied files land here.";s:4:"Type";s:4:"Path";s:7:"Display";s:6:"always";s:8:"Required";s:4:"true";s:4:"Mask";s:5:"false";}s:5:"value";s:27:"/mnt/user/media/bike-racing";}i:2;a:2:{s:11:"@attributes";a:9:{s:4:"Name";s:12:"LIBRARY_ROOT";s:6:"Target";s:12:"LIBRARY_ROOT";s:7:"Default";s:6:"/media";s:4:"Mode";s:0:"";s:11:"Description";s:141:"The container-side path the app uses for the library (must match Library Root's fixed mount point above - you shouldn't need to change this).";s:4:"Type";s:8:"Variable";s:7:"Display";s:8:"advanced";s:8:"Required";s:4:"true";s:4:"Mask";s:5:"false";}s:5:"value";s:6:"/media";}i:3;a:2:{s:11:"@attributes";a:9:{s:4:"Name";s:15:"Downloads Share";s:6:"Target";s:10:"/downloads";s:7:"Default";s:19:"/mnt/user/downloads";s:4:"Mode";s:2:"rw";s:11:"Description";s:660:"The SAME share Transmission's own container maps to /downloads internally - check Transmission's Docker template path mappings to confirm what that is. This is the whole share (not just its 'complete' subfolder). Read-write: the normal ingestion pipeline only ever copies from here, but the Reseed tab's Dedupe feature deletes a torrent's original download-folder copy once it's confirmed hardlinked to the library instead (an explicit, two-click-confirmed action). Set Mode to ro instead if you'd rather keep this share read-only - Dedupe's relink/verify step still works either way, only its optional 'Delete original copy' follow-up needs write access here.";s:4:"Type";s:4:"Path";s:7:"Display";s:6:"always";s:8:"Required";s:4:"true";s:4:"Mask";s:5:"false";}s:5:"value";s:19:"/mnt/user/downloads";}i:4;a:2:{s:11:"@attributes";a:9:{s:4:"Name";s:33:"Hot-folder (read-write, optional)";s:6:"Target";s:21:"/downloads/domestique";s:7:"Default";s:30:"/mnt/user/downloads/domestique";s:4:"Mode";s:2:"rw";s:11:"Description";s:285:"Optional read-write overlay on a 'domestique' subfolder of the share above, for hot-folder ingestion (drop a file/folder here to bypass Transmission entirely). Only takes effect if HOTFOLDER_DIR below is also set to /downloads/domestique; otherwise this is just an unused empty folder.";s:4:"Type";s:4:"Path";s:7:"Display";s:8:"advanced";s:8:"Required";s:5:"false";s:4:"Mask";s:5:"false";}s:5:"value";s:30:"/mnt/user/downloads/domestique";}i:5;a:2:{s:11:"@attributes";a:9:{s:4:"Name";s:11:"Config File";s:6:"Target";s:19:"/config/events.json";s:7:"Default";s:40:"/mnt/user/appdata/domestique/events.json";s:4:"Mode";s:2:"rw";s:11:"Description";s:257:"Persists your show/event definitions across container updates and image upgrades. Auto-created from the image's bundled config/events.json the first time this file doesn't exist yet (see the Overview above) - edit it by hand or through the web UI afterward.";s:4:"Type";s:4:"Path";s:7:"Display";s:6:"always";s:8:"Required";s:4:"true";s:4:"Mask";s:5:"false";}s:5:"value";s:40:"/mnt/user/appdata/domestique/events.json";}i:6;a:2:{s:11:"@attributes";a:9:{s:4:"Name";s:11:"CONFIG_PATH";s:6:"Target";s:11:"CONFIG_PATH";s:7:"Default";s:19:"/config/events.json";s:4:"Mode";s:0:"";s:11:"Description";s:136:"Where the app looks for the config file above, from inside the container. Matches the Config File mount target - no need to change this.";s:4:"Type";s:8:"Variable";s:7:"Display";s:8:"advanced";s:8:"Required";s:4:"true";s:4:"Mask";s:5:"false";}s:5:"value";s:19:"/config/events.json";}i:7;a:2:{s:11:"@attributes";a:9:{s:4:"Name";s:13:"Settings File";s:6:"Target";s:21:"/config/settings.json";s:7:"Default";s:42:"/mnt/user/appdata/domestique/settings.json";s:4:"Mode";s:2:"rw";s:11:"Description";s:529:"Persists your Plex/Discord/hot-folder settings across container updates. Auto-created (seeded from the PLEX_*/DISCORD_*/HOTFOLDER_* variables below) the first time this file doesn't exist yet - edit it live afterward through the web UI's Settings panel instead of these variables. BEFORE FIRST APPLY: from the Unraid terminal, run 'touch /mnt/user/appdata/domestique/settings.json' (or your own path above if changed) - otherwise Docker creates an empty directory there instead of a file, which the app can't clean up on its own.";s:4:"Type";s:4:"Path";s:7:"Display";s:6:"always";s:8:"Required";s:4:"true";s:4:"Mask";s:5:"false";}s:5:"value";s:42:"/mnt/user/appdata/domestique/settings.json";}i:8;a:2:{s:11:"@attributes";a:9:{s:4:"Name";s:13:"SETTINGS_PATH";s:6:"Target";s:13:"SETTINGS_PATH";s:7:"Default";s:21:"/config/settings.json";s:4:"Mode";s:0:"";s:11:"Description";s:140:"Where the app looks for the settings file above, from inside the container. Matches the Settings File mount target - no need to change this.";s:4:"Type";s:8:"Variable";s:7:"Display";s:8:"advanced";s:8:"Required";s:4:"true";s:4:"Mask";s:5:"false";}s:5:"value";s:21:"/config/settings.json";}i:9;a:2:{s:11:"@attributes";a:9:{s:4:"Name";s:12:"Activity Log";s:6:"Target";s:21:"/config/activity.json";s:7:"Default";s:42:"/mnt/user/appdata/domestique/activity.json";s:4:"Mode";s:2:"rw";s:11:"Description";s:392:"Persists the web UI's recent-activity log across container updates and restarts. Auto-created empty the first time this file doesn't exist yet. BEFORE FIRST APPLY: from the Unraid terminal, run 'touch /mnt/user/appdata/domestique/activity.json' (or your own path above if changed) - otherwise Docker creates an empty directory there instead of a file, which the app can't clean up on its own.";s:4:"Type";s:4:"Path";s:7:"Display";s:8:"advanced";s:8:"Required";s:4:"true";s:4:"Mask";s:5:"false";}s:5:"value";s:42:"/mnt/user/appdata/domestique/activity.json";}i:10;a:2:{s:11:"@attributes";a:9:{s:4:"Name";s:13:"ACTIVITY_PATH";s:6:"Target";s:13:"ACTIVITY_PATH";s:7:"Default";s:21:"/config/activity.json";s:4:"Mode";s:0:"";s:11:"Description";s:138:"Where the app looks for the activity log above, from inside the container. Matches the Activity Log mount target - no need to change this.";s:4:"Type";s:8:"Variable";s:7:"Display";s:8:"advanced";s:8:"Required";s:4:"true";s:4:"Mask";s:5:"false";}s:5:"value";s:21:"/config/activity.json";}i:11;a:2:{s:11:"@attributes";a:9:{s:4:"Name";s:12:"Dedupe State";s:6:"Target";s:25:"/config/dedupe-state.json";s:7:"Default";s:46:"/mnt/user/appdata/domestique/dedupe-state.json";s:4:"Mode";s:2:"rw";s:11:"Description";s:560:"Records where a deduped torrent's data lived before the Reseed tab's Dedupe feature relinked it to your library - Transmission itself forgets a torrent's previous location once relocated, so this is the app's own persisted memory of it instead. Auto-created empty the first time this file doesn't exist yet. BEFORE FIRST APPLY: from the Unraid terminal, run 'touch /mnt/user/appdata/domestique/dedupe-state.json' (or your own path above if changed) - otherwise Docker creates an empty directory there instead of a file, which the app can't clean up on its own.";s:4:"Type";s:4:"Path";s:7:"Display";s:8:"advanced";s:8:"Required";s:4:"true";s:4:"Mask";s:5:"false";}s:5:"value";s:46:"/mnt/user/appdata/domestique/dedupe-state.json";}i:12;a:2:{s:11:"@attributes";a:9:{s:4:"Name";s:17:"DEDUPE_STATE_PATH";s:6:"Target";s:17:"DEDUPE_STATE_PATH";s:7:"Default";s:25:"/config/dedupe-state.json";s:4:"Mode";s:0:"";s:11:"Description";s:143:"Where the app looks for the dedupe-state file above, from inside the container. Matches the Dedupe State mount target - no need to change this.";s:4:"Type";s:8:"Variable";s:7:"Display";s:8:"advanced";s:8:"Required";s:4:"true";s:4:"Mask";s:5:"false";}s:5:"value";s:25:"/config/dedupe-state.json";}i:13;a:2:{s:11:"@attributes";a:9:{s:4:"Name";s:12:"Verify State";s:6:"Target";s:25:"/config/verify-state.json";s:7:"Default";s:46:"/mnt/user/appdata/domestique/verify-state.json";s:4:"Mode";s:2:"rw";s:11:"Description";s:404:"Persists the Index tab's 'Verify data' integrity-check results across container updates. Auto-created empty the first time this file doesn't exist yet. BEFORE FIRST APPLY: from the Unraid terminal, run 'touch /mnt/user/appdata/domestique/verify-state.json' (or your own path above if changed) - otherwise Docker creates an empty directory there instead of a file, which the app can't clean up on its own.";s:4:"Type";s:4:"Path";s:7:"Display";s:8:"advanced";s:8:"Required";s:4:"true";s:4:"Mask";s:5:"false";}s:5:"value";s:46:"/mnt/user/appdata/domestique/verify-state.json";}i:14;a:2:{s:11:"@attributes";a:9:{s:4:"Name";s:17:"VERIFY_STATE_PATH";s:6:"Target";s:17:"VERIFY_STATE_PATH";s:7:"Default";s:25:"/config/verify-state.json";s:4:"Mode";s:0:"";s:11:"Description";s:143:"Where the app looks for the verify-state file above, from inside the container. Matches the Verify State mount target - no need to change this.";s:4:"Type";s:8:"Variable";s:7:"Display";s:8:"advanced";s:8:"Required";s:4:"true";s:4:"Mask";s:5:"false";}s:5:"value";s:25:"/config/verify-state.json";}i:15;a:2:{s:11:"@attributes";a:9:{s:4:"Name";s:15:"Match Overrides";s:6:"Target";s:28:"/config/match-overrides.json";s:7:"Default";s:49:"/mnt/user/appdata/domestique/match-overrides.json";s:4:"Mode";s:2:"rw";s:11:"Description";s:515:"Persists a human's own picks from the Index tab's 'Resolve ambiguous files' modal across container updates - without this, a resolved pick silently reverts to 'ambiguous' again on the next update. Auto-created empty the first time this file doesn't exist yet. BEFORE FIRST APPLY: from the Unraid terminal, run 'touch /mnt/user/appdata/domestique/match-overrides.json' (or your own path above if changed) - otherwise Docker creates an empty directory there instead of a file, which the app can't clean up on its own.";s:4:"Type";s:4:"Path";s:7:"Display";s:8:"advanced";s:8:"Required";s:4:"true";s:4:"Mask";s:5:"false";}s:5:"value";s:49:"/mnt/user/appdata/domestique/match-overrides.json";}i:16;a:2:{s:11:"@attributes";a:9:{s:4:"Name";s:20:"MATCH_OVERRIDES_PATH";s:6:"Target";s:20:"MATCH_OVERRIDES_PATH";s:7:"Default";s:28:"/config/match-overrides.json";s:4:"Mode";s:0:"";s:11:"Description";s:149:"Where the app looks for the match-overrides file above, from inside the container. Matches the Match Overrides mount target - no need to change this.";s:4:"Type";s:8:"Variable";s:7:"Display";s:8:"advanced";s:8:"Required";s:4:"true";s:4:"Mask";s:5:"false";}s:5:"value";s:28:"/config/match-overrides.json";}i:17;a:2:{s:11:"@attributes";a:9:{s:4:"Name";s:13:"Archive State";s:6:"Target";s:26:"/config/archive-state.json";s:7:"Default";s:47:"/mnt/user/appdata/domestique/archive-state.json";s:4:"Mode";s:2:"rw";s:11:"Description";s:497:"Persists which torrents you've archived from the Index tab (hidden from the list without deleting anything - see the Settings tab's Archive panel to undo) across container updates. Auto-created empty the first time this file doesn't exist yet. BEFORE FIRST APPLY: from the Unraid terminal, run 'touch /mnt/user/appdata/domestique/archive-state.json' (or your own path above if changed) - otherwise Docker creates an empty directory there instead of a file, which the app can't clean up on its own.";s:4:"Type";s:4:"Path";s:7:"Display";s:8:"advanced";s:8:"Required";s:4:"true";s:4:"Mask";s:5:"false";}s:5:"value";s:47:"/mnt/user/appdata/domestique/archive-state.json";}i:18;a:2:{s:11:"@attributes";a:9:{s:4:"Name";s:18:"ARCHIVE_STATE_PATH";s:6:"Target";s:18:"ARCHIVE_STATE_PATH";s:7:"Default";s:26:"/config/archive-state.json";s:4:"Mode";s:0:"";s:11:"Description";s:145:"Where the app looks for the archive-state file above, from inside the container. Matches the Archive State mount target - no need to change this.";s:4:"Type";s:8:"Variable";s:7:"Display";s:8:"advanced";s:8:"Required";s:4:"true";s:4:"Mask";s:5:"false";}s:5:"value";s:26:"/config/archive-state.json";}i:19;a:2:{s:11:"@attributes";a:9:{s:4:"Name";s:16:"Torrent Registry";s:6:"Target";s:24:"/config/torrent-registry";s:7:"Default";s:45:"/mnt/user/appdata/domestique/torrent-registry";s:4:"Mode";s:2:"rw";s:11:"Description";s:432:"A durable copy of every .torrent Domestique has a record of (staged through the Index tab, or synced in from Transmission's own torrents directory below), keyed by info-hash - lets you download any of them back later or skip re-processing an already-registered one on a repeat batch drop. A directory mount - unlike the file mounts above, there's no first-run empty-directory gotcha here, since a directory is exactly what's wanted.";s:4:"Type";s:4:"Path";s:7:"Display";s:8:"advanced";s:8:"Required";s:4:"true";s:4:"Mask";s:5:"false";}s:5:"value";s:45:"/mnt/user/appdata/domestique/torrent-registry";}i:20;a:2:{s:11:"@attributes";a:9:{s:4:"Name";s:20:"TORRENT_REGISTRY_DIR";s:6:"Target";s:20:"TORRENT_REGISTRY_DIR";s:7:"Default";s:24:"/config/torrent-registry";s:4:"Mode";s:0:"";s:11:"Description";s:146:"Where the app looks for the torrent registry above, from inside the container. Matches the Torrent Registry mount target - no need to change this.";s:4:"Type";s:8:"Variable";s:7:"Display";s:8:"advanced";s:8:"Required";s:4:"true";s:4:"Mask";s:5:"false";}s:5:"value";s:24:"/config/torrent-registry";}i:21;a:2:{s:11:"@attributes";a:9:{s:4:"Name";s:53:"Transmission's own torrents dir (read-only, optional)";s:6:"Target";s:22:"/transmission-torrents";s:7:"Default";s:39:"/mnt/user/appdata/transmission/torrents";s:4:"Mode";s:2:"ro";s:11:"Description";s:566:"Optional: Transmission's OWN .torrent-storage directory (its config dir's 'torrents' subfolder, next to its own settings.json/resume/ - check Transmission's Docker template path mappings to find its config directory's host path). When set AND TRANSMISSION_TORRENTS_DIR below is also set to /transmission-torrents, every .torrent Transmission has ever been handed - including anything autobrr added directly, never touching Domestique - gets synced into the Torrent Registry above automatically. Leave blank to disable; this share is only ever read, never written to.";s:4:"Type";s:4:"Path";s:7:"Display";s:8:"advanced";s:8:"Required";s:5:"false";s:4:"Mask";s:5:"false";}s:5:"value";s:0:"";}i:22;a:2:{s:11:"@attributes";a:9:{s:4:"Name";s:25:"TRANSMISSION_TORRENTS_DIR";s:6:"Target";s:25:"TRANSMISSION_TORRENTS_DIR";s:7:"Default";s:0:"";s:4:"Mode";s:0:"";s:11:"Description";s:193:"Set to /transmission-torrents (matching the mount target above) to enable the sync described there. Leave blank to disable, same as leaving the mount above blank - both need to be set together.";s:4:"Type";s:8:"Variable";s:7:"Display";s:8:"advanced";s:8:"Required";s:5:"false";s:4:"Mask";s:5:"false";}s:5:"value";s:0:"";}i:23;a:2:{s:11:"@attributes";a:9:{s:4:"Name";s:8:"PLEX_URL";s:6:"Target";s:8:"PLEX_URL";s:7:"Default";s:0:"";s:4:"Mode";s:0:"";s:11:"Description";s:242:"One-time seed only: used to create Settings File above if it doesn't exist yet, then ignored - edit Plex settings live afterward via the web UI. Enables a Plex partial-scan refresh after each successful archive. e.g. http://192.168.1.10:32400";s:4:"Type";s:8:"Variable";s:7:"Display";s:6:"always";s:8:"Required";s:5:"false";s:4:"Mask";s:5:"false";}s:5:"value";s:0:"";}i:24;a:2:{s:11:"@attributes";a:9:{s:4:"Name";s:10:"PLEX_TOKEN";s:6:"Target";s:10:"PLEX_TOKEN";s:7:"Default";s:0:"";s:4:"Mode";s:0:"";s:11:"Description";s:141:"One-time seed only (see PLEX_URL above). Your Plex auth token, required if PLEX_URL is set. See the README's Plex section for how to find it.";s:4:"Type";s:8:"Variable";s:7:"Display";s:6:"always";s:8:"Required";s:5:"false";s:4:"Mask";s:4:"true";}s:5:"value";s:0:"";}i:25;a:2:{s:11:"@attributes";a:9:{s:4:"Name";s:15:"PLEX_SECTION_ID";s:6:"Target";s:15:"PLEX_SECTION_ID";s:7:"Default";s:0:"";s:4:"Mode";s:0:"";s:11:"Description";s:107:"One-time seed only (see PLEX_URL above). The racing library's Plex section id, required if PLEX_URL is set.";s:4:"Type";s:8:"Variable";s:7:"Display";s:6:"always";s:8:"Required";s:5:"false";s:4:"Mask";s:5:"false";}s:5:"value";s:0:"";}i:26;a:2:{s:11:"@attributes";a:9:{s:4:"Name";s:17:"PLEX_LIBRARY_ROOT";s:6:"Target";s:17:"PLEX_LIBRARY_ROOT";s:7:"Default";s:0:"";s:4:"Mode";s:0:"";s:11:"Description";s:208:"One-time seed only (see PLEX_URL above). Only needed if Plex's own container sees this library at a different internal path than Library Root above (the same category of issue as the Downloads Share mapping).";s:4:"Type";s:8:"Variable";s:7:"Display";s:8:"advanced";s:8:"Required";s:5:"false";s:4:"Mask";s:5:"false";}s:5:"value";s:0:"";}i:27;a:2:{s:11:"@attributes";a:9:{s:4:"Name";s:13:"HOTFOLDER_DIR";s:6:"Target";s:13:"HOTFOLDER_DIR";s:7:"Default";s:0:"";s:4:"Mode";s:0:"";s:11:"Description";s:272:"One-time seed only: used to create Settings File above if it doesn't exist yet, then ignored - edit hot-folder settings live afterward via the web UI. Set to /downloads/domestique to enable hot-folder ingestion (matches the read-write mount above). Leave unset to disable.";s:4:"Type";s:8:"Variable";s:7:"Display";s:6:"always";s:8:"Required";s:5:"false";s:4:"Mask";s:5:"false";}s:5:"value";s:0:"";}i:28;a:2:{s:11:"@attributes";a:9:{s:4:"Name";s:26:"HOTFOLDER_POLL_INTERVAL_MS";s:6:"Target";s:26:"HOTFOLDER_POLL_INTERVAL_MS";s:7:"Default";s:5:"60000";s:4:"Mode";s:0:"";s:11:"Description";s:142:"One-time seed only (see HOTFOLDER_DIR above). Tuning: how often (ms) to check a hot-folder drop for size/mtime stability before processing it.";s:4:"Type";s:8:"Variable";s:7:"Display";s:8:"advanced";s:8:"Required";s:5:"false";s:4:"Mask";s:5:"false";}s:5:"value";s:0:"";}i:29;a:2:{s:11:"@attributes";a:9:{s:4:"Name";s:22:"HOTFOLDER_STABLE_POLLS";s:6:"Target";s:22:"HOTFOLDER_STABLE_POLLS";s:7:"Default";s:1:"3";s:4:"Mode";s:0:"";s:11:"Description";s:132:"One-time seed only (see HOTFOLDER_DIR above). Tuning: consecutive stable polls required before a hot-folder drop is treated as done.";s:4:"Type";s:8:"Variable";s:7:"Display";s:8:"advanced";s:8:"Required";s:5:"false";s:4:"Mask";s:5:"false";}s:5:"value";s:0:"";}i:30;a:2:{s:11:"@attributes";a:9:{s:4:"Name";s:19:"DISCORD_WEBHOOK_URL";s:6:"Target";s:19:"DISCORD_WEBHOOK_URL";s:7:"Default";s:0:"";s:4:"Mode";s:0:"";s:11:"Description";s:294:"One-time seed only: used to create Settings File above if it doesn't exist yet, then ignored - edit Discord settings live afterward via the web UI. Posts a summary message to a Discord channel after every torrent-done event. Create one via the target channel's Settings, Integrations, Webhooks.";s:4:"Type";s:8:"Variable";s:7:"Display";s:6:"always";s:8:"Required";s:5:"false";s:4:"Mask";s:4:"true";}s:5:"value";s:0:"";}i:31;a:2:{s:11:"@attributes";a:9:{s:4:"Name";s:23:"DISCORD_MENTION_USER_ID";s:6:"Target";s:23:"DISCORD_MENTION_USER_ID";s:7:"Default";s:0:"";s:4:"Mode";s:0:"";s:11:"Description";s:225:"One-time seed only (see DISCORD_WEBHOOK_URL above). A Discord user id to @mention, but only on review-worthy notifications (auto-created shows, warnings, errors). Leave unset to have every notification post without a mention.";s:4:"Type";s:8:"Variable";s:7:"Display";s:8:"advanced";s:8:"Required";s:5:"false";s:4:"Mask";s:5:"false";}s:5:"value";s:0:"";}i:32;a:2:{s:11:"@attributes";a:9:{s:4:"Name";s:14:"WEBUI_PASSWORD";s:6:"Target";s:14:"WEBUI_PASSWORD";s:7:"Default";s:0:"";s:4:"Mode";s:0:"";s:11:"Description";s:223:"Set this to enable the web UI at /ui (events editor, match tester, upload, activity log). Fails CLOSED, not open: leaving this unset keeps /ui and /api/* returning 503, since that surface can read and overwrite your config.";s:4:"Type";s:8:"Variable";s:7:"Display";s:6:"always";s:8:"Required";s:5:"false";s:4:"Mask";s:4:"true";}s:5:"value";s:0:"";}i:33;a:2:{s:11:"@attributes";a:9:{s:4:"Name";s:10:"WEBUI_USER";s:6:"Target";s:10:"WEBUI_USER";s:7:"Default";s:0:"";s:4:"Mode";s:0:"";s:11:"Description";s:150:"Optional: also require this exact username (HTTP Basic Auth) alongside WEBUI_PASSWORD. Leave unset to accept any username, checking only the password.";s:4:"Type";s:8:"Variable";s:7:"Display";s:8:"advanced";s:8:"Required";s:5:"false";s:4:"Mask";s:5:"false";}s:5:"value";s:0:"";}i:34;a:2:{s:11:"@attributes";a:9:{s:4:"Name";s:4:"PUID";s:6:"Target";s:4:"PUID";s:7:"Default";s:2:"99";s:4:"Mode";s:0:"";s:11:"Description";s:412:"Run the app as this user id instead of root (99 = Unraid's 'nobody', the same user most containers including Transmission run as). The container fixes ownership of its two config files automatically; the Library Root (and hot-folder, if used) must be writable by this user - on a default Unraid share that's already true, otherwise run once from the terminal: chown -R 99:100 on those paths. Blank = run as root.";s:4:"Type";s:8:"Variable";s:7:"Display";s:6:"always";s:8:"Requir