raph tag cache. Prefer using the policy file to configure the Open Graph subsystem.";s:4:"Type";s:8:"Variable";s:7:"Display";s:6:"always";s:8:"Required";s:4:"true";s:4:"Mask";s:5:"false";}s:5:"value";s:3:"24h";}i:18;a:2:{s:11:"@attributes";a:8:{s:4:"Name";s:24:"Open Graph - Passthrough";s:6:"Target";s:14:"OG_PASSTHROUGH";s:7:"Default";s:10:"false|true";s:11:"Description";s:130:"If set to true, Anubis will enable Open Graph tag passthrough. Prefer using the policy file to configure the Open Graph subsystem.";s:4:"Type";s:8:"Variable";s:7:"Display";s:6:"always";s:8:"Required";s:4:"true";s:4:"Mask";s:5:"false";}s:5:"value";s:0:"";}i:19;a:2:{s:11:"@attributes";a:8:{s:4:"Name";s:32:"Open Graph - Consider Host Cache";s:6:"Target";s:22:"OG_CACHE_CONSIDER_HOST";s:7:"Default";s:10:"false|true";s:11:"Description";s:146:"If set to true, Anubis will consider the host in the Open Graph tag cache key. Prefer using the policy file to configure the Open Graph subsystem.";s:4:"Type";s:8:"Variable";s:7:"Display";s:6:"always";s:8:"Required";s:4:"true";s:4:"Mask";s:5:"false";}s:5:"value";s:0:"";}i:20;a:2:{s:11:"@attributes";a:8:{s:4:"Name";s:16:"Policy File Name";s:6:"Target";s:12:"POLICY_FNAME";s:7:"Default";s:0:"";s:11:"Description";s:166:"The internal file name containing bot policy configuration. See the bot policy documentation for more details. If unset, the default bot policy configuration is used.";s:4:"Type";s:8:"Variable";s:7:"Display";s:6:"always";s:8:"Required";s:5:"false";s:4:"Mask";s:5:"false";}s:5:"value";s:0:"";}i:21;a:2:{s:11:"@attributes";a:8:{s:4:"Name";s:16:"Redirect Domains";s:6:"Target";s:16:"REDIRECT_DOMAINS";s:7:"Default";s:0:"";s:11:"Description";s:391:"If set, restrict the domains that Anubis can redirect to when passing a challenge. If unset, Anubis may redirect to any domain which could cause security issues in the unlikely case that an attacker passes a challenge for your browser and then tricks you into clicking a link to your domain. Note, if you are host