ent";N;}i:3979;a:35:{s:4:"Name";s:10:"PrintGuard";s:10:"Repository";s:39:"ghcr.io/oliverbravery/printguard:latest";s:8:"Registry";s:69:"https://github.com/oliverbravery/PrintGuard/pkgs/container/printguard";s:7:"Network";s:6:"bridge";s:5:"Shell";s:2:"sh";s:10:"Privileged";s:5:"false";s:7:"Support";s:50:"https://github.com/oliverbravery/PrintGuard/issues";s:7:"Project";s:43:"https://github.com/oliverbravery/PrintGuard";s:8:"Overview";s:954:"PrintGuard watches your 3D-printer cameras with an on-device vision model, pauses or cancels the print the moment it starts to fail, and sends a snapshot to your phone over ntfy, Pushover, Telegram or Discord. No cloud and no account, and camera frames stay on your server unless you choose to send some to help train the model. Works with OctoPrint, Klipper (Moonraker), Elegoo, PrusaLink and Bambu Lab, and publishes every monitor to Home Assistant over MQTT.

Everything is in this one image, the streaming server included, so there is no second container to install. Open the WebUI, add a camera and printer, then create a monitor that binds them.

