s:8:"Overview";s:1866:"An iCUE-style dashboard and fan control for Corsair HXi and RMi digital power supplies.

Corsair's iCUE software is Windows-only, so a Corsair digital PSU in an Unraid server normally means no monitoring and no fan control at all. This adds both, in its own tab.

MONITORING - live per-rail voltage, current and power for +12V, +5V and +3.3V; total power out, estimated power in, efficiency and load; VRM and case temperatures; fan RPM. Every reading carries a running min/max and a live sparkline. Sensors are read from the kernel corsair-psu hwmon driver, so polling costs no USB traffic and cannot collide with other software.

FAN CONTROL - hand the fan to the PSU firmware (zero-RPM idle), hold a fixed duty, or build a custom curve with a drag-and-drop editor mapping VRM temperature to fan duty. Presets for Quiet, Balanced, Performance and Max.

+12V OCP - switch between single-rail and multi-rail overcurrent protection. Single rail uses one combined threshold for the whole +12V output, which means fewer nuisance trips when several drives spin up at once.

The PSU model is detected automatically. Supported: HX750i, HX850i, HX1000i, HX1000i (2022), HX1200i, HX1200i ATX 3.1, HX1500i, RM650i, RM750i, RM850i, RM1000i. An unrecognised Corsair digital PSU still reports every sensor the kernel exposes and keeps fan control; only efficiency and load percentage are hidden, since those need model-specific data.

Self-contained - bundles every Python module it needs, so there is nothing to install by hand and no internet access required at boot.

Note: these PSUs cannot store a fan curve in firmware, so custom curves are driven from Unraid by a small background service, exactly as iCUE does on Windows. Minimum fan duty is 30%.

Tested on real hardware with an HX1000i. The other models share the same detection path but are untested - reports welcome.";s:9:"PluginURL";s:88:"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/racoutlaw/corsair-psu-center/main/corsairpsucenter.plg";s:12:"PluginAuthor";s:9:"racoutlaw";s:7:"Project";s:47:"https://github.com/racoutlaw/corsair-psu-center";s:6:"ReadMe";s:77:"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/racoutlaw/corsair-psu-center/main/README.md";s:6:"IconFA";s:4:"bolt";s:7:"License";s:5:"GPLv2";s:10:"Screenshot";s:87:"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/racoutlaw/corsair-psu-center/main/docs/screenshot.png";s:11:"TemplateURL";s:98:"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/racoutlaw/corsair-psu-center/main/plugins/corsair-psu-center.xml";s:12:"TemplatePath";s:50:"/tmp/GitHub/AppFeed/plugins/corsair-psu-center.xml";s:4:"Repo";s:22:"RacOutlaw's Repository";s:10:"Repository";s:88:"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/racoutlaw/corsair-psu-center/main/corsairpsucenter.plg";s:12:"CategoryList";a:2:{i:0;s:12:"Tools-System";i:1;s:7:"Plugins";}s:6:"Plugin";b:1;s:7:"Support";s:126:"https://forums.unraid.net/topic/200056-plugin-corsair-psu-center-icue-style-dashboard-and-fan-control-for-corsair-hxirmi-psus/";s:13:"pluginVersion";s:10:"2026.09.26";s:6:"MinVer";s:6:"6.12.0";s:6:"Author";s:9:"racoutlaw";s:4:"Icon";s:0:"";s:16:"ChangeLogPresent";s:1:"1";s:9:"downloads";i:279;s:9:"FirstSeen";i:1785341103;s:14:"LastUpdateScan";i:1792411842;s:11:"pluginStats";a:13:{i:10;i:22;i:11;i:0;i:12;i:0;s:2:"01";i:0;s:2:"02";i:0;s:2:"03";i:0;s:2:"04";i:0;s:2:"05";i:0;s:2:"06";i:0;s:2:"07";i:43;s:2:"08";i:174;s:2:"09";i:40;s:1:"T";i:279;}s:8:"Category";s:21:"Tools:System Plugins:";s:2:"ID";i:4270;s:11:"Displayable";b:1;s:13:"DockerHubName";s:18:"corsair psu center";s:8:"RepoName";s:22:"RacOutlaw's Repository";s:10:"SortAuthor";s:9:"racoutlaw";s:8:"SortName";s:18:"Corsair PSU Center";s:6:"random";i:1308235816;s:9:"Blacklist";b:0;s:4:"Path";s:197:"/tmp/community.applications/tempFiles/templates-community-apps/RacOutlaw