Category";s:8:"AI:Tools";s:2:"ID";i:4279;s:11:"Displayable";b:1;s:6:"Author";s:13:"realitymolder";s:13:"DockerHubName";s:8:"odysseus";s:8:"RepoName";s:26:"RealityMolder's Repository";s:10:"SortAuthor";s:13:"realitymolder";s:8:"SortName";s:8:"Odysseus";s:6:"random";i:1810974579;s:9:"Blacklist";b:0;s:6:"MinVer";s:3:"6.0";s:4:"Path";s:121:"/tmp/community.applications/tempFiles/templates-community-apps/RealityMoldersRepository/realitymolder-Odysseus-stable.xml";s:4:"Date";N;s:11:"BrandNewApp";b:1;s:10:"Deprecated";b:0;s:10:"trendDelta";d:-35.638;s:12:"trendAverage";d:42.598;s:10:"Compatible";b:1;s:16:"ModeratorComment";N;}i:4280;a:34:{s:4:"Name";s:13:"redkite-agent";s:10:"Repository";s:42:"ghcr.io/redkite-info/redkite-unraid:latest";s:8:"Registry";s:75:"https://github.com/redkite-info/redkite-agent/pkgs/container/redkite-unraid";s:7:"Network";s:6:"bridge";s:5:"Shell";s:4:"bash";s:10:"Privileged";s:5:"false";s:7:"Support";s:21:"https://redkite.info/";s:7:"Project";s:20:"https://redkite.info";s:11:"TemplateURL";s:88:"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/redkite-info/redkite-unraid-templates/main/redkite.xml";s:8:"Overview";s:1275:"Red Kite watches this server by listening for it. The agent says "I am still here" to a hub
    outside the building every few minutes, and 
**the alarm is the absence of that
    message, not the presence of one** — so a server that loses power, loses its line, or is simply
    switched off is noticed either way. Nothing is opened on your firewall, because nothing ever
    connects inwards.


    It also reports what is quietly going wrong: parity sync errors, a disabled disk being emulated
    from parity, SMART attributes that are climbing, filesystems remounted read-only, memory errors
    the machine is correcting and not mentioning.


    Sleeping disks are left alone. Every SMART read uses -n standby, and temperatures come from
    Unraid's own cached figures, so a spun-down array stays spun down.


    **You need a hub before this will do anything.** Red Kite is self-hosted: you run the hub
    yourself, there is no account with us, and we monitor nothing for anybody. Start at
    redkite.info. Free while it is in open beta.


    **If something is wrong, set the Console to bash and run:** redkite-Unraid --diagnose

    That prints everything it can and cannot see. It is safe to paste anywhere: the token is
