    Point it at PhotoPrism, Immich, or both, add the frames you own, and it uploads the photos that match your rules on a schedule — at the right size and shape for each screen — and takes them back off when they no longer qualify. It remembers what it has already sent, so nothing is uploaded twice. Portrait and landscape frames each get what suits them.

    Nothing needs configuring before the first start. Open the console on port 8770, sign in with the one-time password printed in the container log, and set everything up there.

    Join the iPhone and iPad public beta at https://testflight.apple.com/join/HZ7kN8k9 (iOS/iPadOS 18+, HTTPS access to your Framewrk server).

    Send directly from the Framewrk iOS app or Photos Share Sheet without a photo library. Direct photos are independent of library rules, with delivery history and revocable device tokens.

    All state is one SQLite file under /data, so a backup is one file.

    Immich 3.1 or newer is supported; configure its URL and an API key in the console. Its optional star rating is used by the shared Quality rule. Requires an Aura and/or Nixplay account. Library sync also requires a reachable PhotoPrism and/or Immich server. Free to use; not open source. Not affiliated with Aura, Nixplay, PhotoPrism or Immich.";s:16:"ExtraSearchTerms";s:86:"photoprism immich aura nixplay photo frame digital picture frame sync ios share upload";s:8:"Requires";s:84:"An Aura and/or Nixplay account. PhotoPrism or Immich is optional for direct uploads.";s:4:"Date";s:10:"2026-10-14";s:6:"MinVer";s:4:"6.12";s:7:"License";s:24:"LicenseRef-Framewrk-EULA";s:6:"Config";a:5:{i:0;a:2:{s:11:"@attributes";a:9:{s:4:"Name";s:5:"WebUI";s:6:"Target";s:4:"8770";s:7:"Default";s:4:"8770";s:4:"Mode";s:3:"tcp";s:11:"Description";s:77:"Port for the Framewrk console. Change the host side if 8770 is already taken.";s:4:"Type";s:4:"Port";s:7:"Display";s:6:"always";s:8:"Required";s:4:"true";s:4:"Mask";s:5:"false";}s:5:"value";s:4:"8770";}i:1;a:2:{s:11:"@attributes";a:9:{s:4:"Name";s:4:"Data";s:6:"Target";s:5:"/data";s:7:"Default";s:26:"/mnt/user/appdata/framewrk";s:4:"Mode";s:2:"rw";s:11:"Description";s:135:"Holds sync.db — the settings, the frame list and the sync history. Back this folder up and you have backed up the whole installation.";s:4:"Type";s:4:"Path";s:7:"Display";s:6:"always";s:8:"Required";s:4:"true";s:4:"Mask";s:5:"false";}s:5:"value";s:26:"/mnt/user/appdata/framewrk";}i:2;a:2:{s:11:"@attributes";a:9:{s:4:"Name";s:2:"TZ";s:6:"Target";s:2:"TZ";s:7:"Default";s:13:"Europe/London";s:4:"Mode";s:0:"";s:11:"Description";s:128:"Your timezone as a tz database name, for example America/New_York. Without it every timestamp in the log and the console is UTC.";s:4:"Type";s:8:"Variable";s:7:"Display";s:6:"always";s:8:"Required";s:5:"false";s:4:"Mask";s:5:"false";}s:5:"value";s:13:"Europe/London";}i:3;a:2:{s:11:"@attributes";a:9:{s:4:"Name";s:4:"PUID";s:6:"Target";s:4:"PUID";s:7:"Default";s:2:"99";s:4:"Mode";s:0:"";s:11:"Description";s:103:"User the container writes as. 99 is Unraid's nobody. Leave it alone unless you know you need otherwise.";s:4:"Type";s:8:"Variable";s:7:"Display";s:8:"advanced";s:8:"Required";s:5:"false";s:4:"Mask";s:5:"false";}s:5:"value";s:2:"99";}i:4;a:2:{s:11:"@attributes";a:9:{s:4:"Name";s:4:"PGID";s:6:"Target";s:4:"PGID";s:7:"Default";s:3:"100";s:4:"Mode";s:0:"";s:11:"Description";s:59:"Group the container writes as. 100 is Unraid's users group.";s:4:"Type";s:8:"Variable";s:7:"Display";s:8:"advanced";s:8:"Required";s:5:"false";s:4:"Mask";s:5:"false";}s:5:"value";s:3:"100";}}s:12:"TemplatePath";s:42:"/tmp/GitHub/AppFeed/templates/framewrk.xml";s:4:"Repo";s:24:"smichalczyk's Repository";s:12:"CategoryList";a:2:{i:0;s:15:"MediaApp-Photos";i:1;s:15:"Tools-Utilities";}s:16:"ChangeLogPresent";s:1:"1";s:9:"downloads";i:1195;s:9:"FirstSeen";i:1785928030;s:10:"LastUpdate";i:1790574870;s:14:"LastUpdateScan";i:1791198847;s:8:"Category";s:31:"MediaApp:Photos Tools:Utilities";s:2:"ID";i:4577;s:11:"Displayable";b:1;s:6:"Author";s:11:"smichalczyk";s:13:"DockerHubName";s:8:"framewrk";s:8:"RepoName";s:24:"smichalczyk's Repository";s:10:"SortAuthor";s:11:"smichalczyk";s:8:"SortName";s:8:"framewrk";s:6:"random";i:588411100;s:9:"Blacklist";b:0;s:4:"Path";s:117:"/tmp/community.applications/tempFiles/templates-community-apps/smichalczyksRepository/smichalczyk-framewrk-latest.xml";s:10:"Deprecated";b:0;s:10:"Compatible";b:1;s:16:"ModeratorComment";N;}i:4578;a:35:{s:4:"Name";s:6:"gantry";s:10:"Repository";s:29:"ghcr.io/smidley/gantry:latest";s:8:"Registry";s:55:"https://github.com/smidley/gantry/pkgs/container/gantry";s:7:"Network";s:6:"bridge";s:5:"Shell";s:2:"sh";s:10:"Privileged";s:5:"false";s:7:"Support";s:40:"https://github.com/smidley/gantry/issues";s:7:"Project";s:33:"https://github.com/smidley/gantry";s:8:"Overview";s:1873:"Gantry is a Docker and server monitor built for Unraid. One container -- install it, open the web UI, and set a username and password the first time to secure the dashboard (or preseed them with the variables below for a hands-off install).

Every mount below is pre-filled so a stock install needs no edits. All of them are read-only except two: the notifications mount (so Gantry can hand alerts to Unraid's own notification center) and the config mount (Gantry's own small SQLite database). Monitoring is entirely read-only -- Gantry never writes to /sys and never touches your array configuration. The one exception is deliberate: the Maintenance view lets you remove dangling images and stopped containers, each behind a confirmation, never force-removing and never touching a running container or a volume. Set GANTRY_READ_ONLY=1 below to disable that too and keep the container strictly read-only.

The Extra Parameters are already set for you; there's nothing to add. --pid=host lets Gantry attribute GPU and resource usage to the right container instead of host-only totals, and --cap-add=SYS_PTRACE lets it read other containers' /proc/pid/fdinfo. Gantry runs as an ordinary container (Docker's default capabilities plus SYS_PTRACE); it does not run --privileged and does not use host networking.

Optional, host-level: Unraid ships PSI (Pressure Stall Information) compiled in but disabled. Adding psi=1 to your flash boot device's syslinux append line and rebooting lets Gantry record fuller CPU/memory/IO stall metrics. Nothing to configure on the container itself -- see the PSI note below and docs/psi.md in the repo.

Optional, GPU: if you pass --runtime=nvidia (add it to Extra Parameters) and set NVIDIA_VISIBLE_DEVICES below, Gantry shows per-container GPU utilization. Without it, the GPU panel just shows a plain "not available" hint -- never an error.";s:5:"WebUI";s:24:"http://[IP]:[PORT:8380]/";s:11:"TemplateURL";s:74:"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/smidley/gantry/main/templates/gantry.xml";s:4:"Icon";s:78:"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/smidley/gantry/main/template/gantry-icon.png";s:11:"ExtraParams";s:31:"--pid=host --cap-add=SYS_PTRACE";s:6:"Config";a:12:{i:0;a:2:{s:11:"@attributes";a:9:{s:4:"Name";s:10:"WebUI Port";s:6:"Target";s:4:"8380";s:7:"Default";s:4:"8380";s:4:"Mode";s:3:"tcp";s:11:"Description";s:80:"The Gantry web UI. After the container starts, open http://your-unraid-ip:8380/.";s:4:"Type";s:4:"Port";s:7:"Display";s:6:"always";s:8:"Required";s:4:"true";s:4:"Mask";s:5:"false";}s:5:"value";s:4:"8380";}i:1;a:2:{s:11:"@attributes";a:9:{s:4:"Name";s:13:"Docker Socket";s:6:"Target";s:20:"/var/run/docker.sock";s:7:"Default";s:20:"/var/run/docker.sock";s:4:"Mode";s:2:"ro";s:11:"Description";s:318:"Mounted read-only. Lets Gantry list containers and read their stats, health, logs, and start/stop/health events. The socket is also how the Maintenance view removes dangling images and stopped containers when you explicitly ask it to (confirmable, and disabled by GANTRY_READ_ONLY); nothing else is written through it.";s:4:"Type";s:4:"Path";s:7:"Display";s:6:"always";s:8:"Required";s:4:"true";s:4:"Mask";s:5:"false";}s:5:"value";s:20:"/var/run/docker.sock";}i:2;a:2:{s:11:"@attributes";a:9:{s:4:"Name";s:10:"Host Sysfs";s:6:"Target";s:9:"/host/sys";s:7:"Default";s:4:"/sys";s:4:"Mode";s:2:"ro";s:11:"Description";s:183:"Read-only. Gives Gantry hwmon sensor readings (fan speed, voltages, temperatures), GPU/DRM info, and the cgroup v2 fast path for per-container accounting. Gantry never writes to /sys.";s:4:"Type";s:4:"Path";s:7:"Display";s:6:"always";s:8:"Required";s:4:"true";s:4:"Mask";s:5:"false";}s:5:"value";s:4:"/sys";}i:3;a:2:{s:11:"@attributes";a:9:{s:4:"Name";s:12:"Unraid State";s:6:"Target";s:7:"/unraid";s:7:"Default";s:17:"/var/local/emhttp";s:4:"Mode";s:2:"ro";s:11:"Description";s:215:"Read-only. The same emhttp state files the Unraid webGUI itself reads -- array status, parity check progress, disk and pool assignments, and shares. Gantry never modifies your array configuration through this mount.";s:4:"Type";s:4:"Path";s:7:"Display";s:6:"always";s:8:"Required";s:4:"true";s:4:"Mask";s:5:"false";}s:5:"value";s:17:"/var/local/emhttp";}i:4;a:2:{s:11:"@attributes";a:9:{s:4:"Name";s:13:"Notifications";s:6:"Target";s:7:"/notify";s:7:"Default";s:18:"/tmp/notifications";s:4:"Mode";s:2:"rw";s:11:"Description";s:414:"Read-write -- the only other read-write mount besides Config below. Gantry drops alert notifications here so they show up in Unraid's own notification center (and anywhere you already route Unraid notifications: email, Pushover, Discord, etc). If this mount is missing or unwritable, Gantry keeps running; it just can't deliver Unraid-native alerts, and the Alerts view says so plainly instead of failing silently.";s:4:"Type";s:4:"Path";s:7:"Display";s:6:"always";s:8:"Required";s:4:"true";s:4:"Mask";s:5:"false";}s:5:"value";s:18:"/tmp/notifications";}i:5;a:2:{s:11:"@attributes";a:9:{s:4:"Name";s:13:"Update Status";s:6:"Target";s:34:"/updates/unraid-update-status.json";s:7:"Default";s:41:"/var/lib/docker/unraid-update-status.json";s:4:"Mode";s:2:"ro";s:11:"Description";s:288:"Read-only and optional. Unraid's own record of which containers have an update available. If this file doesn't exist on your system, or you remove this mount, Gantry simply won't show update-available flags -- nothing else is affected. Safe to delete if Docker Manager complains about it.";s:4:"Type";s:4:"Path";s:7:"Display";s:6:"always";s:8:"Required";s:5:"false";s:4:"Mask";s:5:"false";}s:5:"value";s:41:"/var/lib/docker/unraid-update-status.json";}i:6;a:2:{s:11:"@attributes";a:9:{s:4:"Name";s:6:"Config";s:6:"Target";s:7:"/config";s:7:"Default";s:24:"/mnt/user/appdata/gantry";s:4:"Mode";s:2:"rw";s:11:"Description";s:187:"Read-write. Gantry's own SQLite database and settings -- the only place it stores anything persistent. This is the second of the two read-write mounts; everything else above is read-only.";s:4:"Type";s:4:"Path";s:7:"Display";s:6:"always";s:8:"Required";s:4:"true";s:4:"Mask";s:5:"false";}s:5:"value";s:24:"/mnt/user/appdata/gantry";}i:7;a:2:{s:11:"@attributes";a:9:{s:4:"Name";s:22:"NVIDIA_VISIBLE_DEVICES";s:6:"Target";s:22:"NVIDIA_VISIBLE_DEVICES";s:7:"Default";s:0:"";s:4:"Mode";s:0:"";s:11:"Description";s:299:"Optional, only if you have an Nvidia GPU passed through with the Nvidia Driver plugin. Set to all, and also add --runtime=nvidia to Extra Parameters above, to enable per-container GPU utilization. Leave both blank/absent for a CPU-only box -- the GPU panel shows a plain enable hint, never an error.";s:4:"Type";s:8:"Variable";s:7:"Display";s:8:"advanced";s:8:"Required";s:5:"false";s:4:"Mask";s:5:"false";}s:5:"value";s:0:"";}i:8;a:2:{s:11:"@attributes";a:9:{s:4:"Name";s:15:"GANTRY_USERNAME";s:6:"Target";s:15:"GANTRY_USERNAME";s:7:"Default";s:0:"";s:4:"Mode";s:0:"";s:11:"Description";s:485:"Optional, for a hands-off install. Set this together with GANTRY_PASSWORD below to create the login automatically at first boot and skip the one-time setup screen. Leave both blank to choose the username and password yourself the first time you open the web UI. Both must be set together; only one is ignored (Gantry falls back to the setup screen). Changing it later changes the username and signs out all sessions. This is the login username, not a secret -- it is stored as entered.";s:4:"Type";s:8:"Variable";s:7:"Display";s:6:"always";s:8:"Required";s:5:"false";s:4:"Mask";s:5:"false";}s:5:"value";s:0:"";}i:9;a:2:{s:11:"@attributes";a:9:{s:4:"Name";s:15:"GANTRY_PASSWORD";s:6:"Target";s:15:"GANTRY_PASSWORD";s:7:"Default";s:0:"";s:4:"Mode";s:0:"";s:11:"Description";s:549:"Optional, for a hands-off install. Set this together with GANTRY_USERNAME above (at least 8 characters) to create the login at first boot and skip the setup screen. Applied at every container start: changing it here changes the password and signs out all sessions. IMPORTANT: removing this variable later does NOT turn authentication off -- Gantry keeps the stored login so a template edit can never reopen the dashboard. You can change the login any time in Settings &gt; Access. Only the derived argon2id hash is stored, never the password itself.";s:4:"Type";s:8:"Variable";s:7:"Display";s:6:"always";s:8:"Required";s:5:"false";s:4:"Mask";s:4:"true";}s:5:"value";s:0:"";}i:10;a:2:{s:11:"@attributes";a:9:{s:4:"Name";s:11:"GANTRY_AUTH";s:6:"Target";s:11:"GANTRY_AUTH";s:7:"Default";s:0:"";s:4:"Mode";s:0:"";s:11:"Description";s:478:"Optional. Leave blank (or set to auto) for the normal behavior: Gantry requires a login, set on first run or preseeded via GANTRY_USERNAME/GANTRY_PASSWORD above. Set to none to turn authentication OFF entirely -- only for a fully trusted network. Set to proxy if a reverse proxy (authelia, SWAG, nginx auth_request...) already authenticates every request in front of Gantry, which switches Gantry's own login off. Any other value is ignored and treated as auto (login required).";s:4:"Type";s:8:"Variable";s:7:"Display";s:8:"advanced";s:8:"Required";s:5:"false";s:4:"Mask";s:5:"false";}s:5:"value";s:0:"";}i:11;a:2:{s:11:"@attributes";a:9:{s:4:"Name";s:16:"GANTRY_READ_ONLY";s:6:"Target";s:16:"GANTRY_READ_ONLY";s:7:"Default";s:0:"";s:4:"Mode";s:0:"";s:11:"Description";s:335:"Off by default. Set to 1 to make Gantry's write-capable paths (docker mutations, webhook-target configuration) refuse to run -- a kill switch for anyone who wants a strictly read-only monitor. Independent of authentication: read-only limits what a logged-in user can do, the login limits who gets in at all. Leave blank for normal use.";s:4:"Type";s:8:"Variable";s:7:"Display";s:8:"advanced";s:8:"Required";s:5:"false";s:4:"Mask";s:5:"false";}s:5:"value";s:0:"";}}s:12:"TemplatePath";s:40:"/tmp/GitHub/AppFeed/templates/gantry.xml";s:4:"Repo";s:20:"smidley's Repository";s:12:"CategoryList";a:2:{i:0;s:15:"Tools-Utilities";i:1;s:18:"Network-Management";}s:9:"FirstSeen";i:1788240024;s:8:"Category";s:34:"Tools:Utilities Network:Management";s:2:"ID";i:4578;s:11:"Displayable";b:1;s:6:"Author";s:7:"smidley";s:13:"DockerHubName";s:6:"gantry";s:8:"RepoName";s:20:"smidley's Repository";s:10:"SortAuthor";s:7:"smidley";s:8:"SortName";s:6:"gantry";s:6:"random";i:503739287;s:9:"Blacklist";b:0;s:6:"MinVer";s:3:"6.0";s:4:"Path";s:107:"/tmp/community.applications/tempFiles/templates-community-apps/smidleysRepository/smidley-gantry-latest.xml";s:4:"Date";N;s:11:"BrandNewApp";b:1;s:10:"Deprecated";b:0;s:10:"Compatible";b:1;s:16:"ModeratorComment";N;}i:4579;a:38:{s:4:"Name";s:11:"Storyteller";s:10:"Repository";s:59:"registry.gitlab.com/storyteller-platform/storyteller:latest";s:8:"Registry";s:62:"https://gitlab.com/storyteller-platform/storyteller/-/releases";s:7:"Network";s:6:"bridge";s:5:"Shell";s:2:"sh";s:10:"Privileged";s:5:"false";s:7:"Support";s:0:"";s:7:"Project";s:33:"https://storyteller-platform.dev/";s:8:"Overview";s:1477:"Storyteller is a self-hosted platform for creating and reading ebooks with guided narration. It's made up of two components: the alignment server, and the mobile apps. Together, these components allow you to take audiobooks and ebooks that you already own and automatically align them, as well as read or listen to (or both!) the resulting aligned books.

Align your audiobooks and ebooks
---------------------------------------
Switch back and forth between listening and reading without losing your place, or have Storyteller read aloud to you while highlighting the text!

Read or listen however you choose
--------------------------------------
Storyteller produces EPUB 3 compliant ebook files. You can read them with any ebook reader (software or hardware!) that supports EPUB Media Overlays, or you can use the dedicated Storyteller mobile apps.

Own your books
------------------
Storyteller is completely self-hosted. All of your books stay on your hardware, and you're free to move, copy, and back them up as needed.

### AMD HW ACCELERATED TRANSCRIPTION:
To enable support for HW Accelerated transcription, add the "--device='/dev/dri'" parameter added to "Extra Parameters:"

### NVIDIA GPU:
To enable NVIDIA GPU support, ensure that you have installed the Nvidia-Driver plugin and add the "--runtime='nvidia'" parameter added to "Extra Parameters:"

### AMD GPU:
To enable AMD GPU support, ensure that you have installed the Radeon-TOP plugin.";s:5:"WebUI";s:24:"http://[IP]:[PORT:8001]/";s:11:"TemplateURL";s:85:"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/smoores-dev/storyteller-unraid/main/Storyteller.xml";s:4:"Icon";s:127:"https://gitlab.com/storyteller-platform/storyteller/-/raw/main/docs/static/img/Storyteller_Logo.png?ref_type=heads&inline=false";s:8:"Requires";s:169:"&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Nvidia-Driver plugin (nVidia Support)<br>&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Radeon-TOP plugin (AMD Support)";s:6:"Config";a:8:{i:0;a:2:{s:11:"@attributes";a:9:{s:4:"Name";s:8:"App Data";s:6:"Target";s:5:"/data";s:7:"Default";s:29:"/mnt/user/appdata/storyteller";s:4:"Mode";s:2:"rw";s:11:"Description";s:75:"Where to store the Storyteller sqlite db file and other configuration files";s:4:"Type";s:4:"Path";s:7:"Display";s:6:"always";s:8:"Required";s:4:"true";s:4:"Mask";s:5:"false";}s:5:"value";s:0:"";}i:1;a:2:{s:11:"@attributes";a:9:{s:4:"Name";s:14:"Data directory";s:6:"Target";s:20:"STORYTELLER_DATA_DIR";s:7:"Default";s:5:"/data";s:4:"Mode";s:0:"";s:11:"Description";s:168:"Where Storyteller should look for the data directory _within_ the container. This should match the Container path for the App Data path -- there's no need to change it.";s:4:"Type";s:8:"Variable";s:7:"Display";s:8:"advanced";s:8:"Required";s:4:"true";s:4:"Mask";s:5:"false";}s:5:"value";s:5:"/data";}i:2;a:2:{s:11:"@attributes";a:9:{s:4:"Name";s:4:"PUID";s:6:"Target";s:4:"PUID";s:7:"Default";s:2:"99";s:4:"Mode";s:0:"";s:11:"Description";s:0:"";s:4:"Type";s:8:"Variable";s:7:"Display";s:8:"advanced";s:8:"Required";s:5:"false";s:4:"Mask";s:5:"false";}s:5:"value";s:2:"99";}i:3;a:2:{s:11:"@attributes";a:9:{s:4:"Name";s:4:"PGID";s:6:"Target";s:4:"PGID";s:7:"Default";s:3:"100";s:4:"Mode";s:0:"";s:11:"Description";s:0:"";s:4:"Type";s:8:"Variable";s:7:"Display";s:8:"advanced";s:8:"Required";s:5:"false";s:4:"Mask";s:5:"false";}s:5:"value";s:3:"100";}i:4;a:2:{s:11:"@attributes";a:9:{s:4:"Name";s:6:"Assets";s:6:"Target";s:12:"/data/assets";s:7:"Default";s:0:"";s:4:"Mode";s:2:"rw";s:11:"Description";s:91:"Where to store the Storyteller media assets (the uploaded and aligned EPUB and audio files)";s:4:"Type";s:4:"Path";s:7:"Display";s:6:"always";s:8:"Required";s:4:"true";s:4:"Mask";s:5:"false";}s:5:"value";s:0:"";}i:5;a:2:{s:11:"@attributes";a:9:{s:4:"Name";s:11:"Auth secret";s:6:"Target";s:22:"STORYTELLER_SECRET_KEY";s:7:"Default";s:0:"";s:4:"Mode";s:0:"";s:11:"Description";s:213:"A cryptographically random secret key, used to encrypt Storyteller's authentication tokens. See the docs here https://storyteller-platform.gitlab.io/storyteller/docs/installation/self-hosting#secrets for guidance.";s:4:"Type";s:8:"Variable";s:7:"Display";s:6:"always";s:8:"Required";s:4:"true";s:4:"Mask";s:4:"true";}s:5:"value";s:0:"";}i:6;a:2:{s:11:"@attributes";a:9:{s:4:"Name";s:15:"Web server port";s:6:"Target";s:4:"8001";s:7:"Default";s:4:"8001";s:4:"Mode";s:3:"tcp";s:11:"Description";s:43:"The port that the web server will listen on";s:4:"Type";s:4:"Port";s:7:"Display";s:6:"always";s:8:"Required";s:4:"true";s:4:"Mask";s:5:"false";}s:5:"value";s:4:"8001";}i:7;a:2:{s:11:"@attributes";a:9:{s:4:"Name";s:30:"Radeon driver version override";s:6:"Target";s:24:"HSA_OVERRIDE_GFX_VERSION";s:7:"Default";s:6:"10.3.0";s:4:"Mode";s:0:"";s:11:"Description";s:253:"If you have an AMD GPU that has a driver version that is unsupported by your Unraid AMD driver, you may be able to work around it by setting this variable to a supported version number. E.g. for an AMD Radeon RX 6700 XT, this value must be set to 10.3.0";s:4:"Type";s:8:"Variable";s:7:"Display";s:8:"advanced";s:8:"Required";s:5:"false";s:4:"Mask";s:5:"false";}s:5:"value";s:0:"";}}s:12:"TemplatePath";s:35:"/tmp/GitHub/AppFeed/Storyteller.xml";s:4:"Repo";s:19:"smoores' Repository";s:12:"CategoryList";a:3:{i:0;s:5:"Other";i:1;s:14:"MediaApp-Books";i:2;s:17:"MediaServer-Books";}s:9:"FirstSeen";i