lammi/Arrmada/blob/main/docs/unraid.md";s:7:"License";s:3:"MIT";s:8:"Overview";s:770:"Arrmada finds, downloads and organises movies, series, books and audiobooks in one app, with requests for your household, subtitles, Convert and Plex or Jellyfin watch insights.

This container includes qBittorrent and FlareSolverr, already connected: there's nothing to set up for them. To use your own instead, switch either off under Show more settings (ARRMADA_BUNDLE_QBITTORRENT, ARRMADA_BUNDLE_FLARESOLVERR) and add yours in Settings, Connections.

Map the share that holds your media and downloads to /storage, so imports hardlink instead of copying. On first start, open the web UI, create the admin account, and follow the setup: your TMDB key, then each library folder and the Downloads folder under /storage. Never put media in /data: that's the database.";s:5:"WebUI";s:24:"http://[IP]:[PORT:7878]/";s:11:"TemplateURL";s:81:"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/tristenlammi/Arrmada/main/templates/arrmada.xml";s:4:"Icon";s:83:"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/tristenlammi/Arrmada/main/web/public/icon-512.png";s:11:"ExtraParams";s:61:"--cap-add=SYS_NICE --restart=unless-stopped --stop-timeout=30";s:8:"Requires";s:182:"One share holding your media and downloads, mapped to /storage. qBittorrent and FlareSolverr are built in; to seed well, forward the torrent port (56881, TCP and UDP) on your router.";s:6:"Config";a:18:{i:0;a:2:{s:11:"@attributes";a:9:{s:4:"Name";s:11:"Web UI port";s:6:"Target";s:4:"7878";s:7:"Default";s:4:"7880";s:4:"Mode";s:3:"tcp";s:11:"Description";s:71:"The web interface. 7880 on the server, because Radarr usually has 7878.";s:4:"Type";s:4:"Port";s:7:"Display";s:6:"always";s:8:"Required";s:4:"true";s:4:"Mask";s:5:"false";}s:5:"value";s:4:"7880";}i:1;a:2:{s:11:"@attributes";a:9:{s:4:"Name";s:18:"Torrent port (TCP)";s:6:"Target";s:5:"56881";s:7:"Default";s:5:"56881";s:4:"Mode";s:3:"tcp";s:11:"Description";s:172:"The built-in qBittorrent's incoming port. Forward it on your router. To change it, use the same new number on both sides here, in the UDP entry and in Torrent port setting.";s:4:"Type";s:4:"Port";s:7:"Display";s:6:"always";s:8:"Required";s:5:"false";s:4:"Mask";s:5:"false";}s:5:"value";s:5:"56881";}i:2;a:2:{s:11:"@attributes";a:9:{s:4:"Name";s:18:"Torrent port (UDP)";s:6:"Target";s:5:"56881";s:7:"Default";s:5:"56881";s:4:"Mode";s:3:"udp";s:11:"Description";s:73:"The same port for UDP (DHT and peers). Keep it the same as the TCP entry.";s:4:"Type";s:4:"Port";s:7:"Display";s:6:"always";s:8:"Req