sercontent.com/unraid/cache_dirs/master/dlandon.cache.dirs.plg.xml";s:10:"Deprecated";b:0;s:10:"Compatible";b:1;s:16:"ModeratorComment";N;}i:4802;a:40:{s:6:"Plugin";b:1;s:9:"PluginURL";s:93:"https://github.com/unraid/ci-runner-farm/releases/download/nightly/ci-runner-farm-nightly.plg";s:12:"PluginAuthor";s:15:"Lime Technology";s:4:"Beta";s:4:"true";s:4:"Name";s:24:"CI Runner Farm - Nightly";s:8:"Requires";s:441:"Nightly software: this listing tracks mainline changes and may regress. Use only on trusted/private CI projects and keep a stable plugin package available for rollback.<br><br>&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;CI Runner Farm can execute arbitrary pipeline code with privileged Docker-in-Docker. Public fork or merge-request code must never run on these runners. Restrict the provider to trusted repositories, groups, runner groups, and protected tags.";s:7:"Support";s:47:"https://github.com/unraid/ci-runner-farm/issues";s:7:"Project";s:40:"https://github.com/unraid/ci-runner-farm";s:4:"Icon";s:102:"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/unraid/ci-runner-farm/main/community-applications/ci-runner-farm.png";s:10:"Screenshot";s:82:"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/unraid/ci-runner-farm/main/docs/images/fleet.png";s:6:"MinVer";s:6:"6.12.0";s:11:"TemplateURL";s:100:"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/unraid/docker-templates/master/limetech/ci-runner-farm-nightly.xml";s:12:"TemplatePath";s:55:"/tmp/GitHub/AppFeed/limetech/ci-runner-farm-nightly.xml";s:4:"Repo";s:33:"Official Unraid Plugin Repository";s:9:"RepoShort";s:6:"Unraid";s:8:"Overview";s:674:"Early access builds of CI Runner Farm, published from the main branch after validation on the self-hosted runner farm.

    This separately named beta entry contains unreleased mainline changes and is intended for CI Runner Farm fleet validation. Use the stable CI Runner Farm entry for production systems. It preserves the same installed runtime and configuration contract, so switching channels replaces the stable fleet rather than creating a second fleet.

    CI Runner Farm provides concurrent, resource-capped GitHub Actions or GitLab CI/CD runner slots as Docker containers, with warm caches, optional autoscaling, and Docker-in-Docker for services and image builds.";s:10:"Repository";s:93:"https://github.com/unraid/ci-runner-farm/releases/download/nightly/ci-runner-farm-nightly.plg";s:12:"CategoryList";a:4:{i:0;s:12:"Tools-System";i:1;s:18:"Network-Management";i:2;s:12:"Productivity";i:3;s:7:"Plugins";}s:13:"pluginVersion";s:36:"2026.10.15.0342.76-1.14.0-nightly.76";s:6:"Author";s:15:"Lime Technology";s:16:"ChangeLogPresent";s:1:"1";s:9:"downloads";i:6;s:9:"FirstSeen";i:1790262938;s:14:"LastUpdateScan";i:1792077780;s:11:"pluginStats";a:13:{i:10;i:2;i:11;i:0;i:12;i:0;s:1:"T";i:6;s:2:"01";i:0;s:2:"02";i:0;s:2:"03";i:0;s:2:"04";i:0;s:2:"05";i:0;s:2:"06";i:0;s:2:"07";i:0;s:2:"08";i:0;s:2:"09";i:4;}s:8:"Category";s:54:"Tools:System Network:Management Productivity: Plugins:";s:2:"ID";i:4802;s:11:"Displayable";b:1;s:13:"DockerHubName";s:24:"ci runner farm - nightly";s:8:"RepoName";s:33:"Official Unraid Plugin Repository";s:10:"SortAuthor";s:15:"Lime Technology";s:8:"SortName";s:22:"CI Runner Farm Nightly";s:6:"random";i:1609644397;s:9:"Blacklist";b:0;s:4:"Path";s:220:"/tmp/community.applications/tempFiles/templates-community-apps/OfficialUnraidPluginRepository/LimeTechnology-CIRunnerFarmNightly-//github.com/unraid/ci-runner-farm/releases/download/nightly/ci-runner-farm-nightly.plg.xml";s:4:"Date";N;s:11:"BrandNewApp";b:1;s:10:"Deprecated";b:0;s:10:"Compatible";b:1;s:16:"ModeratorComment";N;}i:4803;a:38:{s:6:"Plugin";b:1;s:9:"PluginURL";s:84:"https://github.com/unraid/ci-runner-farm/releases/latest/download/ci-runner-farm.plg";s:12:"PluginAuthor";s:15:"Lime Technology";s:4:"Name";s:14:"CI Runner Farm";s:8:"Overview";s:1045:"Turn your Unraid server into a fleet of GitHub Actions self-hosted BUILD runners — multiple concurrent, resource-capped runners running as Docker containers (no VM), with warm shared caches on a fast pool, queue-aware autoscaling, and Docker-in-Docker so jobs that use services: and docker build just work.

Point it at a repo or organization, paste a GitHub token, and your CI runs on your own hardware — as many jobs in parallel as your box can handle, with pnpm/npm/yarn/Playwright caches that stay hot between runs, at zero cost per minute. Everything is configured from a single webGUI page: store your token, Start/Stop/Restart/Scale, watch live status, and build your runner image.

Security: self-hosted runners execute arbitrary workflow code on your hardware, and DinD runners run privileged. Use them only for trusted/private repositories — never let public/fork-PR code run on a privileged self-hosted runner. The plugin actively warns you when a privileged runner is pointed at a public repo. See the README for full guidance.";s:7:"Support";s:47:"https://github.com/unraid/ci-runner-farm/issues";s:7:"Project";s:40:"https://github.com/unraid/ci-runner-farm";s:4:"Icon";s:102:"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/unraid/ci-runner-farm/main/community-applications/ci-runner-farm.png";s:10:"Screenshot";a:4:{i:0;s:93:"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/unraid/ci-runner-farm/main/docs/images/fleet-log-drawer.png";i:1;s:82:"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/unraid/ci-runner-farm/main/docs/images/fleet.png";i:2;s:89:"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/unraid/ci-runner-farm/main/docs/images/runner-image.png";i:3;s:85:"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/unraid/ci-runner-farm/main/docs/images/settings.png";}s:11:"TemplateURL";s:92:"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/unraid/docker-templates/master/limetech/ci-runner-farm.xml";s:12:"TemplatePath";s:47:"/tmp/GitHub/AppFeed/limetech/ci-runner-farm.xml";s:4:"Repo";s:33:"Official Unraid Plugin Repository";s:9:"RepoShort";s:6:"Unraid";s:10:"Repository";s:84:"https://github.com/unraid/ci-runner-farm/releases/latest/download/ci-runner-farm.plg";s:12:"CategoryList";a:4:{i:0;s:12:"Tools-System";i:1;s:18:"Network-Management";i:2;s:12:"Productivity";i:3;s:7:"Plugins";}s:13:"pluginVersion";s:24:"2026.10.15.0342.0-1.14.0";s:6:"MinVer";s:6:"6.12.0";s:6:"Author";s:15:"Lime Technology";s:16:"ChangeLogPresent";s:1:"1";s:9:"downloads";i:248;s:9:"FirstSeen";i:1783526677;s:14:"LastUpdateScan";i:1792383193;s:11:"pluginStats";a:13:{i:10;i:47;i:11;i:0;i:12;i:0;s:2:"01";i:0;s:2:"02";i:0;s:2:"03";i:0;s:2:"04";i:0;s:2:"05";i:0;s:2:"06";i:0;s:2:"07";i:65;s:2:"08";i:91;s:2:"09";i:45;s:1:"T";i:248;}s:8:"Category";s:54:"Tools:System Network:Manag