Overview";s:772:"A Discord bot that requests movies and TV shows through Seerr (the Overseerr/Jellyseerr successor). The first time a user requests something, the bot asks for their Plex username/email and links their Discord account to their Seerr user, so every request is attributed to them and their per-user quotas/limits are respected. The link is stored locally (SQLite) and written back into Seerr notification settings.

Features: /movie and /tv search with availability indicators and season selection; /quota shows remaining limits and reset time; DM notifications when a request becomes available or is declined; and an optional password-protected admin dashboard (set a Dashboard Password to enable it on port 5056) for managing links, viewing activity, and toggling settings.";s:5:"WebUI";s:24:"http://[IP]:[PORT:5056]/";s:11:"TemplateURL";s:95:"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/vancityactivist/vaultrequestrr/main/unraid/vaultrequestrr.xml";s:4:"Icon";s:85:"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/vancityactivist/vaultrequestrr/main/unraid/icon.png";s:6:"Config";a:14:{i:0;a:2:{s:11:"@attributes";a:9:{s:4:"Name";s:14:"Data Directory";s:6:"Target";s:5:"/data";s:7:"Default";s:32:"/mnt/user/appdata/vaultrequestrr";s:4:"Mode";s:2:"rw";s:11:"Description";s:93:"Stores the SQLite database of Discord↔Seerr account links. Keep this on persistent storage.";s:4:"Type";s:4:"Path";s:7:"Display";s:6:"always";s:8:"Required";s:4:"true";s:4:"Mask";s:5:"false";}s:5:"value";s:32:"/mnt/user/appdata/vaultrequestrr";}i:1;a:2:{s:11:"@attributes";a:9:{s:4:"Name";s:17:"Discord Bot Token";s:6:"Target";s:13:"DISCORD_TOKEN";s:7:"Default";s:0:"";s:4:"Mode";s:0:"";s:11:"Description";s:69:"Bot token from https://discord.com/developers/applications (Bot tab).";s:4:"Type";s:8:"Variable";s:7:"Display";s:6:"always";s:8:"Required";s:4:"true";s:4:"Mask";s:4:"true";}s:5:"value";s:0:"";}i:2;a:2:{s:11:"@attributes";a:9:{s:4:"Name";s:9:"Seerr URL";s:6:"Target";s:9:"SEERR_URL";s:7:"Default";s:24:"http://192.168.1.10:5055";s:4:"Mode";s:0:"";s:11:"Description";s:98:"Base URL of your Seerr instance, including port. Use your LAN address, e.g. http://10.10.0.10:5055";s:4:"Type";s:8:"Variable";s:7:"Display";s:6:"always";s:8:"Required";s:4:"true";s:4:"Mask";s:5:"false";}s:5:"value";s:24:"http://192.168.1.10:5055";}i:3;a:2:{s:11:"@attributes";a:9:{s:4:"Name";s:13:"Seerr API Key";s:6:"Target";s:13:"SEERR_API_KEY";s:7:"Default";s:0:"";s:4:"Mode