es an external CDP endpoint; Chrome is not bundled), camoufox, or none.";s:4:"Type";s:8:"Variable";s:7:"Display";s:6:"always";s:8:"Required";s:5:"false";s:4:"Mask";s:5:"false";}s:5:"value";s:4:"auto";}i:3;a:2:{s:11:"@attributes";a:9:{s:4:"Name";s:12:"Memory Limit";s:6:"Target";s:13:"CRW_MEM_LIMIT";s:7:"Default";s:2:"2g";s:4:"Mode";s:0:"";s:11:"Description";s:132:"Cap on crw-server renderer and document-sandbox memory (e.g. 2g). Raise it when running the heavy Chrome tier or larger parse pools.";s:4:"Type";s:8:"Variable";s:7:"Display";s:8:"advanced";s:8:"Required";s:5:"false";s:4:"Mask";s:5:"false";}s:5:"value";s:2:"2g";}i:4;a:2:{s:11:"@attributes";a:9:{s:4:"Name";s:16:"OpenAlex API Key";s:6:"Target";s:28:"CRW_SEARCH__OPENALEX_API_KEY";s:7:"Default";s:0:"";s:4:"Mode";s:0:"";s:11:"Description";s:117:"Optional OpenAlex API key to lift rate limits on the research search engine. Unauthenticated access works without it.";s:4:"Type";s:8:"Variable";s:7:"Display";s:8:"advanced";s:8:"Required";s:5:"false";s:4:"Mask";s:4:"true";}s:5:"value";s:0:"";}i:5;a:2:{s:11:"@attributes";a:9:{s:4:"Name";s:15:"OpenAlex Mailto";s:6:"Target";s:27:"CRW_SEARCH__OPENALEX_MAILTO";s:7:"Default";s:0:"";s:4:"Mode";s:0:"";s:11:"Description";s:125:"Optional contact email (mailto) sent to the OpenAlex polite pool. Helps reliability; unauthenticated access works without it.";s:4:"Type";s:8:"Variable";s:7:"Display";s:8:"advanced";s:8:"Required";s:5:"false";s:4:"Mask";s:5:"false";}s:5:"value";s:0:"";}i:6;a:2:{s:11:"@attributes";a:9:{s:4:"Name";s:24:"Semantic Scholar API Key";s:6:"Target";s:22:"CRW_SEARCH__S2_API_KEY";s:7:"Default";s:0:"";s:4:"Mode";s:0:"";s:11:"Description";s:88:"Optional Semantic Scholar API key that boosts research result quality. Works without it.";s:4:"Type";s:8:"Variable";s:7:"Display";s:8:"advanced";s:8:"Required";s:5:"false";s:4:"Mask";s:4:"true";}s:5:"value";s:0:"";}i:7;a:2:{s:11:"@attributes";a:9:{s:4:"Name";s:8:"API Keys";s:6:"Target";s:18:"CRW_AUTH__API_KEYS";s:7:"Default";s:0:"";s:4:"Mode";s:0:"";s:11:"Description";s:97:"Optional comma-separated API keys that gate the crw-server REST API. Leave empty for open access.";s:4:"Type";s:8:"Variable";s:7:"Display";s:8:"advanced";s:8:"Required";s:5:"false";s:4:"Mask";s:4:"true";}s:5:"value";s:0:"";}}s:12:"TemplatePath";s:35:"/tmp/GitHub/AppFeed/fastcrw-aio.xml";s:4:"Repo";s:18:"dub19's Repository";s:12:"CategoryList";a:1:{i:0;s:15:"Tools-Utilities";}s:16:"ChangeLogPresent";s:1:"1";s:9:"downloads";i:595;s:9:"FirstSeen";i:1787587644;s:10:"LastUpdate";i:1788496878;s:14:"LastUpdateScan";i:1790187285;s:8:"Category";s:15:"Tools:Utilities";s:2:"ID";i:4929;s:11:"Displayable";b:1;s:6:"Author";s:5:"dub19";s:13:"DockerHubName";s:11:"fastcrw-aio";s:8:"RepoName";s:18:"dub19's Repository";s:10:"SortAuthor";s:5:"dub19";s:8:"SortName";s:11:"fastcrw aio";s:6:"random";i:1148020894;s:9:"Blacklist";b:0;s:6:"MinVer";s:3:"6.0";s:4:"Path";s:107:"/tmp/community.applications/tempFiles/templates-community-apps/dub19sRepository/dub19-fastcrwaio-latest.xml";s:4:"Date";N;s:11:"BrandNewApp";b:1;s:10:"Deprecated";b:0;s:10:"Compatible";b:1;s:16:"ModeratorComment";N;}i:4930;a:41:{s:4:"Name";s:10:"gbrain-aio";s:10:"Repository";s:16:"dub19/gbrain-aio";s:8:"Registry";s:41:"https://hub.docker.com/r/dub19/gbrain-aio";s:7:"Network";s:6:"bridge";s:5:"Shell";s:2:"sh";s:10:"Privileged";s:5:"false";s:7:"Support";s:45:"https://github.com/wgross19/gbrain-aio/issues";s:7:"Project";s:38:"https://github.com/wgross19/gbrain-aio";s:8:"Overview";s:1052:"GBrain all-in-one for Unraid: a hosted knowledge base and MCP server for AI agents (Hermes Agent, OpenClaw, Codex). One container runs GBrain, PostgreSQL 17 + pgvector, Caddy TLS, and the job supervisor. Agents connect over HTTPS — Postgres is never exposed.

Basic/default setup: follow the five first-run steps below and leave optional advanced fields at their defaults. The container includes PostgreSQL and Caddy TLS, and starts the job supervisor.

First run (details are in each field's help text):
1. Set Postgres Password and Admin Bootstrap Token.
2. Set LAN Bind to your host IP. Leave Public URL empty to derive the LAN HTTPS address, unless you use a custom port, DNS name, reverse proxy, or Tailscale origin.
3. Set Brain Path to an empty folder.
4. Start, then open https://lan:3132/admin/ and paste the token.
5. Trust the generated CA once.

