y.applications/tempFiles/templates-community-apps/xompagesRepository/mdhiggins-plexautoskip-latest.xml";s:4:"Date";N;s:11:"BrandNewApp";b:1;s:10:"Deprecated";b:0;s:10:"trendDelta";d:0.502;s:12:"trendAverage";d:2.3424;s:10:"Compatible";b:1;s:16:"ModeratorComment";N;}i:4964;a:51:{s:4:"Name";s:16:"UmlautAdaptarrEX";s:10:"Repository";s:29:"lexfi/umlautadaptarrex:latest";s:8:"Registry";s:47:"https://hub.docker.com/r/lexfi/umlautadaptarrex";s:7:"Network";s:6:"bridge";s:5:"Shell";s:2:"sh";s:10:"Privileged";s:5:"false";s:7:"Support";s:49:"https://github.com/xpsony/UmlautAdaptarrEX/issues";s:7:"Project";s:42:"https://github.com/xpsony/UmlautAdaptarrEX";s:6:"ReadMe";s:65:"https://github.com/xpsony/UmlautAdaptarrEX/blob/main/README.en.md";s:7:"Discord";s:29:"https://discord.gg/src6zcH4rr";s:16:"ExtraSearchTerms";s:158:"umlaut umlaute adaptarr umlautadaptarr arr sonarr radarr lidarr readarr prowlarr nzbhydra indexer proxy newznab torznab german deutsch title rewrite tvdb tmdb";s:5:"WebUI";s:24:"http://[IP]:[PORT:5007]/";s:11:"TemplateURL";s:109:"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/xpsony/UmlautAdaptarrEX-Unraid-Template/main/templates/umlautadaptarrex.xml";s:4:"Icon";s:91:"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/xpsony/UmlautAdaptarrEX-Unraid-Template/main/icon-128.png";s:6:"MinVer";s:4:"6.12";s:7:"License";s:3:"MIT";s:8:"Overview";s:1766:"UmlautAdaptarrEX - Umlaut and multi-language title proxy for Sonarr, Radarr, Lidarr, Readarr and Prowlarr. Complete Next.js + Fastify + Prisma rewrite of the legacy .NET UmlautAdaptarr.

Sits between your *Arr stack and the indexers, rewrites searches and Newznab/Torznab responses on the fly so releases with umlauts, German titles, TVDB aliases or bad naming are reliably found, downloaded and imported. Ships a full Web UI with setup wizard, dashboard, library browser, sync runs, request and rename history, and live WebSocket logs. Configuration and title cache are stored in a persistent SQLite DB under /data - no external database required.

Highlights: Sonarr / Radarr (native via alternateTitles + optional TMDB) / Lidarr / Readarr / Prowlarr / NZB Hydra support, multiple instances per *Arr type, language plugins (German umlauts, Swedish umlauts, French accents) that can be combined, configurable title providers (TVDB, TMDB, db-cache), configurable search fan-out and release renaming, manual title overrides, two operating modes (Prowlarr indexer proxy on 5006 or direct as indexer on 5005), optional headless mode without the Web UI, UI in German, English, Swedish and French.

Ports: 5007 Web UI (open http://[IP]:5007/setup after the first start), 5005 Fastify API - the URL your *Arrs point at, 5006 HTTP-CONNECT proxy for Prowlarr indexers.

IMPORTANT - 1:1 port mapping: each port variable sets both the in-container bind port and the published host port, so host and container side must always be identical. To move a service to another port, change the host port, the container port AND the matching UMLAUTADAPTARREX_*_PORT variable to the same value. A mismatched mapping breaks /api proxying and the indexer URLs your *Arrs point at.";s:6:"Config";a:13:{i:0;a:2:{s:11:"@attributes";a:9:{s:4:"Name";s:11:"Web UI Port";s:6:"Target";s:4:"5007";s:7:"Default";s:4:"5007";s:4:"Mode";s:3:"tcp";s:11:"Description";s:312:"HTTP port for the Next.js web UI. Open this in your browser to reach the setup wizard and admin panel. IMPORTANT: the host port and the container port MUST be identical (1:1 mapping). To use a non-default port, change this value AND set the matching UMLAUTADAPTARREX_WEBUI_PORT variable below to the SAME number.";s:4:"Type";s:4:"Port";s:7:"Display";s:6:"always";s:8:"Required";s:4:"true";s:4:"Mask";s:5:"false";}s:5:"value";s:4:"5007";}i:1;a:2:{s:11:"@attributes";a:9:{s:4:"Name";s:8:"API Port";s:6:"Target";s:4:"5005";s:7:"Default";s:4:"5005";s:4:"Mode";s:3:"tcp";s:11:"Description";s:402:"Fastify API + WebSocket port. This is the URL you point your *Arr instances at (e.g. http://unraid-ip:5005/apikey/sonarr/api). Also serves /api/admin, /api/auth, /titlelookup and /ws/logs. IMPORTANT: the host port and the container port MUST be identical (1:1 mapping). To use a non-default port, change this value AND set the matching UMLAUTADAPTARREX_LEGACYAPI_PORT variable below to the SAME number.";s:4:"Type";s:4:"Port";s:7:"Display";s:6:"always";s:8:"Required";s:4:"true";s:4:"Mask";s:5:"false";}s:5:"value";s:4:"5005";}i:2;a:2:{s:11:"@attributes";a:9:{s:4:"Name";s:18:"Indexer Proxy Port";s:6:"Target";s:4:"5006";s:7:"Default";s:4:"5006";s:4:"Mode";s:3:"tcp";s:11:"Description";s:342:"TCP HTTP-CONNECT proxy for Prowlarr indexers. Configure this as Prowlarr's HTTP proxy so indexer responses get rewritten on the fly. IMPORTANT: the host port and the container port MUST be identical (1:1 mapping). To use a non-default port, change this value AND set the matching UMLAUTADAPTARREX_PROXY_PORT variable below to the SAME number.";s:4:"Type";s:4:"Port";s:7:"Display";s:6:"always";s:8:"Required";s:4:"true";s:4:"Mask";s:5:"false";}s:5:"value";s:4:"5006";}i:3;a:2:{s:11:"@attributes";a:9:{s:4:"Name";s:19:"API Port (variable)";s:6:"Target";s:31:"UMLAUTADAPTARREX_LEGACYAPI_PORT";s:7:"Default";s:4:"5005";s:4:"Mode";s:0:"";s:11:"Description";s:304:"In-container bind port for the Fastify API. MUST match the 'API Port' mapping above (1:1: host port = container port = this value). The image reads ONLY this branded variable -- the legacy PORT fallback was removed in 1.2.2. Leave at 5005 unless you also remapped the 'API Port' above to the same number.";s:4:"Type";s:8:"Variable";s:7:"Display";s:8:"advanced";s:8:"Required";s:5:"false";s:4:"Mask";s:5:"false";}s:5:"value";s:4:"5005";}i:4;a:2:{s:11:"@attributes";a:9:{s:4:"Name";s:22:"Web UI Port (variable)";s:6:"Target";s:27:"UMLAUTADAPTARREX_WEBUI_PORT";s:7:"Default";s:4:"5007";s:4:"Mode";s:0:"";s:11:"Description";s:317:"In-container bind port for the Next.js Web UI. MUST match the 'Web UI Port' mapping above (1:1: host port = container port = this value). The image reads ONLY this branded variable -- the legacy WEB_PORT fallback was removed in 1.2.2. Leave at 5007 unless you also remapped the 'Web UI Port' above to the same number.";s:4:"Type";s:8:"Variable";s:7:"Display";s:8:"advanced";s:8:"Required";s:5:"false";s:4:"Mask";s:5:"false";}s:5:"value";s:4:"5007";}i:5;a:2:{s:11:"@attributes";a:9:{s:4:"Name";s:29:"Indexer Proxy Port (variable)";s:6:"Target";s:27:"UMLAUTADAPTARREX_PROXY_PORT";s:7:"Default";s:4:"5006";s:4:"Mode";s:0:"";s:11:"Description";s:370:"In-container bind port for the Prowlarr HTTP-CONNECT proxy. MUST match the 'Indexer Proxy Port' mapping above (1:1: host port = container port = this value). When set, it overrides the value stored in the d